# Beta 1

_Beta 1 concluded with 0.2.20 (2026-05-21, plus the 2026-05-22 stock-market hotfix). Everything below this line is Beta 1 history._

## [0.2.20] - 2026-05-21

### Added (uniform state metrics + corporate margin model)

- **State metrics are now a shared cross-country catalog** - US / UK / DE / JP / IE / BR / CN state metric documents now get the same extended metric set instead of hiding country-specific fields behind `countryScope`. New shared/defaulted fields include trade balance, productivity growth, R&D intensity, export dependency, manufacturing competitiveness, secondary attainment, apprenticeship rate, public care waiting time, energy transition progress, housing supply growth, debt-to-GDP, co-determination quality, demographic decline, birth rate, and media trust variants. Seed helpers in `src/lib/seeds/shared/uniformStateMetrics.ts` keep new seed docs and baselines aligned, and `scripts/migrations/add-missing-metrics-2026-05.ts` backfills production `stateMetrics` / `stateBaselines` before recomputing national metrics.

- **Corporate sector margins now read the full state metric profile** - The old sparse state-metric modifier path only considered unemployment, grid reliability, corruption, and a few sector-gated fields. The new strategy-aware profile maps every official metric into sector channels such as labor cost, logistics, grid reliability, public safety, regulatory trust, health capacity, housing/land use, innovation, demographics, and public procurement. Effects are capped per metric, per channel, and in total (`STATE_METRIC_TOTAL_CAP = 8`) to keep margins readable. Strategy transitions blend source/target profiles while a sector is changing strategy. `src/lib/corporations/sectorMetricMarginProfiles.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/stockExchangeSnapshot.ts`.

- **Corporation margin diagnostics show metric contributors** - Corporation detail and sector detail queries now load full `stateMetrics`, pass the strategy-aware margin override into `computeAllMarginModifiers`, and expose `stateMetricContributions` plus `legacyStateMetricsModifier` for audit. The sector margin panel has a collapsible "Metric effects" section showing the strongest positive and negative metric contributions behind the margin. `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/sections/MarginsPanel.tsx`, `src/lib/corporations/queries/sectorDetail.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/queries/corporationDetail.ts`.

- **`useGameClock()` client hook and `getGameClock()` server helper** — Centralized game-time access with `gameTimeRef`. Time-remaining formatters now require `gameTimeRef` to prevent accidental wall-clock usage. `src/contexts/useGameClock.ts`, `src/lib/time/gameClock.server.ts`, `src/lib/utils/formatters.ts`.

- **Turn-number deadline fields for bills, cabinet nominations, and coalitions** — DB types and writers now populate `turnNumber` deadline fields alongside existing `Date` fields. Server checks prefer turn numbers; legacy rows fall back to dates. Backfilled by `scripts/migrations/2026-05-20-backfill-deadline-turn-numbers.ts`. `src/lib/db/types/legislation.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/cabinet.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/coalition.ts`.

### Changed

- **Metrics pages render from the unified catalog** - Country metrics pages and shared metric cards now use `metricAppliesToCountry` / actual metric presence instead of country-specific definition filtering, so newly shared fields are visible wherever the document carries values. Metric scoring thresholds were expanded for the new fields. `src/app/country/[code]/metrics/`, `src/components/MetricsCategoryDisplay.tsx`, `src/lib/utils/metricScoring.ts`.

- **National fiscal metrics come from budget documents** - `computeNationalMetrics` now reads federal/national budget docs and writes national `governance.budgetBalance` and `governance.debtToGdp` from actual surplus/GDP and debt-to-GDP values instead of relying only on population-weighted state rows. `src/lib/nationalMetrics.ts`.

- **Macroeconomic tuning** - Inflation now includes a housing/rent pressure component from the national cost-of-living index, and unowned-sector default GDP growth is reduced from 2.0% to 0.5% so owned-sector contractions can pull state GDP negative. `src/lib/budget/inflation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/gdpGrowth.ts`.

- **Metric decay no longer runs a second no-op writer** - `processMetricDecay` is now an explicit compatibility no-op because state metric decay is handled in the state policy effects phase with `stateMetrics` and `stateBaselines` together. This avoids a redundant writer in the parallel turn phase. `src/lib/turn/metricDecay.ts`.

- **News page ships server-rendered initial articles** - `/news` now fetches the first article page server-side for faster initial render and crawler visibility, with a short editorial intro. The client feed restores the server-rendered posts when switching back from ad posts. `src/app/news/page.tsx`, `src/app/news/NewsPageClient.tsx`, `src/components/news/NewsFeed.tsx`.

- **Ad banner placement tightened to public editorial pages** - Player ad banners now render only on public discovery/content surfaces (`/about`, `/contact`, `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/changelog`, `/news`, `/wiki`, `/guides`) instead of broad game UI routes. `src/lib/adTrialPaths.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Forward stock split now blocked when scaled price would fall below MIN_SHARE_PRICE** — The consolidate route previously allowed splits large enough to push the per-share price below the €0.01 floor. Because the turn engine clamps all prices to `MIN_SHARE_PRICE`, such splits inflated market cap by orders of magnitude rather than preserving it. The route now rejects any forward split whose projected price is below the floor and tells the CEO the maximum permitted target at the current price. Bug #1685. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/consolidate/route.ts`.

- **MOP admin reverse split (turn 997)** — MOP's CEO executed a 90.9× forward split (2.75T → 250T shares) followed by a 5% issuance to 262.5T total. The `MIN_SHARE_PRICE` floor held the price at ~€0.01 throughout, inflating MOP's market cap from ~€27B to ~€2.6T and driving the Global Market Index to +5,240%. Shares administratively reverse-split to 2,750,000,000,000 (original count), price restored to €0.01, shareholder allocations recalculated proportionally. Bug #1685.

- **Corporation history preserves old-vs-new state metric margin audit values** - Turn snapshots now store both the new `stateMetricsMod` and temporary `legacyStateMetricsMod` so margin changes can be audited against the previous sparse metric system. `src/lib/db/types/corporationHistory.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/types.ts`.

- **German national-party "State Parties" tab now lists the 16 Länder instead of US states** — `StatePartyLinksTab.tsx` and `CommitteeElectionsPanel.tsx` both fell through to a hardcoded US-state array for any country other than UK or Japan. Germany (`DE`) now maps to `deRegions` so the links show Baden-Württemberg, Bayern, Berlin, etc. Bug #0568. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/StatePartyLinksTab.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CommitteeElectionsPanel.tsx`.

- **Game-clock alignment across elections, bills, cabinet, and coalitions** — A systematic sweep replaced wall-clock `Date` comparisons with turn-number checks throughout the simulation. Election phase labels (endorsements, office page, composition, dashboard, canvassing, PIP, wiki live-stats, landing page), congress leadership windows, snap-election spawn timers, NPP recruitment cooldown, character relocation cooldown, cabinet nomination voting windows, parliamentary votes (PM appointment, no-confidence), caucus whip, and whippable bills (region, caucus, party-level filters) now anchor on the game clock. Legacy rows without turn-number deadlines are backfilled by `scripts/migrations/2026-05-20-backfill-deadline-turn-numbers.ts`. `src/lib/time/gameClock.server.ts`, `src/contexts/useGameClock.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, and ~120 call sites.

- **Turn-system auto-pause on cron drift** — When game clock drift exceeds 4 hours, the turn processor auto-pauses with `pauseKind: "auto"` and surfaces the reason in the turn-status API, moderator panel, and turn controls. A clock-drift banner warns at the 2-hour threshold. Manual resumes clear pause fields correctly. `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/components/moderator/TurnPausePanel.tsx`, `src/components/admin/ClockDriftBanner.tsx`, `src/lib/time/clockDrift.ts`.

- **Maintenance-mode redirect gated at proxy layer** — Maintenance check moved from layout to `src/proxy.ts`, preventing flash-of-content. Adds 5-minute stale-while-revalidate cache, fail-open behavior, and shared bypass-token helper. `src/proxy.ts`, `src/lib/maintenanceStatus.ts`, `src/app/layout.tsx`.

- **Coalition accept paths scoped to the correct coalition** — `acceptInvite`, `acceptJoin`, `kick`, and `leave` now validate the actor's `coalitionId` matches the target coalition, preventing a party from silently belonging to two coalitions at once. Coalition list API returns `memberParties[].partyId` as the sequential ID to match client checks. `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/[id]/`, `src/components/legislature/useCoalitionView.ts`.

- **Election intermediate state: upcoming + started-primary** — Handles the gap between primary spawn and primary start time so the phase status strip no longer renders "Opens in Ended" after an admin timer set. `src/components/elections/ElectionPhaseStatusStrip.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/elections/route.ts`.

- **Cron timezone switched to UTC** — Eliminates DST drift in turn scheduling. Fog-of-war refresh gated on `isActive` so it doesn't run against paused games. `src/lib/cron.ts`.

### Refactored

- **Real-clock countdown helpers extracted** — `formatRealTimeCountdown` separates wall-clock countdown displays (cooldown timers, voting timers, next-turn timer) from game-clock logic. `src/lib/utils/formatters.ts`.

### Docs / Ops

- **Private-corp share market design captured** - Added the bug #0562 design spec for private corporation share issuance, cap-table trading, shareholder caps, and private-corp order-book behavior. `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-19-private-corp-share-markets-design.md`.

- **Sector margin audit tooling** - Added `scripts/debug/audit-sector-metric-margins.mjs` for read-only comparison of old vs. new state metric margin modifiers across production sector data.

- **Repository hygiene** - Redacted raw env values from an archived incident transcript, moved local DB audit scripts to `MONGODB_URI`-driven configuration, and added `.hermes/` to `.gitignore` as local agent scratch output.

- **Germany parity audit and admin tooling** - Added `/api/admin/country/DE/readiness` diagnostic route for pre-launch validation. Added `/api/admin/heal/de-bundestag-seats` diagnostic for per-Land seat count verification. Added `/api/country/DE/map/overview` API support (was UK/CN only). Added tests for DE cabinet constants (`deCabinet.test.ts`), historical seats (`historicalSeats.de.test.ts`), and map overview (`deMapOverview.test.ts`). `src/app/api/admin/country/DE/readiness/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/heal/de-bundestag-seats/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/map/overview/route.ts`.

## [0.2.19] - 2026-05-19

### Added (Governor's Office subsystem)

- **Governor's Office page** at `/country/[code]/region/[id]/office` with Overview / Address / Orders / Endorsements / Legislation Queue tabs. Each office runs on a shared Office AP pool (`governorOfficeState.gubernatorialActions`, cap 3, regen +1 every 18 turns) spent across all four action types. One-row-per-seat plus one row per country's national pseudo-stateId; seeded by `seedOfficeStates` on reset and by `scripts/migrations/createGovernorOffices.ts` for production rollout. `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/office/`, `src/lib/governorOffice/seedOfficeStates.ts`, `src/lib/constants/governorOffice.ts`.

- **State of the State address (v2)** — Governors deliver a multi-effect address: additive approval bump, agenda-bonus cross-pressure nudge on co-partisan NPP voting in emphasized bill categories, and a write-side demographic turnout boost (headroom-clamped ±20). Address row carries `approvalEffect`, `agendaEffect`, and `demographicEffect` with per-effect `expiresAtTurn` windows. Expiry phase `processGovernorAddressExpiry` reverts turnout precisely (per-state map for national scope, scalar for state). Auto-posts to the news wire. `src/lib/governorOffice/address/deliverAddress.ts`, `src/lib/turn/governorAddressExpiry.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/governorAddress.ts`.

- **National Address (federal head-of-government)** — US President delivers the "State of the Union", UK PM delivers "Address to the Nation", DE Chancellor delivers "Government Declaration", JP PM delivers "Policy Speech". Operates on the same `governorAddresses` collection with `stateId = getNationalStateId(countryId)`. National-scope demographic turnout fans out to every state in the country with per-state headroom clamping snapshotted on the address row for precise expiry revert. `src/app/api/country/[code]/executive/address/route.ts`, `src/app/whitehouse/WhiteHouseAddressTab.tsx`, `getNationalAddressName()`.

- **Executive Orders + Orders in Council** — Governors (US) and federal heads of government issue policy nudges that shift the underlying `StatePolicy` by ±1 step (or ±2 with extra AP) for `EXEC_ORDER_DURATION_TURNS` turns or until rescinded/superseded by a passed bill. Two-slot cap per scope; supersession is automatic in `billEnactment`. Parliamentary countries surface the same mechanism as "Order in Council" (UK/DE/JP/etc.) via `getExecutiveOrderName()` / `getExecutiveOrderNamePlural()`. Order issuance posts to the news wire (`generateOrderNews`). `src/lib/governorOffice/orders/issueOrder.ts`, `src/lib/governorOffice/orders/rescindOrder.ts`, `src/lib/turn/governorOrders.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/executive/orders/route.ts`.

- **Governor + Executive endorsements with vote multipliers** — `GovernorEndorsement` and `ExecutiveEndorsement` collections record office-side endorsements distinct from the existing `playerEndorsements`. Governors can endorse races within their state (sub-national + federal house/senate + presidential) via `getEndorseableElectionTypes(countryId)`; federal leaders can endorse races across the country except their own seat via `getExecutiveEndorseableElectionTypes(countryId)`. Both spend Office AP, both block cross-party endorsements, both enforce one-active-per-(endorser, race). Vote-side bonuses: `GOVERNOR_ENDORSEMENT_STATE_BONUS = 1.015` in `presidentialElectionEngine.accumulatePresidentVoteTurn` (state-scoped within endorser's state); `EXECUTIVE_ENDORSEMENT_VOTE_BONUS = 1.015` in `tallyManagement.accumulateVoteTurn` (race-id-scoped). Campaign-side: both endorsement types add to the campaign-actions calculation in `campaignTurn` at `GOVERNOR_ENDORSEMENT_CAMPAIGN_ACTIONS` weight (suppressed for governor→presidential to avoid double-stacking with the state vote bonus). `src/lib/governorOffice/endorsements/`, `src/lib/db/types/{governorEndorsement,executiveEndorsement}.ts`, `src/lib/presidentialElectionEngine.ts:45`, `src/lib/electionEngine/tallyManagement.ts:187`.

- **Auto-withdraw turn phases** — `processGovernorEndorsements` and `processExecutiveEndorsements` run before `processCampaignTurn` each turn and withdraw endorsements when (a) the election is no longer active (`election_ended`), (b) the endorsed candidate is no longer active (`candidate_inactive`), or (c) the endorsing office-holder is no longer in office (`governor_left_office` / `leader_left_office`, via `isSittingLeader`). `src/lib/turn/governorEndorsements.ts`, `src/lib/turn/executiveEndorsements.ts`, `src/lib/governorOffice/isSittingLeader.ts`.

- **Per-party demographic favorability** — Address-driven per-`(party, voterGroup)` favorability delta, persisted in `partyGroupFavorability` with `expiresAtTurn`. When an address targets a demographic group and the leader belongs to a party, that party gets a per-group appeal boost (`ADDRESS_PARTY_GROUP_FAVORABILITY_DELTA = 5`) for the same window as the demographic turnout effect. Election vote-distribution reads active rows and multiplies the group weight by `(1 + delta/100)` in the per-group inner loop. Independent / unaffiliated leaders skip this since there is no party row. Threaded through both `presidentialElectionEngine` and `tallyManagement` via `DistributeVotesOptions.partyGroupFavorabilityByKey`. `src/lib/db/types/partyGroupFavorability.ts`, `src/lib/governorOffice/address/partyGroupFavorabilityLoader.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/voteDistribution.ts:139`.

- **Address + Order news wire** — `generateAddressNews` and `generateOrderNews` post to the "executive" `NewsCategory`, picked up by Discord webhook subscribers via `/api/discord-bot/news?category=executive`. Address news includes the LARP speech body when provided; order news includes the policy-option transition (`Shifting from X to Y`). Both are best-effort try/catch — a news failure never aborts the underlying action. `src/lib/news.ts:189,229`.

- **Tabbed executive pages for parliamentary countries** — UK / DE / JP government pages get the same Overview / Address / Orders / Endorsements tab shell as the US White House. `ExecutiveTabsClient` wraps the existing executive hub layout and reuses `WhiteHouseAddressTab`, `WhiteHouseOrdersTab`, `WhiteHouseEndorsementsTab` with country-aware labels (e.g. "Order in Council" instead of "Executive Order"). Address / Orders / Endorsements tabs are visible only to the sitting head of government or an admin. `src/app/country/[code]/executive/ExecutiveTabsClient.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/executive/{UK,DE,JP}GovernmentExecutiveHub.tsx`.

- **Admin Override for Address / Order issuance** — Admins can act on behalf of vacant or NPP-held offices by setting `adminOverride: true` on the POST. Cooldown is waived, AP / NPI debits are skipped, and the row is tagged `adminProposed: true` for forensic traceability. Route checks `isSittingLeader || (isAdmin && adminOverride)`. `src/lib/governorOffice/address/deliverAddress.ts:111`, `src/lib/governorOffice/orders/issueOrder.ts:74`.

### Fixed (test mocks + pre-existing development-side failures, swept during the full branch audit)

- **`presidentialRaceRebalance.test.ts` + `presidentialBalanceDiagnostic.test.ts`** — `createMockDb` fallbacks were missing `governorEndorsements.find().toArray()` and `partyGroupFavorability.find().project().toArray()`, causing 7 test failures the moment the new election-engine reads were added. Added explicit collection stubs and broadened the fallback to include `.project()` for projection-chained queries.

- **`centralBankChairTurn.test.ts`** — `COUNTRY_CONFIGS.US.id` was missing from the test mock, so `getNationalBudgetId("US")` resolved to `"US"` instead of `"federal"` and the infamy expectations broke. Added `id: "US"` to the mock.

- **`forexTurn.test.ts`** — `expireStaleOrders` was refactored to use the atomic `updateMany → find by status+updatedAt → bulkWrite refunds` pattern, but the test still mocked the old `find → updateMany by _id` flow. Stacked two `mockResolvedValueOnce` calls on `currencyOrders.updateMany` so the stuck-recovery (call #1) returns 0 and the expiry transition (call #2) returns `modifiedCount: 1`, and updated the assertion to match the new filter shape.

- **`stockExchangeSnapshot.test.ts`** — Default collection mock lacked `bulkWrite`, breaking `generateWealthListSnapshots` after the refactor to bulk-upsert `wealthListSnapshots` + `wealthListHistory`. Added `bulkWrite` to the default mock, captured per-collection bulkWrite mocks for the `wealthListSnapshots`/`wealthListHistory` calls, and rewrote the snapshot assertion to read from the bulkWrite ops instead of the no-longer-called `updateOne`.

### Changed

- **Endorsement vote multipliers reduced 3% → 1.5%** — `GOVERNOR_ENDORSEMENT_STATE_BONUS` and `EXECUTIVE_ENDORSEMENT_VOTE_BONUS` are now 1.015 (down from 1.03). Endorsements remain materially valuable via campaign-action boosts but a single endorsement no longer single-handedly moves a state in a close presidential.

- **Endorsement spend moved from character actions to Office AP** — All four office actions (Address, Order, Endorsement, Queue Bill) now draw from the same `governorOfficeState.gubernatorialActions` pool. Character `actions` is untouched by office work.

- **Office AP regen 1 per 18 turns** (down from the prior regen cadence) — Caps governors and federal leaders at 3 actions per ~54 game-hours, matching the action economy for cabinet-level decisions.

- **Governor's Office endorsement GET endpoint** at `/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/office/endorsements` now returns the same race-type allowlist that `createEndorsement` accepts (`getEndorseableElectionTypes(countryId)` + presidential merge), so the API matches the SSR page's race list. The endpoint is currently only consumed for POST/DELETE by the UI; this aligns it for future client-side refresh use.

### Reset / Bootstrap

- **`resetGameWorld` wipes all seven Governor's Office collections** — `governorAddresses`, `governorExecutiveOrders`, `governorEndorsements`, `executiveEndorsements`, `governorOfficeState`, `governorLegislationQueue`, `partyGroupFavorability`. Also clears stale `users.activeCharacterId` pointers (previously caused a login-redirect loop after reset) and reseeds office states. `src/lib/admin/resetGameWorld.ts`.

- **`scripts/migrations/createGovernorOffices.ts` extended to seed national pseudo-state rows** — Now seeds `federal` / `uk_national` / `de_national` / `jp_national` in addition to regional executive seats. Without these, the federal Address / Executive Orders / Orders in Council flows would silently fail on production with "Insufficient office action points." Migration stays local until reviewed per `feedback_migrations_local_only`.

### Profile

- **Authed users without a character redirect to `/create-character`** instead of `/login` — `getProfile` previously returned null for both unauthenticated and no-character cases; the page treated both as "not logged in" and bounced to `/login`, creating a redirect loop after Game Reset. Now distinguishes the two cases. `src/app/profile/page.tsx`.

- **`CareerHistory` no longer leaks ObjectIds through the RSC boundary** — Narrowed the `character` prop to `Pick<Character, "careerHistory" | "currentOffice" | "countryId">` to avoid "Only plain objects can be passed to Client Components from Server Components" on `/profile`.

---

## [0.2.18] - 2026-05-15

### Fixed (corporate dissolution payout — bug #0540)

- **Corporation dissolution now pays every shareholder bucket** — `allocateShareholderPool` previously divided the shareholder pool by `corp.totalShares` but only emitted payout rows for character/imperial shareholders, silently dropping the slice attributable to corporate equity holders and `publicFloat`. On the Elevance Health force-liquidation this destroyed ≈$26.35B of the $56.07B pool. The helper now returns a `ShareholderAllocation` with `characterRows`, `corporationRows`, and a `publicFloatRow`. The bond-default executor credits each corporate shareholder via `$inc liquidCapital`in the receiving corp's home currency, and routes the`publicFloat`slice to the country's central bank`reserveBalance`(via`getBankId`+`writeGovBudgetLocal`). Quick-dissolve POST `/api/corporations/[id]/dissolve`was similarly broken on public corps with passed dissolution votes — it credited the entire`liquidCapital`to the CEO regardless of cap table — and now uses the same pro-rata allocator (private corps still effectively yield 100% to the CEO since they have no other shareholders). Both`bond_default`and`corp_dissolution_distribution`ledger rows carry full reconciliation totals so admin forensic queries balance.`src/lib/bonds/corporateBondDefault.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/executeCorporationBondDefaultDissolution.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/dissolve/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/dissolve/route.ts`.

- **Dissolve preview surfaces the requesting CEO's actual share + full distribution table** — The bond-default crisis modal previously led with "Est. shareholder pool (after bonds)" — the _total_ pool — and the per-character payout list omitted corporate shareholders entirely. CEOs with a 52% stake reading the modal reasonably believed they would receive the headline number. The quick-dissolve panel had the matching defect, labeling `returnedCapitalHome` (full pool) as "Cash you personally receive." Both surfaces now show the CEO's pro-rata cut prominently and expose a breakdown table covering every shareholder bucket including corporate holders and the public-float → central-bank-reserve row. `previewQuickDissolve` adds `ceoShareHome` / `ceoShareAnchor` / `ceoIsSoleShareholder` plus `characterRows` / `corporateRows` / `publicFloatRow`. `src/lib/corporation/previewQuickDissolve.ts`, `src/components/corporation/ceo/CeoAdminSubtab.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/DefaultedBondCrisisModal.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/ceo/useCeoAdminState.ts`.

- **Elevance Health back-pay scripts** — Dry-run + apply scripts at `scripts/recover-elevance-dropped-payout-{dryrun,apply}.mjs`. The apply script credits General Electric (≈$25.75B USD) and Whitlam Manufacturing Corp (≈¥5.21B JPY) at the FX rate snapshotted at the dissolution turn (`exchangeRates.rateHistory` @ turn 877), emits matching `corp_dissolution_distribution` ledger rows tagged with `meta.bugFixCompensation = "0540"`, and refuses to double-pay on re-run. Gated behind `--confirm`; default mode is print-only.

### Security

- **API route audit: scoped directories** — Audited 118 mutating country routes and 8 mutating election routes for auth guards, country isolation, and write consistency. All routes have appropriate auth guards. No unguarded endpoints found.

### Fixed

- **Orphan corporate sectors no longer block attack-sector with "Defender corporation not found"** — When a corp got deleted but its `corporateSectors` rows weren't fully cleaned up (historical dissolution edge case or a cleanup-skipping deletion path), the region economy view rendered the sector as an `"Unknown"` defender with an attack button. Clicking it died at the defender lookup in `POST /api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/attack-sector` with `"Defender corporation not found"` (bugs #0537, #0539). Two-layer fix: (1) `GET /api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy` now filters orphan sectors out of the `owners` list so they no longer surface as attackable rows — their slot is naturally absorbed by the unowned-market display; (2) `POST .../attack-sector` self-heals when it hits an orphan: deletes the stale sector row and returns a 404 with `"That corporation has been dissolved. The sector's market share has been returned to the unowned pool — refresh and use Split Unowned Market."` instead of the bare not-found error. Paired with `scripts/debug/audit-orphan-corporate-sectors.mjs` (report-only) and `scripts/migrations/2026-05-17-heal-orphan-corporate-sectors.ts` (`--apply` to delete the stale rows) to sweep existing orphans out of production data. `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/attack-sector/route.ts`.

- **Bill proposal schema accepts the Bundestag** — `proposeBillSchema.chamber` only allowed `house | senate | joint | commons | shugiin | sangiin`, so German players proposing a Bundestag bill via `POST /api/country/de/legislature/bills` failed Zod validation before reaching the country-aware proposal logic (which already maps `lowerChamber.key` to `bundestag` for DE). Added `bundestag` to the enum. Since the same schema is shared with the US-only `POST /api/congress/bills` route, that route now rejects non-US chambers (`house | senate | joint`) up front with a 400, so an admin can't accidentally produce a US bill with `originChamber: "bundestag"`. `src/lib/api/schemas/congress.ts`, `src/app/api/congress/bills/route.ts`.

- **Party whip routes accept German chambers** — The three whip Zod chamber enums (national party, caucus, regional party) only allowed `house | senate | commons | lords | stateSenate | shugiin | sangiin` (plus `regionalCouncil` on the regional route), so any whip directive issued in a German session — bill, leadership election, PM/no-confidence vote, or cabinet nomination — failed validation with "Invalid enum value" before reaching country-aware logic like `getConfidenceWhipChamber` / `getCabinetWhipChamber` (which already resolve to `bundestag` for DE). Added `bundestag` and `landtag` to all three whip schemas. To prevent the player-whip apply phase from routing German leadership whips into US-only collections (`speakerNominations` / `houseLeadershipNominations` / `senateLeadershipNominations`), the national and caucus routes now reject `targetType: "speakerElection" | "leadershipElection"` when `chamber` is `bundestag` or `landtag` — Germany uses `pmAppointmentVote` / `noConfidenceVote` for executive selection. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip/route.ts`.

- **Home-state surge uses forex-aware fund helpers** — The presidential primary `home-state-surge` endpoint previously read and debited the legacy `funds` field directly, bypassing `currencyBalances.campaign` in forex-enabled countries. It now uses `getCampaignFunds`, `buildCampaignFundsInc`, and `campaignFundsInternalToStored` with an atomic `$gte` guard on the canonical balance field. Also adds an atomic guard on `actions` to prevent TOCTOU race conditions. `src/app/api/elections/[id]/home-state-surge/route.ts`.
- **Caucus tax turn pass uses forex-aware balance check and atomic guard** — The turn-phase caucus tax processor checked the legacy `funds` field for affordability and used it as the atomic guard, which could skip members with sufficient `currencyBalances.campaign` or allow overdraft when `funds` was stale. It now uses `getCampaignFunds` for the pre-check and guards on the canonical field (`currencyBalances.campaign` when forex enabled). `src/lib/turn/caucusTax.ts`.
- **Party creation uses forex-aware atomic guard** — The country party-creation route checked `funds: { $gte: 1000000 }` in its atomic filter while the `$inc` used `buildCampaignFundsInc`, creating the same forex field mismatch. It now guards on `currencyBalances.campaign` when forex is enabled. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/route.ts`.
- **Cabinet bill proposal uses atomic `$inc` for national influence** — The cabinet-bills route decremented `nationalInfluence` via `$set` (absolute value) instead of `$inc`, creating a TOCTOU race where concurrent bill proposals could over-spend NPI. The error-recovery rollback also restored a stale read value via `$set` instead of rolling back with `$inc`. Both paths now use atomic `$inc`. `src/app/api/country/[code]/legislature/cabinet-bills/route.ts`.
- **Economy attack routes use atomic `$inc` for split escalation** — Both `attack-sector` and `attack` (unowned-sector split) incremented `splitEscalation` via `$set` after reading the current value, allowing concurrent attacks to overwrite each other and lose increments. Both now use `$inc: { splitEscalation: 1 }`. `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/attack-sector/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/attack/route.ts`.
- **Country isolation hardening across 8 routes** — Multiple mutating routes loaded states, corporations, bills, elections, or discussion posts by `_id` without verifying they belong to the URL's `countryId`. Added `countryId` (and `partyId` where applicable) to the query filters in: economy attack-sector and attack (state + defender corp), state-party tax (state), national and caucus whip (bill re-fetch), slate invitation withdrawal (election re-fetch), national and state-party discussion post deletion. Prevents cross-country entity ID enumeration and accidental mutations against foreign data.

### Added

- **Home-state surge integration tests** — Four focused tests covering legacy-funds success, insufficient funds rejection, forex-aware debit, and duplicate-surge conflict. `src/app/api/elections/__tests__/home-state-surge.test.ts`.
- **Nation dropdown with country switcher** — The navbar "Nation" dropdown now shows the active country's flag and name, and includes a "Switch Nation View" button that opens an inline picker to jump to any configured country. `src/components/NationDropdown.tsx`.

### Performance

- **23 N+1 MongoDB query batching fixes across turn system** — All per-document loops in turn processing replaced with batched `find` + `bulkWrite` patterns. Key reductions: `gameHealthSnapshot` 77→12 queries/turn, `metricHistory` 50+→2, `tradeGrowthMirror` 12→2, `centralBankChairTurn` 4N→4. Files touched: `gameHealthSnapshot.ts`, `metricHistory.ts`, `metricDecay.ts`, `tradeGrowthMirror.ts`, `centralBankChairTurn.ts`, `interestRateSnapshot.ts`, `stockExchangeSnapshot.ts`, `crisisTurn.ts`, `forexTurn.ts`, `ukBillLifecycle.ts`, `deBillLifecycle.ts`, `jpBillLifecycle.ts`, `billLifecycle.ts`, `billEnactment.ts`, `partyActionGeneration.ts`, `ministerialOrderProcessing.ts`, `voteReminders.ts`, `primaryResolution.ts`, `generate.ts`, `resolve-primaries/route.ts`, `electionOpponents.ts`.

### Fixed (policy / parliamentary)

- **German federal policy multiplier corrected** — National policy proposals in Germany applied effects using the US 1/50 per-state divisor instead of the correct DE 1/16 (one Bundestag bill covers 16 Länder). Added `DE_FEDERAL_MULTIPLIER` constant and wired it into `FEDERAL_MULTIPLIER_BY_COUNTRY`; `policyEffects.ts` and `demographicEffects.ts` now apply DE national policies to all German Länder at the correct scale. `src/lib/constants/formulas.ts`, `src/lib/turn/policyEffects.ts`, `src/lib/turn/demographicEffects.ts`.
- **UK and JP cabinet transitions use correct collections** — `cabinetTransition.ts` previously routed both UK and JP cabinet updates through the UK-specific `ukCabinetMembers` path. JP now correctly reads from `cabinetMembers`. `src/lib/turn/cabinetTransition.ts`.
- **Cabinet cleared on parliamentary seat updates and government dissolution** — `clearCabinetOnTransition` and a `deleteMany` on `cabinetMembers` are now called in both `updateParliamentaryGovernmentSeats` and `unformGovernmentAndVacatePM`, preventing ghost cabinet records after elections or VONC votes. `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`.
- **Party chair NI bonuses always apply regardless of player count** — `actionRefresh.ts` gated the national-influence bonus behind `characters.length < 10`, silently dropping it in larger games. Gate removed. `src/lib/turn/actionRefresh.ts`.

### Fixed (forex / turn)

- **Forex expiry loop processes correct order set** — `expireStaleOrders` previously iterated the pre-transition `expiring` set; a crash mid-loop could re-expire and double-refund the same orders on the next run. The loop now iterates `justExpired` (queried after status transition) so only genuinely-just-expired orders are refunded. `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`.
- **Forex limit-order filling uses atomic claim before crediting funds** — `processTriggeredLimitOrders` now flips an order from `open`/`partial` → `processing` atomically before crediting proceeds, preventing double-fills on concurrent runs. Stuck `processing` orders older than 2 turns are automatically reset to `open` for recovery. `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`.
- **Forex intervention and limit orders route to correct bank document** — `persistInterventionSideEffects` and `processTriggeredLimitOrders` now use `getBankId()` so eurozone member countries (e.g. DE) update the ECB document rather than a phantom per-country record. `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`.

### Fixed (state bills / sovereign default)

- **State bill lifecycle uses `findOneAndUpdate` claim loops** — `stateBillLifecycle.ts` previously used `find` + loop + `update` patterns that could process the same bill twice on concurrent turn runners. All stage transitions now use `findOneAndUpdate` atomic claims. `src/lib/legislature/stateBillLifecycle.ts`.
- **`countryId` written into new state bill documents** — `proposeStateBill.ts` now sets `countryId` at creation time, enabling country-isolation queries downstream. `src/lib/legislature/proposeStateBill.ts`.
- **Crisis auto-action repudiates countries stuck after executive decision window** — `crisisAutoAction.ts` (new) auto-repudiates countries still in `crisisPending` after the 48-hour window expires without an executive decision. Called from `bondTurn.ts` before `legislativeTurn`. `src/lib/turn/sovereignDefault/crisisAutoAction.ts`, `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`.

### Fixed (central bank routing)

- **Central bank operations route to correct document for eurozone members** — `savingsInterestTurn.ts`, and the admin `appoint`, `chair-controls`, and `account/detail` routes previously filtered or updated by `countryId`, routing DE and other eurozone members to a phantom per-country document instead of the shared ECB record. All now use `getBankId()`. `src/lib/turn/savingsInterestTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/central-bank/`.

### Fixed (elections)

- **General election resolution uses atomic claim guard** — `resolveOneGeneralElection` now atomically flips a `resolving` flag before processing; concurrent turn runners that lose the claim bail out immediately instead of double-writing office data. `src/lib/turn/election/generalResolution.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/election.ts`.
- **Presidential incumbent `currentOffice` cleared on replacement** — When a losing incumbent president or VP is replaced, `presidentResolution.ts` now also clears `currentOffice` on the character document so the title doesn't persist after the `electedOfficials` record is removed. `src/lib/turn/election/presidentResolution.ts`.
- **NPP incumbents excluded from Phase 2 election entry** — Incumbents defending a seat now only enter via Phase 1 (their own seat); they are skipped in the Phase 2 open-seat sweep so they can't land in a higher-priority race when their next-cycle primary hasn't been created yet in the same turn. `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.ts`.

### Fixed (multi-country)

- **Brazil and other presidential-government countries no longer read inflation from the US federal budget** — Seven files used `governmentType === "presidential" ? "federal" : countryId` to pick the federal budget document ID, routing Brazil (presidential) to the US `_id: "federal"` budget instead of its own `_id: "BR"` document. All now call `getNationalBudgetId()` from `@/lib/bonds/sovereign`. Affected: `interestRateSnapshot.ts`, `countryCentralBankDetail.ts`, `inflationDiagnostics.ts`, `centralBankChairTurn.ts`, `gameHealthSnapshot.ts`, `tradeGrowthMirror.ts`.
- **Party merge proposal no longer fails with "Invalid ID format"** — The `CreateProposalForm` merge tab fetched the parties list and sent `party.id` as `targetPartyId`, but `id` in the list response is the sequential integer string (e.g. `"5"`), not the MongoDB ObjectId. The server schema validates `targetPartyId` against a 24-char hex regex and rejected every submission. Added `objectId: party._id.toString()` to the parties list response and switched the form to send `target.objectId`. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CreateProposalForm.tsx`.

- **NATIONAL_SCOPE extended to BR, IE, CN, NG** — Four additional country codes added to the national-scope lookup so policy, bill, and budget queries work correctly for Brazil, Ireland, China, and Nigeria. `src/lib/constants/nationalScope.ts`.
- **State tick rates no longer fall back to "federal" scope for non-US countries** — `computeStateTickRates` previously used `"federal"` as the fallback national scope ID when a country had no entry in `NATIONAL_SCOPE`, silently applying US federal policies to non-US states. Non-US countries with no national-scope ID now get an empty national-policy list instead. `src/lib/api/stateTickRates.ts`.
- **Bill country resolution uses `COUNTRY_CONFIGS` instead of hardcoded list** — `inferCountryIdFromStateId` now checks `prefix in COUNTRY_CONFIGS` rather than a hardcoded US/UK/DE/JP whitelist, so any configured country can be resolved from its `{cc}_national` state ID. `src/lib/congress/resolveBillCountryId.ts`.
- **Bill enrichment national-scope fallback uses `{cc}_national` pattern** — `resolveBillProvisions` falls back to `${countryId.toLowerCase()}_national` instead of `"federal"` for countries not yet in `NATIONAL_SCOPE`. `src/lib/congress/billEnrichment.ts`.
- **Budget ID lookup replaced with `getNationalBudgetId`** — Hardcoded `BUDGET_ID_BY_COUNTRY`/`BUDGET_ID_BY_SCOPE` maps removed from `billEnactment.ts` and `budget/spending.ts`; both now call `getNationalBudgetId()` from `@/lib/bonds/sovereign`. `src/lib/billEnactment.ts`, `src/lib/budget/spending.ts`.

### Fixed (corporations)

- **Corporation vote resolves immediately when threshold is met** — The vote POST route now re-fetches the vote after each ballot and calls `resolveCorporationVoteIfReady` in-request; when a decisive vote is cast (e.g. 68% YES meeting a 50% threshold), effects are applied and notifications sent immediately rather than waiting for the next turn. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/votes/[voteId]/vote/route.ts`.
- **Share issuance vote approval records share trade history** — `voteEffects.ts` now calls `recordShareTrade` with `kind: "issuance"` when a share issuance vote passes, keeping the trade history consistent with other issuance paths. `src/lib/corporations/votes/voteEffects.ts`.

### Chore

- **Committee system fully removed (pending redesign)** — The party national committee and congressional committee assignment systems have been stripped out until a replacement design is ready. Removed: `committeeIds` from `PoliticalParty`; `CommitteeAssignment`, `committeeDelays`, `delayedUntil` from `Bill` and `EnrichedBillDetail`; `committee_delay` bill action and `canCommitteeDelay` enrichment; committee notification types; committee election/candidate/vote types and collections; turn-phase `nationalCommitteeElections`; committee influence bonus branch in `partyInfluenceTurn`; committee proposal and voting system; all committee API routes (`/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/committee/*`, `/api/admin/committee-assignments`, `/api/congress/committee-assignments`); committee UI tabs and panels (Congress committees tab, party committee tab, national committee election panel, committee proposals section, admin committee assignments section); committee wiki page; committee-related achievements and seeds. Character relocation, retirement, and ban cleanup no longer reference committee seats or elections.

- **Dead-code audit: 59 unused files removed** — Unreferenced modules, components, scripts, and public assets identified via static analysis and deleted. `1800c8f44`.
- **DB integrity audit: 18 creation-path gaps fixed** — Audited all major collection creation paths against TypeScript types and migration history. All gaps now initialized at creation time: NPP economy fields (`funds`, `donorBaseLevel`, `actionPoints`, `lastActionProcessedTurn`, `archetypeApprovals`, `electionCooldowns`) across 5 paths; character defaults (25+ optional fields) in character creation route; `isAppointment: false` across 11 elected-official creation paths; `stateMetrics.countryId` in type and reference seed; sovereign bond `restructure*` audit fields in `buildSovereignBondDoc` and both corporate bond creation paths; `laborParticipation` and `matchingFriction` in US reference seed; 14 missing hot-path and slow-query indexes added to `src/lib/admin/seed/indexes/`.

## [0.2.17] - 2026-05-14

### Performance

- **NPP slate materialization batched in turn loop** — `syncPersistentSlateAssignments` previously issued ~3,960 sequential `materializeSlateAssignmentsFromTemplate` calls (88 open primaries × 45 parties). It now batch-fetches all existing slates in one query, counts candidates per slate in one aggregate, and only materializes genuinely empty/missing pairs. `materializeSlateAssignmentsFromTemplate` gains an optional `knownEmptySlate` parameter to skip redundant `findSlateForElection` + `countDocuments` checks when the caller has already verified emptiness. `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponses.ts`, `src/lib/db/recruitmentSlateLookup.ts`.

- **`processSlateResponses` now writes via `bulkWrite`** — Replaced per-row `updateOne` with a single `bulkWrite` for all invited/considering slate candidates. `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponses.ts`.

- **NPP context index plan** — Design doc `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-npp-context-indexes.md` proposes four compound indexes for hot `loadNPPContext` queries: `electedOfficials` `{ isNPP: 1, nppId: 1 }`, `elections` `{ status: 1, primaryEndTime: 1 }`, `electionCandidates` `{ electionId: 1, isNPP: 1, status: 1 }`, `billWhips` `{ targetType: 1, targetId: 1, audience: 1 }`. Recommends adding them to the existing `scripts/migrations/add-perf-indexes.ts` migration.

### Added

- **Game Starting State wiki: 1991 / 2019 toggle** — The `/wiki/game-starting-state` dashboard now exposes a start-date toggle at the top of the page. **2019** is the canonical opening with the full economy/party/region/specialty audit (fiscal-year labels for US/UK/DE/JP relabeled from FY 2020 → FY 2019). **1991** shows the seeded historical seat composition for the four countries with `1992-default` preset data: US 102nd Congress, UK post-April 1992 Commons, JP post-1990 Shugiin / post-1989 Sangiin, DE 12th Bundestag, plus 1992 Ministerpräsidenten. BR / CN / IE display an "unseeded" placeholder for the 1991 view. The `RESET_PRESETS` entry display name was renamed `1992 Start Date - Default Parties` → `1991 Start Date - Default Parties` so the admin reset UI matches; preset id remains `1992-default`. Macro economics and 1991-era party rosters are still to be reworked. `src/components/wiki/widgets/StartingStateDashboard.tsx`, `src/lib/seeds/wiki/startingStateScenarios.ts` (new), `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/gameStartingState.ts`, `src/lib/constants/historicalSeats.ts`.

- **Public API v1** — Versioned public API (`/api/public/v1/*`) with read-only endpoints for characters, corporations, economies, elections, game state, government, legislation, markets, news, and parties. Full service layer in `src/lib/publicApi/` with per-domain tests and centralized error handling. Reference doc at `docs/api/public-v1.md`. `src/app/api/public/v1/`, `src/lib/publicApi/`.

- **Election appeal floor** — `APPEAL_POSITION_FLOOR = 0.5` guarantees no demographic group is ever fully locked out of any candidate (appeal approaches 0 but never reaches it). Party position weight flipped from `pw = 3` (75% party) to `pw = 1/3` (75% candidate) for presidential races, making candidate ideology the primary signal. `src/lib/utils/demographicAppeal.ts`.

- **Minority PM bids allowed when a majority bloc exists** — Parliamentary government formation now permits minority prime-minister bids even when a majority bloc already exists, matching real-world Westminster convention. `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`.

- **Admin seed refactor** — Migrations reorganized into `scripts/migrations/deprecated/` with README. New reset-and-bootstrap contract documented. Index seeds extracted to `src/lib/admin/seed/indexes/`. `UniversalSeeder` UI expanded. `src/lib/admin/seed/seedManifest.ts`, `scripts/reset-and-bootstrap.ts`, `src/components/admin/UniversalSeeder.tsx`.

- **Sainte-Laguë seat allocation for German Landtag elections** — `allocateLandtagSeatsToCandidates` distributes seats proportionally to candidates within each party using the Sainte-Laguë method. `src/lib/turn/election/germanyLandtag.ts`.

- **1991 starting-state wiki: economy and resource panels for all countries** — Seeded countries (US/UK/JP/DE) now show `StartingEconomyPanel`, `ResourceCapacityPanel`, and `SectorSpecialtyPanel` below their chamber-composition bars in the 1991 view. Unseeded countries (BR/CN/IE) each get their own section with the same panels (sourced from the 2019 baseline) plus a note that macro data is not yet 1991-era. Jump-index nav expanded to cover all seven countries. `src/components/wiki/widgets/StartingStateDashboard.tsx`.

- **Sovereign crisis decision panel redesigned** — The panel now shows a consequence table before any resolution is chosen, with per-path impact rows (market lockout, GDP hit, FX effect, bond-holder haircut) color-coded by severity using design tokens. Inflation rate shown in the header. Auto-action countdown badge when the 48-hour deadline is active. Monetize unavailability surfaced explicitly (no opacity hack). Vote-tally progress bar capped at 100%. Resolution label strings humanized ("repudiate" → "Repudiate (full default)" etc.). `src/components/country/SovereignCrisisDecisionPanel.tsx`.

### Fixed

- **Demographic archetype leans rebalanced and all 51 states reseeded** — Voter archetype partisan leans recalibrated and US state demographics reseeded. `src/lib/seeds/demographicCategories.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/stateDemographics.ts`.

- **Negative campaign funds prevented** — Race conditions and unguarded deductions in donation and influence spend paths could drive campaign balances below zero. All deduction sites now guard against overdraft. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/donate/route.ts`, `src/app/api/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/donate/route.ts`, `src/lib/influence/executor.ts`, `src/lib/influence/simpleInfluence.ts`, `src/lib/turn/caucusTax.ts`.

- **NPP actions diversified and save heuristic corrected** — NPP AI action selection now produces more varied behavior across turns; the save heuristic was over-counting cached actions. `src/lib/npp/actionAi.ts`.

- **NPP direct interaction panel shows campaign funds in home currency** — Previously displayed a raw figure without conversion for non-USD characters. `src/app/politicians/npp/[id]/NppCapitalPanel.tsx`, `src/lib/npps/commands/directAction.ts`, `src/lib/npps/queries/directAction.ts`.

- **`countryId` included in NPP direct-interaction projection** — Missing field caused key mismatches for non-US NPPs. `src/lib/npps/queries/directAction.ts`.

- **Withdrawn / primary candidates no longer render as "Unknown" on presidential views** — `_enrichElection` now collects every candidate referenced in state-level vote data, vote-over-time snapshots, and EV-by-turn series — not just the active display set — so presidential state maps, historical breakdowns, and EV charts always have a name/party/color for every cid that appears. `src/lib/elections/enrichElection.ts`.

- **Campaign panels show real party names** — The `/api/elections/[id]/campaigns` route now joins `politicalParties` and returns a `partyName` field; `CampaignManagerTab` and `CampaignsListPanel` use `partyName ?? party` so the UI shows e.g. "Democratic Party" instead of a numeric party id. Both panels also tightened their loading/error paths (re-fetches now reset state explicitly, request failures clear the list instead of leaving stale data). `src/app/api/elections/[id]/campaigns/route.ts`, `src/app/elections/[id]/components/CampaignManagerTab.tsx`, `src/app/elections/[id]/components/CampaignsListPanel.tsx`.

- **Election countdown timers now use wall-clock time** — All four election display components previously passed `gameTimeRef` (last turn processed) to `formatTimeRemaining`, causing countdowns to lag behind real time by however far the cron was behind (up to 14h in the observed incident). All components now pass `null` so the timer falls back to `new Date()`, keeping the countdown consistent with the absolute date shown. Fixes `ElectionCard`, `ElectionPhaseStatusStrip`, the election detail page header, and the cycle-status bar. `src/app/elections/[id]/components/`.

- **Party membership events tracked** — Join, leave, purge, and recruit actions are now recorded in `partyMembershipEvents` for audit and future UI display. `src/lib/parties/membershipEvents.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/partyMembershipEvent.ts`.

- **Anti-abuse guards on party membership actions** — Rate limits and cooldowns prevent rapid membership churn across join/leave/purge/recruit paths. `src/lib/parties/antiAbuseGuards.ts`, `src/lib/parties/antiAbuseGuards.test.ts`.

- **Region-level party whip route** — `POST /api/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip` added alongside the existing national whip, giving region-scoped whip operations their own endpoint. `src/app/api/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip/route.ts`.

- **Presidential election display improvements** — Election list cards now label the vote section "Popular Vote". The electoral-vote line chart gains a dashed 270 EV threshold line. The endorsements section shows an NPP / player count summary with type badges. Econ/social position columns removed from the candidate tally table to reduce width. `src/app/elections/[id]/components/ElectionDetailCharts.tsx`, `src/app/elections/[id]/components/PresidentialCandidateTable.tsx`, `src/components/elections/ElectionCard.tsx`.

- **1991 view per-country panels for unseeded countries** — BR, CN, and IE now each get their own section in the 1991 wiki view (with economy, resource capacity, and sector specialty panels sourced from the 2019 baseline) rather than sharing a single combined "not yet seeded" notice. `src/components/wiki/widgets/StartingStateDashboard.tsx`.

- **Crisis display: dark-mode and design-token overhaul** — `SovereignDebtWatchPanel` state labels humanized (`crisisPending` → "Crisis — pending", etc.); all `zinc-*` color classes replaced with design tokens; dark-mode variants added throughout. `SovereignRecoveryProgressPanel` shows "Bond market access locked for X more turns (until turn Y)" instead of a raw absolute turn number. Severity-based badge colors (rose/amber/zinc by tick magnitude) on the crises page; the Pre-Crisis Risk Monitor collapses into an accordion. `CrisesManager` admin panel uses `bg-primary` / `text-primary` / `text-primary-foreground` tokens and formats start dates as LARP dates. `src/components/world/SovereignDebtWatchPanel.tsx`, `src/components/country/SovereignRecoveryProgressPanel.tsx`, `src/app/world/crises/page.tsx`, `src/components/admin/crises/CrisesManager.tsx`.

- **German and UK/JP region office labels corrected** — Remove-official and resign notifications now produce human-readable role names for Landtag ("Member of Landtag") and Regional Council ("Regional Councillor") offices instead of raw `officeType` key strings. `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/region/[id]/remove-official/route.ts`, `src/app/api/officials/[id]/resign/route.ts`.

- **Vacant-seat counts and region page now use country-config sub-national chamber key** — Previously hardcoded to `"stateSenate"`, both now read `COUNTRY_CONFIGS[countryId].subNationalChamber?.key` so UK Councillors, JP regional officials, and DE Landtag members appear in the correct slots. `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/region/[id]/vacant-seats/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/page.tsx`.

- **Presidential election resolution is idempotent** — A concurrent duplicate cron firing could resolve the same presidential election twice. The tally-finalization `updateOne` now guards on `finalized: { $ne: true }`; if `modifiedCount === 0`, the process logs and returns early without writing downstream state or triggering the Discord webhook. `src/lib/turn/election/presidentResolution.ts`.

- **Barnstorm works correctly for UK/non-USD characters** — The atomic debit guard was checking `funds: { $gte: 100000 }`, but characters created before forex was enabled have a stale home-currency value in `funds` rather than anchor units. The guard now branches on forex: for forex characters it checks `currencyBalances.campaign ≥ cost × homeFxRate`. The influence action UI was also silently discarding non-OK server responses, causing "barnstorm not working" with no feedback — failed actions now surface the server error on the card. `src/lib/influence/simpleInfluence.ts`, `src/app/profile/components/InteractCard.tsx`.

### Changed

- **State economy page redesigned** — `StateEconomy` component layout overhauled: new card grid, sectioned data panels, and improved data display. `src/components/state/StateEconomy.tsx`.

- **BondMarketDemandWidget migrated to design-system tokens** — Hardcoded `zinc-*` / `dark:` classes replaced with `bg-card`, `border-card-border`, `text-muted`, and dark-aware color variants. No functional change. `src/components/country/BondMarketDemandWidget.tsx`.

