## [0.2.16] - 2026-05-11

### Added

- **LoC payment mode toggle (P/I ⇄ I/O)** — Per-currency switch on each central-bank LoC tab between Principal+Interest (default) and Interest-Only. I/O carries a +2.00pp spread surcharge applied during interest accrual and sizes the scheduled auto-payment to `arrears[c]` (which after this turn's accrual equals "fresh interest + any prior arrears"), keeping principal flat. 24-turn cooldown per currency enforced server-side by `paymentModeChangedAt[c].turn`. New `paymode_change` ledger type records every flip; `meta.paymentMode` and `meta.ioSurchargePoints` now annotate `interest` and `auto_payment` rows for audit. Player-driven from `CentralBankLoanTab` with a confirmation step when flipping to I/O; the Portfolio loans pane shows an `I/O` chip next to currencies running interest-only. Draws, manual repays, garnishment, and DTI math are unchanged. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/locLedger.ts`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/locMath.ts`, `src/lib/turn/lineOfCreditTurn.ts`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/buildSnapshot.ts`, `src/app/api/character/loc/payment-mode/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/CentralBankLoanTab.tsx`, `src/app/portfolio/page.tsx`.

- **Two new commodities: Network Services and Entertainment Services** — `network_services` (base $1200/subscription-equivalent) is the unique output of Telecom sectors; `entertainment_services` (base $600/event-equivalent) is the unique output of Entertainment sectors. Both have GDP-fraction macro demand (`NETWORK_SERVICES_GDP_DEMAND_FRACTION = 1e-6`, `ENTERTAINMENT_SERVICES_GDP_DEMAND_FRACTION = 6e-7`) wired in `computeRawSupplyDemand`. A third new constant `CONSTRUCTION_SERVICES_GDP_DEMAND_FRACTION = 5e-7` adds an infrastructure demand signal for construction_services. All three are seeded in `commodityPrices` at turn 748. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/wiki/pages/commodities.ts`.

- **Starting-state sector specialization audit** — The Game Starting State wiki dashboard now surfaces each country's regional sector specialties: top primary/secondary counts, the +10pp/+5pp margin bonus rules, and expandable per-region rows showing the local sector seed share behind each specialty for the US, UK, DE, JP, BR, CN, and IE. Regression tests now require explicit sector seed weights for every audited playable region and guard representative top-sector outcomes plus non-US specialization variety. `src/components/wiki/widgets/StartingStateDashboard.tsx`, `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/gameStartingState.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/reference/sectorSeedWeights.test.ts`, `src/lib/admin/seed/seedStateSectorSpecializations.test.ts`.

- **1992-default reset preset** — New `ResetPreset` `"1992-default"` added to `src/lib/constants/historicalSeats.ts` with full historical seat data: US 102nd Congress (House 268D/166R/1I, Senate 57D/43R, Governors 28D/20R/2I), UK post-April 1992 election (Commons: Con 336/Lab 271/LD 20/SNP 3/Plaid 4), JP post-1990 election (Shugiin: LDP 275/JSP 136/Komeito 45, Sangiin: LDP 109/JSP 66), DE 12th Bundestag (CDU/CSU 319/SPD 239/FDP 79/PDS 17/Greens 8) with 1992 Ministerpräsidenten. `getPresetSeats("1992-default")` returns the concatenated arrays.

- **Econ-only countries wired into `bootstrapGameWorld`** — Brazil, China, and Ireland reference data (regions, parties, demographics, state metrics, baselines, government formation) plus budget seeders now run during world bootstrap alongside the active four. Japan Emperor NPP (`seedJPEmperor`) is now also called during bootstrap so Japan has its imperial head of state on reset.

- **`seedSeats` now covers BR, CN, and IE** — Added seat definitions for Brazil (Chamber of Deputies, Senate, Governors), China (NPC Delegates, Governors), and Ireland (Dáil, Seanad) to `seedSeats.ts` so all seven playable countries have routable election seats on bootstrap. `src/lib/admin/seed/seedSeats.ts`.

### Fixed

- **`resetGameWorld` now re-seeds DE budgets** — Germany's federal budget seeder (`seedDeBudgets`) was missing from the post-wipe re-seed block, leaving DE without budget data after a standalone reset.

- **Imperial characters now survive `resetGameWorld`** — The reset pipeline unconditionally wiped the `imperialCharacters` collection, destroying UK, DE, and JP head-of-state characters on every reset. The `deleteMany` is removed; only user references are cleared. Characters are preserved across resets.

### Changed

- **Commodity balance deep rebalance** — Comprehensive rebalance across 17 sector types to address persistent shortages (iron 3.38×, nat_gas 3.68×, oil 2.70×, steel 2.41×, copper 2.16×) and oversupply (food 0.85×, plastics, software). Key changes: extraction diversified supply down ~20% (200/233 sectors on standard were flooding all resource markets and hitting the +30 surplus cap trivially); focused extraction strategies up 15–30%; nuclear energy steel demand 0.30→0.20 with iron 0.08 added (nuclear was the single largest steel consumer at 125/202 energy sectors); renewables output 0.50→0.55 with input reductions; EV electronics demand 0.30→0.22 redistributed to rare_earth/software/steel; agriculture food output −9% (oversupplied); healthcare pharma/electronics inputs −27%; `GOVT_HEALTHCARE_DEMAND_RATE` 0.018→0.013; real estate and construction input reductions; Telecom electronics/copper demand down with new network_services supply; Entertainment adds entertainment_services supply to all strategies; live_venue construction_services demand 0.12→0.08. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/constants/sectorStrategies.ts`.

- **High interest rates now suppress demand 3× more aggressively** — `MONETARY_COEFF` split into asymmetric coefficients: `MONETARY_COEFF_LOW = 0.4` (rates below neutral, unchanged) and `MONETARY_COEFF_HIGH = 1.2` (rates above neutral, tripled). A 7% rate vs 3% neutral previously produced −1.6 pp; it now produces −4.8 pp. `src/lib/budget/inflation.ts`.

- **Deflation is now uncapped** — `MIN_INFLATION` floor removed (was −2%). Inflation can fall to any negative value; prolonged deflationary spirals are no longer bounded. `src/lib/budget/inflation.ts`.

- **Deflation margin penalty doubled** — `DEFLATION_PENALTY_COEFF` raised from 2 to 4. Each pp of deflation now applies a −4 pp margin modifier to all sectors in that country (was −2 pp). The 0%–2% low-inflation bonus zone is unchanged. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.

- **Rate-sensitive commodity demand for food, vehicles, financial services** — Adds a per-turn macro demand block driven by `stateBudgets.stateGdp` (anchor-normalised). `delta = anchorGdp × fraction × (neutral − primeRate) / basePrice` — zeroes out at 2.75% neutral rate, negative at high rates (suppresses demand), positive at low rates (stimulates demand). Calibrated fractions: food `4e-8` (~~−7% at current rates), vehicles `4e-7` (~~−20%), financial_services `1e-7` (~−4%, stacked on existing latent demand block). Also merges `weightedProductionPolicyLevel` and `negativeProductionSustainedTurns` during sector buy, hostile takeover, and duplicate-sector repair. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.ts`.

- **Sector seed rebalance** — Unowned sector revenues now seeded proportionally to real-world GDP composition per country and state, replacing the previous equal 17-way split. New constant `SECTOR_SEED_SCALE = 450` in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts` increases seed scale 4.5×. California technology seeds at 20× extraction; West Virginia extraction seeds at 20× technology. `src/lib/seeds/reference/sectorSeedWeights.ts` provides per-country baseline weights for all 7 audited countries plus explicit playable-region overrides across the US, UK, DE, JP, BR, CN, and IE. `SECTOR_MARKET_GDP_FRACTION` (100) is unchanged and continues to drive all live game calculations.

- **Commodity balance: aggregate margin caps added** — `computeBlendedMarginModifiers` in `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts` now clamps the post-blend input modifier to `−COMMODITY_AGGREGATE_INPUT_CAP (30)` and the surplus modifier to `+COMMODITY_AGGREGATE_SURPLUS_CAP (30)`. Stacked shortages could previously drive energy, autos, and construction to −35+ net commodity margin from routine market conditions; extraction could earn +40 from broad diversified shortages. Both constants are exported and referenced in new guard tests.

- **Tradable resource state stabilizer** — Extractable resources (oil, gas, iron, copper, timber, coal, rare earth) now use `EXTRACTABLE_RESOURCE_STATE_STABILIZER = 2500` instead of the default `STATE_COMMODITY_SUPPLY_DEMAND = 250` in the state-leg margin blend. States without local extraction no longer take extreme local penalties for globally-traded commodities; state-level prices remain unchanged (visual locality preserved).

- **Extraction strategy rebalance** — Diversified extraction output rates reduced ~12% (iron 0.25→0.22, coal 0.2→0.18, oil 0.2→0.18, rare_earth 0.1→0.09, copper 0.1→0.09, nat_gas 0.12→0.10, timber 0.08→0.07) to make focused strategies more attractive. Focused strategies buffed 15–25%: iron_mining iron 0.55→0.65, oil_gas oil 0.4→0.47 + nat_gas 0.2→0.24, coal_mining 0.55→0.65, copper_mining 0.5→0.60, timber_logging 0.45→0.54. Rare earth unchanged. `SECTOR_SUPPLY["extraction"]` in `commodities.ts` and all matching entries in `sectorStrategies.ts` updated in sync.

- **Phase 4 commodity gap fixes** — Added plastics co-production to `chemical_industries` `SECTOR_SUPPLY` (rate 0.15) to address plastics D/S ~2.6×. Raised energy sector output 0.6→0.65 and reduced energy's oil input 0.1→0.07 and copper input 0.07→0.04. Raised agriculture food output 0.5→0.55. Reduced construction building_materials 0.25→0.20 and timber 0.15→0.10 to ease input stacking. All matching strategy definitions in `sectorStrategies.ts` updated.

- **Macro service demand reduction** — `GOVT_HEALTHCARE_DEMAND_RATE` reduced 0.025→0.018 (−28%); `FINANCIAL_DEMAND_ISSUANCE_FRACTION` reduced 0.0000335→0.000022 (−34%). Live healthcare D/S was 2.38× and financial_services D/S was 2.67× before these changes.

### Fixed

- **Pass-through corps no longer display phantom corporate tax on sector page** — `sectorDetail.ts` was returning the raw federal and state/regional rates without applying the `corpTaxMultiplier`, so pass-through structures (S-Corp, LLC, GK, LLP, ie_uc, ng_ulc) showed non-zero tax in the sector financials panel even though the turn engine charged 0. Preferential structures (DE SE, CN SOE, BR Ltda) also now show their correctly discounted effective rates. `src/lib/corporations/queries/sectorDetail.ts`.

### Added

- **Interactive sector-seed map widget** — New `SectorSeedMap` component on the Game Starting State wiki page (`/wiki/game-starting-state`). Shows regional sector weight distribution as a teal heatmap for any of the 17 sector types across all 7 countries. Registered in `src/lib/wiki/componentRegistry.ts` as `sector-seed-map`.

- **Commodity balance audit script** — `scripts/debug/audit-commodity-balance.mjs` queries live DB for global D/S ratios, 48-turn average price/base, shortage frequency, and corp marginDiagnostic winners/losers. Supports `--json` flag. Baseline at turn 738 logged in commit message.

- **Commodity guard tests** — `src/lib/constants/commodities.test.ts` expanded with `computeCommodityPressureRatio` tests, `COMMODITY_BASE_PRICES` coverage check, and five aggregate cap tests (energy/autos/extraction/construction stacked-shortage scenarios). All 58 commodity tests pass.

- **Wiki seed updates** — `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/commodities.ts` and `corporations.ts` updated to reflect all v0.2.16 balance changes: aggregate cap paragraph, extractable stabilizer bullet list (250/2500), extraction strategy table with focused vs diversified guidance, plastics co-production note, updated healthcare demand rate (1.8%). Both slugs re-seeded to production DB.

- **Portfolio garnishment warning** — Portfolio Overview pane shows an error banner when bond income is actively being garnished, displaying the per-turn amount captured. Loans pane adds a per-account garnishment notice when `garnishedPerTurnInternal > 0`. `LocSnapshot` extended with the `garnishedPerTurnInternal` optional field. `src/app/portfolio/page.tsx`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/buildSnapshot.ts`.

### Fixed

- **LOC auto-pay now pulls from savings as overflow when the wallet falls short** — Previously `processLineOfCreditTurn` only counted the personal wallet toward `availableBalance`, so a borrower whose income had been garnished at source saw the wallet-only auto-pay attempt €0 and the loan only moved by whatever garnishment captured (~€1.45M/turn against a live €403M principal). The auto-pay's `availableBalance` per currency is now `personal + savings`, and step 4 deducts personal first then savings as overflow per currency (`fromPersonal = min(totalDeduct, initialPersonal); fromSavings = remainder`). Campaign funds are explicitly out of scope — they're legally separate from personal cash and remain off-limits to LOC collection. Cross-currency conversion still works the same way, it just has a larger pool to draw from. `src/lib/turn/lineOfCreditTurn.ts` (PR #1600).

- **Admin LOC ledger UI now shows garnishment / distress-drain rows as payments** — `CentralBankAdminTab.tsx` only recognised `repay` and `auto_payment` as payment-type rows. Garnishment rows (which write `interestPortion` / `principalPortion` correctly into `locLedger`) showed up as `+€X` with both split columns rendering `—`, making it look like a deposit instead of a debt reduction with split. Added a `LOC_PAYMENT_TYPES` set covering `repay`, `auto_payment`, `garnishment`, `distress_drain`; rows of any of those types now show the `−` prefix and the interest/principal split when stored. Type display name added for `garnishment` ("Garnishment") and `distress_drain` ("Distress Drain"). `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/CentralBankAdminTab.tsx`.

- **US canvassing and GOTV modifiers now actually affect elections and polls** — `resolveTurnout` / `buildLiveTurnouts` in `src/lib/electionEngine/resolvedTurnout.ts` only summed modifiers keyed by archetype ID (e.g. `voterGroups.young_renters`). US canvassing (`/api/canvassing/route.ts`) and party GOTV spend (`src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`) store modifiers keyed by Layer-1 demographic group instead (`modifiers.race.white`, `modifiers.age.young`, …), so the lookup never matched and **every Layer-1 modifier was silently dropped** before vote distribution. State Demographics & Turnout page, opponent share prediction, and turnout decay were all wired correctly, but `tallyManagement.ts:108` and `primaryStaggerPhase.ts:351` (the actual election tally) and the poll voter-group breakdown saw none of it. Fixed by detecting registered Layer-1 configs in `stateCensusData` and recomputing per-archetype baselines through `deriveGroupTurnout` with `stateSpecificTurnout = baseline + modifier`, then layering any remaining archetype-keyed modifier on top. UK/JP/etc paths (already keyed by archetype) are unchanged. Regression coverage added in `src/lib/electionEngine/turnoutWiring.integration.test.ts`.

- **Poll "Likely Voter Turnout by Demographic" panel now reflects active modifiers** — `computeStateDemographicTurnout` in `src/lib/seeds/stateDemographics.ts` read raw `DEMOGRAPHIC_TURNOUT_RATES` constants and ignored `stateDemographicTurnout.modifiers`. The state's Demographics & Turnout "Combined" view and the election engine both apply those modifiers, so the poll panel drifted away from reality after canvassing / GOTV / suppression / decay. The function now takes the modifier map, applies `baseline + modifier` (clamped 0–100) per group, and the poll route (`src/app/api/actions/poll/route.ts`) loads the doc and passes it in. Tooltips/footer text in `DemographicTurnoutPanel.tsx` updated to say "effective" rather than "national baseline".

- **Poll "est. total voters" header no longer 4× the actual electorate** — `DemographicTurnoutPanel.tsx` summed turnout across all four demographic dimensions (race + age + education + wealth), but each dimension is the same population sliced a different way, so every voter was counted ~4 times (GA showed 25.15M in a state of ~10.7M). The header now averages the four dimensional estimates so it sits in the same ballpark as each individual section's subtotal.

- **Party org building now works for non-US parties (DE, JP, UK)** — `processPartyGOTV` fetched characters and NPPs without `countryId` in the MongoDB projection, so `c.countryId` was always `undefined`. The character-by-party-state lookup key fell back to `DEFAULT_LEGACY_COUNTRY_ID = "US"`, causing a key mismatch (`"US:8_RP"` stored vs `"DE:8_RP"` looked up) for every non-US party. Revenue resolved to 0 → org building spend was 0 → state-level org never accumulated. Fixed by adding `countryId: 1` to both the `characters` and `npps` projection queries in `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`.

- **Deflation now penalises sector margins instead of boosting them** — `getInflationMarginModifier` in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts` previously treated any rate below the 2% target with the same "low-price bonus" formula, so −1.1% deflation produced a spurious +3.1 pp bonus. Deflation (inflation < 0%) now applies a penalty at 2× the per-pp rate of the inflation penalty (`DEFLATION_PENALTY_COEFF = 2`). The 0%–2% low-inflation bonus zone is unchanged.

- **Sustained-negative-production penalty tripled, ramp shortened** — `SUSTAINED_NEGATIVE_PRODUCTION_MAX_PENALTY` raised from −15 to −45 pp and `SUSTAINED_NEGATIVE_PRODUCTION_FULL_TURNS` reduced from 528 to 144 in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`. The full penalty is now reached in ~3 game days instead of ~11. Grace period (48 turns) unchanged.

- **Bill revote no longer applies compass shift twice** — `castStateBillVote` and `performNationalBillAction` both called `applyBillVotePolicyShift` unconditionally on every vote. Re-voting after abstaining (or changing vote direction) stacked an additional ±0.25 shift on each axis per provision. The shift is now skipped when the character already has a non-abstain vote recorded on the bill (`bill.votes[charId]`). `src/lib/legislature/commands/stateBillActions.ts`, `src/lib/legislature/commands/nationalBillActions.ts`.

- **Corporation Income/Hr no longer overstates net income for pass-through and dominant corps** — The corporation page's `loadCorporationDetailView` diverged from the turn loop in three places, so the displayed Income/Hr could be 2× the cash that actually flowed into `liquidCapital`. (1) Per-sector market share is now resolved via `buildMarketShareBySectorId` instead of being hardcoded to `0`, so the dominance margin penalty is applied. (2) Per-sector dominance regulatory burden is accumulated and folded into `operatingCosts`. (3) Dividend distribution is computed using `max(corp.dividendRate clamped, legalStructure.minimumDividendRate × 100)` and capped by income, mirroring `sectorCalculations.ts:735-745` — pass-through structures (us_llc, us_s_corp, uk_llp, jp_gk, …) no longer silently extract a payout the display ignores. Hero subtracts `dividendDistribution` from `income`; FinancialsTab gates the Distributions panel on `effectiveDividendRate` and shows a "Legal floor" badge when the structure floor is binding. Real-world impact: Costco (us_llc) hero went from +$3.4M/hr to the ~$1.5M/hr the turn loop actually writes; Monroe Inc (jp_kk telecom) Net Income reflects the dominance penalty plus regulatory burden so reported income no longer disagrees with cash flow. `src/lib/corporations/queries/corporationDetail.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/turnReferenceData.ts` (project `state.gdp` so the GDP-derived market floor works in production), `src/lib/corporations/financialFogOfWar.ts`, `src/components/corporation/CorporationPageTypes.ts`, `src/app/corporation/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/FinancialsTab.tsx`.

- **Private corporation page now loads for non-CEO viewers** — `shouldRedactCorporation` returns `financials: null` for non-CEO, non-admin viewers of private corps. The corporation page's error guard treated `!financials` as a fatal error, showing "Corporation not found" to all regular users even though the corp existed. Fixed by: (1) narrowing the guard to `!financials && !corporation.isPrivate`; (2) hiding financial tabs (Financials, Credit Rating, Bonds, Charts) for private-corp non-CEO viewers; (3) rendering a "Private Corporation — financials not publicly disclosed" notice on the Overview tab when `financials` is null. `src/app/corporation/[id]/page.tsx`.

- **Campaign fund affordability check now uses home currency for non-USD characters** — UK characters' campaign balance is stored in GBP (`currencyBalances.campaign`), but the ₳ action cost was compared directly against it. The check now converts ₳ → home currency via the live forex rate before comparing, so "Insufficient funds" no longer fires when a GBP character can actually afford the action. `src/lib/capital/actions.ts`.

- **Commodity table national view shows total supply/demand instead of highest/lowest state** — When viewing a national exchange (NYSE, LSE, TSE, DAX) in the commodities tab, the two rightmost columns now display total national supply and demand units rather than the state with the highest or lowest price. `src/app/country/[code]/stockmarket/components/CommodityTable.tsx`.

- **Commodity detail page breadcrumb no longer strips the tab parameter** — The "Commodities" breadcrumb link pointed to `/stockmarket/US?tab=commodities`, which hit a redirect shell that dropped `?tab`, landing players on the Stocks tab instead. Fixed to link directly to `/country/us/stockmarket?tab=commodities`. `src/app/commodity/[type]/CommodityDetailClient.tsx`.

- **Central bank chair nomination timing copy clarified** - The empty nominations panel now says nominations open in `X` turns, during the final year of the chair's term, instead of saying `X` turns before the term expires. This makes the 70% executive-nomination selection pool read as the selection chance, not the nomination-window timing. `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/NominationsPanel.tsx`.

- **Corporation dissolution votes now auto-execute** — `applyPassedVoteEffects` was a no-op for the `"dissolution"` case; it relied on the CEO clicking a separate "Execute Dissolution" button after the vote passed. Dissolution now runs immediately when the vote settles, using `executeCorporationBondDefaultDissolution` under the existing settlement lock so it is race-safe with the bond turn. `src/lib/corporations/votes/voteEffects.ts`.

- **Line of credit — garnished borrowers no longer stay frozen indefinitely** — `processLineOfCreditTurn` marks a borrower as distressed when they can't cover their scheduled payment. If income was garnished this turn before it reached the wallet, the wallet looks empty even though the borrower earns enough to pay. The turn processor now accumulates the scheduled payment total in internal units and compares it to the borrower's income; a frozen borrower whose income meets the threshold is un-distressed even when their wallet balance is zero. `src/lib/turn/lineOfCreditTurn.ts`.

- **Line of credit — income cap and equity cap now visible separately in the credit-limit panel** — Investigation of bug #0502 ("bonds held not counted as equity") confirmed that bond holdings _are_ correctly counted in the equity-based ceiling. The actual binding constraint is the income-based DTI cap, which is a 48-turn rolling average of bond coupons, salary, and dividends — so new or recently-enlarged bond positions take up to 48 turns to fully raise the income ceiling even though they immediately raise the equity ceiling. Previously the UI showed only the final `min(income cap, equity cap)` limit with no breakdown, making it impossible for players to tell why their available credit was lower than their bond equity suggested. Both limits are now displayed as "Income cap: ₳X · Equity cap: ₳Y" beneath the usage bar, with the binding (lower) figure highlighted, on both the central-bank LoC tab and the portfolio Loans pane. `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/CentralBankLoanTab.tsx`, `src/app/portfolio/page.tsx`.

- **Mobile responsive fixes** — Multi-batch pass covering the highest-impact display issues on 320–360 px phones: navbar dropdowns capped to `max-w-[calc(100vw-1rem)]` to prevent right-edge overflow; admin tables wrapped to prevent horizontal scroll blowout; TurnControls drops to 1-column on the smallest screens with reduced horizontal padding; StatusBar character name always truncates at 140 px on mobile; UniversalSearch example chip grid collapses to 1 column below `sm`; ActionsHero stat cards step down `min-w` thresholds; slate-tab map tooltip and StatsCard decay tooltips capped to viewport width; heal-panel and IP-bans diagnostic tables drop to 1 column; UsersTab long strings use `break-all`; Mobile/Tablet admin badge layout fixed. `src/components/Navbar.tsx`, `src/components/StatusBar.tsx`, `src/components/UniversalSearch.tsx`, `src/app/actions/components/ActionsHero.tsx`, `src/components/admin/*`, `src/components/StatePartyChairElection.tsx`, and related files.

