## [0.2.14] - 2026-05-07

### Fixed

- **Dividend income display in status bar** — The "+X/turn" value in the dividend breakdown tooltip was passing `dividendIncome` (already in internal anchor units) through `compactHome`, which re-converts from home currency to internal. This over-inflated the displayed dividend for non-USD home currencies. Replaced with `compactInternal` so dividends display correctly across all currency modes. Also removed the now-dead `compactHome` helper.

- **Caucus tax now levied on per-turn income, not total balance** — `caucusTax.ts` was computing the tax as `taxRate% × campaignFunds`, where `campaignFunds` was the character's full accumulated balance. For a character with $40M+ in funds and a 2.5% caucus tax rate this silently drained ~$1M/turn. Tax is now computed against `getTotalFundGeneration` (the same per-turn income figure used by `processFundGeneration`) so the deduction is proportional to what a character earns each turn, not what they've saved. Also adds a `caucus_tax_debit` entry to the financial transaction log so the deduction is visible to the player.

- **IPO share price and proceeds double-conversion** — `CorporationStructureActions.tsx` was passing the raw corp home-currency `sharePrice` directly to `formatAmount`, which expects ₳ anchor units. For JPY corporations (rate ≈107×) this inflated the displayed share price from ¥56,825 to ¥6.1M and treasury proceeds from ~¥18.9B to ~¥2T. Fixed by wrapping all share-price and proceeds values in `toInternalFrom(amount, liquidCode)` before calling `formatAmount`/`formatPrice`. Affected: description share price, IPO preview card treasury proceeds, and the post-IPO success message.

### Added

- **National committee proposals.** Any national committee member may now propose a party rename, ideological position shift (±1 on economic or social axis, clamped to −5…+5), election method change, or election duration change; the party chair may additionally propose a merger with another party. All proposals are voted on with a 24-turn window and simple-majority threshold (`yes > N/2`). Eligible voters include committee members plus the national chair, vice chair, and treasurer — the eligible-voter count (not just `committeeIds.length`) is used for both the majority threshold and the `notVoted` display. Merge proposals require a concurrent majority vote from the _target_ party's committee as well — both sides must pass before the merge executes. On merge: all characters and NPPs transfer to the target party (partyInfluence halved on transfer), 50% of each state org's `organization` is added to the target's state org (new doc created if absent), and 100% of the national treasury is transferred. The proposing party is marked `isDefunct` (not deleted) and excluded from the parties list and join flows. Defunct parties show a banner on their party page.
  - **Election method proposals** — The committee can change how national leadership elections (chair, vice chair, treasurer) are tallied: `"party"` (all members, one vote each — default), `"committee"` (committee members + national leadership only, one vote each), or `"influence"` (all members, votes weighted by each voter's `partyInfluence` score at cast time). Stored on `PoliticalParty.leadershipElectionMethod`; `voterPartyInfluence` snapshotted on each vote doc when the method is `"influence"`. Enforced in the candidacy/vote routes and turn-system tally.
  - **Election duration proposals** — The committee can set a custom duration for future national leadership elections, between **168 turns** (1 week) and **420 turns** (2.5 weeks). Stored as `PoliticalParty.customElectionDurationTurns`; applied the next time elections are created by the turn system.
  - New DB collection: `committeeProposals`; new DB types `CommitteeProposal`/`CommitteeProposalVote`; new fields on `PoliticalParty`: `isDefunct`, `defunctAtTurn`, `mergedIntoPartyId`, `leadershipElectionMethod`, `customElectionDurationTurns`. New API routes: `GET/POST /api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/committee/proposals`, `POST /api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/committee/proposals/[proposalId]/vote`. Turn phase `nationalCommitteeElections` now expires stale open proposals. UI: `CommitteeProposalsSection`, `ProposalCard`, and `CreateProposalForm` components added to the party page committee tab.

### Refactored

- **Codebase health — Phase 2 / Phase 6 incremental.** Continued work against the 2026-05-07 codebase-health spec.
  - `WikiManagementTab.tsx`: 19 `useState` calls migrated to a single `useReducer` via the new `useWikiManagementState` hook (modelled after `useNavbarState.ts`). Adds 7 reducer-level tests. Drops the file from `USE_STATE_ALLOWLIST` in `scripts/architecture-audit.mjs`. `src/components/admin/wiki/useWikiManagementState.ts`, `src/components/admin/WikiManagementTab.tsx`.
  - `useStatusBarLayout` hook extracted from `StatusBar.tsx` (1110 → 1071 LOC). Owns the server/localStorage layout-preference seeding and the cross-tab `storage` listener. The `StatusBarLayout` type is re-exported so the `AppearanceSection` import path is unchanged. `src/components/statusbar/useStatusBarLayout.ts`.
  - `CongressClient.tsx` dropped from `USE_STATE_ALLOWLIST` — at 11 useState calls it's already under the 15-call block threshold.
  - `bondTurn.ts` Phase-3.6 credit-penalty per-corp `updateOne` loop converted to a single `bulkWrite` (one round-trip instead of N for defaulted corps). `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`.
  - `corporationDetail.ts` — three independent queries at the tail of `loadCorporationDetailView` (parent-corp lookup, subsidiary-candidates query, hostile-takeover eligibility build) now fan out via a single `Promise.all` instead of running sequentially. `src/lib/corporations/queries/corporationDetail.ts`.
  - `createNotifications(inputs[])` batch helper added — collects N notification inputs into one `insertMany`. Applied in `bondTurn.ts` (`corp_bond_due_soon` + `corp_bond_repaid` per-bond fan-out), `primaryResolution.ts` (`primary_win`/`primary_loss` per candidate), `coalitionDisbandCheck.ts` (`coalition_disbanded` per chair), and `cabinetTransition.ts` (cabinet-resigned per US/UK member, plus the per-member character lookup batched via `$in`). The existing `createNotification` is retained for one-off call sites. `src/lib/notifications.ts` and the four call-site files (+ test updates).
  - Handoff doc at `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-07-codebase-health-handoff.md` updated to reflect the new state — 4/13 notification call sites migrated, 9 remaining on the same recipe.

### Platform

- **Railway build caching** — Added `nixpacks.toml` with `cacheDirectories` for both `node_modules` (install phase) and `.next/cache` (build phase). Set `cleanDistDir: !railwayEnv` in `next.config.ts` so the nixpacks-restored `.next/cache` is not deleted by Next.js at build start. Together these enable Turbopack incremental compilation cache to persist across Railway deploys.
- **Build time savings on non-production Railway builds** — `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors: true` in `next.config.ts` removes the `run-typescript` phase (~82s) from the Railway build critical path; CI `tsc --noEmit` remains the type-error guard. `sourcemaps: { disable: !isProductionBuild }` skips Sentry's `after-production-compile` source-map processing (~167s) on staging and feature-branch deploys.
- **Railway environment detection corrected** — Replaced all `VERCEL_ENV` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV` references with `RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_NAME` throughout `next.config.ts` and both Sentry configs. `isPreview` now correctly flags any non-production Railway environment; `isProductionBuild` uses `railwayEnv === "production"` instead of `NODE_ENV` (which is always `"production"` on Railway even for staging). Sentry was silently disabled on all Railway environments because `sentryEnabled` was tied to the now-absent `VERCEL_ENV`; now enabled for any Railway deployment.
- **CI parallelization** — `.github/workflows/ci.yml` restructured from a single serial job into two independent parallel jobs: `quality` (lint, format check, tsc, architecture audit, security audit) and `test` (vitest with coverage). Halves wall-clock CI time for every push.

