## [0.2.13] - 2026-05-06

### Added

- **Germany — Landtag system.** Player-eligible state legislatures for Germany's 16 Länder, with proportional vote-share seat allocation distinct from the FPTP model used by US/UK state houses. New `germanyLandtag.ts` election turn handler; `seatAllocation.ts` extended with proportional path. Land elections, sitting members, and admin tooling all flow through the new system. (Authored by **Arlebina/Dani**.) `src/lib/turn/election/germanyLandtag.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/germanyLandtag.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/seatAllocation.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/de/deLandtag.ts`. Plan docs at `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-06-de-implementation-phase-4-landtag.md`.
- **Germany — historical seeders.** Independent admin seeders for Bundestag 2021 election results and the 2020 line-up of Land Minister-Presidents, runnable via the admin UI. (Dani.) `src/lib/admin/seed/seedDE.test.ts`, plus the seed wiring in the same file. Plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-06-de-implementation-phase-2-historical-seeds.md`.
- **Germany — Land terminology + Imperial Character config.** Region/Province/State labels collapsed to "Land" / "Länder" throughout the UI for Germany; Imperial Character settings wired in. (Dani.) Phase-1 plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-06-de-implementation-phase-1-rename-and-imperial.md`.
- **NPP auto-generation generalized to all countries.** `handleGenerateNPPs` previously hard-coded for US and UK; now country-agnostic with per-country eligible-state and party-pool configuration. Powers admin seeding for Germany, Japan, Canada, Brazil. (Dani.) `src/app/api/admin/npps/lib/generate.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/npps/lib/generate.test.ts`. Plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-06-de-implementation-phase-3-npp-generation.md`.
- **Germany — Bundesrat tab disabled.** Disabled in the country UI matching the UK Lords pattern (members appointed by Land governments, not directly elected). (Dani.) Phase-5 plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-06-de-implementation-phase-5-bundesrat-and-cleanup.md`.

- **Private and Public corporation founding paths.** Founders now choose between staying private (you own 100%, financials are hidden from non-CEO viewers) or doing a public IPO (issue new shares to the public float for additional treasury cash; founder ownership drops below 100% but you keep majority control via a 49% float cap). Private corps can later IPO via a "Go Public" CEO action (96-turn cooldown). Public corps where the CEO holds >75% can call a 24-turn shareholder buyout vote at sharePrice × 1.10; on pass, all non-CEO holdings are bought out, public float is retired (corp treasury receives the equivalent buyback), and the corp returns to private. While a vote is open, share issuance, splits, and dividend changes are blocked. Fog of war: private corps redact treasury, income, share price, dividend rate, per-sector revenue/profit/workers, bond amounts, and portfolio data from non-CEO/non-admin viewers across the directory and detail GET routes. New constants in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`; new `Corporation.isPrivate/lastIpoTurn/lastPrivatizationTurn/privatizationCooldownUntilTurn` fields and `corporationPrivatizationVotes` collection (`src/lib/db/types/corporationPrivatizationVote.ts`); new commands `src/lib/corporations/ipoIssuance.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/redaction.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/commands/capitalOperations/goPublic.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/commands/privatization/{open,cast,resolve,cancel}PrivatizationVote.ts`, `openVoteGuard.ts`; new routes `POST /api/corporations/[id]/go-public`, `POST /api/corporations/[id]/privatize`, `POST /api/corporations/[id]/privatize/[voteId]/{vote,cancel}`, `GET /api/corporations/[id]/privatize/[voteId]`; UI in `FoundCorporationModal.tsx`, `CorporationHero.tsx`, new `CorporationStructureActions.tsx` and `PrivatizationVotePanel.tsx`. Three new `FinancialTxType` variants for buyout ledger entries. Backfill migration at `scripts/migrations/2026-05-07-backfill-corporation-isprivate.ts`.
- **Party member purge** — National party chairs can now expel regular members (not vice chair or treasurer) from their party. The action costs the chair +25 infamy and deducts `floor(target.partyInfluence / 2)` from the chair's own party influence. The target is set to independent with `partyInfluence = 0`, existing candidacies and state party positions cleaned up via the existing leave utilities, `electedOfficials` records backfilled to `party: "independent"`, and the target receives a `party_kicked` notification. A 6-turn cooldown per party is enforced via `PoliticalParty.lastPurgeAtTurn`; constants extracted to `src/lib/constants/partyActions.ts` (shared between route and UI). `POST /api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/purge` uses `requireAuthWithCharacter`; `lastPurgeAtTurn` added to `PoliticalParty` type and `PartyData` DTO (alongside `currentTurn` for client-side cooldown display); `"party_kicked"` added to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with an "Expelled" badge config; "Purge Member" danger button + modal added to `ChairOfficeTab.tsx`.

### Documentation

- **Germany audit-pass cleanup (9 passes, 26 findings closed).** Cross-cutting fixes from a focused audit of the Germany implementation across `landtag` / Phase 4 surfaces: chamber-set gaps, recalibrate-timers for Landtag/Bundestag, election UI labels, character UI labels, admin appointment, `adminAssignSeatSchema` enum, additional `electionType` switches in tests, and `PoliticiansClient` office-priority sort. (Authored by **Arlebina/Dani**.)
- **Wiki fact-check pass.** Many wiki articles rewritten or substantially corrected to match implementation: Sovereign Bonds, Government Approval, Stock Market, Currency Exchange, Central Banks, Corporate Bonds (pricing formula, IMF bailout, national-corp restrictions), Subsidies (fiscal cost, market sentiment), Tariffs (inflation impact, sentiment clamp, ending mechanics, fiscal sync), Commodities (audit + correction, unowned-sector fallback), Election Mechanics, Voting & Whips (cross-pressure model), National Budget (debt ceiling, state grants timing, fiscal year), Corporations (type-switch cooldown, strategy penalty, commodity caps, optional starting capital, power-grid modifier), Bills, Game Loop, Turn Order, Campaign Strategy. `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/*.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/wiki/pages/*.ts`.
- **CLAUDE.md updates.** Added the version-bump policy (no unprompted `package.json` version edits) and the PR-base-branch rule (target `development`, not `master`).

### Changed

- **Corporate bonds: longer tenors now carry a term premium** — 2yr bonds are unchanged (base rate = prime + credit spread + 1.0pp). 5yr bonds add +1.00pp on top; 7yr bonds add +1.75pp. The issuance form now shows the exact coupon rate next to each maturity option so CEOs can compare the cost before committing. Refinance and relocation bonds also inherit the term premium for their respective durations. `CORPORATE_BOND_TERM_PREMIUMS` exported from `src/lib/constants/bonds.ts`; `getBondCouponRate` gains an optional `maturityTurns` parameter. `src/lib/constants/bonds.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/corporateBondDefault.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/issueRelocationBond.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bonds/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/BondsTab.tsx`.
- **Corporate bond per-issuance cap now scales with revenue** — The flat $100M ceiling per bond issuance is replaced with 25% of annual gross revenue, floored at $100M so small corporations are unaffected. A $21B corporation generating $2B/year in revenue can now issue up to $500M per bond. `sumCorporateSectorAnnualRevenue` helper added to `src/lib/bonds/corporateCredit.ts`; constants `MAX_BOND_ISSUANCE_REVENUE_FRACTION` and `MIN_BOND_ISSUANCE_PER_ISSUE` in `src/lib/constants/bonds.ts`. The bonds GET endpoint returns the computed `maxPerIssuance` and the Issue Bond panel displays it as "Per-issuance cap". The what-if debt slider in the Credit Rating tab also respects the new cap. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bonds/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/BondsTab.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/CreditRatingTab.tsx`.
- **Wiki Full Page List is paginated and auto-gen sorts newest-first** — The `/wiki` Full Page List previously dumped all ~1,095 auto-generated entries plus every player and system page into three uncapped masonry columns. Each section now paginates server-side at 10 entries per page via independent `?auto=N&player=N&system=N` URL params (page 1 omitted from the URL), with a condensed Prev / 1 … N / Next nav and section-anchor preservation. Auto-gen entries sort by recency (`endTime` for elections, `updatedAt` for db-stored auto-gen pages) before alphabetical tiebreak; static office/seat/party entries with no date fall to the end. `AutoGeneratedWikiPageSummary` gained an optional `sortDate?: Date`. `src/app/wiki/page.tsx`, `src/lib/wiki/autoGeneratedPages.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Electricity output now rises with growing energy sectors** — The commodity price turn already supported production-policy output/input multipliers, but it did not fetch `productionPolicyLevel` from sectors before building commodity supply/demand. Energy sectors with active production policy could therefore show falling Electricity output even while sector revenue/growth moved upward. The commodity turn now passes `productionPolicyLevel` into `computeRawSupplyDemand`, and the commodity detail API applies the same output/input multipliers to Top Producers and Top Consumers so the page matches stored market totals. Added an energy regression test for +25 production policy supply. `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/commodities/[type]/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.test.ts`.
- **Reverse split unblocked when a placer corp was dissolved** — `cancelShareOrderAndRefund` hard-failed with `"Buyer corporation not found"` whenever a buy order's `placerCorporationId` referenced a corporation that had been dissolved/deleted. Because the consolidate route auto-cancels every open order before a restructure, a single orphan order from a dead corp blocked stock and reverse splits indefinitely (ticket #0461). The placer-corp branch now mirrors the existing orphan-character fallback: if the placer corp is missing, cancel the order without refund (escrow can't be returned, but the orphan can't keep blocking the target either). New unit test asserts the orphan-corp path returns `ok` and never attempts an `updateOne` on the missing placer. Three orphan orders against `Unlimited Power`, `E.ON`, and `Gangrel Global` cleaned up in development DB. `src/lib/corporations/cancelShareOrder.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/cancelShareOrder.test.ts`.
- **Marketing Strength tooltip stops describing elections** — The status-bar MS chip (corp / full layout) carried a tooltip blurb claiming MS "increases voter reach and demographic campaign effectiveness" — a hallucinated electoral effect on a corporation stat. Replaced with what MS actually does: boosts the share of unowned market captured per sector split (+MS/100 on top of the 2% baseline) and grows from daily marketing spend. `src/components/StatusBar.tsx`.
- **UK regional metrics no longer stuck at placeholder `100`** — `educationSpending`, `powerGridReliability`, `violentCrimeRate`, and `testPerformance` were added to `src/lib/seeds/uk/ukStateMetrics.ts` after UK regions had already been seeded. The seed isn't idempotent for new fields, so existing regions kept their fall-through default of `value: 100`, and no per-turn calculator updates these four metrics — so they sat flat at 100 across all 96 turns of history (visible as `$100` Current Value with a flat-line chart on the per-region detail page). DB audit confirmed all 12 UK regions affected; US was already clean. New `scripts/migrations/backfill-uk-metrics.ts` reads the seed and writes the four target paths into existing `stateMetrics` docs, but only when DB value is exactly `100` and seed value differs (organic turn drift on `testPerformance` for 4 regions was preserved). After regional updates, `computeNationalMetrics` runs to refresh the `uk_national` aggregate so the country dashboard reflects the fix immediately. Migration applied to development DB this release.
- **Multi-winner primaries surface all nominees in the general phase** — Post-primary dedup in `enrichElection` capped displayed candidates at one per party, stripping the other 2 nominees from polling and the tally filter for countries where `primaryWinners > 1` (UK=3, JP=3). Replaced the dedup with a top-N-per-party cap driven by `getElectionSystemPrimaryWinners(countryId)`. Same pattern fixed in the Discord-bot race route. `src/lib/elections/enrichElection.ts`, `src/app/api/discord-bot/race/route.ts`.
- **Presidential CS column now shows real values** — The `campaigns` projection in `fetchDepsForElection` only fetched `_id`, `candidateId`, and `funds`, so `camp.campaignStrength` (and `camp.color`) were always undefined when read by `candidateEnrichment`. The CS column on the presidential candidate table fell back to "—" for every row. Projection now includes `color` and `campaignStrength`, and the table cell prints `0` instead of "—" when CS is exactly zero so freshly-created campaigns read correctly. `src/lib/elections/enrichElection.ts`, `src/app/elections/[id]/components/PresidentialCandidateTable.tsx`.
- **NPP relocate respects state capacity** — The national party `relocate_state` influence action skipped the recruitment-slot check, letting players push NPPs into states already at capacity. `validateNppStateRelocationRequest` now applies the same `calculateRecruitmentSlots(stateOrg)` gate used by recruitment, rejecting with `"<State> has no available NPP slots for your party (N/M)."` before any actions/treasury debit. `getNationalPartyInfluenceOptions` now exposes `currentNPPs`, `maxSlots`, and `full` per target state, and the relocate dropdown disables full options with a `— full (N/M)` suffix. `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorValidation.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutor.ts`, `src/lib/parties/dto/partyView.ts`, `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorValidation.test.ts`.
- **Cabinet ministerial actions actually spend** — Cabinet members created via the US nomination lifecycle and admin force-confirm were inserted into `cabinetMembers` without `ministerialActions` / `lastActionGrantedTurn`. The briefing route showed `2/2` via the `?? 2` fallback, but the order route's atomic `{ ministerialActions: { $gte: 1 } }` filter doesn't match missing fields, so `Declare` returned `"No ministerial actions remaining"`. Inserts now seed both fields to `(2, 0)`, and the order route backfills legacy members on first action so existing cabinets don't stay stuck. `src/lib/cabinetNominationLifecycle.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/cabinet-nominations/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/[positionId]/order/route.ts`.
- **Late-IPO cooldown no longer fires on freshly-founded private corps** — `goPublic` was anchoring the 96-turn cooldown on `max(foundedAtTurn, lastPrivatizationTurn)`, so a corp founded as private at turn N got blocked from going public until turn N+96 — making "found private, then IPO" effectively impossible despite the founding modal advertising both paths. The cooldown's purpose is to prevent rapid public↔private oscillation; a corp that has never been public has nothing to oscillate, so founding turn is no longer an anchor. The check now keys on `lastPrivatizationTurn` only — corps that have actually been privatized still wait 96 turns from that event. Test `rejects when within IPO_COOLDOWN_TURNS of founding` flipped to `allows IPO immediately after founding private`. `src/lib/corporations/commands/capitalOperations/goPublic.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/commands/capitalOperations/goPublic.test.ts`.

---

## [0.2.12] - 2026-05-06

### Sovereign Default subsystem

A complete sovereign-debt crisis system shipping across phases 1–11b. Triggered when an auction fails or the recovery state machine determines fiscal standing is unsustainable; resolved by Executive proposal + Legislative ratification (or NPC auto-flow); cascades into the wider economy with bond write-downs, corporate insolvency, and sector margin penalties.

- **Schema and migrations (phase 1)** — Extended `FederalBudget` with crisis state, IMF sovereign facility, and IMF Board override fields; added `restructure` audit fields to `Bond`; new `sovereignCrisisDecisions` collection. `src/lib/db/types/federalBudget.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/bond.ts`, `src/lib/db/migrations/sovereignDefault/*`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/tunables.ts`.
- **Bond market demand model (phase 2)** — `synthetic-demand` formula and snapshot loader, `/api/country/[code]/sovereign-status` route, country-dashboard bond market demand widget. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/demand.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/snapshotLoader.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/sovereign-status/route.ts`, `src/components/sovereignDefault/BondMarketDemandWidget.tsx`.
- **Player and entity demand contribution (phase 3)** — `sumQualifyingEntitySovereignHoldings` helper, `computeRequiredIssuance`, Model B entity contribution in demand formula, per-country sovereign holdings panel on the character portfolio. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/entityHoldings.ts`, `src/components/portfolio/SovereignHoldingsPanel.tsx`.
- **Crisis state machine (phase 4)** — Pure auction-outcome classifier and crisis-state transition rules, per-country detection orchestrator hooked into the fiscal-year close, system news emitters for auction outcomes, new `sovereign` `NewsCategory`. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/auctionOutcome.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/crisisState.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/crisisDetection.ts`, `src/lib/turn/fiscalYear.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/news.ts`.
- **IMF Bailout resolution (phase 5)** — IMF sovereign bailout facility math, austerity cap proportional scaler that caps spending while bailout is active, `bailoutGranted` news emitter, decision-panel UI on the country dashboard, `POST /api/country/[code]/sovereign-resolution`, per-turn facility payments hooked into `bondTurn`. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/imfFacility.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/austerityCap.ts`, `src/components/sovereignDefault/CrisisDecisionPanel.tsx`.
- **Repudiate / Restructure / Monetize resolutions (phase 6)** — Three additional resolution orchestrators, exchange-rate depreciation helper for monetize, cross-country trust-hit helper, `markCountryBondsRepudiated` and `restructureCountryBonds` mutators, news emitters, `recoveryGdpPenalty` field on `FederalBudget`, inflation-gate UI for the Monetize option, all 4 choices wired through the resolution route. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/resolutions/{imfBailout,repudiate,restructure,monetize}.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/exchangeRate.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/crossCountryTrust.ts`.
- **Contagion cascade (phase 7)** — Depth-bounded cascade orchestrator for bond write-downs across holders, corporate insolvency detector, write-down severity calc, mass-cascade news, local + global sector margin penalty (`GLOBAL_CONTAGION_MULTIPLIER`), per-corp margin modifier aggregator wired into the corp turn pipeline. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/cascade.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/sectorMarginPenalty.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corp/marginModifiers.ts`.
- **Recovery state machine (phase 8)** — Pure recovery state-transition function, primary-surplus fiscal standing check, per-turn recovery processor hooked into `bondTurn`, `recoveryComplete` news emitter. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/recovery.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/recoveryTurn.ts`.
- **Recovery UI + IMF International page (phase 9a)** — Recovery progress panel on the country dashboard with new fields surfaced on `sovereign-status`, per-corp cascade news emitter, `isImfBoardMember` helper, `GET /api/imf/overview` and `POST /api/imf/board/override`, new `/international/imf` page with overview / bailouts / overrides panels. `src/app/international/imf/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/imf/*`.
- **Legislative ratification (phase 9b)** — Per-turn legislative ratification processor and chamber-outcome tally rule, legislative-phase types and decision-row fields, legislative phase builder, `POST /api/.../sovereign-resolution` now routes through legislative ratification, legislator-vote endpoint for sovereign crises, legislative voting panel UI and active-phase surfacing on `sovereign-status`. Orchestrator state guard widened to accept `crisisResolving`. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/legislativeRatification.ts`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/legislativePhaseBuilder.ts`, `src/components/sovereignDefault/LegislativeVotingPanel.tsx`.
- **NPC algorithm + balancing + tests (phase 10)** — NPC executive auto-propose at crisis-fire, NPC option scoring + tie-break + `chooseResolution`, NPC legislator auto-vote per chamber, IMF Board statement news + catalogue completeness test, modify-terms UI controls in the board override panel, comprehensive end-to-end NPC + player flow tests. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/npc/*`, `src/lib/sovereignDefault/npc.test.ts`.
- **Economic realism polish (phase 11a)** — IMF cumulative-payment accumulator with UI display, debt sustainability index + UI gauge, recovery credibility bonus on coupon rate, mass-cascade global alert + dismissible banner, `/world/crises` pre-crisis warning dashboard. `src/components/sovereignDefault/DebtSustainabilityGauge.tsx`, `src/app/world/crises/page.tsx`.
- **Political ramifications (phase 11b)** — Executive favorability/infamy hit on resolution, legislator favorability impacts at chamber tally, parliamentary no-confidence auto-trigger on Repudiate/Monetize, populist favorability surge on crisis-fire, civil unrest events post-resolution. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/politicalRamifications.ts`.
- **Audit hardening (phases 9–11)** — Closed vote/override race, preserved legislative-rejected state, orchestrator-failure fallback + executive double-click guard, deferred trust hit until atomic guard succeeds, FX-converted bond write-downs and IMF facility payments, preserved NPC votes across tally + best-effort auto-propose, renamed internal `Response` interface to avoid shadowing DOM `Response`. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/orchestrator.ts`.
- **Player-enabled gate** — Crisis trigger gated on the Players Enabled flag so live-server bootstrap can run without firing crises. `src/lib/sovereignDefault/crisisDetection.ts`.

### Architecture restructure (waves 0–7)

- **Wave 0 — foundations** — domain reuse guidelines, shared types, base patterns. `docs/architecture/*`, multiple barrel/types files.
- **Wave 1 — legislature exemplar** — restructured legislature flows; turn-lock reset admin log action. `src/lib/legislature/**`.
- **Wave 2 — corporation exemplar** — corp domain reorganized around the new architecture template. `src/lib/corp/**`.
- **Wave 3 — campaign exemplar** — campaign code regrouped to match the architecture template. `src/lib/campaign/**`.
- **Wave 4 — party / NPP exemplar** — party + NPP domain reorganized. `src/lib/parties/**`, `src/lib/npp/**`.
- **Wave 5 — finance + intorg exemplar** — finance and international-organization domains regrouped. `src/lib/finance/**`, `src/lib/intorg/**`.
- **Wave 6 — support + government exemplar** — support and government domains regrouped. `src/lib/support/**`, `src/lib/government/**`.
- **Wave 7 — simulation refactor** — turn/simulation pipeline reorganized to match domain template. `src/lib/turn/**`, `src/lib/simulation/**`.

### Party Charter system (Phase 6 of political-system rework)

- **Charters gate third-party creation** per Phase 6 D1. Every non-default party now begins as a `partyCharters` row that requires 3-of-3 founder co-signatures before the `politicalParties` row materializes. Default parties (`isDefault: true`) — Democrat, Republican, Labour, etc. — bypass the charter system at creation, migration, and cleanup gates per Phase 6 D5.
- **8-state lifecycle**: `draft → pending-signatures → ratified` is the forward path; side paths cover `rejected` (any founder rejects), `founder-replacement` (a founder is voided / banned with a fresh deadline window), `expired` (deadline missed), and the migration-only `migrated` / `migrated-incomplete` states for back-filled charters. Schema in [src/lib/db/types/partyCharter.ts](src/lib/db/types/partyCharter.ts).
- **Lifecycle commands** in [src/lib/charters/](src/lib/charters/): `draftCharter`, `signCharter`, `rejectCharter`, `replaceFounder`, internal `ratifyCharter`. Race-safe: `signCharter` / `rejectCharter` use positional `signatures.$.signedAt` updates so concurrent founders can't clobber each other's signatures, and `ratifyCharter` uses an atomic `findOneAndUpdate` claim on `pending-signatures → ratified` so concurrent 3rd-signers can't double-spawn the party row (the loser rolls back its draft party insert and returns the winner's `partyId`). `signCharter` re-reads the charter post-update for an authoritative count before deciding ratification.
- **Overton guardrails** per Phase 6 D2: each platform axis is bounded to `[-60, +60]`; post-ratification amendments cap each axis delta at `±10`. Helpers + 14 unit tests in [src/lib/charters/overtonGuardrails.ts](src/lib/charters/overtonGuardrails.ts).
- **`expireCharters` per-turn phase** + cleanup-immunity hook per Phase 6 D4. Sweeps `draft` / `pending-signatures` past `expiresAt` and `founder-replacement` past `founderReplacementDeadline`, transitioning to `expired`. Filters `$ne: null` so ratified / migrated charters (null deadlines) are never touched. Wired into `demographicsAndPartySetup` group BEFORE `emptyPartyCleanup`. The cleanup pass now exempts non-default parties referenced by a charter in `ratified` / `migrated` / `migrated-incomplete` status from auto-deletion via composite `countryId:partyId` keys (avoids cross-country sequentialId collisions). [src/lib/turn/charters/expireCharters.ts](src/lib/turn/charters/expireCharters.ts), [src/lib/turn/partyOrg/emptyPartyCleanup.ts](src/lib/turn/partyOrg/emptyPartyCleanup.ts).
- **Deadline rule** per Phase 6 D4: every deadline (initial draft window + founder-replacement window) is `max(14 turns, 72 IRL hours)` from start. [src/lib/charters/charterDeadlines.ts](src/lib/charters/charterDeadlines.ts).
- **Migration script** ([scripts/migrations/2026-05-06-migrate-existing-parties-to-charters.ts](scripts/migrations/2026-05-06-migrate-existing-parties-to-charters.ts)) back-fills a charter row for every pre-Phase-6 non-default party. Founder selection: chair → vice → treasurer → oldest-joining party-affiliated characters, deduped by userId, capped at 3. Result statuses: `migrated` (3 founders), `migrated-incomplete` (0–2 founders, with `pendingFounderSlots = 3 - founders`). Platform inferred from existing economic / social position fields scaled `[-5, +5] → [-60, +60]`; foreign-policy + culture default to 0. Standard `--apply` / dry-run + `--db=local|live` flags. Idempotent: re-running skips parties that already have a charter row.
- **Presidential-primary gate** per Phase 6 D7: a `migrated-incomplete` charter blocks US president filings until its missing founder slots are filled. The check runs only for `electionType === "president"` AND `electionCountry === "US"`; ratified / migrated parties pass freely; default parties (no charter row) bypass. Wired into `POST /api/elections/[id]/enter` with the unfilled-slot count surfaced in the error message. [src/lib/charters/presidentialPrimaryGate.ts](src/lib/charters/presidentialPrimaryGate.ts).
- **API surface** (Phase 6 D6 redirect): legacy `POST /api/country/[code]/parties` now creates a charter draft (no party row), responding with `{ ok, charterId, redirectTo: "/charters/[id]" }`. Companion endpoints under [/api/charters/](src/app/api/charters/): `POST /api/charters` (create draft), `GET /api/charters?countryId=&me=&status=` (list), `GET /api/charters/[id]` (single), `POST /api/charters/[id]/sign`, `POST /api/charters/[id]/reject`, `POST /api/charters/[id]/replace-founder` (founder-only auth).
- **Minimal-MVP wizard UI** per Phase 6 D6: server-rendered list page at `/charters` (charters where the viewer is a founder), detail page at `/charters/[id]` (read-only platform sliders, founder roster with sig status, sign/reject actions when applicable), draft form at `/charters/new`. Shared components in [src/components/charters/](src/components/charters/): `PlatformSliders` (4-axis range sliders, reusable read-only mode), `DraftCharterForm`, `CharterActions`. The legacy `CreatePartyModal` was removed; the parties page's "Create Party" button now navigates to `/charters/new`.

### Campaign Manager extension to non-presidential US races (Phase 5.5 of political-system rework)

- **Eligibility extended** beyond US president to US senate, governor, house, and state senate races. The single source of truth ([src/lib/campaigns/isCampaignEligible.ts](src/lib/campaigns/isCampaignEligible.ts)) now consults a typed `NON_PRESIDENTIAL_RACE_FAMILIES` set gated by the new `CountryConfig.campaignManagerNonPresidentialEnabled` flag. US has the flag set; UK / JP / DE / IE remain explicitly ineligible per Phase 5.5 D4 until their country-specific campaign-finance models are audited and adapted.
- **Campaign-strength contribution lifted** from the hardcoded `electionType === "president"` gate to the broader eligibility check ([src/lib/campaigns/commands/campaignCommands.ts](src/lib/campaigns/commands/campaignCommands.ts)). Players can now contribute NPI-driven campaign strength to senate, governor, house, and state-senate candidates in the US.
- **Race-family copy adapter** ([src/lib/campaigns/raceFamilyCopy.ts](src/lib/campaigns/raceFamilyCopy.ts)) — typed helper returning swing-area / mobilization-scope / ground-game-effect strings localized per race family: president → "swing states" / "national"; senate / governor → "swing counties" / "statewide"; house / state senate → "swing precincts" / "district". Mechanic stays unified across families; only the player-facing language localizes.
- **DTO + queries thread the adapter** so the Ground Game upgrade card shows race-appropriate copy: `getCampaignCategoriesForElection(election)` ([src/lib/campaigns/dto/campaignView.ts](src/lib/campaigns/dto/campaignView.ts)) and the next-upgrade-cost effect string is localized in [src/lib/campaigns/queries/campaignQueries.ts](src/lib/campaigns/queries/campaignQueries.ts).
- **Tests** — eligibility matrix coverage expanded from 6 → 12 tests covering each newly-eligible US race family, non-US explicit denials, cross-country leak guards, and defensive guards. Race-family copy adapter has 9 tests (each electionType + fallback + percent interpolation + family-distinctness).
- **Documented gaps** — per-race-family cost scaling (a state-house race doesn't realistically have $5M/turn fundraising at L10) is explicitly a tuning concern deferred to a Balance Appendix follow-up; the model works at any scale, the absolute numbers are calibration-only. Non-US extension waits on country-specific finance-model adapters.

### General-election shell rework (Phase 5b of political-system rework)

- **`generalViewModel` server-side pure builder** ([src/lib/elections/generalViewModel.ts](src/lib/elections/generalViewModel.ts)) — composes per-state margin tiers (safe / likely / lean / tossup matching the existing popular-vote shading bands), per-state Reg-as-partisan-lean breakdowns, and a derivable persuasion-driver list. 14 tests cover boundary classification, leader resolution, missing-data fallbacks, sort ordering, clamping, and view-model composition.
- **`BattlegroundMap`** component ([src/components/elections/general/BattlegroundMap.tsx](src/components/elections/general/BattlegroundMap.tsx)) — pure margin-emphasis wrapper around `USAMapPaths`. Shades each state by margin tier using the same 4-band derivation as `PresidentialMapWithStateDetail`'s popular-vote view. Optional `highlightedStates` prop wraps the existing 5-closest filter with a "Battleground (N)" label. The exported `shadeColorForTier` helper has 6 tests.
- **`RegistrationInfluenceCard`** ([src/components/elections/general/RegistrationInfluenceCard.tsx](src/components/elections/general/RegistrationInfluenceCard.tsx)) — read-only display of per-state Reg as partisan-lean influence. Honest framing per Phase 5b D3: values labeled "X% lean" (never "X% votes"). Bootstrap-deferred fallback: when the row's `registration` is `undefined` (Phase 1.5 / Phase 2 prereq seed not yet run), the card shows a dashed-border "data populating" placeholder rather than fabricating zeros. Stacked bar with party shares + Independent solid + Unregistered diagonal-stripe pattern.
- **`PersuasionDrivers`** ([src/components/elections/general/PersuasionDrivers.tsx](src/components/elections/general/PersuasionDrivers.tsx)) — diverging-bar visualization of why a state leans toward / away from focus. Each driver gets a horizontal bar anchored at a midline; positive grows right (focus color), negative grows left (red). Bars share a common max-magnitude scale for fair cross-driver comparison. Per Phase 5b D4 the component is agnostic to driver data source — the parent passes a typed `PersuasionDriver[]` from the view-model. Coattails currently renders as `0` per Phase 5b D7 (placeholder pending a real coattail mechanic).
- **Shell mounted on `GeneralPhaseView` for US presidential general elections** ([src/app/elections/[id]/components/GeneralElectionShellClient.tsx](src/app/elections/[id]/components/GeneralElectionShellClient.tsx)) — composes `TierSelector` (Pres-only active per Phase 4 D2; Senate / Gov / House remain non-clickable per Phase 5b D6 since per-tier general-election aggregator surfaces don't yet exist) + `BattlegroundMap` + per-state grid (`RegistrationInfluenceCard` + `PersuasionDrivers`). Coexists with the existing `PresidentialMapWithStateDetail` per D5 — different emphasis: this shell shows margin tiers + driver explainers; the existing map keeps EV totals + state-detail modal.
- **Acceptance gap documented**: tier-selector chip activation across non-presidential tiers (Senate / Gov / House) is deferred to Phase 5.5+ since those surfaces don't exist as country-wide aggregators yet (Phase 5b D6).

### General-election formula migration (Phase 5a of political-system rework)

- **Org consumed as normalized state-pool share** in general-election vote distribution. Replaces the legacy `partyOrgScalar` (1.0–1.6× soft scalar) with each party's `org / Σstate_org`, matching the Phase 0.5 §7.3.2 contract that "Organization enters as a normalized 100% pool share." Falls back to legacy `partyOrgScalar` when total state Org is 0 (test fixtures, unbootstrapped seeds), preserving backward-compat per Phase 5a D5. `src/lib/electionEngine/voteDistribution.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/electionFormulaFactors.ts`.
- **Reg as persuasion-resistance multiplier** (1.0–1.3× linear) — own-Reg adds modest resistance to peeling per Phase 0.5 §4.2. Threaded through the new `DistributeVotesOptions.regByParty: Map<string, number>` parameter; gracefully degrades to 1.0× when undefined or when bootstrap of `StatePartyOrg.registration` hasn't run for this state. Consumed only when `isGeneralElection: true`; primary path is unaffected. `src/lib/electionEngine/electionFormulaFactors.ts`.
- **Support as candidate-mood multiplier** (0.6–1.4× from `[0, 100]`, neutral at 50) — short-term momentum from debates / endorsements / scandals. Read from the new `ElectionCandidate.support` field per Phase 0.5 §3.1 canonical store; threaded through `EnrichedCandidate.support` via `candidateEnrichment.ts`. Undefined → 1.0× (no penalty for pre-Phase-4 candidates). `src/lib/db/types/election.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/candidateEnrichment.ts`.
- **All 12+ general-election race families** (US presidential / senate / gov / house / state senate; UK commons / regional council; JP shugiin / sangiin; DE bundestag) are updated through the single shared `distributeVotesByGroupLevelAllocation` engine. The `isGeneralElection` flag — already passed by `tallyManagement.ts` and `presidentialElectionEngine.ts` — gates the new formula on; primaries continue using the legacy intra-party math.
- **Backward-compat**: with all Reg / Support undefined and a populated Org map, the new formula preserves relative ordering against the legacy formula (party with larger Org still wins). The change is honest about its dynamics — eight new migration tests cover Org normalization (2x ratio + 30/40/30 split), Reg resistance (high own-Reg measurably bumps share), Support contrast (100 vs 0 produces clear delta), neutral defaults, empty-Org fallback, primary-path gate, and the §"Acceptance" invariant.

The 5a / 5b split was confirmed at kickoff: this phase ships the formula migration alone. The new UI shell (RegistrationInfluenceCard, PersuasionDrivers, BattlegroundMap, generalViewModel) lives in a follow-up Phase 5b once 5a is merged and stable per the plan rule.

### Primary Screen Rework + Tier Selector (Phase 4 of political-system rework)

- **Race Tier chip strip** at the top of `/president/primary/[partyId]` — Presidential / Senate / Governor / House. Per Phase 4 D2, the strip is hidden entirely on non-US surfaces (no presidential primary equivalent on JP / UK / DE / IE). Per Phase 4 D3, only the Presidential chip is live; Senate / Governor / House are visible-but-disabled with a "Coming in Phase 5" tooltip per the §16 acceptance rule. `src/components/elections/primary/TierSelector.tsx`.
- **PrimaryCalendar timeline** — vertical timeline with one row per primary wave (Iowa / NH / NV+SC / Super Tuesday / Mid-March / Closing). Past waves render in muted styling; upcoming waves use the party-color accent. Per-state chips on each row dispatch `onSelectState` for the parent to drive the carve-up panel. `src/components/elections/primary/PrimaryCalendar.tsx`.
- **CarveUpPanel** — conic-gradient pie chart of candidate slices in the currently selected state with per-candidate breakdown rows. Slices come from a shared view-model that runs the existing `projectPrimaryByState` math. Renders an honest empty state when no candidate has run; a "View state details →" link on the header deep-links to the per-state primary detail page. `src/components/elections/primary/CarveUpPanel.tsx`.
- **primaryViewModel server-side builder** — pure builder that folds the existing `/president/primary/[partyId]` page data (candidates, projection.byState, tally votedStates) into the shape the new components expect. Defensive: skips slices for unknown candidate IDs (handles withdrawn-candidate vote residuals); falls back to wave-vs-currentTurn flagging when `votedStateIds` isn't available. `src/lib/elections/primaryViewModel.ts`.
- **Map click drives carve-up selection** — `PrimaryMapWithLinks` got a `mode` prop (default `"select"`); clicking a state now updates `?state=NN` so the carve-up panel below the map updates in sync. The legacy navigation behavior is preserved as `mode="navigate"` for any future surface that needs it; the per-state detail page is still reachable via the new "View state details →" link on the carve-up header. Matches the Phase 4 acceptance criterion. `src/app/president/primary/[partyId]/PrimaryMapWithLinks.tsx`, `src/app/president/primary/[partyId]/PrimaryShellClient.tsx`, `src/app/president/primary/[partyId]/page.tsx`.

### Political Strength migration + Party Hub rework (Phase 3 of political-system rework)

- **`actionPool` renamed to `politicalStrength`** across `Party` and `StatePartyOrg` documents (140 replacements in 47 source / test / seed files). Idempotent migration script handles existing DB rows in place. The user-facing wiki page rewritten to describe Political Strength as a reserve grown by sustained investment, not a flat-spend wallet. `scripts/migrations/2026-05-05-actionPool-to-politicalStrength.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/party.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/statePartyOrg.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/partyActions.ts`.
- **PS reserve generation** replaces the legacy flat `+5/turn` cap-100 generator. Each turn applies a `+1` passive trickle plus a country-normalized treasury-driven gain (`US $75k / UK £60k / DE €70k / JP ¥5M` per `+1` PS, with state-party generation at 50% of the national rate). Soft-cap slowdown bands (100% / 75% / 50% / 0%) taper treasury gain as the pool fills. Cap formula: `max(100, round(80 + 4 * regionCount))` for national parties (US 280, UK 128, DE 144, JP 112) with optional `Party.politicalStrengthCap` override; `STATE_PS_CAP_DEFAULT = 30` for state parties. `src/lib/turn/partyActionGeneration.ts`, `src/lib/turn/politicalStrength/strengthConstants.ts`.
- **Per-geography PS pressure ladder** — repeated PS spends in the same state escalate effective cost by `+1` each time, capped at `8`, with `−3/turn` decay. Acting in Arizona doesn't raise the cost in California. New `partyStrengthPressure` collection tracks per-`(party, state)` pressure with the new `pressureDecay` turn-phase processor handling decay. `src/lib/db/types/partyStrengthPressure.ts`, `src/lib/turn/politicalStrength/pressureDecay.ts`.
- **Shared `spendPoliticalStrength` command** centralizes PS debit + pressure escalation + audit-ledger writes for every PS-spending action. Atomic `findOneAndUpdate` with conditional `$gte` for clean concurrent-spend semantics. `src/lib/parties/commands/spendPoliticalStrength.ts`.
- **Live Contest action** on the State Politics tab — chair / vice-chair spends `4` PS (plus per-state pressure) to reduce a rival party's Org by `0.5` percentage points. Defense floors prevent bullying the home default party below its tier minimum (`Strong 18 / Solid 14 / Lean 10 / Competitive 0`). Org reduction logged in `orgRegLedger` with `source: "poach"`. `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/contest/route.ts`, `src/components/state/politics/ContestActionPanel.tsx`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/defenseConstants.ts`.
- **National Agenda system** — chair-set headline + detail per party, surfaced on the National Party Hub, State Party Hub, and State Politics tab via the new `AgendaBanner` component. One active agenda per party at a time; setting a new one supersedes the old. New `partyAgendas` collection. Chair-only POST API; GET available to any authenticated viewer. `src/lib/parties/queries/currentAgenda.ts`, `src/lib/parties/commands/setNationalAgenda.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/agenda/route.ts`, `src/components/party-hub/AgendaBanner.tsx`, `src/components/party-hub/AgendaBannerWithEdit.tsx`.
- **`PsStrengthCard`** replaces the legacy `+5 actions/hour · Cap: 100` chrome on both Party Hub pages. Shows current PS / cap, soft-cap band indicator (full speed / 75% / 50% / at cap), and a help tooltip explaining the reserve / pressure model. `src/components/party-hub/PsStrengthCard.tsx`.
- **Passive Org→Reg drift + Reg decay turn-phase** (`regDriftDecay`) implements Phase 0.5 §8.3 steps 3-4 as one merged phase. Drift moves each party's Reg toward its own Org by `0.04 pp/turn`; Reg decays `0.004 pp/turn` with eligible parties (Org ≥ `10%`) catching losses via `sqrt(Org%)` weights, else routed to non-party buckets with bias toward Independent. Phase is a no-op until Phase 1.5 / Phase 2 prerequisite seeds the `StateRegistrationPool` rows. `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/regDriftDecay.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/pacingConstants.ts`.
- **Priority Region** field on `Party` plus per-turn validator that auto-evicts ineligible states (state split / merged / party lost presence). Lock survives chair turnover; slot stays empty until the `168-turn` cooldown expires. `src/lib/turn/politicalStrength/priorityRegionDecay.ts`.
- **Audit ledger `partyPoliticalStrengthLedger`** tracks every PS reserve movement (passive trickle, treasury-driven gain, action spend, decay). Distinct from `orgRegLedger` per Phase 0.5 §5.6 — this ledger is for PS reserve movements only, not Org / Reg / Support mutations. `src/lib/db/types/partyPoliticalStrengthLedger.ts`.
- **Phase 3 turn-phase wiring** — three new phases (`regDriftDecay`, `pressureDecay`, `priorityRegionDecay`) inserted into the `demographicsAndPartySetup` group between `partyOrgTurn` and the parallel block of party elections. `src/simulation/phases/turnPhaseRegistry.ts`, `src/simulation/phases/turnPhaseNames.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/turnLog.ts`.
- **PS pressure-ladder steady-state walkthrough** lands in the plan's Balance Appendix with 9 calibration traces (60% / 80% / 100% cap × 1, 2, 3 spends/turn) plus a cross-geography sanity check. The simulator script re-runs in <1 second; tuning iterations run it locally before committing constant changes. Headline finding: 1 spend/turn is sustainable; 2-3 spends/turn drain the wallet within 50-100 turns at the default 5% treasury investment, suggesting a chair-set per-party investment override is the right tuning lever. `scripts/debug/ps-steady-state.mjs`.
- **Existing party-action routes retain the inline `$inc`** for Phase 3 (don't yet route through `spendPoliticalStrength`). The PS debit semantics continue to work on those routes; only the per-state pressure ladder and `partyPoliticalStrengthLedger` audit rows are deferred until a follow-up "Phase 3.5 — PS spend-site wiring sweep" lands. The new Contest action is the first end-to-end consumer of the shared command.

### State Politics tab rework (Phase 2 of political-system rework)

- **Sectors-style party-Org breakdown** replaces the old org chart on the State Politics tab — a horizontal stacked bar segmented by party share with an Unaffiliated remainder, plus a per-party legend. `src/components/state/politics/PartyOrgSectorBreakdown.tsx`.
- **Regional-executive chip** (governor / Ministerpräsident) on the State Politics tab consumes the Phase 1 `getRegionalExecutive` helper and tints with the executive's party color. Renders an honest "no comparable executive" placeholder for UK and JP per Gate 0 audit. `src/components/state/politics/GovModifierChip.tsx`.
- **Registration Ledger placeholder card** surfaces an honest "not yet seeded" state until the bootstrap backfill ships in Phase 1.5 / Phase 2 prerequisite. `src/components/state/politics/RegistrationLedgerCard.tsx`.
- **Contest preview panel** ships as a visible-but-disabled card with a "Coming in Phase 3" badge and tooltip — no fake success toast, no spinner. `src/components/state/politics/ContestActionPanel.tsx`.
- **GOTV / Suppression budget summary cards** — read-only display of the viewer-party's current GOTV / Suppression budget % and targeting for this state, with a deep-link CTA to the State Party page where mutation lives. `src/components/state/politics/GotvDriveCard.tsx`, `src/components/state/politics/SuppressionCounterOpsCard.tsx`.
- **Quick Actions panel** — new hub: live actions (Org Building / GOTV / Suppression) deep-link to the State Party page; preview-only actions (Contest, Field Office, Establish Presence, Rally, Ad Buy, Endorse) render as visible-but-disabled buttons with "Coming in Phase 3" tooltips per the plan's §16 acceptance criterion. `src/components/state/politics/QuickActionsPanel.tsx`.
- **State page server fetches `partyBudget` data** for the new summary cards via a new `getStatePartyBudgets()` helper, indexed by partyId for O(1) viewer-party lookups. `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/page.tsx`.

### State Overview tab (Phase 1 of political-system rework)

- **New "Overview" tab on every state / region page** — shows a 4-card KPI strip (party Org%, party Reg%, GDP, Competitive Races), an all-party Org donut chart, a political summary card (rank + gap to leader + regional-executive chip + Phase 1 placeholder action buttons), an economy summary, a primary-contest card, and a race watchlist. Defaults to this tab on first navigation; existing `?tab=elections`, `?tab=politics`, etc. deeplinks load their original tabs unchanged. `src/components/state/StatePageTabsOverview.tsx`, `src/components/state/overview/*`, `src/components/state/StatePageTabsConstants.tsx`, `src/components/StatePageTabs.tsx`, `src/components/uk/UKRegionPageTabs.tsx`.
- **Server-side overview aggregator** — `getStateOverview()` reads `statePartyOrg`, `politicalParties`, `states`, and the new regional-executive lookup in parallel; sorts parties by Org with deterministic tie-break; clamps the Unaffiliated remainder to `[0, 100]`; flags Reg% as `derived` (placeholder) until the bootstrap backfill ships. `src/lib/states/overview/getStateOverview.ts`, `src/lib/states/overview/types.ts`.
- **Country-aware regional-executive helper** — `getRegionalExecutive()` resolves the seated governor (US) or Ministerpräsident (DE) and returns `null` for UK / JP per Gate 0 audit (no devolved-executive office types modeled today). `src/lib/states/regionalExecutive.ts`.
- **Hot-race classifier + competitive-races count** — `classifyRace()` and `countCompetitiveRaces()` surface hot+lean races for the KPI; defaults `≤8` hot / `>15` safe / lean otherwise. Calibration script at `scripts/debug/race-margin-distribution.mjs`. `src/lib/states/overview/hotRaces.ts`.
- **Schema additions for Phase 0.5 design lock** — added `StatePartyOrg.registration?: number` (placeholder field — values stay `undefined` until Phase 1.5 / Phase 2 bootstrap backfill), new `stateRegistrationPool` and `orgRegLedger` collection types with full schemas + index plans + the `POOL_SENTINEL_PARTY_ID` constant. `src/lib/db/types/statePartyOrg.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/stateRegistrationPool.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/orgRegLedger.ts`.

### Election scoring rework

- **State-level primary score now weights state position alongside party position** — alignment splits 25 pts (state cached lean) + 15 pts (party position) when state cached lean is available; falls back to today's 40-pt party-only alignment when state lean is missing. State-position alignment is the primary influence on a candidate's primary chances, with party-position alignment a meaningful secondary input. `src/lib/primaryScore.ts`, `src/lib/elections/candidateEnrichment.ts`, `src/lib/elections/enrichElection.ts`, `src/lib/turn/primaryResolution.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/elections/resolve-primaries/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/elections/trigger-primaries/route.ts`.
- **Infamy now penalizes both primary and general election performance** — multiplicative penalty of up to 5% at infamy=100 (linear). Applied in `calcPrimaryScore`, `calcPresidentPrimaryScore`, and `distributeVotesByGroupLevelAllocation`. NPPs lack infamy and are unaffected. `src/lib/utils/infamy.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/voteDistribution.ts`.
- **Political-influence sub-score uses a softer (sqrt) curve** — the old log curve compressed PI=85 vs PI=99 to a 0.8-pt difference out of 25; the new sqrt curve yields ~1.8 pts. State primary scoring already clamps PI at 100; presidential general elections lose the previous >1.0 reach bonus (the log curve climbed to 2.0 above NPI=100). Presidential primary's separate national-reach function is unchanged. `src/lib/utils/normalizeNPI.ts`.
- **Election line graph and bar now use unified candidate colors** — the chart legend, line, pie slices, and the leader bar all use the same color-per-candidate via `buildCandidateColorMap`, eliminating cases where a candidate's bar color differed from their line graph color. `src/app/elections/[id]/components/ElectionDetailCharts.tsx`.
- **Admin "start general" route now uses the canonical presidential primary score** — replaced a duplicated formula (alignment 50 / fav 30 / inf 20) with `calcPresidentPrimaryScore`, so admin force-resolves apply the same weights, infamy penalty, and party-org input as turn-time primary resolution. `src/app/api/admin/elections/[id]/start-general/route.ts`.
- **Poll preview applies the infamy penalty** — `computePollData` now plumbs infamy into both the per-archetype head-to-head share calculation and the in-race vote simulation, so the poll page matches what the live election engine will produce. `OpponentForShare` gained an optional `infamy` field. `src/lib/actions/pollCalculations.ts`.
- **Real-world per-state allocation defaults for GOP primary** — GOP per-state allocations now default to real-world rules instead of generic proportional. `src/lib/electionEngine/allocations.ts`.
- **Reconcile primary vote share vs delegate share display** — primary detail cards now reconcile vote-share and delegate-share figures against the same source data so they don't disagree. `src/app/elections/[id]/components/PrimaryShareCards.tsx`.
- **Restored intra-party position differentiation in primary projection** — primary projection no longer averages out party positions, so two same-party candidates with different policy positions get different scores. `src/lib/primaryScore.ts`.
- **Wiki content refreshed for the new curve and infamy penalty** — primaries, election mechanics, reference formulas, general elections, demographics targeting, and stats/actions wiki pages now describe the sqrt curve, state/party alignment split, and infamy multiplier accurately. Requires reseed to publish. `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/primaries.ts`, `electionMechanics.ts`, `referenceFormulas.ts`, `generalElections.ts`, `demographicsTargeting.ts`, `statsActions.ts`.

### Added

- **Sector secondary market** — CEOs can list any of their corporation's sectors at 75% of NPV, and another CEO can buy with corporate treasury. Asking price is locked at listing time, fully forex-aware (corp→corp transfer at live FX, sector revenue and growth-cost re-denominated to buyer's currency on transfer). Sectors with non-positive base profit can't be listed; you can't buy a sector type you already operate in that state. Listings show as a `For Sale` badge on the sector hero, the corp's `Sectors` tab, and the state economy market participants list. `src/lib/sectorMarket/listing.ts`, `src/lib/sectorMarket/purchase.ts`, `src/app/api/corp/sectors/[id]/list/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corp/sectors/[id]/buy/route.ts`, `src/components/sectorMarket/*`.
- **Presidential Campaign Strength system** — New `campaignStrength` field on `Campaign`/`CampaignData`, surfaced via `getCampaign` and election detail. `CampaignStrengthPanel` component renders on presidential campaign pages; presidential candidate table now has a campaign strength column and a Support button. `POST /api/campaign/[id]/campaign-strength` records contributions (with character-deduction rollback on failure). Per-candidate vote accumulation in presidential resolution now applies the campaign strength multiplier; `campaignStrength` resets to 0 on election resolution. `src/lib/db/types/campaign.ts`, `src/app/api/campaign/[id]/campaign-strength/route.ts`, `src/components/campaign/CampaignStrengthPanel.tsx`, `src/lib/turn/presidentialResolution.ts`.
- **Cabinet acting appointments** — A non-confirmed cabinet officer can be installed as Acting in a vacant role; carries an approval penalty until confirmed. `src/lib/cabinet/actingAppointment.ts`, `src/components/cabinet/ActingAppointmentControls.tsx`.
- **UK constituency selection extended to Prime Ministers** — UK PMs now pick a real Westminster constituency from their region, matching MP behavior. `src/app/profile/components/ConstituencyPicker.tsx`, `src/lib/uk/constituencies.ts`.
- **DE labour minister + ministerial orders** — Germany's Labour Minister office added with its own page, metrics, ministerial orders, and refreshed Foreign Minister wiring. `src/lib/seeds/cabinet/de/*`, `src/app/country/de/cabinet/labour-minister/page.tsx`.
- **Country roster expansion** — Ireland (IE), Brazil (BR), and China (CN) added as econ-only countries; Nigeria (NG) added as a planned rollout in `runtime` availability. Country runtime states unified across the codebase. `src/lib/seeds/countries/*`, `src/lib/countries/runtime.ts`.
- **Inflation diagnostics admin panel** — New admin panel that surfaces per-input contributions to the inflation calc, side-by-side with the recalc output. `src/app/admin/inflation-diagnostics/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/inflation/diagnostics/route.ts`.
- **Admin Reset Lock control** — `POST /api/admin/turn/reset-lock` endpoint and a Reset Lock button on `TurnControls` for clearing stuck turn locks; logs to admin audit. `src/app/api/admin/turn/reset-lock/route.ts`, `src/app/admin/turn/components/TurnControls.tsx`.
- **Moderator activity timeline + update-positions** — Moderator panel now exposes profile and character timeline events in the activity log; new `update-positions` route and panel form for positional moderator changes. `src/app/admin/mod/components/ActivityLog.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/mod/positions/route.ts`.
- **User-managed bot keys with scoped auth + logging** — Players can mint, scope, and revoke API keys for bots. Bot API auth path narrowed and hardened, with structured logging on auth failures. Public token now enforced on the elections view endpoint. `src/lib/botKeys/*`, `src/app/api/auth/bot-key/*`, `src/lib/botAuth.ts`.
- **Google Privacy & Messaging CMP support** — Site-level support for Google's certified Privacy & Messaging flow via the standard AdSense page tag, including footer-based consent revocation, consent-mode-ready Google Analytics defaults for EEA/UK/Switzerland traffic, and a documented `NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT` environment variable. `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/components/CookieConsent.tsx`, `src/components/SiteFooter.tsx`, `src/lib/googlePrivacyMessaging.ts`, `.env.example`.
- **Google Ads conversion tag (AW-18130975758)** — Wired Google Ads conversion measurement on the registration funnel. `src/components/analytics/GoogleAdsConversion.tsx`.
- **Coalition and caucus Discord invite links** — Coalition Chairs and Caucus Chairs can now save a Discord invite URL from their existing chair-management surfaces, and the saved link appears as the clickable Discord button in coalition headers, coalition cards, and selected caucus headers. Invite URLs reuse the same normalization and validation rules as national parties. `src/components/DiscordInviteButton.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/[id]/settings/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/[id]/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/components/CoalitionCard.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/coalition/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusesTab.tsx`.
- **Discord OAuth referral code** — Referral code is now passed through the Discord OAuth registration flow so signups via Discord are credited correctly. `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`, `src/lib/auth/referral.ts`.
- **Landing page Discord CTA** — A Join the Discord call-to-action card in the landing-page support section. `src/app/components/Landing/SupportSection.tsx`.
- **In-process cron jobs for Railway deployment** — Internal scheduler runs hot-path turn jobs in-process when deployed on Railway, complementing Vercel cron. `src/lib/cron/inProcess.ts`, `src/instrumentation.ts`.

### Changed

- **Privacy policy consent flow** — The privacy policy now documents Google consent handling and intentionally excludes Privacy & Messaging and consent-managed Google tags from `/privacy`, matching Google's guidance for the policy URL used in Privacy & Messaging. `src/app/privacy/page.tsx`, `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/lib/googlePrivacyMessaging.ts`.
- **Tangible-book weight in stock-price formula raised to 1.0 (from 0.8)** — Brings displayed market cap closer to balance-sheet truth and reduces the residual gap on cash-heavy corps. `src/lib/turn/sharePriceCalculation.ts`.
- **Corporate monopoly pressure + sustained-negative-production penalties** — Corps with persistent monopoly market share now face a soft growth-cost penalty; corps that have run sustained negative production take an escalating margin penalty until they reverse course. `src/lib/turn/corp/monopolyPressure.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corp/sustainedNegativeProduction.ts`.
- **fundamentalSharePrice scales on stock split / reverse split** — Splits now scale `fundamentalSharePrice` along with the live price so the next-turn snap-back effect is fully eliminated. `src/lib/turn/sharePriceCalculation.ts`.
- **Tariff sentiment pulses + inflation pressure are now FTA-aware** — Inflation pressure and sentiment pulses skip pairs that share an active FTA. Foreign-side sentiment also fires on FTA rescission with the appropriate cleanup migration. `src/lib/inflation/tariffPressure.ts`, `src/lib/sentiment/tariffPulses.ts`, `src/lib/db/migrations/ftaCleanup.ts`.
- **Campaign funds stored in home currency** — Campaign-fund balances are now persisted in the character's home currency under forex; legacy `funds` field is no longer the source of truth for forex-enabled characters. `src/lib/campaign/funds.ts`.
- **Hourly turn cadence restored, stock exchange refresh corrected to 15 min** — Cron schedules normalized after the deployment-target switch. `src/lib/cron/turn.ts`, `src/lib/cron/stockExchange.ts`.
- **Slur filter no longer blocks "queer"** — Removed from the moderation slur list for news/posts. `src/lib/moderation/slurs.ts`.
- **Adsense readiness hardened + age floor lowered to 13+** — Final compliance pass for AdSense; minimum signup age dropped to 13. `src/lib/auth/registration.ts`, `src/components/CookieConsent.tsx`.
- **Performance: cache hot polled endpoints** — High-frequency polled API routes now use short-TTL response caching to cut Vercel CPU during quiet periods. `src/lib/api/cache.ts`.
- **Performance: bypass slow custom image paths + reduce global chrome bootstrap overhead** — Removed several render-path bottlenecks identified in the perf audit. `next.config.ts`, `src/components/Layout/GlobalChrome.tsx`.
- **Stability: Sentry noise gate, abort-controllers, NPP upsert fix, N+1 batches** — Sentry now drops known no-op errors; long fetch chains gain abort controllers; NPP upsert race fixed; several N+1 query loops batched. `src/lib/sentry/*`, `src/lib/db/queries/*`.
- **Vercel ↔ Railway env var sync** — Added a script and workflow to sync env vars between Vercel and Railway, plus support for project-scoped Railway tokens via explicit IDs. `scripts/syncVercelRailwayEnv.ts`, `.github/workflows/sync-vercel-railway-env.yml`.

### Fixed

- **Stuck turn processing closed on multiple paths** — Two stuck-processing gaps closed and the turn-lock recovery hardened so a stuck turn can no longer block the world indefinitely. `src/lib/turn/turnLock.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/turn/reset-lock/route.ts`.
- **Cross-country political actions blocked** — The action authorization layer now enforces that political actions (campaign, NPP, party) target same-country entities, closing a class of cross-country exploits. `src/lib/security/sameCountry.ts`, plus call-site guards across action routes.
- **Inflation recalculation hardened + repair migration** — Reworked recalc inputs and added a wave-8 backfill migration to fix corrupted historical rows; FX pressure clamped to a sane range and diagnostic commodity clamping aligned. `src/lib/inflation/recalc.ts`, `src/lib/db/migrations/inflationWave8.ts`.
- **Inflation uses correct budget ID for non-US presidential countries** — A presidential-country-specific bug caused inflation to read the wrong budget under forex; now resolves the right budget per country. `src/lib/inflation/budgetResolution.ts`.
- **Inflation floor budget bug** — Inflation floor was being read from the wrong budget snapshot. `src/lib/inflation/floor.ts`.
- **Stock-price formula** — Stuck-share-price audit closed several manipulation paths around limit-order fills and concurrent buys. `src/lib/markets/orderRouting.ts`, `src/app/api/stocks/orders/[id]/route.ts`.
- **Bond maturity flows folded into pre-default delta** — Maturity payouts no longer trip a spurious default check on the same turn. `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`.
- **Bond cash payoff fallback when MongoDB replica set unavailable** — When the cluster falls out of replica-set state, bond payoff now falls back to a non-transactional path instead of failing the turn. `src/lib/db/transactions.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/payoff.ts`.
- **Corp `liquidCapital` converted to anchor before returning to UI** — Corp detail responses now FX-normalize `liquidCapital` to the anchor before returning, eliminating mixed-currency totals on the UI. `src/lib/corp/queries/liquidCapital.ts`.
- **Forex strength semantics clarified** — Internal labels and downstream UI for "strength" matched up; previously some surfaces showed inverted semantics. `src/lib/forex/strength.ts`.
- **Settled wealth and portfolio history snapshotting** — Settled-wealth and portfolio-history rows now snapshot the source values they depend on, so historical chart points don't repaint when underlying inputs change. `src/lib/portfolio/history.ts`, `src/lib/turn/settledWealth.ts`.
- **Portfolio charts: snapshot FX rates per history point** — Each history point stores the FX rate used at the time, so portfolio charts no longer repaint historical USD values when the live FX rate changes. `src/lib/portfolio/history.ts`.
- **Portfolio charts return most recent 500 history points** — Previously returned the oldest 500. `src/lib/portfolio/queries/history.ts`.
- **CEO Vote button only shows for HQ-eligible shareholders** — Previously the Vote CEO button appeared for shareholders ineligible to vote (non-HQ-country). `src/components/corp/CorpShareholdersTable.tsx`.
- **CEO public-float buying allowed; whip notifications link to bill** — CEOs can now buy from public float through normal flows; whip notifications now deep-link to the relevant bill page. `src/app/api/corp/shares/buy/route.ts`, `src/lib/notifications/whip.ts`.
- **Corp FX fees applied to corp trades** — Corporate forex trades now correctly debit the spread fee, matching player trades. `src/lib/forex/corpTrades.ts`.
- **Subsidy income aligned with turn processing** — Corp Financials subsidy line now matches the actual debit on the turn. `src/lib/turn/corp/subsidies.ts`.
- **Subsidies budget bug** — A budget-line accounting mismatch on subsidies caused the displayed budget to disagree with the live charge. `src/lib/budget/subsidies.ts`.
- **JP propose flow, cabinet portfolios, country-scoped fiscal year** — JP legislation propose flow restored; JP cabinet portfolios now use the correct seeds; fiscal year is country-scoped instead of global. `src/lib/legislature/jp/propose.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/cabinet/jp/*`, `src/lib/turn/fiscalYear.ts`.
- **JP Shugiin override surfaced in whip/vote paths; NPP cross-pressure rescaled** — Shugiin override is now applied in JP whip and vote-handler paths; NPP cross-pressure rebalanced for JP. `src/lib/legislature/jp/shugiinOverride.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/billVoting.ts`.
- **Income tax fiscal-year handling hardened** — Tax and "suspect flag" handling reworked so multi-currency income tax doesn't double-count or escape the fiscal-year window. `src/lib/turn/taxYear.ts`.
- **Median income clamps within bounds** — `medianIncome` now uses min/max value bounds in the metric definition to prevent clamping to 100 in some currencies. `src/lib/seeds/metrics/medianIncome.ts`.
- **Auto-reelection targets the correct seat** — A bug in the auto-reelection seat-matching logic caused entries into the wrong race in the same state; now matches by `senateClass`/`chamberClass`. `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`.
- **Settings page refreshes active character on load** — A stale-cache bug could leave the settings page tied to a previous character. `src/app/settings/page.tsx`.
- **Currency: portfolio respects display preference** — Portfolio formatting now honors the user's display-currency preference instead of always using anchor currency. `src/components/portfolio/CurrencyDisplay.tsx`.
- **Currency display bug** — Several UI labels formatted currency with mixed scales (e.g. JP showing M when it should show B). `src/lib/format/currency.ts`.
- **Pres campaign support: show CS immediately after support; strengthen org weight** — Campaign-strength contributions now appear on the candidate row immediately after the action; presidential org weight rebalanced. `src/components/campaign/CampaignStrengthPanel.tsx`, `src/lib/turn/presidentialResolution.ts`.
- **Block no-op stat actions when target is at cap or floor** — Influence actions that would land at 0 effect on a capped/floored stat now show an explicit error instead of consuming actions for nothing. `src/lib/influence/validation.ts`.
- **Vacate prior office when winning a different one** — Winning a new race now correctly vacates the prior office instead of leaving the player double-seated. `src/lib/elections/onWin.ts`.
- **Enforce exclusive leadership seats** — A character can only hold one of Speaker/Pres-pro-tem/Whip at once; concurrent-write bug fixed. `src/lib/parties/leadership/exclusivity.ts`.
- **State-party elections show cooldown message instead of membership error** — Failure path was misclassified. `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/elections/route.ts`.
- **NPP endorsements are now manual-only and relationship/policy gated** — Removed turn-time organic NPP campaign endorsements, converted the player `Request Endorsement` action to a hidden deterministic relationship threshold based on economic/social policy distance, and updated the NPP profile picker to show only `Likely to Accept` / `Likely to Decline` chips for active campaigns. Active organic endorsements are now withdrawn by the turn cleanup pass, while arranged endorsements persist only for the currently active campaign and must be requested again in future races. `src/lib/nppEndorsements.ts`, `src/lib/nppEndorsements.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/endorsements.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/endorsements.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/nppBehavior.ts`, `src/lib/capital/actions.ts`, `src/lib/capital/actions.test.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.test.ts`, `src/app/politicians/npp/[id]/NppCapitalPanel.tsx`, `docs/design/npp-system.md`, `docs/design/campaign-manager.md`, `docs/design/party-influence.md`, `docs/design/core-systems.md`, `docs/design/turn-processing.md`.
- **Player-to-NPP direct actions now read the correct campaign-fund balance under forex** — The NPP direct-interaction route now uses the same forex-aware campaign-funds helpers as the rest of the actions system, so the panel balance, affordability checks, and spend/refund path all read from `currencyBalances.campaign` when forex is enabled instead of the legacy `funds` field. `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.test.ts`.
- **Player NPP boost actions no longer require positive relationship** — `Boost Favorability` and `Boost Influence` on the player-to-NPP panel now gate only on actions and campaign funds, so hostile or neutral relationships no longer block those two stat-raising actions. `src/lib/capital/actions.ts`, `src/lib/capital/actions.test.ts`.
- **Caucus chair votes can now be withdrawn** — Caucus members can now clear their own vote during an active caucus chair election, matching the flexibility of the main party leadership election surfaces. The caucus vote route accepts a withdraw action, and the caucus election panel now exposes a `Withdraw Vote` button when you have an active vote recorded. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/election/vote/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusChairElectionPanel.tsx`.
- **Player NPP direct-action panel now supports reduce actions and fund costs** — The player-facing NPP profile interaction panel now includes `Reduce Favorability` and `Reduce Influence`, and all four stat-shaping actions (`Boost/Reduce Favorability`, `Boost/Reduce Influence`) now charge both actions and campaign funds. The direct-action route enforces those fund gates, logs fund spend, and refunds both actions and funds on fallback rollback if a later write fails. `src/lib/db/types/politicalCapital.ts`, `src/lib/capital/actions.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.test.ts`, `src/app/politicians/npp/[id]/NppCapitalPanel.tsx`, `docs/design/npp-system.md`, `docs/design/stats-actions.md`, `docs/design/getting-started.md`.
- **Incumbent NPP re-entry now respects Senate and chamber classes** — Seat-defending NPPs now match primaries by `senateClass` and `chamberClass` as well as office type and state, so a sitting incumbent can no longer auto-file into the wrong staggered seat in the same state or region. This fixes reports of Senate NPPs re-entering the other class's primary instead of defending the seat they actually hold. `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.test.ts`.
- **Slate reassignment no longer hard-declines active NPP candidates** — High-fit NPPs who are already filed in another race now accept party Slate reassignment instead of declining with `already in a race`. On the next filing pass, the existing Slate mover withdraws them from the old race and files them into the newly assigned one. `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponse.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponse.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponses.test.ts`.
- **NPP voting behavior** — Multiple corrections to NPP autonomous voting on bills, including federal-vs-local pressure rebalancing, hidden-roll edge cases for hard whips, and tally regression where strong cross-pressure swung NPP votes incorrectly. `src/lib/turn/npp/billVoting.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/billVoting.test.ts`.
- **NPP direct-action fallback rollback** — Player-to-NPP direct actions now fully compensate on non-transaction fallbacks when a later write fails: action points are refunded, relationship changes are restored, temporary NPP stat bumps are reverted, and same-election endorsement rows are rewound to their pre-action state instead of leaving partial side effects behind after a 500. `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.test.ts`, `src/lib/nppEndorsements.ts`.
- **National NPP relocation requests now auto-resign and auto-withdraw** — National party `Request Relocation` no longer blocks when the target NPP is already serving in office or running in an active election. Accepted relocation requests now automatically vacate the NPP's current office, trigger Senate vacancy notification when applicable, withdraw the NPP from any still-open election, clean the related tallies, and then complete the home-state move. `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorValidation.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorEffects.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorValidation.test.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorEffects.test.ts`.
- **Line of credit underwriting no longer snowballs off debt-funded income** — LOC draw limits now carry a hard net-worth ceiling alongside an income-based DTI ceiling that uses a 48-turn rolling average of recurring personal income instead of a one-turn snapshot, so debt-funded bond purchases can no longer recursively expand the same borrower's credit line. Draw-limit feedback now distinguishes pool exhaustion, net-worth ceilings, and recent-income ceilings more accurately. `src/lib/lineOfCredit/currencyIncomeEstimate.ts`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/buildSnapshot.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/central-bank/loan-tracker/route.ts`, `src/app/api/character/loc/draw/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/CentralBankLoanTab.tsx`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/currencyIncomeEstimate.test.ts`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/buildSnapshot.test.ts`.
- **Central bank LOC exploit closed** — A path that allowed bypassing LOC draw caps via reused state was patched, alongside additional concurrency guards on draw flows. `src/app/api/character/loc/draw/route.ts`, `src/lib/lineOfCredit/concurrency.ts`.
- **National party recent activity no longer floods GOTV rows per state** — The national party `Recent activity` feed now filters treasury rows to true national-party holders only, so state-party GOTV spends no longer spam the national card. National turnout spending also now emits separate per-tick treasury rows for aggregated `GOTV operations` and `Suppression operations` instead of rolling both into a single generic GOTV output. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/activity-feed/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/activity-feed/route.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.test.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/treasuryTransaction.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/treasury/transactions/route.ts`.
- **Party treasury logs now bundle turnout spending by turn** — The national party Treasury transaction log now rolls all `GOTV` and `Suppression` spend for the same turn into one row per category instead of listing a separate state/regional entry for each downstream spend, and the Overview `Recent activity` feed now hides GOTV, suppression, org-building, and fund-generation noise so the card stays focused on higher-signal party actions. `src/lib/db/treasuryTransactionLookup.ts`, `src/lib/db/treasuryTransactionLookup.test.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/treasury/transactions/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/activity-feed/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/activity-feed/route.test.ts`.
- **National GOTV treasury math is now country-scoped and the UI estimate includes NPP states** — National GOTV/suppression spending now computes revenue using country-scoped party member buckets instead of mixing same-`sequentialId` parties across countries, and the national party treasury detail now includes NPP home states when building its hourly revenue estimate so the displayed spend forecast matches the turn-time deductions more closely. `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.test.ts`, `src/lib/parties/queries/partyDetail.ts`, `src/lib/parties/queries/partyDetail.test.ts`.
- **National treasury logs now show national-party rows only** — The national party treasury transaction log no longer bundles in state-party or caucus treasury rows, so the ledger matches the national treasury panel instead of showing mixed-scope GOTV totals. The holder-scoped lookup now keeps the route's `countryId` guard so same-`sequentialId` parties in other countries cannot bleed into the national ledger, and the subtitle plus hover copy explicitly say that state-party and caucus treasury activity lives on their own pages. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/treasury/transactions/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/treasury/transactions/route.test.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/TreasuryTransactionLog.tsx`, `src/lib/db/treasuryTransactionLookup.ts`.
- **State party chair appointments now keep their country scope** — The country-scoped state-party leadership appointment route now verifies the target state by both `_id` and `countryId`, preventing same-code regions in other countries from satisfying the lookup. `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/leadership/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/leadership/route.test.ts`.
- **Party logos** — Logo upload + redirect-route URLs now bypass the next/image optimizer so static logos render correctly in all contexts. Stock market and logo fallback rendering also stabilized. `next.config.ts`, `src/components/Layout/PartyLogo.tsx`.
- **Party office overlap** — Office-card layout overlapped on narrow viewports; constrained widths and spacing fixed. `src/app/parties/[id]/components/OfficeCard.tsx`.
- **Filter capitalization / filter update** — Filter chips now use consistent capitalization and survive cross-page navigation. `src/components/Filters/*`.
- **Site issue rollups** — Multiple `fix/site-issue` PRs (#1473, #1477, #1480, #1481, #1491, #1507, #1518) addressing image fallbacks, navigation regressions, and small UI breakages.
- **Auth: redirect users without setup to /create-character on sign-in; exempt admins** — Sign-in now correctly funnels new users into character creation, while admins are exempted from that redirect so they can land on admin pages. `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`.
- **Auth: sign-in redirect** — Followed up the create-character redirect with a final pass that fixed regressions in the OAuth callback flow. `src/lib/auth/redirect.ts`.
- **Deployment: railway healthchecks, env handling, standalone assets, HOSTNAME** — Multiple Railway-deployment hardening passes including healthcheck path correction, env-var resolution, restoring standalone assets in the build, setting `HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0` in `railway.toml`, enabling Next.js standalone output, and project-scoped Railway tokens. `railway.toml`, `next.config.ts`, `scripts/postbuild-standalone.ts`.

