## [0.2.11] - 2026-04-30

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Organic NPP endorsement lifecycle** - NPPs now run a turn-time endorsement pass that can create, hold, switch, and withdraw endorsements across any active race they can plausibly care about, using weighted relationship, ideology, party, relevance, and viability scoring. Endorsements now track whether they were `organic` or `arranged`, re-evaluate every 4 turns plus on field-change triggers, and arranged endorsements get extra staying power before an NPP will defect. Active NPP endorsements also now contribute a small capped direct favorability bump in candidate enrichment so endorsements matter in race calculations beyond campaign-action generation. `src/lib/nppEndorsements.ts`, `src/lib/nppEndorsements.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/endorsements.ts`, `src/lib/turn/nppBehavior.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.ts`, `src/lib/influence/executor.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorEffects.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/candidateEnrichment.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/candidateEnrichment.test.ts`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/endorsements/route.ts`, `src/lib/elections/candidateEnrichment.ts`, `docs/design/npp-system.md`, `docs/design/campaign-manager.md`

- **Caucus health dashboard** - National party `Analytics` now includes a `Caucus Health` summary, and each caucus `Overview` now shows a richer health panel with `Healthy / Strained / Fragile` status, recent joins/leaves/forced exits, active caucus-whip defiance counts, chair-election activity, and NPP members drifting toward the chair-relationship exit threshold. The health snapshot is shared across the analytics route and caucus detail routes so both surfaces read the same churn, election, and retention signals. `src/lib/caucus/caucusHealth.ts`, `src/lib/caucus/caucusHealth.test.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/analytics/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/PartyAnalyticsTab.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusesTab.tsx`

- **Whip defiance watch** - Party, state-party, and caucus `Whip Room` surfaces now include a live `Defiance` view that shows only active non-compliance against current whip directives, split into `Players` and `NPPs`. The watch is derived from current whips plus current votes rather than stored as a permanent ledger, so rows disappear automatically once the voter comes back into line. National and state/regional `Analytics` discipline summaries now also surface active player and NPP defiance counts. `src/lib/partyWhips/whipDefiance.ts`, `src/lib/partyWhips/whipDefiance.test.ts`, `src/components/party/WhipDefiancePanel.tsx`, `src/components/party/WhipTabs.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/whip/defiance/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip/defiance/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/whip/defiance/route.ts`, `src/lib/partyAnalytics/discipline.ts`, `src/lib/partyAnalytics/types.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/PartyAnalyticsTab.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/components/StatePartyAnalyticsTab.tsx`

- **Coalition priorities system** - Coalitions now use a real `Priorities` mechanic instead of a placeholder tab. Coalition chairs can propose up to three active priorities at a time across `policy themes`, `live bills`, and `leadership goals`, with each member party chair voting `support`, `oppose`, or `abstain` to activate them. Public and internal visibility are supported, coalition cohesion now summarizes active support vs dissent, and bill or leadership priorities auto-expire when their live target window ends while manual archive remains available. `src/lib/db/types/coalition.ts`, `src/lib/coalitions/priorities.ts`, `src/lib/coalitions/priorityApi.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/[id]/priorities/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/[id]/priorities/[priorityId]/vote/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/[id]/priorities/[priorityId]/archive/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/components/CoalitionPrioritiesPanel.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/coalition/[id]/page.tsx`

- **Caucus chair elections** - National-party caucuses now have an `Elections` sub-tab with real `Caucus Chair` election windows, candidate entry and withdrawal, active-member voting, winner promotion, and caucus-member notifications. The caucus election cadence is anchored to the parent party's national chair election window so caucus leadership turns over on the same schedule as the broader party leadership cycle. `src/lib/db/types/caucusChairElection.ts`, `src/lib/caucusChairElections.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/election/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/election/enter/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/election/vote/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusChairElectionPanel.tsx`, `src/lib/nationalPartyElections.ts`

