- **National NPP relocation requests** - National Party Chairs and Vice Chairs can now manage same-party NPPs in any state, even when active player members are already present there, and can request that an NPP relocate to another state for 25% of the target state's normal recruitment cost through the restored `NPPs -> Management` panel. `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/influence/route.ts`, `src/lib/influence/*`, `src/lib/npp/recruitment.ts`

### Fixed

- **Slate template bleed across Senate classes** - State and national Slate template carry-forward now keeps `senateClass` and `chamberClass` races isolated, so assigning a player or NPP in one Senate class can no longer auto-materialize the same row into a sibling class panel in the same state. `src/lib/db/recruitmentSlateLookup.ts`, `src/lib/db/recruitmentSlateLookup.test.ts`
- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Party NPP rework rollout indexes** - Hardened the `add-party-npp-rework-indexes` migration so it replaces stale legacy index definitions in place, splits `nppVotePredictions` uniqueness between federal `billId` rows and local `stateBillId` rows, and adds missing live-query indexes for latest NPP forecasts, endorsement lookups, and caucus chair election workloads. `scripts/migrations/add-party-npp-rework-indexes.ts`
- **Party NPP rework migration invariants** - The rollout migration now deduplicates bad live `slateCandidates` and active `caucusChairElections` rows before creating the new unique indexes those systems rely on, and it adds the missing `(electionId, candidateId, isActive)` endorsement lookup index used by campaign and election enrichment reads. `scripts/migrations/add-party-npp-rework-indexes.ts`
- **Turn telemetry and state-party country scoping** - Restored `caucusTax`, `nppRelationshipMaintenance`, and `autoReelectionEntry` to the canonical turn-phase name list so aborted-turn telemetry and admin phase-status reporting cannot silently omit live phases, and tightened branch-touched state-party detail/transfer routes to scope `states` lookups by both `_id` and `countryId` while using the canonical party key for state treasury-plan lookups. `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/transfer/route.ts`

- **National party NPP management tab** - The national party `NPPs` page now has `Recruitment` and `Management` sub-tabs. Recruitment keeps the rework branch's current NPP recruitment flow, while Management restores the live `National Party NPP Influence` panel with state-scoped NPP selection, queued influence actions, and the supporting `/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/influence` route plus restored party-influence executor files in `src/lib/influence/`. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/influence/route.ts`, `src/lib/influence/*`

- **Bill detail whip panel** - Added a `Whip Panel` to Congress bill detail pages beneath the bill description so party chairs and vice chairs can issue both Player Whips and NPP Whips without leaving the bill. The panel reads the same `/whippable-bills` summaries and posts to the same national-party `/whip` endpoint as the party Actions -> Whip tab, including the per-audience whip-attempt count blurb, so whips issued from either surface stay in sync and immediately refresh the bill's vote counters. `src/components/bills/BillWhipPanel.tsx`, `src/app/congress/bills/[id]/page.tsx`

- **Wiki Elections category seeded (Phase 2)** — Eleven player-facing election pages added to the seed pipeline: `election-mechanics` (featured), `primaries`, `general-elections`, `polling`, `fundraising-ads`, `canvassing`, `demographics-targeting`, `campaign-strategy` (featured), `campaign-manager`, `primary-general-tactics`, `snap-elections`. All pages use the current primary score formulas (state: alignment 0-40 + favorability 0-35 + influence 0-25; presidential: alignment 0-40 + party org 0-25 + NPI 0-25 + favorability 0-10), the actual FPTP spoiler mechanics, the correct campaign upgrade tables, and the 4-country legislature set (US, UK, DE, JP). Content in `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/*.ts`, wired through `src/lib/seeds/wiki/pages/elections.ts`. Wiki remains admin-only until Phase 8.

- **Wiki Getting Started category seeded (Phase 1)** — Eight player-facing pages added to the new wiki seed pipeline: `getting-started` (featured), `create-a-character`, `core-systems` (featured), `stats-actions`, `the-game-loop`, `player-progression`, `relocation`, and `first-campaign-walkthrough` (featured). Each page is multi-country aware (US, UK, DE, JP) and uses the current action economy, fund-generation, and turn-system numbers rather than the outdated design-doc values. Content lives in `src/lib/seeds/wiki/content/*.ts` and is wired through `src/lib/seeds/wiki/pages/gettingStarted.ts`. Pages remain admin-only until Phase 8 flips the public wiki toggle.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Party and NPP design docs reconciled to the live rework** - Updated `docs/design/npp-system.md`, `docs/design/parties.md`, `docs/design/party-building.md`, `docs/design/party-influence.md`, `docs/design/party-whips.md`, `docs/design/coalitions.md`, `docs/design/campaign-manager.md`, and `docs/design/README.md` so the documented intended rules now match the current NPP election entry, bill voting, endorsement lifecycle, player-only congressional leadership voting, party analytics, Slate, caucus, whip, treasury, and coalition-priorities systems.

### Removed

- **Standing Orders backend** - Removed the unused `standingOrders` backend feature, including its national and caucus API routes, collection/type helpers, turn-time compliance phase, and related cleanup hooks, because the system no longer has a live UI surface and no current `Slate` or `Whip` flows route through it. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/standing-orders/*`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/standing-orders/*`, `src/lib/db/standingOrderLookup.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/standingOrder.ts`, `src/lib/turn/standingOrderCompliance.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **NPP incumbent defense and Slate challenger filing** - NPP race entry now lets incumbents auto-defend their own seat even if a same-party challenger is already active, while still capping same-party Slate challengers to one per race and clearing accepted Slate rows for retired or invalid NPP targets instead of retrying them forever. `src/lib/turn/nppEntryLogic.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponses.ts`

- **National party NPP stat display rounding** - National `NPPs -> Management` now rounds displayed NPP stats to one decimal place so the management card matches the cleaner state and regional formatting instead of rounding to whole numbers. `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`

- **State party NPP stat display rounding** - State and regional `NPPs -> Management` panels now round displayed NPP stats to one decimal place instead of exposing raw floating-point values in the management card. `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/components/StatePartyInfluencePanel.tsx`

- **Coalition detail page keys now tolerate duplicate party rows** - Hardened the coalition detail page lists and select menus to use composite React keys for member parties, invites, and join requests instead of relying on raw `partyId` or `sequentialId` alone, preventing duplicate-key render warnings from breaking the coalition page when legacy or duplicated coalition rows exist. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/coalition/[id]/page.tsx`

- **Coalition creation and reset cleanup** - Coalition creation now atomically reserves the founding party before inserting the coalition and debits actions before commit, preventing duplicate coalition records from rapid repeat submits by the same National Party Chair. Full game resets now also delete all coalition documents and clear `coalitionId` pointers from surviving default parties so stale coalition cards cannot persist after a reset. `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/coalitions/route.test.ts`, `src/lib/admin/resetGameWorld.ts`, `src/lib/admin/resetGameWorld.test.ts`

- **Caucus chair elections now purge departed, deleted, and banned players immediately** - Leaving a caucus, self-deleting, or being banned now withdraws that character from any live caucus-chair election, removes caucus-chair votes they cast or received, and clears stale caucus membership/chair pointers so caucus leadership tallies and rosters cannot retain ineligible players. `src/lib/caucus/cleanupCaucusParticipationForCharacters.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/members/[memberId]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/auth/delete-account/route.ts`, `src/lib/elections/cleanupPartyElectionsForBannedUser.ts`, `src/lib/account/stripPartyMembershipForBannedUser.ts`

- **Treasurer reserve editing is now role-gated correctly** - The national and state Treasurer planning cards remain visible to broader treasury leadership, but only the actual Treasurer for that scope or an Admin can edit and save reserve targets. The matching `/treasury-plan` routes now enforce the same Treasurer/Admin-only rule instead of inheriting Chair and Vice Chair access from the rest of treasury management. `src/components/party/TreasuryPlanningCard.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/TreasuryPanel.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/components/StatePartyFundraisingPanel.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/components/fundraisingTypes.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/treasury-plan/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/treasury-plan/route.ts`

- **Treasurer reserve inputs now use party treasury currency consistently** - Fixed the new Treasurer planning forms so reserve fields initialize, compare, and save in the same party-local currency basis that the dashboard cards display, preventing soft-target math from drifting into off-by-one or mixed-unit totals like `$30K` vs `$29,999`. `src/lib/currency/treasuryReserveDisplay.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/TreasuryPanel.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/components/useStatePartyData.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/components/StatePartyFundraisingPanel.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`

- **Corporate sector removals now restore unowned market pools** - Fixed three sector-deletion paths that could silently shrink a state market instead of returning revenue to Unowned: direct sector abandon, quick corporation dissolve, and bond-default dissolution now all credit `unownedSectors` before deleting `corporateSectors`. The corporation sector detail route also now treats a persisted zero-value unowned pool as authoritative instead of falling back to GDP market size. Added regression coverage and live-data tooling for audit/heal workflows, including batch manifest support for screenshot-derived repairs. `src/lib/corporations/restoreSectorsToUnowned.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/abandon/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/dissolve/route.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/executeCorporationBondDefaultDissolution.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/route.ts`, `scripts/migrations/inspect-dropped-sector-unowned-loss.ts`, `scripts/migrations/heal-dropped-sector-unowned-loss.ts`
- **Presidential primary stagger waves now bootstrap and catch up correctly** - The turn phase no longer waits until post-primary general-election setup to create the presidential tally, so Iowa and later stagger waves can persist results as soon as the election enters the T-5 window. If a live election is already behind, the stagger processor now catches up every due wave in the same turn instead of replaying just one missing wave per hour forever. The presidential primary pages were also aligned to the canonical T-5..T-0 calendar math so their "up next" labels match the backend thresholds. Added a live-safe dry-run/commit heal tool that audits the current presidential election via `MONGODB_URI_LIVE`, preserves already resolved full waves, and backfills missing due waves without resetting the whole race. `src/lib/turn/primaryStaggerPhase.ts`, `src/lib/turn/primaryResolution.test.ts`, `src/app/president/primary/[partyId]/page.tsx`, `src/app/president/primary/[partyId]/state/[stateId]/page.tsx`, `scripts/heal-presidential-primary-stagger.ts`
- **US presidential term caps and cabinet continuity** - U.S. presidential entry now blocks any character who has already served two presidential terms, the same term cap now removes those characters from VP selection and tentative running-mate auto-assignment, and presidential succession refuses to promote a term-limited VP into a third term. Legacy worlds are handled in place: prior presidential service is inferred from `careerHistory` when the stored counter is missing, and presidential / vice-presidential `electedOfficials` rows without `countryId` are rewritten as they resolve. Presidential resolution also preserves the sitting U.S. cabinet on same-president re-election and only clears it when the presidency actually changes hands. `src/app/api/elections/[id]/enter/route.ts`, `src/app/api/elections/[id]/running-mate/route.ts`, `src/app/api/elections/[id]/running-mate/characters/route.ts`, `src/lib/elections/executiveTermLimits.ts`, `src/lib/turn/primaryResolution.ts`, `src/lib/turn/presidentialSuccession.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/presidentResolution.ts`
- **Congressional leadership whip syncing** - Restored party-page Player Whips for U.S. Speaker and House/Senate leadership elections by aligning the national whip API with the live `"current"` / role-string target IDs and `speakerElections` / `houseLeadershipElections` / `senateLeadershipElections` collections, while adding regression coverage for the congressional leadership whip path. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/whip/route.test.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/billWhip.ts`
- **Leadership election auto-reopen coverage** - Fixed `resolveOneGeneralElection()` so House and Senate leadership elections reopen even when a chamber race resolves through the `!tally` or `ranked.length === 0` branches, and added regression tests for those recovery paths. `src/lib/turn/election/generalResolution.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/generalResolution.test.ts`
- **Majority-only incumbent auto-nominations** - Prevented Speaker and President Pro Tempore incumbents from being auto-nominated after falling out of the majority bloc in both turn-triggered and admin-started elections. `src/lib/congress/leadershipElections.ts`, `src/lib/congress/speaker/actions.ts`, `src/app/api/congress/senate-leadership/route.ts`, `src/lib/congress/leadershipElections.test.ts`

- **FX intervention was cosmetically active but functionally inert** — `computeInterventionPressure` fed synthetic volume into the organic volume-pressure channel (capped at ±5%, weighted at 20% via `VOLUME_DIRECTION_WEIGHT`), giving CB intervention a maximum per-turn rate correction of 1% against macro drift that routinely moves 2–3%/turn. Spend was also absolute (`|breach| × INTERVENTION_AGGRESSIVENESS × baseRate`), so a €251k reserve pool spent only ~€260/turn at a 15% breach (0.1% of reserves). Replaced with a direct multiplicative rate shift applied after organic volume pressure and independent of its cap: spend now scales as `|breach| × INTERVENTION_RESERVE_FRACTION × availableReserves` (at the 2.0 default a 3% persistent breach drains reserves in ~17 turns); rate shifts by `min(CB_INTERVENTION_RATE_CAP, |breach| × INTERVENTION_DIRECT_RATE_FACTOR)` (5% cap, 0.5 factor), scaled by spend efficiency when reserves are constrained. `organicVolumes` and `macro` removed from `applyIntervention`'s args (no longer needed). Removed `INTERVENTION_AGGRESSIVENESS`; added `INTERVENTION_RESERVE_FRACTION = 2.0`, `INTERVENTION_DIRECT_RATE_FACTOR = 0.5`, `CB_INTERVENTION_RATE_CAP = 0.05`. `src/lib/currency/interventionCalculator.ts`, `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`, `src/lib/constants/currencies.ts`.

- **FX intervention log "Spent" column showed bare integers with no currency symbol** — `InterventionRecord.internalUnitsSpent` was always denominated in local currency (EUR/GBP etc.) drawn directly from `forexRevenue`/`reserveBalance`, but the misleading name and the UI both omitted the symbol. Renamed to `reservesSpent`; the Chair-view log now renders `€281` instead of `281`. Column header updated to "Reserves spent". `src/lib/db/types/exchangeRate.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/CentralBankInterventionTab.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **State and regional NPP bill voting parity** - NPP legislators in `stateSenate` and `regionalCouncil` now auto-vote on local `stateBills` using the same deterministic ideology + whip + district + donor framework as federal bills, but with heavier home-region pressure and lighter donor pressure. Local vote predictions now persist alongside federal ones, the NPP forecast card can read either source, and state-party whippable-bill lists now surface both federal delegation bills and local chamber bills while routing local NPP whips to actual `stateBills`. The national `Player Whip` surface also no longer exposes unsupported state-legislature bill whips, so the UI matches the currently implemented mechanics instead of presenting a dead-end path. `src/lib/turn/npp/stateBillVoting.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/context.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/crossPressure.ts`, `src/lib/turn/nppBehavior.ts`, `src/lib/congress/applyWhipVotes.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whippable-bills/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whippable-bills/route.test.ts`, `src/components/party/NppWhipPanel.tsx`, `src/components/party/PlayerWhipPanel.tsx`, `src/components/party/whipTabsLayout.tsx`, `src/app/politicians/npp/[id]/NppForecastCard.tsx`, `src/lib/db/types/nppVotePrediction.ts`, `docs/design/npp-system.md`, `docs/design/bills-legislation.md`

- **NPP race-entry priority and incumbent defense** - Removed `president` from the deterministic NPP race-priority ladder now that presidential auto-entry is blocked, moved `commons` between `house` and `senate`, and tightened incumbent seat defense so incumbent NPPs automatically re-file into their defending primary before generic party fill even if that race has a cooldown stamp. Accepted Slate NPPs still file immediately after the incumbent-defense pass, so a slated challenger can create a same-party primary against the defending incumbent instead of being suppressed by the fallback one-NPP-per-party rule. `src/lib/turn/nppEntryLogic.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/slateResponses.ts`, `src/lib/turn/nppBehavior.ts`, `docs/design/npp-system.md`

- **NPP whip compliance** - National, state/regional, and caucus NPP whips now use a hidden `loyalty` / `stubbornness` success roll instead of a hard compliance threshold, with `hard` whips getting a stronger built-in bonus than `soft` whips. For bills specifically, `soft` NPP whips are now advisory only: they no longer write the vote immediately, they persist as a lighter cross-pressure force for autonomous bill voting, and `hard` bill whips keep the current immediate hidden-roll behavior. Failed hard rolls still fall back to the existing bill cross-pressure, leadership-fit, government-bloc, or cabinet heuristics instead of blindly obeying. `src/lib/partyWhips/whipSuccess.ts`, `src/lib/partyWhips/whipSuccess.test.ts`, `src/lib/congress/applyWhipVotes.ts`, `src/lib/congress/applyWhipVotes.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/crossPressure.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/crossPressure.test.ts`, `src/components/party/NppWhipPanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/caucuses/[slug]/whip/route.ts`, `docs/design/party-whips.md`

- **Caucus membership share chart** - The national party `Caucuses` tab now includes a pie-chart overview that splits caucus-aligned members across all active caucuses, with percentage labels and a matching legend that also acts as a caucus selector. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusesTab.tsx`

- **Party analytics Phase 1B drill-ins** - The national `Analytics` tab now exposes richer org, discipline, and Slate thresholds with additional summary counts, status labels, and state-scoped Slate drill-ins. Org rows now label `Near Cap` and `Underbuilt` states, discipline rows now tag `Critical` and `Elevated` NPP risk, and Slate analytics links now open the party Slate tab already focused on the relevant state. `src/lib/partyAnalytics/types.ts`, `src/lib/partyAnalytics/org.ts`, `src/lib/partyAnalytics/discipline.ts`, `src/lib/partyAnalytics/slate.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/PartyAnalyticsTab.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/SlateTab.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`

- **Caucus Chair visibility** - `Chair's Office` is now hidden from non-chairs in caucus detail views instead of showing a chair-only management tab that members could still click into. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusesTab.tsx`

- **Party page non-member visibility** - Non-members now only see the `Overview` and `Members` tabs on national and state/regional party pages, while party-only surfaces like `Analytics`, `Whip Room`, `Slate`, `NPPs`, `Elections`, and `Treasury` are hidden unless the viewer belongs to that party scope or is an Admin. National party analytics also now reject non-member requests server-side. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/analytics/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`

- **National party Overview privacy** - The `Discipline Watch` and `Recent Activity` cards on the national party `Overview` tab are now hidden from non-members, leaving only the public-facing overview panel visible to outside viewers. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`

- **State party Treasury tab cleanup** - Removed the `Primary Delegate Allocation` control from state and regional party pages so the Treasury surface stays focused on state-party finance instead of presidential-primary configuration. `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`

- **Party analytics Org display** - The national party `Analytics` tab now shows per-state `Growth` instead of raw `Momentum` in its org cards, using expected org change per turn derived from each state party's treasury `Organization Building` setting and projected hourly income. `src/lib/partyAnalytics/org.ts`, `src/lib/partyAnalytics/types.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/PartyAnalyticsTab.tsx`

- **Party analytics loading and tab layout** - National party analytics now prefetch in the background from the main party page so the `Analytics` tab opens much faster after the initial page load, and both national and state party page main navigation bars now wrap into two rows instead of forcing horizontal scrolling as the party feature set grows. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/PartyAnalyticsTab.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`

- **Slate race ordering and upper-chamber class labels** - Slate race lists now sort by office priority within each state or region instead of alphabetically: upper-chamber races first, then lower chamber, then governor-level races, and state or regional legislature races last. Upper-chamber Slate cards now also display their chamber class directly in the title, such as `Class II`, so staggered races are easier to distinguish at a glance. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/slate/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/SlateTab.tsx`

- **Player NPP direct interaction actions** - The player-facing NPP profile menu now replaces `Horse trade` with deterministic `Boost Favorability` and `Boost Influence` actions, removes `Threaten Primary`, and spends the character's normal action pool instead of a separate Political Capital resource. Both boost actions directly raise the target NPP's corresponding stat while also improving the player's relationship score with that NPP, and the old Political Capital refresh phase and `/api/me/political-capital` route have been removed. `src/app/politicians/npp/[id]/NppCapitalPanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/npps/[id]/direct-action/route.ts`, `src/lib/capital/actions.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/politicalCapital.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`

- **Caucus panel copy and roster labels** - The caucus founding and detail surfaces now consistently capitalize `Tax` and `Chair`, remove stale default-whip copy from the caucus overview text, and replace the old whip-mode summary in caucus cards with cleaner member/tax metadata. `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/components/CaucusesTab.tsx`

- **National NPP management action mix** - `Request Opposition` has been removed from the national `NPPs -> Management` action list, while `Strengthen Party Loyalty` and `Improve Cooperation` now explicitly use the hidden loyalty/stubbornness-driven willingness roll instead of behaving like guaranteed stat boosts. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/influence/route.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutor.ts`

- **National NPP management actions** - The management panel now shows Slate-style `Likely to Accept` / `Likely to Decline` chips instead of a raw success percentage, `Boost Favorability` and `Boost Political Influence` now succeed automatically, and `Request Leadership Support` has been removed from the available management actions. `src/components/influence/InfluencePanelShared.tsx`, `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/influence/route.ts`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutor.ts`

- **National NPP management influence rules** - Removed the extra-funds success boost from national NPP management actions, shifted estimated success to the same loyalty/stubbornness-style acceptance model used by Slate assignments, then softened that hidden national-management roll slightly so loyal, less stubborn same-party NPPs are a bit easier to persuade than before. `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/lib/influence/partyExecutorCalculations.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/influence/route.ts`

- **Legislature tab defaults** - Reordered the national and subnational legislature tab bars so `Bills` is the first tab and the default initial view across Congress, Parliament, the Diet, the Bundestag, and state legislature pages. `src/app/congress/CongressClient.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/legislature/UKParliamentPage.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/legislature/JPDietPage.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/legislature/DEBundestagPage.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/legislature/StateLegislatureClient.tsx`
- **U.S. congressional leadership elections** - House and Senate leadership races now run on 24-hour windows with automatic incumbent nominations after chamber election resolution, bloc-aware majority eligibility labels, non-majority-party access for minority leader races, and player-only participation so NPPs cannot run for or vote in Speaker, House leadership, or Senate leadership elections. `src/lib/congress/leadershipElections.ts`, `src/lib/congress/speaker/actions.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/generalResolution.ts`, `src/app/api/congress/house-leadership/route.ts`, `src/app/api/congress/senate-leadership/route.ts`, `src/app/congress/components/LeadershipRoleSection.tsx`, `src/app/congress/components/SpeakerSection.tsx`, `src/components/party/NppWhipPanel.tsx`

- **Wiki content pipeline is now DB-native (Phase 0)** — Replaced the deprecated `src/lib/wiki/config.ts` + `docs/design` sync flow with a single seed pipeline at `src/lib/seeds/wiki` (aggregated `WIKI_SEED_PAGES` + idempotent `seedWikiPages` function). New `scripts/seed-wiki.ts` (`npm run seed:wiki`, plus `--force` variant) upserts pages non-destructively; pages with admin edits are preserved unless `--force` is passed. New `POST /api/admin/wiki/reseed` and "Reseed wiki" / "Force reseed" buttons in the Admin → Wiki tab drive the same pipeline from the UI. Removed the "Sync all from docs/design" and per-slug "Override" buttons. Deleted `src/lib/wiki/config.ts`, `src/lib/wiki/syncDesignDocs.ts`, `src/lib/wiki/designDocSources.ts`, `/api/admin/wiki/sync-design`, and `/api/admin/wiki/design-source/[slug]`; `src/lib/wiki/searchIndex.ts` and `WikiManagementTab`/`WikiPageTable` switched to DB-only mode. The historical one-shot wiki migration moved to `scripts/archive/migrations/migrate-wiki-to-db.ts`. Content seeding itself (Phases 1–7) and the public toggle flip (Phase 8) follow in subsequent PRs.

## [0.2.8] - 2026-04-23

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Corporate R&D system** — Corporations can now set a daily R&D budget alongside marketing and logistics. The budget feeds an `rdScore` that accumulates via the same log-scaled, diminishing-returns curve as marketing (base 1/turn + 0.65 × ln(1 + budget/100k)), decays 3%/turn, and drives a periodic breakthrough phase. Every 6 turns each corp rolls `probability = min(1, rdScore/200)`; on success one random sector receives a permanent revenue `$inc` — 1–10% for regular corps and 1–5% for extraction corps. Extraction breakthroughs additionally grow the sector's state resource capacity by `rdScore × 50` units, split across every extractable resource in the sector's active strategy supply map weighted by supply rate (so `oil_gas` boosts oil + natural gas; `iron_mining` grows iron only; `standard` diversified spreads across everything). Breakthroughs fire an `rd_breakthrough` notification to the CEO. R&D budget counts against the existing 150% overhead cap and is deducted from liquid capital each turn alongside marketing/logistics/CEO salary. Design calls (Q1–Q6) — per-corp roll, 1% symmetric floor, unbounded state capacity growth, supply-weighted multi-resource split, cap-enforced, mirror-of-marketing UI — are locked and documented in `docs/design/corporations.md` → "R&D Budget & Innovation". Key files: `src/lib/turn/corporation/rdInnovation.ts` (new turn phase + 11 unit tests), `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts` (`RD_*` constants + `calcRdGrowth` / `calcRdScoreAfterTurn`), `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts` (rdBudget deducted from `costsBeforeCeo`), `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/settings/route.ts` (rdBudget validation + cap enforcement), `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts` (returns `rdBudget` / `rdScore` / `rdScoreNetChange`), `src/components/corporation/ceo/CeoBudgetSubtab.tsx` (slider + projection).

- **Financial Transaction Ledger (admin + moderator)** — New `financialTxLog` collection records every money movement on the platform (wires, share trades, bond flows, treasury credits/debits, dividends, salaries, payouts). Admins get a "Financial Ledger" subtab under Admin → Economy with a paginated timeline filterable by subject, type, currency, amount range, turn range, and flagged status, plus a Suspect Alerts tab that groups flagged transactions by subject via a MongoDB `$group` aggregation. Moderators receive a narrower `ModeratorTransactionsTab` under Moderator → Content, with the ability to review/dismiss individual flags (mod audit logged). Shared helpers `buildTxLogFilter` / `queryTxLog` / `queryTxAlerts` live in `src/lib/financialTxLog/queryLogs.ts` so the admin and moderator paths stay in lockstep. Design spec: `docs/design/financial-transaction-log.md`. Key files: `src/components/admin/FinancialLedgerAdminPanel.tsx`, `src/components/moderator/ModeratorTransactionsTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/financial-logs/**`, `src/app/api/moderator/financial-logs/**`.

- **News post deletion (content moderation)** — Moderators can now delete news posts that violate content guidelines; deletion records a mod audit entry. Part of the broader content-moderation toolset alongside the new player banner ad review. `src/app/api/moderator/news/**`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **R&D system shipped unusable prior to this audit** — The R&D score accumulated on the turn but: (1) `rdBudget` was not deducted from corp costs so R&D spend was free money; (2) the currency conversion in the breakthrough phase double-multiplied the revenue boost through the corp's FX rate, inflating JP boosts ~150×; (3) the settings API had no `rdBudget` field, so the whole feature was inaccessible without direct DB writes; (4) corp detail API did not expose `rdScore` or the projected net change; (5) the breakthrough notification used `category: "corporation"` which doesn't match any filter label. All five fixed. The extraction capacity boost was also reworked from a single "highest-supply resource wins" to a supply-rate-weighted split across every extractable the sector's strategy actually produces, and regular-corp breakthroughs now have a 1% minimum boost floor mirroring extraction. Full audit and six locked design calls in `docs/design/corporations.md` → "R&D Budget & Innovation"; resource-capacity policy amendment in `docs/design/resources.md`.

- **Forex macro signs inverted across all four sensitivity terms** — Rate convention is "local currency per internal unit" (higher = weaker), but `computeMacroTarget` in `src/lib/currency/rateCalculation.ts` had signs flipped so higher prime rates / GDP / trade balances were pushing the rate up (weakening the currency) instead of down (strengthening it), and higher inflation was strengthening instead of weakening. `applyVolumePressure` / `computeRateUpdate` had the same inversion: net buy pressure was raising the rate (weakening the bought currency) instead of lowering it. UI surfaces (`ExchangeRatesTable`, forex page, currency detail) also rendered positive vs-base deviation as green when it's actually depreciation (red). All sensitivity signs flipped; `(1 + pressure)` → `(1 - pressure)`; vs-base colors inverted; stock-market `ForexTable` now conditionally inverts by view mode (native-per-internal / cross invert, internal-per-native does not). Every `rateCalculation.test.ts` and `forexTurn.test.ts` case that encoded the wrong convention was fully rewritten with correct math. `src/lib/currency/rateCalculation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`, `src/components/forex/ExchangeRatesTable.tsx`, `src/components/stockmarket/ForexTable.tsx`.

- **`ForexTable` sparkline trend color** — Raw rate increasing always means the local currency weakened regardless of view mode, so `isUp` should map to `error` (red), not `success` (green). `src/components/stockmarket/ForexTable.tsx`.

- **Sector action costs misaligned with actual spend** — Attack-sector, expand-suggestion, and region-economy routes computed display costs via divergent formulas from the turn processor's debit math, showing players a number different from what was charged. Extracted a single `computeSectorActionCost` helper in `src/lib/corporations/marketActionCosts.ts` that every surface and route calls; unit tests cover both attack and expansion paths. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/expand-suggestions/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/attack-sector/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/economy/attack/route.ts`.

- **Corporation displayed income diverged from turn-processor math** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]` computed sector income with a different extraction-resource supply formula than `sectorCalculations.ts` used on the turn, so the Financials tab showed a projection that didn't match what actually hit `liquidCapital`. Extraction-resource effective supply logic consolidated into `src/lib/corporations/extractionResourceSupply.ts` with unit tests; both the display route and the turn phase call the same helper. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`.

- **Corporation Strength budget projections misnormalised** — Marketing and logistics strength projections in `GET /api/corporations/[id]` mixed anchor and local-currency values, so the CEO Budget tab's "projected strength next turn" label drifted from reality after FX moves. Pulled the normalisation into `src/lib/corporations/strengthProjection.ts` with a deterministic conversion and regression tests; budget tab and the API response now agree. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/ceo/CeoBudgetSubtab.tsx`.

- **Legislation: bill and policy displays repaired** — Congress, UK Parliament, JP Diet, and state bill endpoints had drifted from the shared `billEnrichment` contract; category filters, status filters, and enriched display data were missing or wrong on multiple surfaces. `billEnrichment.ts` grew explicit enrichment guarantees; `billProposalLimits.ts` added per-country and per-session caps; `billStatusFilters.ts` + `legislationTypeAliases.ts` were introduced to normalise filter semantics across pages. The policy route was rebuilt end-to-end with type-safe country policy resolution and 255 lines of test coverage. Affected surfaces include `CongressBillsTab`, `JPDietPage`, `UKParliamentPage`, national policy page, `BillCard`, `BillCompactRow`, and `BillListControls`. `src/lib/congress/billEnrichment.ts`, `src/lib/congress/billProposalLimits.ts`, `src/lib/legislationTypeAliases.ts`, `src/lib/legislature/billStatusFilters.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/policy/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/policy/page.tsx`.

- **Reverse-split zero-rounded 1-share holders and blocked the restructure** — Reverse splits previously truncated tiny holders (e.g. a single-share owner in a multi-million-share corp) to zero, tripping the drop-holder invariant and failing the CEO's restructure entirely. Allocation now guarantees every non-float holder with positive input weight receives at least 1 share, stealing from whichever non-float holder holds the most when rounding forces a choice. When the invariant does trip, the error surfaces character / imperial / corporation names instead of raw ObjectIds so CEOs can see which holder broke the math. `src/lib/corporations/shareConsolidation.ts`.

- **Corporation expansion modal overflowed tall viewports** — `ExpandMarketModal` had no height ceiling, pushing the Confirm button below the fold on ~1080p laptop screens with the sector list expanded. Now capped with flex-column + inner scroll so the footer stays anchored. `src/components/corporation/ExpandMarketModal.tsx`.

- **Extraction sector margin skew from unavailable commodities** — Sectors were contributing supply from resources their host state had zero capacity for, skewing the extraction margin modifiers downward. Corp lookups now load `stateResourceCapacity` and filter `effectiveSupply` before passing to margin math; `/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]` route `priceImpact` display is also zeroed for zero-capacity resources. The economy-preview gate on `CountryCard`, `WorldMapSVG`, and `worldMetricHighlight` lost its `status === "active"` filter so beta-status countries can expose economy windows independently of playability. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/app/world/components/CountryCard.tsx`, `src/app/world/components/WorldMapSVG.tsx`.

- **Sentry null guards — `toFixed()` crashes across corp, forex, and budget UI** — Addressed the top recurring crash cluster caused by numeric fields arriving as `null`: `StatusBar.priceChange1h ?? 0` (277 events on `/profile`), `LocWalletStrip.composite ?? 0` + `spreadPercentPoints ?? 0` (32 events), `BudgetDisplay.inflationRate ?? 0` (30 events on `/country/*/budget`), `forex/page` + `forex/[currency]/page` rate finite-check before `.toFixed()` (16 events), and `search/universal` `COMMODITY_LABELS[type] ?? ""` before `.toLowerCase()` (9 events). `src/components/StatusBar.tsx`, `src/components/currency/LocWalletStrip.tsx`, `src/components/BudgetDisplay.tsx`, `src/app/forex/page.tsx`, `src/app/forex/[currency]/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/search/universal/route.ts`.

- **Bond page 500 errors on DB connectivity issues** — `bond/[id]/layout.tsx` `generateMetadata` now wraps DB calls in try/catch so transient connectivity failures return `{}` instead of a 500. Matches the pattern on other metadata generators. `src/app/bond/[id]/layout.tsx`.

- **Market-maker `Math.floor` rounding could take money and return nothing** — `executeMarketMakerTrade` used `Math.floor` on `toAmount`, which in edge cases truncated the converted balance one unit below `costLocal`, causing the buy route to reject the purchase **after** the source-currency debit had already committed. Switched to `Math.round`; regression tests cover the off-by-one case. `src/lib/currency/marketMaker.ts`.

- **StatusBar "Personal Cash" showed home-currency only** — The chip rendered `personalHomeLiquid` (home currency balance) instead of `cashOnHand` (FX-normalised total across every currency held), so multi-currency players saw only part of their cash and perceived money as "vanished" after a cross-currency trade. Now uses `compactInternal(cashOnHand)` to display the true total. `src/components/StatusBar.tsx`.

- **Germany regional map** — Switched `GermanyMapPaths` rendering to `react-simple-maps` + `d3-geo` with updated `de-laender.json`, aligning DE's map with the other countries and fixing layout drift. `src/components/maps/GermanyMapPaths.tsx`, `src/data/maps/de-laender.json`.

- **Player banner ads not rendering on any pages** — `AD_BANNER_PATH_PREFIXES` in `adTrialPaths.ts` was never updated after the multi-country migration moved game content to `/country/[code]/...`. `usePathname()` returns the post-redirect URL, so every country-prefixed page (legislature, executive, elections, parties, stockmarket, metrics, central bank, forex) silently failed `isAdBannerPath` and the ad slot returned null. Added `/country/` as the first entry; also added `/dashboard`, `/campaign`, `/wiki`, and `/approval`. `src/lib/adTrialPaths.ts`.

- **User-uploaded images not displaying** — `bypassNextImageOptimization` now returns `true` for `/api/uploads/*` paths (local file-serving routes) and `*.public.blob.vercel-storage.com` URLs (Vercel Blob CDN). Both store pre-optimized WebP content, so routing them through the Next.js Image Optimization API added overhead and could fail when the server made internal subrequests to itself. With `unoptimized=true`, the browser loads these URLs directly. `src/lib/images/bypassImageOptimization.ts`.

- **Admin/Moderator Grant Resources mislabelled currency** — The Grant Resources panel (Admin Panel > Players > Grant Resources, and the Moderator equivalent) labelled Campaign Funds and Cash on Hand inputs as `$` despite the forex migration storing campaign funds in anchor (₳) units and depositing cash-on-hand in each player's home currency. Inputs now clearly display `₳`, and a live FX-rate conversion preview (`≈ $X USD / £Y GBP / ¥Z JPY / €Z EUR`) renders below each amount so admins can see what each country receives before granting. The admin/moderator route log text was also updated from `$` to `₳` for consistency — backend grant logic was already correctly gated on `isForexEnabled()` and targets `currencyBalances.campaign` / `currencyBalances.personal.<code>` with live-rate conversion for cash-on-hand grants; no behavioural change for grants themselves. `src/components/ResourceGrantManager.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/resources/grant/route.ts`, `src/app/api/moderator/resources/grant/route.ts`.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Moderator banner ad review** — Added a "Banner Ads" subtab under Moderator Panel → Content. Moderators can see all submitted player banner ads (image preview, character name, country, view count, cost, link, status) and permanently delete any ad that violates content guidelines. Deletion records a mod audit log entry. `src/components/moderator/PlayerAdsModTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/moderator/player-ads/route.ts`, `src/app/api/moderator/player-ads/[id]/route.ts`, `src/components/moderator/tabs/ModeratorContentTab.tsx`, `src/components/moderator/tabs/ModeratorTabsConfig.tsx`.

- **Stock-split / reverse-split audit entries in Share History** — New `stock_split` and `reverse_split` `ShareTradeKind` rows are emitted from the CEO restructure route with a full `structureChange` payload (before/after shareholder names, share counts, percents; old/new totalShares, sharePrice, publicFloat; triggering CEO character id). The Share History tab renders split entries as expandable rows showing the pre- and post-split register side by side so players can audit every structural change. `src/lib/db/types/shareTradeHistory.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/shareTradeHistory.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/structureChangeSnapshot.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/consolidate/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/history/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/shares/ShareHistoryPanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/shares/hooks/useShareHistory.ts`.

- **Per-turn shareholder register snapshot** — `CorporationHistory` now carries the corporation's shareholder list and `publicFloat` on every hourly snapshot, so any future share-structure change (or admin intervention) has a trustworthy before-state record. Pre-v0.2.7 snapshots omit the field and readers should treat it as optional. `src/lib/db/types/corporationHistory.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/marketCapSnapshot.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Corporation Portfolio & Wallet showing $0 Net Worth for cash-only corps** — `/api/corporations/[id]/portfolio` returned `totalPortfolioValue = stocks + bonds` with no reference to the corp's `liquidCapital`, and `CorporationPortfolioView` surfaced it as "Total Net Worth" — so a corp with $5M liquid and zero investments showed as worth $0 in the Portfolio & Wallet corp-mode view (`/portfolio?corp=N`). The character-mode flow has always included cash in its Net Worth (`page.tsx:277-279`); corp mode now matches. Added anchor-normalized `cashOnHand` to the API response and rolled it into `totalPortfolioValue`; added a Liquid Capital StatCard + Cash rail item + Cash chart series to `CorporationPortfolioView`. `CorporationPortfolioHistory` snapshots now capture `cashValue` every turn — `snapshotCorporationPortfolioValues` seeds every corp with its liquidCapital rather than only corps with shareholder rows, so cash-only corps stop silently dropping off the chart. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/portfolio/route.ts`, `src/app/portfolio/components/CorporationPortfolioView.tsx`, `src/app/portfolio/page.tsx`, `src/lib/turn/portfolioSnapshot.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/corporationPortfolioHistory.ts`.

- **Stock-split smoothing cooldown — prevent post-split cap collapse/jump** — The share-price formula now uses biased smoothing weights (`0.7 / 0.2 / 0.1` for prev / balance-sheet / income) for `STOCK_SPLIT_PRICE_SMOOTHING_TURNS` (2) turns after any stock split or reverse split, instead of the normal `0.15 / 0.6 / 0.25`. Previously the consolidate route would write a cap-preserving scaled price (e.g., `oldPrice × 10` on a 10:1 reverse), but the next corp turn would overwrite 85% of it with `balanceSheetEquity / newTotalShares` — collapsing #18 Bob's Building Yard from $861M → $213M and similar swings on other split-during-incident corps. The cooldown lets the cap drift gradually across multiple turns instead of snapping in one. The post-bond recompute phase also swaps its smoothing prior from turn-1 history to the just-set `corp.sharePrice` during cooldown — otherwise the recompute would pull the price back to the pre-split value and undo the corp turn's work. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`.

- **Reverse-split wiping corporate and imperial shareholders** — `buildAllocParts` in `src/lib/corporations/shareConsolidation.ts` was keyed on `characterId` only, silently dropping every shareholder row owned by an `imperialCharacterId` or `corporationId`. On any CEO-driven stock split or reverse split the wiped holders' weight was absorbed by the remaining character holders (and public float), while the route's own invariants passed because both the pre-check (counts all holder types) and post-check (sums the allocator's own output) held. Rewrote the allocator to key holders by `(kind, ownerId)` across all three owner types and preserve each row's `avgCostPerShare` scaled by `oldTotal / newTotal`. Reported by players after corps 217 (Harris Industries) and 221 (British Chemical Company) lost corporate positions on reverse split. The consolidate route also gains an `assertShareStructureChangePreservesHolders` defence-in-depth check that rejects any allocation that silently drops a holder. Live-data reparations for the two affected players are in `scripts/migrations/2026-04-22-reverse-split-victim-reparations.ts`. `src/lib/corporations/shareConsolidation.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/shareConsolidation.test.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/consolidate/route.ts`.

- **Null-rate market-maker drain (turns 270–277 downstream incident)** — Downstream of the turn-269 NaN cascade, every auto-convert trade on turns 270–275 and 277 recorded `tradeHistory` rows with `rate: null`. Root cause: the NaN `gdpGrowth` from corrupted `stateMetrics` poisoned `computeMacroTarget` → `computeRateUpdate` → `exchangeRates.rate` became NaN. `executeMarketMakerTrade` (`src/lib/currency/marketMaker.ts`) then computed `crossRate = toRate / fromRate = NaN` and `toAmount = Math.floor(netAmount * NaN) = NaN`. MongoDB's `$inc` applied the source-currency deduction while dropping the NaN destination credit, leaving players with a debited balance and nothing in return. 217 trades across 40 characters were affected; largest single loss was character **Quintus Rockefeller** losing 39.55M GBP when his 39,500-unit Smiths Manufacturing bond matured on turn 271 (~$41.4M USD equivalent). Added rate-validity and cross-rate finiteness guards in `executeMarketMakerTrade` so a malformed `exchangeRates.rate` fails the trade up front instead of silently draining the source balance. Same guard applied to the `forexTurn` limit-order fill path (also did its own `$inc`). Regression tests cover the missing-field, NaN-rate, and zero-rate cases. A one-shot remediation script (`scripts/remediate-null-rate-trades.ts`, idempotent by `tradeHistory.sourceRef`) refunds the debited source currency to each affected character; pre-existing NaN balances are detected and skipped rather than silently swallowed by `$inc`.

- **Inflation pinned to 15% cap across US / UK / JP / DE (commodity-duplicate aftermath)** — `scripts/migrations/heal-nan-cascade-spread.ts` (run live at turn 275, 2026-04-22 11:00 UTC) filtered `commodityPriceHistory` on the field `commodityType` instead of `commodity`. Both sides evaluated to `undefined`, so the query matched every history row; the first finite-`globalPrice` hit (a turn-268 copper snapshot) was then spread over every NaN-contaminated `commodityPrices` row, overwriting their `commodity` field to `"copper"` and their `nationalPrices` with copper's. The `basePrice` field isn't stored in `commodityPriceHistory` so each corrupted row retained its original `basePrice` — producing 20 duplicate `copper` rows whose `nationalPrice / basePrice − 1` ratios ranged from +113% to +56,000%, ballooning `commodityPressure` in `src/lib/turn/inflationRecalc.ts` to 74–88 and pinning inflation at `MAX_INFLATION = 15.0` on every country with national prices populated. Healed via `scripts/migrations/heal-commodity-prices-copper-duplicates.ts` (deletes 20 duplicates, resets the canonical row's `globalPrice` to `basePrice` and clears `statePrices`/`nationalPrices` so `commodityPriceTurn` rebuilds them). Prevention: new unique index on `commodityPrices.commodity` (`scripts/migrations/add-commodity-prices-unique-index.ts`) so a future bulk mis-write throws `E11000` instead of silently duplicating; `heal-nan-cascade-spread.ts` filter corrected to `commodity` with a defensive `good.commodity !== cp.commodity` skip-guard; and `inflationRecalc.ts` now clamps each row's pressure contribution to `[-0.9, 10]` so a single corrupt row can't detonate the average.

- **Sovereign bond self-buy check crash** — Calling `bond.corporationId.toString()` in the corp bond-buy route threw a `TypeError` for sovereign bonds (which have no `corporationId`), returning a misleading 500 error after the capital check passed. Added a null guard so the "cannot buy own bonds" restriction only runs for corporate bonds. `src/app/api/bonds/[bondId]/buy/route.ts`.

- **NaN cascade across corporation financials (turn 269 incident)** — The `growthRate → targetGrowthRate + currentGrowthRate` split (commit `7a7aa9b99`) shipped without running its data migration, leaving 1,337 live sectors with undefined growth fields. `src/lib/turn/gdpGrowth.ts` multiplied `undefined × revenue`, poisoning `stateMetrics.gdpGrowth` with NaN, which cascaded into corporation income → `liquidCapital` → `sharePrice` → `marketCap` on 158 of 169 corps starting turn 269 (2026‑04‑22 06:00 UTC). Added legacy-field fallbacks (`currentGrowthRate ?? growthRate ?? 0`) to `gdpGrowth.ts` (projection + reader), `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts` (sector list + weighted-average), and the three discord-bot + region-economy routes that returned raw `currentGrowthRate`. Healed live data via `scripts/migrations/heal-nan-cascade-turn-269.ts` (sectors back-filled, corp liquidCapital/sharePrice restored from turn-268 `corporationHistory`, NaN history rows deleted) and `scripts/migrations/backfill-nan-cascade-history-268.ts` (flat-copied turn-268 snapshots into turns 269–275 across `corporationHistory`, `corporationPortfolioHistory`, `marketCapHistory`, `wealthListHistory`, `portfolioHistory`; stale upserted `stockExchangeSnapshots` cleared for regeneration). Each backfilled history row is marked `healed: true, healedReason: "nan-cascade-turn-269"`. Character funds were unaffected (verified 0 NaN across 286 characters).

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **FX Intervention (Central Bank Chair)** — Chairs can post a soft-band FX intervention policy (floor + ceiling) that the turn phase defends using `forexRevenue` first, then `reserveBalance`. Intervention rides inside the existing ±5% volume-pressure cap, so it can't move the rate further in a single turn than organic trades already could. Widening is free; narrowing or cancelling requires a 6-turn cooldown (mirrors the prime-rate cadence). Failure infamy (`INTERVENTION_FAILURE_INFAMY = 15`) applies when both reserve pools deplete while the rate is still outside the band, deduped to once per breach cycle via `lastInfamyChargedAtTurn`. Band persists across chair transitions; IMF lock (`chairControlsLocked`) blocks policy changes but not ongoing defense. `src/lib/currency/interventionCalculator.ts`, `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/central-bank/intervention/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/components/CentralBankInterventionTab.tsx`, `src/components/forex/CentralBankPolicyStrip.tsx`.

- **Treasury → FX Reserve Transfer (Finance Minister)** — New cabinet action on the finance-minister office page (US Secretary of the Treasury, UK Chancellor, JP/DE Finance Minister) that moves federal surplus into the central bank's FX reserve pool. Rate-limited to one transfer per turn, capped at 0.5% of annual revenue. Routing is config-driven via `CountryConfig.financeMinisterCabinetId` — future countries wire the action up automatically by setting that field. `src/app/api/country/[code]/cabinet/treasury-transfer/route.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/[positionId]/office/components/FxReserveTransferPanel.tsx`.

- **Admin FX reserve seeding** — One-shot idempotent admin tool (button on `ForexAdminPanel`) that seeds `reserveBalance` for active forex countries at launch. Falls back to per-country flat baselines (US / UK / DE = 3–5B; JP = 500B yen) when trade history is sparse. `src/app/api/admin/forex/seed-reserves/route.ts`.

- **Post-election Confidence Motion (S#17)** — After every lower-chamber general election (regular or snap), if the incumbent PM retained their seat, a 24-hour Confidence Motion is auto-filed in `pmAppointmentVotes` (with `isConfidenceMotion: true`). PM stays in office during the motion. Passes: PM confirmed. Fails (with no alternative seated): PM vacated, gov → pending, 96-turn vacancy clock re-armed, legislation freeze activates. Closes the "incumbent with unfavorable coalition math can cling to office" loophole. `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`, `src/lib/turn/countryPhases.ts`.

- **Legislation freeze during gov formation (S#17)** — While a parliamentary country's `governmentFormations.status === "pending"`, bill proposal / modification / cabinet-action routes return 400, and UK/JP bill-lifecycle turn phases skip entirely. Lifts automatically when a PM is seated. Creates direct political pressure to form a government. `src/lib/api/parliamentaryFreeze.ts`, `src/lib/turn/ukBillLifecycle.ts`, `src/lib/turn/jpBillLifecycle.ts`.

- **VONC-parallel PM nominations (S#17)** — PM appointment votes can now be filed during an active VONC (in addition to the existing "gov is pending" window). If the VONC fails, all parallel appointment votes are cancelled and nominees are notified. Lets opposition parties pre-position successors during no-confidence proceedings. `src/app/api/country/[code]/pm/appoint/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`.

- **Snap election VONC gate** — A sitting Prime Minister can no longer trigger a snap election while an active vote of no confidence exists for the country. Closes a loophole where a PM could preempt an imminent VONC loss by dissolving the chamber. Admin-forced snaps continue to bypass (consistent with `SNAP_ELECTION_LIMIT` and cooldown bypass). `src/lib/turn/snapElection.ts`.

- **Universal Search System** — New `UniversalSearch` component with debounced API calls integrated into the navbar. Search covers corporations, politicians, political parties, and legislation with dropdown results. Search indexes seeding added via `seedSearchIndexes()`. Corporation sector pages updated to use the new search UI. Migration script for sector growth rates included. `src/components/UniversalSearch.tsx`, `src/components/Navbar.tsx`, `src/app/api/search/universal/route.ts`, `src/lib/admin/seed/indexes/search.ts`, `scripts/migrations/migrate-sector-growth-rates.ts`.

- **Three new themes — Cloakroom, Broadsheet, Cold War** — `Cloakroom` is a warm dark (ivory `#f5ecd8` on graphite `#12100e`) with oxblood primary `#9b2a2a` and brass secondary `#c99a3d` — a statesman mood intended for campaign/diplomacy surfaces. `Broadsheet` is an editorial day theme (cream `#f3efe6` paper, deep-ink `#1a1614` text, single crimson `#8c1c1c` accent) that reads like a paper of record. `Cold War` is amber `#f5c46a` on near-black `#0a0906` with salmon primary `#ff7849` and slate-blue secondary `#6fa8dc` — a grown-up sit-room console aesthetic distinct from the existing `retro` CRT theme. All three are wired through `Theme` union, `VALID_THEMES`, `User.theme`, `themeSchema`, and the appearance carousel (now 11 options across 3 carousel pages). `src/app/globals.css`, `src/contexts/ThemeContext.tsx`, `src/lib/db/types/user.ts`, `src/lib/api/schemas/settings.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/AppearanceSection.tsx`.

- **Enhanced Universal Search** — Building on the navbar search introduced earlier in this release, results now include admin-only tabs/subtabs (gated + styled with an animated red glow when present), all 50 US states matched by name or abbreviation, national country pages (US / UK / CA / DE / JP) promoted as prominent results, and a rotating placeholder with clickable example queries (Nicola Sturgeon, General Electric, California, Parliament, Texas, Bond Markets, FTSE 100, Legislation). Vibrant animated glow on the search bar signals when admin-only hits are in the dropdown. `src/components/UniversalSearch.tsx`, `src/app/api/search/universal/route.ts`.

- **Japan map on `/api/map/overview`** — Japan is now included alongside the US/UK/DE overview payload so the landing-page map renders JP regional data without a separate fetch. `src/app/api/map/overview/route.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Snap election PM vacate** — When the Prime Minister or an admin triggers a snap election, the PM is now immediately vacated and the government is unformed. Government status transitions to `pending`, cabinet is cleared, `currentOffice` is cleared on the character and NPP docs, and the 96-turn PM-vacancy clock is re-armed. Brings runtime behavior in line with `docs/design/snap-elections.md`. `src/lib/turn/snapElection.ts`, `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`.

- **Currency display standardised to ₳** — Replaced every hardcoded `$` in party fundraising, donate route, action messages, and Zod validation error strings with `₳` / `formatAmount`. `forexEnabled` now threads through `ActionExecuteRow` batch simulation so per-row previews honour the same currency convention as the row. `src/app/api/parties/**/donate/route.ts`, `src/components/actions/ActionExecuteRow.tsx`, various schema files.

- **Resource capacities rebalanced ~1.5× across US / UK / DE / JP** — State/region resource capacity values scaled up to widen the extraction margin band and give commodity sectors more headroom before saturation. `src/lib/constants/resourceCapacity.ts`.

- **Spread-fee reserve seeding (10% to `reserveBalance`)** — FX spread fee now seeds 10% of every collected fee into the central bank's `reserveBalance` instead of 100% into `forexRevenue`. Builds up FX reserves passively so chair interventions have ammunition without a manual `treasury-transfer` call on day one. `src/lib/currency/spreadFees.ts`.

- **`updateCentralBanks` covers all `FOREX_ACTIVE_COUNTRIES`** — The phase previously hardcoded US / UK / JP and silently dropped DE; now uses a `bulkWrite` upsert across the full forex-active list so Germany's European Central Bank doc refreshes every turn alongside the others. `src/lib/turn/forexTurn.ts`.

- **`TxAlertGroup` gains `flagTypes` aggregation** — Suspect-alert admin view surfaces the union of flag types across a group instead of just the first hit, so moderators see why a subject is flagged without opening every row. `src/lib/db/types/financialTxLog.ts`.

### Security

- **48h new-character cooldown after voluntary retirement** — Retiring a character now pins a cooldown on the user account; they cannot create a replacement character until 48 real hours have elapsed. Closes an abuse vector where players cycled through fresh characters to reset action economies, relocation history, and party-leadership eligibility. `src/app/api/character/retire/route.ts`, `src/app/api/character/create/route.ts`.

- **CEO 5% minimum stake when listing a private offer** — CEOs must retain at least 5% of the corporation's total shares when creating a private listing. Prevents insider dumps where the CEO would list their entire stake the turn before a public disclosure hit and walk away with the liquidity. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/listings/route.ts`.

- **Wire transfer daily cap — ₳5M per 24h (anchor-normalised)** — Character-to-character wires capped at ₳5M per rolling 24-hour window, normalised through anchor units so the limit is uniform across USD / GBP / JPY / EUR senders. Prior behaviour allowed arbitrarily large transfers, enabling fast liquidity flight from compromised or retiring accounts. `src/app/api/character/wire/route.ts`.

### Performance

- **Forex rate caching and parallelised slow page loads** — `/forex`, `/stockmarket`, and country central-bank pages now read exchange rates from a short-lived in-memory cache and issue their DB reads in parallel where they were previously sequential, trimming TTFB on the heavy pages. `src/lib/currency/rateCache.ts`, `src/app/forex/page.tsx`, `src/app/stockmarket/page.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/page.tsx`.

- **Lower-chamber dissolution clears the slate** — When a lower-chamber general election resolves (US `house`, UK `commons` + `snap_commons`, JP `shugiin` + `snap_shugiin`), bills currently in the lower chamber are failed and active VONC votes are cancelled. Bills in the upper chamber (US Senate, UK Lords, JP Sangiin), in JP `cabinet_review`, or already `enrolled` are preserved — those chambers are not dissolved. Snap-trigger-time bill fail now applies the same chamber-scoped rule (previously failed every in-progress bill regardless of chamber). `src/lib/turn/countryPhases.ts`, `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`.

- **Default theme warmed up** — Background shifted from `#09090d` to `#14141c`, card from `#111118` to `#1d1d2a`, card-border from `#1d1d2e` to `#2a2a3d`, and foreground softened from `#f0f0f4` to `#e8e8ee`. Separation between page and card is now legible without the "admin dashboard" tone of the prior cold graphite. `src/app/globals.css`.

- **OLED theme hardened for true black** — Background pinned to `#000` (was `#000` already but with a near-black card that washed out the effect). Card lifted only to `#070710`; `card-border` raised to `#242436` so card edges actually register against the void. Foreground pushed to pure `#ffffff`. Accents re-punched to stay saturated at high contrast: primary `#ff3b3b`, secondary `#4d8cff`, success `#2ee064`, warning `#ffd60a`, error `#ff5a5a`. `src/app/globals.css`.

### Added (docs)

- **Design system documentation** — Three new engineering docs capture the design contract that was previously tribal knowledge: `docs/engineering/design-system.md` (top-level: tenets, tokens, layout, iconography, imagery, anti-patterns, token-addition + theme-addition checklists), `docs/engineering/design-system-themes.md` (role + full token table + failure modes for each of the 11 themes, plus a per-PR testing checklist), `docs/engineering/design-system-components.md` (contracts for Button / Badge family / Input / Label / Modal / Slider / Toast / Tooltip / Skeleton / EmptyState / loading states / ResponsiveTable / MobileSelect / SectionLabel / HeroStatsStrip, with do/don't examples).

- **Design system audit** — `docs/audits/design-system-audit.md` catalogues theme-compatibility regressions across 22 files and prescribes fixes with severity tiers.

### Fixed (design system)

- **`dark:` Tailwind variants removed from 20 files (66 of 68 hits)** — AHD applies themes via `[data-theme="..."]` attribute; it never sets a `.dark` class, so every `dark:bg-gray-800`, `dark:text-gray-300`, etc. was silently dropped. Replaced throughout with semantic utilities: `text-success` / `text-error` / `text-warning` / `text-info` / `text-muted` / `text-foreground`, and `bg-card` / `bg-card-elevated` / `border-card-border` for surfaces. Alert callouts use the 10%/30% tint convention (`bg-<color>/10 border-<color>/30 text-<color>`). Touched files include `TurnoutDisplay.tsx` (19 hits), `StatePageTabsDemographicsAndTurnout.tsx` (10), `AppointSenatorModal.tsx` (8), `VacanciesPanel.tsx` + `ResignButton.tsx` (8), `WikiReviewTab.tsx`, `WikiEditorClient.tsx`, `VoteShareCalculator.tsx`, `HealUKGovernment.tsx`, cabinet `AppointModal.tsx`, and a dozen badge/label spots. The 2 remaining `dark:text-amber-400` hits in `Navbar.tsx` + `MobileMenuPanel.tsx` are deferred to the nav workstream.

- **Modal backdrop theme-aware** — `src/components/ui/Modal.tsx` previously used `bg-black/60`, which was correct on dark themes but a jarring near-opaque curtain on Broadsheet (cream) and Light. Introduced `--modal-backdrop` token per theme (dark: 55–75% black; light: 40–65% of the theme's ink color; USA/Solarized blend their own tints). Modal now reads `var(--modal-backdrop)` inline.

- **Badge solid default no longer pins Default theme muted** — `src/components/ui/Badge.tsx` had `bg-[#6b6b7a]` hard-coded for the `solid` variant of `color="default"`. Replaced with `bg-muted` so the chip adapts per theme (Broadsheet tan `#6b6258`, OLED lighter gray `#7a7a8a`, Cloakroom warm beige `#8a7f6d`, etc.).

- **`bg-white` on game-facing modals/panels replaced** — `AppointSenatorModal.tsx` and `VacanciesPanel.tsx` rendered as white islands on Default/OLED because their `bg-white + dark:bg-gray-800` pair relied on a dead `dark:` variant. Both rewritten to use `bg-card border border-card-border` throughout, with inset rows promoted to `bg-card-elevated`.

- **`AppointSenatorModal` backdrop uses `--modal-backdrop`** — Previously `bg-black bg-opacity-50` inline; now `var(--modal-backdrop)` for theme-aware dimming.

### Changed (design system)

- **`prose-invert` always applied** in `WikiEditorClient.tsx` and `WikiReviewTab.tsx` — prior `dark:prose-invert` never activated, so wiki content rendered as dark-text on all dark themes. Until prose tokens are themed per-theme, always-invert is the correct fallback given 8 of 11 themes are dark.

- **Design system docs updated** — `design-system-themes.md` gets a "restart dev server after adding a theme" gotcha section (Turbopack HMR does not reliably pick up newly-added `[data-theme=...]` blocks). `design-system.md` adds the same step to the "Adding a new theme" numbered checklist.

### Refactored

- **Post-election turn flow reorganized (S#17)** — `runPostElectionGovernmentPhases` no longer calls `resetParliamentaryGovernmentAfterElection` for regular lower-chamber election resolution; instead it opens a Confidence Motion and runs a new lightweight `updateSeatCountsOnly` helper. Reset is still called from the snap-trigger path (where the PM is vacated upfront). Cleanly separates "election-time cleanup" from "PM-vacancy cleanup".

- **Shared `unformGovernmentAndVacatePM` helper** — Extracted the "clear PM + unform gov + clear cabinet + clear `currentOffice` + re-arm vacancy clock" pattern into a single helper in `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`. `resolveParliamentaryNoConfidenceVote` (passed-branch) and `resetParliamentaryGovernmentAfterElection` (no-sitting-PM branch) now call the helper instead of inlining the same logic. Callers retain their own notifications and cycle-specific recalcs. Behavior preserved (regression tests assert identical end state).

- **Character financial data extracted to `src/lib/character/financialData.ts`** — The profile page's inline derivation of donor / campaign / personal / portfolio totals now lives in a shared helper, and the profile page delegates financial strip rendering to `FinancialStrip` directly. Makes the same breakdown reusable from the character page and drops duplicated math. `src/app/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/profile/components/FinancialStrip.tsx`, `src/app/character/[id]/page.tsx`.

---

## [0.2.7] - 2026-04-21

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Foreign Corporate Tax Legislation (PR 2)** — Four new bills unlock the foreign-rate lever at both federal/national and state/regional levels: `us_federal_foreign_corporate_tax_rate` (0–60%, 11 options), `us_state_foreign_corporate_tax_rate` (0–40%), `uk_foreign_corporation_tax` (0–65%), `jp_foreign_corporation_tax` (0–65%). Each bill applies uniformly to all corporations headquartered outside the jurisdiction — no country targeting. Option stances span libertarian-right (free-markets, low rates), progressive-left (redistribution, mid-to-high rates), and populist-right (economic nationalism, high rates with negative social modifier) to reflect the real political coalitions around foreign capital policy.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Corporate Tax Schema Split (PR 1)** — Split `FederalTaxRates.corporateTax` / `StateTaxRates.corporateTax` and their `corporateProfits` tax-base counterparts into `domesticCorporateTax` + `foreignCorporateTax` on federal and state budget docs. Per-sector tax selection in the corp-turn simulation now branches on `corp.countryId === sector.countryId` — domestic corps pay the domestic rate, foreign corps pay the foreign rate — at both tiers. Bond coupon income always uses the domestic rate (always domestic from the corp's perspective). Existing `us_federal_corporate_tax_rate`, `us_state_corporate_tax_rate`, `uk_corporation_tax`, `jp_corporation_tax`, and `de_corporate_tax_rate` legislation bills renamed to `*_domestic_*` ids; foreign rate defaults to the domestic rate on day one (migration: `scripts/migrations/splitCorporateTaxDomesticForeign.ts`). Foreign legislation bills will ship in PR 2.

### Refactored

- **Corporation turn tax calc** — Four rate lookup maps (`domesticCorpTaxRateByCountry`, `foreignCorpTaxRateByCountry`, plus state-level equivalents) replace the prior two in `CorporationLookups`. Per-corp history gains parallel `taxPaidByCountry{Domestic,Foreign}` / `taxPaidByState{Domestic,Foreign}` breakdowns alongside the existing combined totals. UI surfaces (national budget, state budget, state metrics, corp financials, corp charts, policy page) display the two rates separately with pre-migration fallbacks for historical rows.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Share Trade History** — New `shareTradeHistory` collection plus `GET /api/corporations/[id]/shares/history` endpoint paginated 25/page, newest first. Every share-movement code path (CEO issuance, market buy/sell, limit-order immediate + turn-processor fills, peer order fills, private listing offer accepts, hostile-takeover squeeze-outs) writes to it via the new `recordShareTrade` helper. `SharesTab` now renders two sub-tabs, `Market Overview` (existing content unchanged) and `Share History` (paginated list with event badges, from/to links, ₳ price + total, turn stamp). Correction rows are intentionally omitted for the Corp 16 reversal — history starts empty and accumulates forward trades only. `src/lib/db/types/shareTradeHistory.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/shareTradeHistory.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/history/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/shares/ShareHistoryPanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/shares/hooks/useShareHistory.ts`.

- **Player Banner Ad System** — Players can purchase a banner ad slot at `/player-ads`. Cost is 25% of the average active character LC balance, capped to one submission per 24 hours. `AdSlot` renders ads in the site footer across ad-eligible pages, showing the lowest-viewCount active ad first to equalize exposure. Admin gains a "Banner Ads" sub-tab under Players for list, toggle, and remove. API: `GET/POST /api/player-ads`, `GET /api/player-ads/next`, `POST /api/player-ads/[id]/view`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/admin/player-ads/[id]`. Images stored via Vercel Blob (disk fallback), resized to 970×250 max at quality 82. LC deducted atomically with conditional `findOneAndUpdate`. `src/app/player-ads/`, `src/app/api/player-ads/`, `src/components/AdSlot.tsx`, `src/components/admin/PlayerBannerAdsTab.tsx`, `src/lib/db/types/playerBannerAd.ts`.

- **Germany Economy Preview Mode** — New `economyPreview` flag on `countryGameStates` exposes Germany's map, metrics, stock market, central bank, budget, and forex to non-admin players while keeping elections, legislature, parties, politicians, and executive hidden. Country layout reads `x-pathname` from the Vercel proxy header to classify routes and apply the access gate. Admin panel gains an Economy Preview toggle (visible only when country players are disabled). `src/lib/countryAccess.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/layout.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/settings/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/CountryOverviewCard.tsx`.

- **EUR Forex** — Euro added to `FOREX_ACTIVE_CURRENCIES`/`FOREX_ACTIVE_COUNTRIES` with initial rate 0.92 (EUR/₳). `DE` added to `ECONOMIC_BASELINES`. Exchange rate document seeded; forex turn will maintain it from next run. `src/lib/constants/currencies.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`.

- **Banner Ad Composer** — Inline player ad upload in the news post modal via a tab toggle between text post and banner ad, showing live cost and balance info. `src/components/news/BannerAdComposer.tsx`, `src/app/news/NewsPageClient.tsx`.

- **`targetGrowthRate`/`currentGrowthRate` split** — `Sector.growthRate` replaced by two fields: `targetGrowthRate` (CEO-set target) and `currentGrowthRate` (smoothed actual). `currentGrowthRate` ticks toward `targetGrowthRate` at 0.5%/turn each turn processing run, so instant growth-rate swings cannot be used to spike NPV or stock-price snapshots. All economic calculations (GDP, stock snapshots, bond credit, bond-default) use `currentGrowthRate`. Migration `scripts/migrations/add-growth-rate-fields.ts` back-fills both fields from the legacy `growthRate`. Key files: `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/gdpGrowth.ts`, `src/lib/turn/stockExchangeSnapshot.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/corporateCredit.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/corporateBondDefault.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Share price/market cap discrepancy between top bar and Market Overview** — The corporation hero displayed `sharePrice` via anchor-normalized `toInternalFrom(local, liquidCurrencyCode)` → `formatPrice(anchor, code)`, but `MarketOverviewPanel`, `SelfIssuancePanel`, `PublicIssuancePanel`, and `ShareIssuanceModal` passed the raw LOCAL value to format helpers that expect ₳ — treating LOCAL as ₳ and then converting again, under-displaying every sharePrice-derived value by the FX rate (≈10% off for USD, ≈25% for GBP/EUR, ≈7× for JPY). A new `useLocalCurrency(code)` hook in `src/hooks/useLocalCurrency.ts` encapsulates the LOCAL → ₳ → wallet-pref pivot so call sites render `fmtLocalPrice(corporation.sharePrice)` without touching `toInternalFrom`. All four panels migrated; `dilutedPrice`, `ceoPricePerShare`, `ceoTotalCost`, and share-issuance proceeds now honor the viewer's Wallet display preference consistently with the hero. `src/hooks/useLocalCurrency.ts`, `src/components/corporation/shares/MarketOverviewPanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/shares/SelfIssuancePanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/shares/PublicIssuancePanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/shares/ShareIssuanceModal.tsx`.

- **CEO self-issuance insufficient-funds check mismatched currencies** — `ShareIssuanceModal` compared `ceoTotalCost` (corp LOCAL) against `liquidPersonalInHome` (viewer HOME) — a silent mismatch whenever corp currency ≠ CEO home that could block affordable purchases or admit unaffordable ones. `maxCeoSharesByFunds` divided HOME balance by LOCAL price and the "Short by" banner subtracted mixed units for the same reason. All three now pivot through ₳ to mirror the server-side `/shares/self-issue` math (`LOCAL → ₳`, `balance → ₳`, compare in ₳). The "Spendable liquid" line drops the `(homeCurrency)` annotation since the value now renders in the viewer's Wallet preference. `src/components/corporation/shares/ShareIssuanceModal.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/SharesTab.tsx`.

- **Share purchase price display for foreign-currency corps** — `BuyFromFloatPanel` and the at-market mode of `SharePurchaseModal` used `sharePrice` (stored in corp home currency post-v0.2.6) directly as ₳, inflating the displayed cost by the FX rate (≈132× for JPY corps). The server-side charge was always correct. Also fixed: initial limit-price default, limit-vs-market fill indicator comparisons, and three orderbook fill-cost displays. `src/components/corporation/shares/BuyFromFloatPanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/shares/SharePurchaseModal.tsx`.

- **`pricePerShareAnchor` not converted to anchor currency** — Private-listing offer accept route and the turn-processor share-order fill computed `pricePerShareAnchor` from the local price without FX conversion, understating recorded trade costs for non-₳ corps. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/listings/[listingId]/offers/[offerId]/accept/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/shareOrders.ts`.

- **Turn-processor share fills missing cost basis** — `fillPendingShareOrders` now stamps `avgCostPerShare` on brand-new shareholder entries it pushes, matching `/api/corporations/[id]/shares/buy` behavior. Previously, limit buy orders filled during turn processing created shareholder rows with no cost basis, so portfolio PnL displayed `—` for those holdings. Also threads `turn` into the function for future audit hooks. `src/lib/turn/corporation/shareOrders.ts`.

- **Self-deleted CEOs no longer orphan corporation shares** — `DELETE /api/auth/delete-account` and `POST /api/admin/users/delete` previously deleted the `characters` row without cascading to corporations, so the deleted character's shareholder entry and CEO seat stayed pointing at a hard-deleted `_id` (e.g. Corp #116 held 10.2M orphaned shares under a ghost CEO). Both delete routes now call a new `cascadeCharacterDeletion` helper that, for each corp the character holds shares in, `$pull`s the entry and `$inc`s `publicFloat` by the exact share count (CAS-guarded on `shares` to defuse concurrent trades), marks `ceoVacant` on any corp the character was CEO of (mirroring `vacateCeoForBannedUser`, also `$unset`s `ceoId` / `userId`), and `$unset`s `pendingCeoCharacterId` on any corp that had offered the deleted character the CEO seat. One-off cleanup `scripts/migrations/release-corp-116-orphan-shares.ts` returned Corp #116's 10,236,229 shares to public float; the generic `scripts/migrations/heal-ghost-shareholders.ts` pass released 41,152,696 additional orphan shares across 11 other corps and vacated 6 un-vacated ghost CEO seats (backlog of prior self-deletes). Key files: `src/lib/account/cascadeCharacterDeletion.ts` (new), `src/lib/account/cascadeCharacterDeletion.test.ts` (new), `src/app/api/auth/delete-account/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/users/delete/route.ts`, `scripts/migrations/release-corp-116-orphan-shares.ts` (new), `scripts/migrations/heal-ghost-shareholders.ts` (new).

- **Hostile takeover blocked against insolvent targets** — `POST /api/corporations/[id]/hostile-takeover` now rejects takeovers when `target.liquidCapital < 0` (HTTP 400) and clamps any negative `targetCashAnchor` to zero as defense-in-depth — the raw negative balance was previously applied as a `$inc`, draining the acquiring corp's cash by `|target.liquidCapital| × FX rate`. The catch block now reverses both the minority-payout debit AND the cash-transfer credit (previously only the debit was refunded on partial failure, leaking the credit). A heal script corrected Corp #71 (Her Majesty's Arsenal), which lost ~141.5B JPY on 2026-04-21 via a Bank of America takeover while at `liquidCapital = −$851M USD`. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/hostile-takeover/route.ts`, `scripts/migrations/heal-corp-71-hostile-takeover-bug.ts`.

- **Share Purchase modal clipped on short mobile viewports** — The Buy/Sell Shares panel exceeded 100dvh with no outer height cap, pushing the Cancel/Buy footer below the fold with no way to reach it. Rewritten with flex-column pattern: header/mode-picker/footer `shrink-0`, body `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`, panel capped at `calc(100dvh-2rem)`. `src/components/corporation/shares/SharePurchaseModal.tsx`.

- **Next.js 16 production build failure — duplicate middleware/proxy** — `src/middleware.ts` and `src/proxy.ts` cannot coexist in Next.js 16 ("Both middleware file and proxy file are detected"), breaking Vercel builds. Folded the `x-pathname` header injection from `middleware.ts` into `proxy.ts` via a passthrough helper, then deleted `middleware.ts`. `src/proxy.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Corp 16 shareholder correction** — One-shot migration (`scripts/migrations/reverseCorp16MysteryTrades.ts`) reversed all 7 non-CEO share transactions on AURORA Group: refunded each buyer in their home currency at 1.25× the ₳ notional they paid (25% goodwill bonus), returned all 93 shares to the CEO (KIMI ANTONELLI), and cleared the stale `lastShareIssuance` stamp. A companion script (`scripts/migrations/purgeCorp16CorrectionHistory.ts`) removed the 7 audit rows the initial run wrote so Share History starts empty per operator direction.

- **Cross-country corp relocation converts treasury currency** — HQ moves that cross a currency boundary now convert `liquidCapital`, `sharePrice`, `marketingBudget`, `logisticsBudget`, `ceoSalary`, and all owned-sector `revenue` + `currentGrowthCost` from the old currency to the new via the spot FX rate. Open share orders and listings are cancelled and refunded before the conversion (escrow denominated in old currency). Existing bonds retain their original `currencyCode` per the "denomination fixed at issuance" contract. Applies to all three HQ-move paths (player `/relocate`, combined `/relocate-with-corp`, admin `/hq`). See `src/lib/corporations/convertCorpCurrency.ts`.

- **Adsterra removed; platform switches to player-run ads** — `AdsterraBanner` component deleted. `AdSlot` now renders player-submitted ads only. Patreon ad preference collapsed from 3 options (ad-free / player-only / all-ads) to 2 (ad-free / player ads). Ad display area uses a compact bordered footer card (`max-height 80px`). Ad coverage extended to `/profile`, `/portfolio`, `/stockmarket`, `/actions`, `/corporation`, `/notifications`. `src/components/AdSlot.tsx`, `src/components/settings/PatreonBenefitsSection.tsx`, `src/lib/adTrialPaths.ts`.

- **Terms of Service / Privacy Policy update** — ToS gains a new content discretion notice (the game is not age-restricted, but as an open online environment players may encounter user-generated content and should exercise discretion); sections renumbered; effective date updated to April 21 2026. Privacy Policy removes the Adsterra advertising cookies section and updates the third-party table. Cookie consent removes the ad-network filter. `src/app/terms/page.tsx`, `src/app/privacy/page.tsx`, `src/components/CookieConsent.tsx`.

- **ECB rename** — Germany's central bank renamed from Deutsche Bundesbank to European Central Bank. `sharedBankId?` stub added to `CentralBankConfig` for future Eurosystem multi-country support. `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`.

### Refactored

- **`capacityMultiplier` added to `CommodityFlow`, world map enhancements** — `CommodityFlow` gains a `capacityMultiplier` field for resource extraction scaling. World map (`WorldMapSVG`, `CountryCard`, `MapTooltip`, `StatusBadge`) gains capacity-based country highlights and tooltip improvements. `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/types.ts`, `src/app/world/components/`, `src/lib/turn/gdpGrowth.ts`.

