## [0.2.6] - 2026-04-19

Corporate economy money fields migrated from ₳ (anchor) storage to each corp's native currency (`marketingBudget`, `logisticsBudget`, `ceoSalary`, `sharePrice`, sector revenue / growth cost, history fields). Bonds gain an explicit `currencyCode` stamped at issuance. Government budgets were already stored in country-local currency and do not require migration — only documentation and display paths were updated. Cross-entity aggregation anchor-normalizes; UI renders via wallet preference (internal / home / pinned / local). Two atomic migration scripts ship with the release — see `scripts/migrations/README.md`.

---

## [0.2.6] - 2026-04-20

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Combined character + corporation relocation** — CEOs can now move their corporation along with them when relocating from a region page. The "Relocate here" button shows a three-option chooser (`Cancel` / `Relocate & Abandon Corporation` / `Relocate & Move Corporation`) with inline cost, cash/bond payment, and disabled-state tooltips reporting the specific failing constraint (insufficient Liquid Capital, bond cooldown turns remaining, leverage limit exceeded). Imperial CEOs' corporations auto-move with the character at no cost. New endpoint `POST /api/character/relocate-with-corp` orchestrates the transaction via `performRelocation` with a new `skipCeoResignForCorpId` option so the CEO role is preserved. `src/components/RelocateButton.tsx`, `src/app/api/character/relocate-with-corp/route.ts`, `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`.
- **Cross-country HQ relocation** — CEO Office → Administration → Relocate Headquarters now supports moves to any country. Out-of-country moves cost **2× the base 7% of market cap** (14%). The form has a new Country selector above the existing State/Region selector, a "Cross-country move — cost doubled" badge on the cost summary, and an amber warning when the CEO does not reside at the destination. `CROSS_COUNTRY_RELOCATION_MULTIPLIER = 2` in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`. `src/components/corporation/ceo/CeoAdminSubtab.tsx`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/relocate/route.ts`.
- **Shared relocation helpers** — New `computeCorpRelocationCost` (cost math) and `previewRelocationBond` + `issueRelocationBond` (bond preflight + insertion) helpers de-duplicate logic across corp-only and combined relocation routes. `src/lib/corporations/relocationCost.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/issueRelocationBond.ts`.
- **`corpRelocation` preview field on `GET /api/character/relocate`** — Returns the active CEO corp's `corpId`, `corpName`, `currentHqState`, `currentCountryId`, `isImperialCeo`, `marketCap`, `liquidCapitalAnchor`, `bondCooldownTurnsRemaining`, and `bondLeverageAvailable` so the region-page dialog can render without extra round-trips. `src/app/api/character/relocate/route.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **HQ relocation CEO auto-vacate** — If a HQ relocation leaves the CEO's `homeState` different from the new HQ state, the CEO seat is auto-vacated (`ceoVacant: true`, `ceoId` / `userId` unset). Previously the corp-only route hard-blocked such moves. The UI warns the player before submission; the action is no longer blocked. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/relocate/route.ts`.
- **"Cash on hand" → "Liquid Capital" relabel** — Corporate-funded payment option on the CEO Office relocation form now reads "Liquid Capital" to distinguish it from player personal cash. `src/components/corporation/ceo/CeoAdminSubtab.tsx`.

- **Alt / bot mitigation — registration controls + leadership cooldown** — Four additive admin gates against alt-account abuse of party elections. (1) A master **Registration** kill-switch on Admin → Dashboard → Registration Controls closes every new-user path simultaneously (`/api/auth/register`, Google OAuth callback new-user branch, Discord OAuth callback new-user branch). (2) The same card hosts an **IP collision check** toggle (disabled by default) that, when on, blocks any registration whose client IP matches an existing user's `registrationIp`. (3) A new **IP Bans** sub-tab under Admin → Players manages a `bannedIps` collection with manual ban rows (always enforced) and allowance rows that carry a `maxAccounts` cap and permit multi-account sign-up from verified shared locations. Collisions are resolved via an inline read-only status strip that links back to the Dashboard toggle. (4) A 24-hour **new-character cooldown** anchored on `max(user.createdAt, character.createdAt, character.partyJoinedAt)` blocks enter-candidacy and cast-vote on national party leadership, national committee, and state/regional party leadership routes (`parties/[id]/election/{enter,vote}`, `parties/[id]/committee/{enter,vote}`, `region/[id]/party/[partyId]/election/{enter,vote}`). The new shared helpers live at `src/lib/auth/newCharacterCooldown.ts` (pure function) and `src/lib/auth/registrationGate.ts` (DB-aware). Normalized IP comparison via `src/lib/utils/ipNormalize.ts` (collapses IPv4-mapped IPv6, rejects the `"unknown"` sentinel). Admin mutations are logged via `createAdminLog` with new `AdminLogAction` values. New sparse index on `users.registrationIp` and unique index on `bannedIps.ip`. Key files: `src/components/admin/RegistrationControlsPanel.tsx`, `src/components/admin/IpBansTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/registration/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/ip-collision-check/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/ip-bans/{route,[id]/route,[id]/allow/route}.ts`.

- **Propose trade bills with tariff provisions** — Players in all five countries can now propose trade bills from the Bills tab. Selecting `Category = trade` in the Propose Bill modal replaces the Policy Type panel with a `TariffProvisionEditor` that lets the sponsor add up to 3 tariff rows, each with scope (economy-wide / sector / origin-country), a conditional target field, and a 0–100% rate slider. The origin-country dropdown pulls from `/api/game/countries` and excludes the proposing country. `POST /api/country/[code]/legislature/bills` now handles `type: "tariff"` provisions at parity with `/api/congress/bills` (previously silently dropped them and would crash on tariff-only bills). A new `checkDuplicateTariffProvisions` helper blocks two active bills from targeting the same `(scopeType, target)` and is applied in both national bill-proposal routes. Corporation-scoped tariffs remain admin-only for now. Key files: `src/components/bills/TariffProvisionEditor.tsx`, `src/components/bills/tariffProvisionTypes.ts`, `src/lib/congress/billProposalLimits.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/legislature/bills/route.ts`, `src/app/api/congress/bills/route.ts`, `src/app/congress/components/ProposeBillModal.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/legislature/UKParliamentPage.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/legislature/JPProposeBillModal.tsx`.

- **Presidential campaign contributions** — Candidates and campaign managers can now contribute personal Campaign Funds directly to their presidential campaign from the Campaign Manager page (`/campaign/[id]`). National party chair, vice chair, and treasurer can authorize contributions from the National Party Treasury to their party's presidential nominee. Both flows go through `POST /api/campaigns/[id]/donate`, are recorded in `Campaign.donationLog`, and emit `fund_event` activity log entries (treasury entries now include `donorRole`). Minimum contribution is $1,000; maximum is the donor's available balance.
- **Officer redirect on Campaign Manager gateway** — Party chair / vice chair / treasurer who are neither candidate nor campaign manager are now routed from `/campaign` to their party's presidential nominee's campaign page so they can authorize treasury contributions without spelunking.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Navbar — Campaign Manager link visibility** — The "Campaign Manager" link is now hidden from users with no presidential‑campaign role. Visible to admins, candidates in active presidential elections, campaign managers of active presidential campaigns, and chair / vice chair / treasurer of a party with an active presidential candidate. Driven by a new `canSeeCampaignManager` flag on `/api/client-nav`.
- **Treasury donation authorization** — `POST /api/campaigns/[id]/donate` now accepts treasury contributions from the chair, vice chair, or treasurer (was chair only) and additionally enforces a same‑party check: the donating party (sequentialId + countryId) must match the campaign's party-of-record.

### Removed

- **Misleading "Candidate Funds 10%/turn" line in Campaign Manager budget panel** — The Budget panel previously showed a "Candidate Funds: 10% of personal funds per turn" line, but `processCampaignTurn` never actually transferred any character funds into the campaign. With manual contribution controls now available, the orphaned line is gone from `BudgetSection`, the `/api/campaigns/[id]` and `/api/elections/[id]/campaigns` responses, the `CampaignData.budget.income` type, and the integration test that asserted the fictional contribution.
- **Misleading "Political Influence × $500" and "Fundraising Ops × $10,000" lines in Budget panel** — Both lines fabricated values not used in `processCampaignTurn` (which only adds `FUNDRAISING_INCOME[fundraisingLevel]`, a non-linear lookup table where L5 = $200k, L10 = $5M — not the $50k / $100k the old display implied). The income block now collapses to a single "Fundraising Income" row sourced from the same `calculateCampaignIncome` value the turn processor uses. `CampaignData.budget.income` is reduced to `{ total: number }`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Presidential campaigns could bleed into unbounded negative balance** — `processCampaignTurn` in `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.ts` applied `netIncome = income − maintenance` via MongoDB `$inc` with no floor. When a campaign's per-turn Ground Game + Media Spending maintenance exceeded its Fundraising income, `campaigns.funds` drained indefinitely; one US presidential candidate reached `-$3,461,317` with L5/L5/L5 levels before the fix. The turn processor now calls a new `computeAutoDowngrade` helper (`src/lib/campaigns/autoDowngrade.ts`) that demotes the most expensive current-level maintenance tier one step at a time — tie goes to Media Spending — until `funds + income ≥ maintenance` or both tiers hit level 0. Demotions are recorded to `activityHistory` as `downgrade` entries with `reason: "insolvency"`. Passive favorability effects for that turn still use pre-downgrade levels (one last gasp); the maintenance deduction uses post-downgrade levels. The `CampaignActivity.type` union was extended to `"upgrade" | "downgrade"` and gained an optional `reason` field. `CampaignTurnResults` now includes `campaignsAutoDowngraded`. A one-shot migration at `scripts/migrations/autoDowngradeInsolventCampaigns.ts` applies the same policy to existing `funds < 0` campaigns (does not heal the negative balance — the campaign still owes what it overspent, it just stops draining). Design doc: `docs/design/campaign-strategy.md` → "Insolvency & Auto-Downgrade". Key files: `src/lib/campaigns/autoDowngrade.ts` (new), `src/lib/campaigns/autoDowngrade.test.ts` (new), `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.test.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/campaign.ts`, `scripts/migrations/autoDowngradeInsolventCampaigns.ts` (new).

- **Campaign Manager UI ignored the viewer's display currency preference** — `ResourceOverview`, `BudgetSection`, `ActivityLog`, `OperationsSection`, `CanvassingPanel`, and the `/elections/[id]` page's `CampaignsListPanel` / `CampaignManagerTab` printed every fund value as raw internal (`$20,000`) with a hardcoded dollar sign — even for viewers who had pinned their preference to JPY/GBP/internal or were living under a non-USD home currency. `OperationsSection` pulled the home-currency symbol correctly but displayed the unconverted internal number next to it (e.g. "¥50,000" where "¥50,000" was actually 50,000 internal, not 50,000 yen). Every surface now routes through `useCurrency().formatAmount` / `formatFull`, so campaign totals, upgrade costs, maintenance, activity log entries, canvassing costs, and election-page campaign panels convert and symbol-prefix consistently with the rest of the site. Net-income lines use a small `formatSigned` helper so negative balances render as "−$9,500" rather than the "$-9,500" formatFull produces. Key files: `src/app/campaign/[id]/components/ResourceOverview.tsx`, `.../BudgetSection.tsx`, `.../ActivityLog.tsx`, `.../OperationsSection.tsx`, `.../CanvassingPanel.tsx`, `src/app/elections/[id]/components/CampaignsListPanel.tsx`, `src/app/elections/[id]/components/CampaignManagerTab.tsx`.

- **Campaign endpoints leaked ineligible and cross-country campaigns to the navbar** — `GET /api/campaigns/mine` returned any campaign attached to the user (driving the "My Campaign" link in `NationDropdown`) without checking whether the underlying election was Campaign Manager-eligible, so a pre-cleanup JP shugiin campaign still surfaced. The same endpoint's `partyCampaign` lookup matched only on `sequentialId`, which collides across countries — a JP player whose party was sequential ID 6 could see a US party 6's presidential campaign as their "party campaign". `GET /api/campaigns/[id]` served any campaign by id, so direct URL navigation bypassed the creation gate. Added defense-in-depth: `/api/campaigns/mine` now filters to eligible elections AND requires the party campaign's election country to match the viewer's character country; `/api/campaigns/[id]` returns 404 when the campaign's election is ineligible (or orphaned), with an admin bypass so moderators can still inspect legacy / orphan docs by ID for cleanup. Key files: `src/app/api/campaigns/mine/route.ts`, `src/app/api/campaigns/[id]/route.ts`.

- **Sector market totals appeared to shrink turn-over-turn for pinned-preference viewers** — Sector-level "Market Position" panels on `/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]` and the state economy tab (`StateEconomy`) formatted `totalMarket`, `ownedRevenue`, and `unownedRevenue` through the viewer's `displayCurrencyPreference`. When that preference pinned to a currency whose forex rate was drifting (e.g. USD weakening vs the internal anchor ~1% per turn), the displayed market size appeared to shrink even when the underlying state economy was stable or growing — players read this as "unowned sectors shedding like vacant-CEO corps." Added `formatAmountIn` / `formatAmountChipIn` helpers (backed by a pure `resolveForcedDisplay` module) that force-format in a specified currency, ignoring viewer preference. `MarketPositionPanel` and `StateEconomy` now render every economy-anchored value (`totalMarket`, `ownedRevenue`, `unownedRevenue`, each owner's sector revenue) in the sector's home-country currency, with a dashed-underline tooltip explaining the convention. Wallet-transactional values (growth-adjust cost, split cost, attack cost, estimated capture into your treasury) keep the viewer's preference. `GET /api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]` now returns `sector.countryId` so the UI can resolve the sector currency without a round-trip. Key files: `src/lib/currency/resolveForcedDisplay.ts` (new), `src/lib/currency/resolveForcedDisplay.test.ts`, `src/contexts/CurrencyContext.tsx`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/route.ts`, `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/sections/MarketPositionPanel.tsx`, `src/components/state/StateEconomy.tsx`.

- **Amount inputs silently divided by the wrong currency rate for pinned-preference users** — `useCurrency().toInternal()` always divided by the player's home-country rate, regardless of `displayCurrencyPreference`. A JP player with preference pinned to "USD" saw their `character.funds` formatted as "$156K" (USD rate 1.11), typed "50000" thinking USD, and the client divided by the JPY rate (≈108.59) → ~460 internal units. Contribution attempts hit the $1,000-minimum wall, transfers on Party Treasury / fund-transfer / influence-interact / share-limit cards were likewise scaled wrong. Extracted a pure `resolveSourceRate(preference, homeCurrencyCode, rates)` helper that mirrors `resolveDisplay`: "internal" → 1, "home" / "local" → home-country rate, pinned CurrencyCode → that currency's rate, with explicit fallbacks. `toInternal` now uses this helper, so typed amounts round-trip through the same currency the UI is showing. `inputSymbol` updated in lockstep so pinned-preference inputs prefix the correct symbol (USD pref shows "$", not the home "¥"). Key files: `src/lib/currency/resolveSourceRate.ts` (new), `src/lib/currency/resolveSourceRate.test.ts`, `src/contexts/CurrencyContext.tsx`.

- **Campaign Manager spawning for non-US-presidential races** — `POST /api/elections/[id]/enter` created a `Campaign` doc for every election candidacy — JP shugiin, UK commons, US senate / house / governor — leaking the Campaign Manager page, `/campaign/[id]`, the navbar "My Campaign" link, and ground-game / media maintenance drains into contexts the system was never designed for. Stray non-presidential campaign docs were also firing the media-spending and opposition-research favorability deltas in `processCampaignTurn`, giving a handful of senate / governor / shugiin players ongoing favorability boosts the design never intended. Creation is now gated by a new `isCampaignEligibleElection(election)` helper that requires `electionType === "president"` AND the election's country forms its executive by direct election. Gate is applied identically in `POST /api/elections/[id]/enter`, `POST /api/admin/elections/[id]/start-general`, and `POST /api/admin/elections/[id]/place-candidate`. `processCampaignTurn` additionally gates media-spending, opposition-research, and travel-presence favorability passes on `electionType === "president"` as defense-in-depth so any stray campaign doc (admin placement, partial cleanup, future bug) cannot resurrect the effects. Cleanup script `scripts/migrations/dropNonPresidentialCampaigns.ts` drops every pre-existing ineligible or election-orphaned campaign doc (run with `--apply` to execute, `--live` to target the live DB). `docs/design/campaign-manager.md` updated to describe the scope. Key files: `src/lib/campaigns/isCampaignEligible.ts` (new), `src/lib/campaigns/isCampaignEligible.test.ts`, `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.test.ts`, `src/app/api/elections/[id]/enter/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/elections/[id]/start-general/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/elections/[id]/place-candidate/route.ts`.

- **Corporation share-order cancel button missing from Open Orders panel** — Orders marked `isMine` in the Open Orders panel on `/corporation/[id]` previously showed a "(You)" tag but no cancel affordance, forcing users into the Trade modal to cancel. The panel now renders an inline Cancel button (wired to the existing `useShareTrading.handleCancelOrder`) on both buy and sell sides for any order where the placing character matches the viewer. Handles personal and corporation-placed orders identically (order.characterId is the placing CEO on corp orders). Key files: `src/components/corporation/shares/OpenOrdersPanel.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/SharesTab.tsx`.

- **Share-structure change could be blocked indefinitely by other players' open orders** — `POST /api/corporations/[id]/shares/consolidate` previously returned 400 with "Cancel all open share orders for this corporation before changing share structure." whenever any open `shareOrder` existed, but the CEO had no authority to cancel third-party orders — a griefer could park a stale limit order to block any restructure. The route now auto-cancels every open order on the target corp before the restructure runs, refunding buy-side escrow (to placer corp `liquidCapital` or character wallet, home-currency converted) and restoring corp sell-side reserved shares via `creditSharesToCorp`. Response now includes `cancelledOpenOrders: number` and the Stock-split toast surfaces the count. The cancel+refund logic is extracted into a shared helper `cancelShareOrderAndRefund(db, order)` so the DELETE endpoint and the consolidation path use identical semantics. Key files: `src/lib/corporations/cancelShareOrder.ts` (new), `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/consolidate/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/orders/[orderId]/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/shares/hooks/useShareTrading.ts`, `docs/design/corporations.md`.

- **Player favorability bounced back to ~50 when attacks drove it to 0** — `simpleInfluence.ts` used `target.favorability || 50` on the `/api/characters/[id]/influence` GET and POST paths, which treated the perfectly valid value `0` as "missing" and substituted the 50 default. The Interact panel therefore displayed 50 for any target whose favorability had been attacked down to 0, and the very next Support/Attack/Barnstorm action wrote `max(0, 50 - 1) = 49` (or `51`) back to the DB — actively corrupting a bottomed-out target up to 49 on the next click. Swapped the three buggy fallbacks to `?? 50` so only genuinely missing values (null/undefined) fall through to the default; real zeros now pass through as zeros on both display and write. Heal script `scripts/migrations/healKarlKarlsonFavorability.ts` resets the one reported victim (Karl Karlsson) to 0, the value his 145 logged successful -1 attacks should have produced. Key files: `src/lib/influence/simpleInfluence.ts`.

- **US sovereign bonds disappearing when the budget ran a surplus** — `issueScheduledSovereignBondSeries` treated issuance as purely deficit-driven, so any quarter with a positive `budget.surplus` produced no new bonds. Bonds kept maturing, and the US tradable float drained (from 3 active series down to 2 between consecutive quarterly ticks, with no replacement). Quarterly issuance now computes `issueAmount = rolloverAmount + deficitAmount`, where `rolloverAmount` is the summed `totalIssued` of active sovereign bonds maturing in the upcoming 12 turns. Surplus countries still refinance their maturing debt at the current prime rate; deficit countries do the same on top of their deficit-driven issuance. New `calculateSovereignRolloverAmount` helper + tests in `src/lib/bonds/sovereign.ts`. Design doc `docs/design/sovereign-bonds.md` updated to describe the combined formula.

- **Stale "elected" / "lost_election" `careerHistory` entries left by `recalibrate-timers` Step 0** — Follow-up to the heal below. `scripts/migrations/healRecalibrateWithdrawals.ts` had two gaps that left ghost career events in place: (1) DOUBLE-ACTIVE candidates (a player who re-entered the same election after the bug) were hard-skipped, so their original stale event was never pulled; (2) cases where the officeholder row was re-seated by a later turn (officeholder `electedAt` no longer matched `withdrawnAt ±2s`) fell into the `"other"` bucket, which restores the candidacy but never pulls the career event. Reported as bug #0145 — Hikaru Mori (JP sangiin KNS candidate) saw their profile claim "Elected to House of Councillors" while being blocked from proposing bills because `electedOfficials` had no matching row. Added `scripts/migrations/healStaleElectedCareerEvents.ts` (surgical pull scoped to active/upcoming elections where the character has no matching seat) for case (2); extended `healRecalibrateWithdrawals.ts` to collect stale `(type, electionId, date≈withdrawnAt)` career events for DOUBLE-ACTIVE characters and pull them during apply for case (1). Combined, 18 stale events were cleaned on the live DB (6 from the standalone heal + 12 from the patched heal). Key files: `scripts/migrations/healStaleElectedCareerEvents.ts` (new), `scripts/migrations/healRecalibrateWithdrawals.ts`.

- **Players involuntarily withdrawn from active primaries by `recalibrate-timers` Step 0** — `POST /api/admin/elections/recalibrate-timers` Step 0 (added in commit 88017cd3 to "reactivate prematurely completed elections") flipped any `completed`/`resolved` election whose canonical endTurn was still in the future back to `status: "active"`, but did not undo the resolution side-effects: the winner stayed in `electedOfficials`, and every candidate was left as `withdrawn`. From the player's perspective, their candidacy showed `withdrawn` in an "active" primary they should still have been in. Step 0 now skips reactivation when either the election has a finalized vote tally or its seat is held by a sitting officeholder — those signals mean resolution actually ran, and reviving the doc would only corrupt state. Logic extracted to a testable `shouldReactivatePrematureElection` helper with regression tests covering finalized-tally skip, seated-seat skip, US senate `senateClass` key matching, and JP Sangiin `chamberClass` key matching (so a Class 1 win doesn't falsely block a premature Class 2 reactivation). Heal script `scripts/migrations/healRecalibrateWithdrawals.ts` recovers victims from prior runs by restoring withdrawn candidates, vacating prematurely-elected seats (`electedOfficials.characterId` → null, character `currentOffice` → null, matching `careerHistory: { type: "elected" \| "lost_election" }` entries pulled — filter scoped by both `senateClass` and `chamberClass` so a Sangiin Class 2 vacate doesn't accidentally clear a Class 1 official), and re-adding entries to `electionVoteTallies.candidateNames` / `candidateParties` / `totalVotes`. Restoration skips DOUBLE-ACTIVE conflicts (character already re-entered the same election) plus voluntary, party-switch, relocation, and primary-loss withdrawals. Key files: `src/app/api/admin/elections/recalibrate-timers/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/elections/recalibrate-timers/route.test.ts`, `scripts/migrations/healRecalibrateWithdrawals.ts`.

- **Banned users still appeared on National Party Members list** — `GET /api/country/[code]/parties/[id]` now drops characters whose owning user is banned before building the members list, expected hourly income, party-influence bonus actions, and member count. The state-party route already filtered banned users; the national counterpart did not. `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/route.ts`.

- **Banned users' party-leadership and committee votes/candidacies persisted** — The admin ban handler previously withdrew only governmental election candidacies; it left `nationalPartyCandidates`, `statePartyCandidates`, `nationalCommitteeCandidates`, and the corresponding `*Votes` collections untouched, so banned voters continued to count toward chair / vice chair / treasurer / committee tallies and banned candidates remained on ballots. New helper `cleanupPartyElectionsForBannedUser` (called from `/api/admin/users/ban`) withdraws active candidacies and deletes votes across all three election types. As a defense against accounts banned before this code shipped, `processCompletedElections`, `processCompletedNationalElections`, `processCompletedCommitteeElections`, and the three election GET routes also resolve banned character IDs via the new `getBannedCharacterIds` helper and exclude their votes/candidacies from tallies and displays. The four party-election write endpoints (national + state leadership vote/enter, committee vote/enter) reject banned accounts with 403 (auth helper now exposes `isBanned` on `AuthUser`). `retireCharacter` also gained the missing `nationalPartyCandidates`/`nationalPartyVotes` cleanup so retired players' leadership footprint is purged. New script `scripts/migrations/purgeBannedUsersFromPartyElections.ts` (dry-run by default; `--apply` writes) cleans up existing banned-user state on the live DB. Key files: `src/app/api/admin/users/ban/route.ts`, `src/lib/elections/cleanupPartyElectionsForBannedUser.ts`, `src/lib/utils/bannedCharacters.ts`, `src/lib/{state,national}PartyElections.ts`, `src/lib/nationalCommitteeElections.ts`, `src/lib/auth.ts`, `src/lib/utils/statePartyElectionValidation.ts`.

- **Banned users still seated as party chair / vice chair / treasurer / committee member** — The election-cleanup work above purged candidacies and votes but did not vacate seats they currently held; the route filters hid them from display, but `politicalParties.{chair,viceChair,treasurer}Id`, `politicalParties.committeeIds[]`, and `statePartyOrg.{chair,viceChair,treasurer}Id` still pointed at banned accounts, so any leadership-gated authorization that read those pointers directly would still resolve to a banned user. New helper `vacatePartyLeadershipForBannedUser` (called from `/api/admin/users/ban` immediately after the election cleanup) nulls out every seat the banned user's character(s) occupy across `politicalParties` and `statePartyOrg`, pulls them from `committeeIds[]`, and clears `coalitions.chairCharacterId` both directly and as a cascade for any party that lost its chair (matches the existing `retireCharacter` cascade). The migration script gained a matching seat-vacation pass with per-position counts surfaced in the dry-run summary. Key files: `src/lib/elections/vacatePartyLeadershipForBannedUser.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/users/ban/route.ts`, `scripts/migrations/purgeBannedUsersFromPartyElections.ts`.

- **State bill UI showed "Voting Open" after the voting deadline passed** — A bill's DB `status` only transitions out of `active` / `veto_override` when the hourly turn cron runs `processStateBillTimers`, so there was a window (up to ~1 hour) where `votingEndsAt` had passed but the bill was still `active`. The status badge rendered "Voting Open" and exposed Aye/Nay/Abstain buttons, while the VoteBar countdown correctly showed "Expired" and `/vote` rejected submissions with "Voting has ended." The UI now reconciles the stale status with the real-time deadline: a new `isVotingDeadlinePassed` helper is consumed by `mapStateBillToBillDisplay` (to drop `canVoteOrigin`), the state bill detail page (to gate the VoteBar's `canVote`/`onVote` and swap the status chip to "Voting Closed"), and the shared `BillCard` / `BillCompactRow` (to render an orange "Voting Closed" badge and hide the vote buttons). Matches the server-side deadline check in `/vote`. Reported as Bug #0125 (NY State Senate "Tax reform act"). Key files: `src/lib/legislature/billVotingWindow.ts`, `src/lib/legislature/mapStateBillToBillDisplay.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/legislature/bills/[billId]/page.tsx`, `src/components/bills/BillCard.tsx`, `src/components/bills/BillCompactRow.tsx`.

- **Admin `POST /api/admin/elections/resolve-primaries` hardcoded 1-winner-per-party** — The manual primary-resolution admin tool compared party candidate counts against `1` and called `scored.slice(1)` to pick losers, ignoring each country's `primaryWinners` config. If an admin ever invoked this endpoint on a UK or JP election, every party would be pruned down to a single candidate instead of the intended three. Route now computes `maxAdvancing = getElectionSystemPrimaryWinners(countryId)` and prunes with `scored.slice(maxAdvancing)`. `src/app/api/admin/elections/resolve-primaries/route.ts`.

- **Multi-winner primary resolution wiped general-phase vote tally every turn (UK / JP)** — `resolvePrimariesIfNeeded` used `partyCounts.values().some((v) => v > 1)` to skip elections whose primaries were already resolved. That guard was built for 1-winner primaries (US/CA/DE): post-primary each party has exactly 1 active candidate, so the check correctly skips on subsequent turns. For countries where `primaryWinners = 3` (UK commons, JP shugiin/sangiin), parties kept up to 3 active candidates after the primary resolved, so `some(v > 1)` stayed `true` every turn — primary resolution re-entered, hit `initElectionVoteTally` (a `replaceOne` with `upsert: true`), and wiped the general-phase tally's `turnSnapshots` and `totalVotes`. All 12 live UK commons elections were stuck showing exactly 1 turn of accumulated votes regardless of how many turns had elapsed in the general phase. Guard now compares against `getElectionSystemPrimaryWinners(countryId)` instead of the hard-coded `1`, so multi-winner countries skip correctly once no party exceeds the max that can advance. `src/lib/turn/primaryResolution.ts`.

- **Character payment currency conversion across all personal credits** — Dividend, CEO salary, bond coupon, bond-maturity face-value, bond-default dissolution payouts, user-triggered bond-default cash payoffs, and parent-corp bond payoffs to characters (and imperial characters) are now converted from anchor (₳) to the payout country's local currency before being credited to `currencyBalances.personal.<CODE>`. Previously the raw ₳ value was deposited into the local-currency balance field — under-paying JP players ~96× and over-paying UK players ~1.25×. The corresponding corp-to-corp flows (`anchorToCorpCapital` / `anchorToCorpLiquidCapital`) already converted correctly; character flows now mirror the same conversion. Pre-forex characters (single legacy `cashOnHand` in ₳) are unchanged. Fallback to raw ₳ if the FX rate is missing / zero / invalid. Key files: `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/executeCorporationBondDefaultDissolution.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/cash/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/parent-bond-payoff/route.ts`.

- **Profile FinancialStrip now uses FX-aware formatter** — Donor, Campaign, and Cash panels on the profile Personal Cash breakdown now use `formatFull` from `useCurrency()` instead of `formatCurrencyFull(value, sym)` — so income values (passive donor income, per-level rate, fundraise yield, CEO salary, bond coupon, dividend income, portfolio value) are FX-converted to the user's display preference. Previously the formatter slapped a currency symbol on the raw ₳ value without conversion, so a JP player saw `¥229K/turn` dividend when the corp Financials tab simultaneously reported the dividend pool as `¥22M/turn`. Matches the corp Financials tab + StatusBar conventions. Audited in `docs/audits/2026-04-14-currency-display-audit.md` item 2. Key files: `src/app/profile/components/FinancialStrip.tsx`.

- **Phantom shares from corp-detail GET self-heal** — The `GET /api/corporations/[id]` route no longer writes to the DB on read and now subtracts shares reserved in open private listings and corp-placed sell orders before deciding whether legacy shares need CEO backfill. Was the root cause of Quinn Industrial Holdings showing 200% ownership and 15 other corps over-allocated on the live server. Shared invariant helper `computeAccountedShares` extracted to `src/lib/corporations/shareInvariant.ts` so the same formula is used by the detail route and the admin heal. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/lib/corporations/shareInvariant.ts`.

- **Phantom shares from `/shares/sell` race with pending limit orders** — The market-sell route now subtracts shares reserved in the seller's open character sell orders before allowing a sell. Previously a holder could market-sell shares that were already reserved in a pending limit order; when the limit order later filled, `debitShares` silently no-oped (entry already pulled) while `creditShares` still credited the filler — creating shares from thin air. Mirrors the reservation check already present in listings POST and orders POST. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/sell/route.ts`.

- **Admin share heal ignored open listings** — `/api/admin/heal/corporation-shares` now counts reserved shares from open `shareListings` in its `correctTotal`. Previously only corp-placed sell orders were counted, so an admin run while listings were active would shrink `totalShares` below actual issued shares and produce phantom shares on the next listing acceptance. Key files: `src/app/api/admin/heal/corporation-shares/route.ts`.

- **Hostile takeover invariant break** — When an absorbed subsidiary held equity in other corporations, stripping it from those corps' `shareholders` arrays now folds the stripped shares into each host corp's `publicFloat` so `totalShares` stays balanced. Previously the `$pull` silently deleted the equity, leaving the host corps under-allocated. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/hostile-takeover/route.ts`.

- **LOC repay no longer mints free money for the central bank** — A refactor that removed the bank debit on `draw` (deposits are savings liabilities, not lendable cash — see `/api/character/loc/draw/route.ts`) left `repay` and the turn auto-payment crediting the full principal + interest back into `centralBanks.reserveBalance`. That asymmetry meant every borrow→repay cycle silently inflated the lending bank's reserves by the principal amount — a Patreon tester demonstrated it by repeatedly borrowing+repaying £15M against the BoE and watching reserves climb. The 70% of (deposits + reserves) system-wide cap surfaced in `buildLocSnapshot` also grew with the fake reserves, so the exploit compounded — you could "run" until the bank held billions in phantom cash. Fix: only the interest portion (`takeA` / `interestPortions[c]`) now credits `reserveBalance` as bank revenue; principal is destroyed symmetrically to how `draw` creates it. Key files: `src/app/api/character/loc/repay/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/lineOfCreditTurn.ts`. **Note:** existing `centralBanks.reserveBalance` on live may already be inflated from players exercising this loop; a one-shot admin reconciliation pass is worth considering separately.

- **Corporate share price — sovereign bond holdings now count** — Sovereign bonds held by a corporation now contribute to its balance-sheet equity in the share-price formula, matching the corporation API's portfolio view. Previously the corp turn's `bondsHeldByCorpId` lookup filtered to corporate bonds only, so any cash a corp parked in US Treasuries / gilts / JGBs disappeared from the share-price math even though the API still showed it as a portfolio asset. Discovered after Aurora Group dropped 38.4% in one turn (turn 192, 2026-04-19) without an obvious cause. Splits the issuer-side and holder-side loops in `buildLookups.ts` so the credit-rating logic stays corporate-only while the portfolio-anchor map includes all active bond holdings. Key files: `src/lib/turn/corporation/buildLookups.ts`.

- **Corporate share price — issued bond debt now reduces equity** — Issued bond debt is now subtracted from balance-sheet equity in the share-price formula. Previously, bond issuance proceeds counted as cash without offsetting the debt liability, artificially inflating share prices for any leveraged corp; issuing bonds was a way to pump price with no economic substance. Bond issuance is now neutral on share price (cash up, debt up, net zero) — shareholder value only moves when the cash is productively deployed. **National enterprises (`countryOwnerId` set) are exempt** — their interest is already government-subsidized via `perTurnBondDragOnNetIncome=0`, and treating their principal as a corp liability while waiving interest would be internally inconsistent. Defaulted bonds are also excluded — the bondTurn settlement model treats default as final. Key files: `src/lib/turn/corporation/types.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/buildLookups.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`.

- **Corporate share price now refreshes after bond turn (no more 1-turn lag)** — Previously the share-price formula ran during the corporation turn and used start-of-turn bond data, so this turn's bond marketPrice updates, maturities, and coupon cash flows didn't show up in the price until the _following_ turn. A new turn-system phase (`recomputeSharePricesAfterBondTurn`) now runs sequentially after `processBondTurn` and re-runs the formula against fresh state, overwriting both `corporations.sharePrice` and the same-turn `corporationHistory.sharePrice`/`marketCap`. Eliminates the lag for: bond maturities (matured bonds drop out of the holdings map immediately), marketPrice updates from credit spread changes, and coupon income/expense already applied to `liquidCapital`. The iterative cross-holding formula was extracted into a pure module (`sharePriceFormula.ts`) so the corp turn's initial pass and the post-bond-turn recompute share the same math. Three new optional fields persisted on `corporationHistory` (`sectorNPV`, `perTurnBondCouponIncome`, `perTurnBondDragOnNetIncome`) so the recompute can rebuild inputs without re-deriving from sectors. Group 1b in the turn pipeline split into bondTurn+commodity (1b), recompute (1c), and price-reading snapshots (1d) to enforce the sequencing. Key files: `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/marketCapSnapshot.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/corporationHistory.ts`.

- **Corporation API totalEquity formula aligned with share-price math** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]` and the discord-bot equivalent now report `equity.totalEquity = cash + sectorNPV + portfolio − issuedBondDebt` (subtracting natcorp debt to zero), matching what the turn-system uses. Previously the API's `totalEquity` ignored debt entirely while `bookValue` subtracted it, so the two figures disagreed for any leveraged corp. `bookValue` is unchanged. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/discord-bot/corporation/route.ts`.

- **Bond transactional routes + bond turn helpers — `bond.currencyCode` is the single source of truth for denomination** — Six code paths resolved a bond's currency via `corp.countryId → COUNTRY_CURRENCY_MAP` instead of `bond.currencyCode` first. Within the player-facing flows this was harmless (corp HQ relocation is intra-country by design), but the admin HQ route (`PATCH /api/admin/corporations/[id]/hq`) can move a corp across countries — and every one of these paths would then silently re-denominate outstanding bonds into the corp's new currency: bond turn coupon payouts (bondTurn.ts `payoutCountryId`), maturity face-value payouts, character buy/sell/buyback proceeds, and any downstream math derived from them. Additionally, the corp-side transactional paths (buy `A19`, sell `A20`, buyback `A21`) fed LOCAL-bond values directly into `anchorToCorpLiquidCapital` (which expects ₳) — mixed-unit by `bond.fxRate`×. Fix: `addCharPayment` / `addImperialPayment` now take `CurrencyCode` directly, `payoutCountryId` is deleted (new `resolveBondCurrency` helper uses `bond.currencyCode ?? COUNTRY_CURRENCY_MAP[bond.countryId]`), and each transactional route computes `costLocal → costAnchor` via the bond's own FX rate before comparing against corp capital and deducting. Response payloads add `costCurrency` / `proceedsCurrency` for explicit client-side display. Design decision documented at `docs/design/corporations.md` §HQ Relocation → Bond denomination. Key files: `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/bonds/[bondId]/buy/route.ts`, `.../sell/route.ts`, `.../buyback/route.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Party-org cap weights redistributed for UK and JP** — UK's 85-point electoral cap allocation now splits commons (60) + regionalCouncil (25); JP's splits shugiin (60) + sangiin (25). Total cap ceiling (100) unchanged. Previously regionalCouncil and sangiin had no `CAP_WEIGHTS` / `MOMENTUM_WIN` / `CYCLE_TURNS` entries, so their resolutions silently skipped the state-party-org cap/momentum update. Now both chambers contribute to party cap via the multi-seat proportional formula. Live UK/JP state-party docs will drift toward the new targets over the next cycle's worth of turns. `src/lib/constants/partyOrg.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/calculations.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/statePartyOrg.ts`.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Snap elections for UK and JP** — Prime Ministers of the UK and Japan can now dissolve their lower chamber and call a snap election via a new Leadership-tab button. Up to 2 per PM appointment, gated by a 336-turn (2 real-week) cooldown between uses. Dissolution cancels all active lower-chamber races, fails every in-progress bill, spawns fresh `snap_${lowerChamberKey}` races (48h window, 24h primary + 24h general), and resets the government to `pending`. `src/components/parliamentary/PMSnapElectionButton.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/pm/snap-election/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/snapElection.ts`.
- **96-turn PM-vacancy auto-snap** — Whenever `governmentFormations.status` transitions into `pending` — post-election, post-no-confidence, admin PM vacate — `pmVacancyDeadlineTurn` is set to `currentTurn + 96`. A new turn phase (`parliamentaryVacancyWatcher`, runs after `parliamentaryGovernmentPhases` in group 10) fires an auto-snap via `triggerSnapElection(..., { bypassLimits: true })` when the deadline elapses unfilled. Counter increments but limit/cooldown are bypassed. `src/lib/turn/pmVacancyDeadline.ts`, `src/lib/turn/countryPhases.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`.
- **`snap_commons` election type** — Labels, schema enums, admin filter, and MULTI_SEAT_TYPES coverage now match the existing `snap_shugiin` support. `DEFAULT_DURATIONS` registers both.
- **Generic admin snap route** — `/api/admin/elections/snap/[code]` replaces the UK-hardcoded `/api/admin/elections/snap-uk`. Works for any parliamentary country with `snapElectionsAllowed`, delegates to `triggerSnapElection` with `bypassLimits: true` so side effects match the PM path exactly.
- **Snap-elections design doc** — `docs/design/snap-elections.md` codifies eligibility, trigger rules, cycle-reset math, and the 96-turn auto-snap flow.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **`ensureUKElections` / `ensureJPElections` are snap-aware** — Both respawn helpers now query regular and snap types together when building live/completed sets. After a `snap_${lowerChamberKey}` resolves, the next regular election waits the full country cycle period (UK: 240 turns = 5 game-years; JP: 192 turns = 4 game-years) from the snap's `endTime` before spawning, and never inherits the snap's 48h `durationHours`. `src/lib/turn/perpetualElections.ts`.
- **`recalibrate-timers` is history-aware** — `canonicalTurns` accepts optional `priorEndTurn` for `commons` / `regionalCouncil` / `shugiin`. The POST handler looks up the most recent resolved regular-or-snap for each region and anchors the next cycle's end-turn to `priorEndTurn + cyclePeriodHours`, keeping the LARP schedule aligned after a snap. Client-side `canonicalEndTurn` mirrors the same rule. `src/app/api/admin/elections/recalibrate-timers/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/electionsAdminTypes.ts`.

### Removed

- **`/api/admin/elections/snap-uk`** — Superseded by the generic `/api/admin/elections/snap/[code]`. Callers (UKParliamentPage admin override) already re-pointed.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Corporate tax base — currency-unit regression from the forex migration** — `federalBudget.taxBases.corporateProfits` and `stateBudgets.taxBases.corporateProfits` use a 75% GDP + 25% actual-corp-income blend. GDP is stored in each country's local currency (JPY 550T for JP, GBP 2.9T for UK) while corp income accumulates in anchor (₳/USD). The blend was mixing the two directly — the 25% contribution was ~150× too small for JP budgets (effectively zero) and ~25% too small for UK, so non-USD national/regional tax-revenue figures were driven almost entirely by the GDP-derived floor regardless of actual corporate activity. The blend now multiplies anchor-unit income by each jurisdiction's fx rate (`exchangeRatesByCurrency.get(COUNTRY_CURRENCY_MAP[countryId])`) before mixing. State-budget path derives currency via the newly-exposed `lookups.stateCountryMap`. USD paths are numerically unchanged. Key file: `src/lib/turn/corporation/index.ts`.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **National Party Player Whip** — National-party Chair and Vice Chair can now issue a one-shot Player Whip on bills, speaker / leadership elections, PM appointment votes, no-confidence motions, and cabinet nominations. The whip force-overwrites every seated party character's vote in the relevant chamber to the whipped direction, preserves each pre-whip value in a new `whippedFromVote` snapshot, and sends an in-game mail plus `party_whip_issued` notification to each affected character. Characters may revert through the normal vote endpoints, which auto-clear the snapshot and hide the "Whipped by Party" badge. The existing NPP whip mechanic is unchanged (2 attempts; NPPs vote probabilistically via loyalty/ideology); it now lives under a new sub-tab alongside the Player Whip. NPP-reading code (`src/lib/turn/npp/context.ts`, `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`) filters to `audience: "npp"` so character whips never drive NPP behavior. Spec: [`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-18-national-party-player-whip-design.md`](docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-18-national-party-player-whip-design.md).

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Party Whip UI restructured** — Party-page Whip tab now splits into Players and NPPs sub-tabs, each with Bills / Leadership / Cabinet (US-only) sub-sub-tabs and chamber chips under Bills. State-party pages hide the Players sub-tab (state parties can't Player-Whip). Files: `src/components/party/WhipTabs.tsx`, `src/components/party/PlayerWhipPanel.tsx`, `src/components/party/NppWhipPanel.tsx` (renamed from `WhipPanel.tsx`), `src/components/party/whipTabsLayout.tsx`.

- **PM-appointment and no-confidence vote endpoints now accept revotes** — Previously a 400 error if the character had already voted; now decrements the old tally and writes the new value so whipped characters can revert. `src/app/api/country/[code]/pm/appoint/[voteId]/vote/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/pm/no-confidence/[voteId]/vote/route.ts`.

- **`GET /api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/whippable-bills` and `/whippable-leadership` responses carry per-audience whip status** — Each item now includes `nppWhip` and `playerWhip` objects (each with `existingWhips[]` + `canWhip`). Legacy `existingWhips` / `canWhip` keys remain as aliases mirroring `nppWhip.*` for back-compat.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Per-turn tax metrics persisted to `corporationHistory`** — `CorpSnapshot` already computed `federalTaxPaid` / `stateTaxPaid`, but `marketCapSnapshot.ts` dropped them before writing to `corporationHistory` — 0 of 185+ stored snapshots for any corporation carried tax data. `marketCapSnapshot.ts` now persists `corporateTaxPaid` (fed + state combined), `federalTaxPaid`, `stateTaxPaid`, `incomePreDividends`, and the per-country / per-state breakdown maps (`taxPaidByCountry`, `taxPaidByState`, omitted for single-jurisdiction corps). `CorporationHistory` type extended with matching optional fields. `CorpSnapshot` extended with `taxPaidByCountry` / `taxPaidByState` Maps populated during the per-sector tax loop in `sectorCalculations.ts`. Key files: `src/lib/db/types/corporationHistory.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/types.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/marketCapSnapshot.ts`.

- **`GET /api/corporations/[id]/history` projection exposes tax fields** — Adds `incomePreDividends`, `corporateTaxPaid`, `federalTaxPaid`, `stateTaxPaid`, `taxPaidByCountry`, `taxPaidByState` to the projected shape. Matching optional fields added to the client-side `CorpHistoryPoint` type. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/history/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/CorporationPageTypes.ts`.

- **Corporate Tax chart on ChartsTab** — New metric plots Federal vs State/Regional corporate tax paid per turn as a dual-line chart. Pre-persistence snapshots render as zero via `?? 0` fallback; new snapshots onward plot real values. `src/components/corporation/ChartsTab.tsx`.

- **Forex rate & macro chart — extended history + timeframes** — Exchange-rate and central-bank macro histories are retained for five in-game years; the forex **Rate** and **Monetary policy** charts gain stock-style range controls (**24h / 1y / 5y / All**) via `ForexChartTimeframeTabs`, `chartSeriesUtils`, and `forexChartTimeframe.ts`, with persistence tweaks in `forexTurn` / `interestRateSnapshot` and `turnTime` constants. `register.registrationGate.integration.test.ts` now skips unless `MONGODB_URI` and `TEST_SERVER_URL` are set so the default suite stays green.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **UK Commons propose-bill UI — multi-provision parity with JP** — Rebuilt around a multi-row provisions editor (up to `MAX_PROVISIONS=3`) instead of a single hardcoded row; preserves the UK slider fallback for legislation types without discrete policy options. `UKParliamentPage.tsx`.

- **`GET /api/country/[code]/legislature/bills` stripped non-UK responses** — JP/CA/DE bill cards rendered without provisions, category, or sponsor party because the route returned a minimal shape outside the UK. Responses are now unified to the enriched `BillDisplay` for every country. `split isMember` into `canPropose` vs `canVoteOrigin` so a Shūgiin-only member viewing Sangiin-origin bills no longer sees enabled vote buttons for chambers they cannot vote in. `src/app/api/country/[code]/legislature/bills/route.ts`, `.../bills/__tests__/route.test.ts`.

- **`statePolicies` missing `scope` on state bill enactment** — `onBillEnacted` now writes `scope` when upserting `statePolicies` so downstream lookups key correctly. `scripts/migrations/backfillStatePolicyScope.ts` backfills existing docs missing `scope`. `src/lib/billEnactment.ts`.

- **JP `jp_national` metric detail pages 404** — Metric route used a local national map omitting `jp_national`; it now uses the canonical `NATIONAL_SCOPE` constant. `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/metrics/[category]/[metricId]/route.ts`, regression coverage in `route.test.ts`.

- **JP prefecture metric pages showed US federal policy** — `nationalPoliciesByScope` in `stateTickRates.ts` and the prefecture branch only considered `{ federal, uk_national }`, defaulting JP states to US federal policy for tick-rate math and UI. Both paths now `$in`-query all national-scope policies and select the row matching the state's `countryId`. `src/lib/api/stateTickRates.ts`.

- **UK Parliament Leadership — PM & Opposition Leader blank after general election** — `GET .../legislature/leaders` read PM from `characters.currentOffice` / legacy `parliamentaryGovernments`, which clears after Commons GE; canonical `governmentFormations` is now primary with legacy fallback. Opposition leader resolution now reuses coalition-aware `resolveOppositionLeader` shared with the UK/JP executive hubs. `src/app/api/country/[code]/legislature/leaders/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`, `.../leaders/__tests__/route.test.ts`, `UKGovernmentExecutiveHub.tsx`, `JPGovernmentExecutiveHub.tsx`.

- **US presidential general — legend & popular-vote summary all purple** — Tally stored country-scoped party `sequentialId` strings that `getPartyHex` did not resolve; server-side enrichment now maps through `partyMap` into `generalVotes.candidateColors` and threads through `PresidentialElectoralMap`, `PresidentialMapWithStateDetail`, `StateDetailModal`, and `GeneralPhaseView`. `src/lib/elections/enrichElection.ts`, `electionResponseTypes.ts`, `ElectionDetailTypes.ts`.

- **`ElectionCard` primary tint defaulted to purple** — Prefer server-provided `polling.candidatePartyColors` (already `partyMap`-resolved) before any client `getPartyHex(sequentialId)` lookup so country-scoped party ids tint correctly. `src/components/elections/ElectionCard.tsx`.

- **Campaign Manager — operations UI past real per-category maximums** — `OperationsSection` now uses `getMaxLevel` per upgrade category for level display, `LevelBar` max, and upgrade affordance so bars cannot exceed the server's true cap (was using a single overstated max). `src/app/campaign/[id]/components/OperationsSection.tsx`.

- **Campaign Manager — fog-of-war estimates exceeded real upgrade caps** — `applyFog` added random variance without clamping, so public/party opponent views could show levels above the cost-table ceiling (or negative) while the owner's true levels stayed in range. Now clamps each category to `[0, getMaxLevel(category)]`; `scripts/migrations/clampCampaignFogOfWar.ts` clamps existing `publicFogOfWar` / `partyFogOfWar` docs. `src/lib/campaigns/fogOfWar.ts`, `upgradeCosts.ts`, `fogOfWar.test.ts`.

- **County map showing "Unknown" for candidates** — Candidates who entered an election after its vote tally was initialized (on a subsequent vote-accumulation turn) had their votes tracked but their names missing from `candidateNames`, causing them to display as "Unknown" on the county/CD results map and table. `accumulateVoteTurn` now syncs names and parties for any active candidate not yet present in the tally. Additionally, `propagateCharacterNameChange` was using `characterId` as the map key for `electionVoteTallies.candidateNames`, but that map is keyed by `ElectionCandidate._id`; the propagation now resolves candidate IDs first.

