## [0.2.5] - 2026-04-18

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Parliamentary minority government threshold lowered** — `MINORITY_SEAT_FRACTION` reduced from `0.2` to `0.1538`, which drops the UK Commons minority-attempt floor from 130 seats to 100 (JP House of Representatives falls from 93 to 72). A smaller third party can now nominate a PM when no majority exists. `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`, `docs/design/uk-elections.md`, `src/app/guides/running-for-office/intl/page.tsx`.

- **Corporate taxation — territorial, per-sector** — Federal and state/regional corporate tax now apply fully territorially at the sector level. Each sector pays its country's federal rate and its state's rate on its revenue-weighted apportioned share of corporate income. Corp-wide overhead (marketing, logistics, CEO salary, growth) is allocated across sectors by revenue share; losing sectors pay $0; federal and state stack independently without credits or SALT deduction. Cross-border corporations now pay federal tax to each country where they operate, not just their HQ country. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/buildLookups.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/index.ts`.

- **State-scope tax rate bills now apply on enactment** — `onBillEnacted` now handles `scope: "state"` tax legislation by writing the new rate to the bill's `stateBudgets[stateId].taxRates[taxType]` and immediately recalculating state revenue/surplus (was previously a no-op comment). Federal-scope behavior unchanged. `src/lib/billEnactment.ts`.

- **Corporate profits tax base keyed by operating state/country** — `stateBudgets[S].taxBases.corporateProfits` and `federalBudget[C].taxBases.corporateProfits` are now aggregated from per-sector operating income keyed by `sector.stateId`/`sector.countryId` instead of the corporation's HQ. The 75% GDP / 25% actual-income blend is unchanged.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Federal + state tax rows on FinancialsTab** — The corporation Financials tab splits the old single "Corporate Tax" row into "Federal Tax" (with a tooltip showing per-country breakdown for cross-border corps) and "State / Regional Tax" (aggregated). `src/components/corporation/FinancialsTab.tsx`.

- **Per-sector tax display on sector detail page** — Each sector detail page (`/corporation/[id]/sector/[id]`) shows the federal and state/regional corporate tax rates applying to that sector plus an approximate tax amount on the sector's own operating profit. Tooltip notes that the authoritative per-turn deduction uses revenue-weighted cost allocation. `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/sections/FinancialsPanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Federal corporate tax projection** — `buildCorporationLookups` was fetching `federalBudget` without projecting `taxRates`, so `corporateTaxRateByCountry` was always empty at runtime and the federal corporate tax deduction silently never fired in production. Tests passed because they use `makeLookups` directly, bypassing the broken projection. Fix is a one-line projection addition. `src/lib/turn/corporation/buildLookups.ts`. **Impact:** From the next turn after deploy, profitable corporations start paying real federal corporate tax (plus new state tax via apportionment) deducted from `liquidCapital`. Expect a visible one-turn contraction of corp balances and share prices as markets adjust.

