## [0.2.4] - 2026-04-17

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Central Bank rate-change Discord webhooks** — Successful prime rate changes now post to the country-specific Discord channel (US/UK/JP) and the global game webhook, with cut/hike-aware coloring (green/red), basis-point delta, and a Chair field that preserves the existing "(admin)" label on admin overrides. `src/lib/centralBankWebhook.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/central-bank/rate/route.ts`.

- **JP Diet member bill proposals** — Seated Shūgiin and Sangiin members can now propose national bills from the Japan legislature page. Origin chamber matches the sponsor's seat; Sangiin-origin bills rejected by the Shūgiin fail outright (Shūgiin supremacy), while Shūgiin- and cabinet-origin bills retain the 2/3 Shūgiin override path. Cabinet proposals are unchanged. `src/app/api/country/[code]/legislature/bills/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/jpBillLifecycle.ts`, `src/app/country/[code]/legislature/JPProposeBillModal.tsx`, `JPDietPage.tsx`.

- **Central Bank chair selection — pending acceptance** — Chair term expiry proposes a nominee (`chairSelectionPending`) instead of seating immediately; the player accepts or declines via API and the central bank overview. Economic-pool declines advance to the next wealthiest eligible character; political-pool declines re-run weighted selection with exclusions. Discord events for executive nominations and pending/accept/decline (`src/lib/centralBankChairEvents.ts`, `notifyCbExecutiveNominationDiscord`, etc.). Routes: `POST .../central-bank/chair-selection/accept`, `decline`; `GET .../central-bank` exposes pending state; admin appoint clears pending.

- **US presidential primary campaign expansion** — Campaign branding and staffing APIs (`GET/PATCH /api/campaigns/[id]/color`, `/manager`); presidential primary UI (`EndorseButton`, `PrimaryCampaignControls`, `PrimaryMapWithLinks`, per-state page); region-party **primary allocation** (`POST .../primary-allocation`, `PrimaryAllocationPanel`); **home-state surge** (`POST .../elections/[id]/home-state-surge`); poll and elections routes updated for primary flows. Files under `src/app/president/primary/`, `src/app/api/elections/`, `src/lib/campaigns/`, `src/lib/primaryProjection.ts`.

- **Commodity national balances** — `nationalBalances` module + tests; aggregation exports for economics/corporation UIs. `src/lib/commodity-map/nationalBalances.ts`, `nationalBalances.test.ts`, `commodityAggregation.ts`.

- **Relocation career history** — Every character relocation appends a `"relocated"` entry to `careerHistory` with `fromState`/`toState` (plus `fromCountry`/`toCountry` on cross-country moves). Rendered on the profile page career timeline and in the retired-character view. `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/character.ts`, `src/app/profile/components/CareerHistory.tsx`, `src/app/retired/[id]/page.tsx`.
- **IMF corporate bailout (admin)** — Distressed corporations can be placed under IMF restructuring: bond-holder haircut with character mail, dilutive issuance to a seeded IMF institution corporation (USD), amortizing IMF facility in anchor (₳) with per-turn payments capped at 45% of operating income and remittance to the IMF corp in USD, −15% share price while active, dividends and CEO salary forced to zero with API blocks, bond-default refinance disabled, admin panel metrics in ₳, and admin-only force liquidation reusing bond-default dissolution settlement. Key files: `src/lib/imf/`, `src/lib/turn/imfBailoutTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/corporations/[id]/imf-bailout/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/corporations/[id]/force-liquidate/route.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/executeCorporationBondDefaultDissolution.ts`, `scripts/seed-imf-institution.ts`, `docs/design/imf-corporate-bailout.md`.
- **Remove bill co-sponsorship** — Co-sponsors can remove their endorsement while a bill is still `proposed` or `active` via `POST /api/congress/bills/[id]` with `action: "uncosponsor"` and a **Remove co-sponsorship** button on the bill page. Key files: `src/app/api/congress/bills/[id]/route.ts`, `src/lib/congress/billEnrichment.ts`, `src/app/congress/bills/[id]/page.tsx`.
- **Portfolio & Wallet redesign — command-center layout** — `/portfolio` now uses a sticky sidebar rail on desktop (Overview, Cash & FX, Stocks, Bonds, Transfers) with each rail item showing a live value and turn-over-turn % delta. On mobile the rail collapses to a horizontally scrollable pill strip that auto-scrolls the active section into view. Owner toggle (My Assets ↔ CEO corporation) is integrated into the masthead as a two-line segmented control instead of a floating pill above the page. Transfers is now a first-class section rather than an always-visible card. Layout is shared between personal and corporation views via a new `PortfolioShell` component. Legacy `?tab=` URLs redirect to the new `?section=` param. Key files: `src/app/portfolio/page.tsx`, `src/app/portfolio/components/PortfolioShell.tsx`, `src/app/portfolio/components/CorporationPortfolioView.tsx`.
- **Multi-currency wire transfers** — Wire transfers now support any held forex currency (USD / GBP / JPY), not just the sender's home currency. The Wire Transfer card shows a currency picker of non-zero personal balances (plus home as a stable default), the amount input prefix reflects the selected currency symbol, and the recipient is credited in the same currency the sender sent. Same-country restriction retained. API: `POST /api/characters/[id]/wire` gains an optional `currency` enum field; responses include `currency` and `remainingBalance`. Pre-forex mode rejects non-home currencies explicitly. Key files: `src/app/api/characters/[id]/wire/route.ts`, `src/app/portfolio/components/WireTransferCard.tsx`.
- **Traffic analytics: 24h view, device / country / performance** — The admin **Traffic** tab now supports an hourly resolution (24h / 48h ranges) in addition to the existing 7 / 14 / 30 / 60 / 90-day windows, a **Page views ↔ Unique visitors** metric toggle, top-countries ranking (flag + bar), device-class breakdown (mobile / tablet / desktop), and a **Slowest paths** panel ranked by client-reported navigation timing (Navigation Timing API). Stat callouts surface the busiest weekday and busiest 6-hour EST time slot. Page-view ingestion now captures `deviceType`, `country` (from Vercel / Cloudflare geo headers), and `loadTimeMs` alongside the existing path / visitor / auth fields. Key files: `src/app/api/admin/traffic/summary/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/tabs/AdminTrafficTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/analytics/pageview/route.ts`, `src/components/SiteTrafficTracker.tsx`, `src/lib/analytics/siteTraffic.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/siteTrafficPageview.ts`.
- **Cookie consent banner & AdSense GDPR signal** — First-visit banner with **Accept all** / **Reject** options, persisted in `localStorage` and re-openable via a **Cookie preferences** link in the site footer. Until consent is given (or if the user rejects), `AdBanner` sets `adsbygoogle.requestNonPersonalizedAds = 1` so AdSense still serves but without personalization cookies. About page gains a **Credits & attributions** section covering flagcdn, Unsplash, Wikimedia Commons, Geist / Lora typefaces, and the underlying open-source stack. Key files: `src/components/CookieConsent.tsx`, `src/components/AdBanner.tsx`, `src/components/SiteFooter.tsx`, `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/app/about/page.tsx`.

- **News vs sponsored posts** — Free **News** (12h cooldown per author) and paid **Sponsored** posts (5 AP + $100k personal cash, 30m cooldown). `/news` uses tabs plus “Post news” / “Place ad”; `newsPosts.feedType`; `GET /api/news?feed=article|advertisement|ticker`. **Admin remove** on player posts (uses `DELETE /api/admin/news/[id]`). Reply bodies use slur-only filtering.

- **Forex UI overhaul** — Comprehensive improvements to the `/forex` page: rate chart now normalizes all currencies to % change from base (fixing JPY dominating the scale), with X-axis turn labels and a dashed zero line; cross-rate matrix cells are now clickable and navigate to the Trade tab with the pair pre-selected; Direct Trade replaces the raw MongoDB ObjectId field with a debounced player name search with autocomplete dropdown; current rate displayed beneath the “To” dropdown before any amount is entered; Trade History tab implemented (was a stub — fetches filled/cancelled/expired orders from new `?view=history` endpoint); My Orders gains Placed, Fee, and Expires columns; Order Book gains per-pair filter pills; hero banner replaced with a financial district image and gains a live market stats strip showing rate, % change, and 24h volume per currency.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **`proposeBillSchema.chamber` enum** — Widened to include `shugiin` and `sangiin` so the shared bill proposal schema accepts Diet chamber identifiers. `src/lib/api/schemas/congress.ts`.

- **Relocation auto-withdraws candidacies** — Relocation no longer blocks on active campaigns. The player is withdrawn from every active general/primary, state-party, national-party, and committee election as part of the move. `src/lib/utils/electionCandidacy.ts` (new `withdrawAllActiveCandidacies`), `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`, `src/app/api/character/relocate/route.ts`.
- **Relocation preserves within-country standing** — `nationalInfluence` and `partyInfluence` now only reset on cross-country moves. Within-country relocations keep both. `donorBaseLevel` still resets to 0 on any relocation, and `politicalInfluence` and `groupFavorability` still fully reset. `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`.
- **Relocation keeps party membership within a country** — Party is only reset to Independent on cross-country moves. Same-country moves preserve the character's party. `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`.
- **Relocation strips old-state party leadership on every move** — State/region-party `chairId`/`viceChairId`/`treasurerId` in the state you're leaving is vacated whether the relocation crosses countries or not (previously only on country change). `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`.
- **Admin/moderator character-location overrides run the full pipeline** — `PATCH /api/admin/characters/update-country`, `PATCH /api/admin/characters/update-state`, `PATCH /api/moderator/characters/update-country`, and `PATCH /api/moderator/characters/update-state` now delegate to `performRelocation`, running the same cleanup and bookkeeping as a player-initiated move. Country codes are validated via zod enum and target states must exist in the requested country. `src/app/api/admin/characters/update-country/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/characters/update-state/route.ts`, `src/app/api/moderator/characters/update-country/route.ts`, `src/app/api/moderator/characters/update-state/route.ts`.
- **Relocation confirmation dialog** — The dialog now lists the actual effects (influence resets, donor-base reset, leadership stripping, candidacy withdrawal counts, office/CEO/chair auto-resignation) and highlights cross-country-only consequences when the target country differs. Replaces the previous inaccurate "funds and actions reset" copy. `src/components/RelocateButton.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/uk/region/[regionId]/UKRegionClient.tsx`.
- **Relocation party-presence recompute** — `updatePartyPresence` now runs **after** the character update so the headcount doesn't double-count the relocating player. `src/lib/character/performRelocation.ts`.
- **Corporate share price — investment portfolio** — Each turn’s share-price “balance sheet” leg now includes the same mark-to-market portfolio used on corporation financials: held bond value, cross-corporate stock (shares × issuer listed quote), and IMF facility principal receivable for lender corps. Built once in `buildCorporationLookups` via `buildPortfolioAnchorValueByCorpId` so holding companies no longer list near floor price while assets show large portfolio lines. Key files: `src/lib/corporations/portfolioAnchorValuation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/buildLookups.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/types.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `docs/design/corporations.md`.

- **Corporate bonds — spreads and maturities** — New issues use `prime + CREDIT_RATING_SPREADS + CORPORATE_BOND_SPREAD_PREMIUM` (default +1.0 percentage point; sovereign/treasury coupons unchanged). Issuance maturities are 2 / 5 / 7 game years only (`CORPORATE_BOND_MATURITY_ISSUANCE_OPTIONS`: 96, 240, 336 turns); legacy 1yr corporate bonds stay valid. Relocation bond payment uses the 7yr tenor. Admin sovereign issuance remains 48/96/240. Key files: `src/lib/constants/bonds.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/bond.ts`, `src/lib/api/schemas/bonds.ts`, `src/lib/api/schemas/bondDefault.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/relocate/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/BondsTab.tsx`, `src/app/guides/bonds/page.tsx`.

- **Corporation Shares tab — corporate shareholder avatar** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]` includes `logoUrl` on corporate shareholder rows; the Market Overview shareholder list uses the same `Avatar` image treatment as characters (replacing the generic “C” tile). `ShareholderInfo.logoUrl`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `MarketOverviewPanel.tsx`, `ShareholderRegister.tsx`.

- **Turn controls: Feature toggles row** — Extracted **Forex system** and **Fast mode** out of the generic control-button grid into a dedicated “Feature toggles” section with an explicit enabled / disabled state chip and description. The previous layout hid the Enable Forex button entirely once forex was already on and displayed the fast-mode control as a status string (`Fast: 30m` / `Normal: 60m`) rather than an action, so admins could miss both toggles. Key file: `src/components/TurnControls.tsx`.
- **Status bar layouts** — Standard and **Full** layouts use the original centered online line (“N Player(s) Online” in the middle of the bar). Corp and Elections compact layouts keep a slim inline count next to the timer. CEOs on standard view get a corp treasury chip with profile stats. **Full** in Settings → Appearance combines profile, elections, and corporation stats in a taller bar.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **No-confidence vote — PM removal on resolution** — Parliamentary (UK, JP) executive hubs and `/api/country/[code]/executive` read the canonical `governmentFormations` document but fell back to legacy `parliamentaryGovernments` via `??` when `pmCharacterId` was `null`. Because the new-system resolver intentionally nulls that field post-collapse (while the legacy collection is never updated), the Downing Street card kept showing the deposed PM until the legacy document was edited by hand. The fallback now only triggers when the canonical doc is missing entirely. Same fix applied to `requireCurrentPrimeMinister` (cabinet-eligibility auth), which otherwise could authorize a deposed PM for PM-only actions. Key files: `src/app/country/[code]/executive/UKGovernmentExecutiveHub.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/executive/JPGovernmentExecutiveHub.tsx`, `src/lib/uk/cabinetEligibility.ts`.
- **No-confidence / PM-appointment vote — resolution latency** — Vote `closesAt` is 24 real hours from proposal, but resolution only happened when the next hourly turn processor ran — leaving up to a one-hour window where the UI showed "Voting ended" with the incumbent PM still in office. Executive hubs and the executive API route now invoke `processParliamentaryGovernmentVotes` inline before reading state, so expired votes resolve on the first page load past `closesAt`. Resolution is race-safe against the turn processor: `resolveParliamentaryNoConfidenceVote` and `resolveParliamentaryAppointmentVote` now use a `findOneAndUpdate` atomic claim on `{ _id, status: "active" }` so side effects run exactly once. `GovernmentVotePanel` labels the transient window "Voting ended — awaiting resolution" as a fallback for cached client views. Key files: `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/executive/route.ts`, `src/components/uk/GovernmentVotePanel.tsx`.

- **Party treasury consistency across views** — The Party Resources card and the NPP Influence panel on national and state party pages now always show the same treasury and action-pool numbers — previously the panel refreshed its own `/influence` fetch after each action but never told the parent page to refetch, so the card above stayed pre-action while the panel showed post-action values. The party-chair campaign-donation flow now actually reads and debits the real party treasury (was reading and writing a dead `partyBudget.treasury` field that is always 0, so every chair donation returned "Insufficient party funds"). National-scope action recommendations source treasury from `politicalParties` instead of the same dead field, so the GOTV suggestion at the 100k threshold now fires correctly. Key files: `src/components/NationalPartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/components/StatePartyInfluencePanel.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/parties/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/campaigns/[id]/donate/route.ts`, `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts`, `src/app/api/actions/recommendations/route.ts`.

- **Map tooltips clipped for southern/lower regions (UK, US, Japan)** — Hovering the lower half of any country map cut off the per-party seat breakdown because the tooltip container had `overflow-hidden` and the tooltip extended downward past the map's bottom edge. The tooltip now flips above the cursor when the pointer is in the lower half of the map, revealing the full breakdown; the redundant `overflow-hidden` on the map wrapper is removed (the SVG keeps its own `overflow: hidden`). `src/components/UKMapPaths.tsx`, `src/components/JapanMapPaths.tsx`, `src/components/USAMapPaths.tsx`.
- **Relocation design doc** — Corrected cooldown from 48 hours to 24 hours (matches the code) and added reset-rule tables covering same-country vs cross-country moves. `docs/design/relocation.md`.
- **Corporate bond issuance — atomic bond + treasury credit** — `POST /api/corporations/[id]/bonds` wraps bond insert and `liquidCapital` increment in a MongoDB transaction so debt and proceeds commit together (requires a replica set, e.g. Atlas). Proceeds use the same FX snapshot as equity validation (`postCorpFxRate`).

- **commodityPriceTurn test — state hard peg** — The state hard-peg unit test now includes a mocked `states` document for `US-CA` so `statePrices` for that state is asserted against real turn behavior.

- **National party treasury — send / transfer / donate validation** — Client-side checks used `parseFloat` on typed amounts then `toInternal()` while still comparing to a **1,000 internal-unit** floor, so players with a **display currency** (forex) could enter thousands of yen (or comma-formatted numbers) and always fail validation. Minimum hints and errors now use `formatFull(1000)` (converted minimum in the viewer’s currency), inputs go through `parseMoneyAmountInput()` (comma / full-width digit safe), and member/state missing vs under-minimum show clearer messages. Key files: `TreasuryPanel.tsx`, `TreasuryTransferControls.tsx`, `src/lib/utils/parseMoneyAmountInput.ts`.

- **Corporation effective margin — owned sectors vs sector detail** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]` now applies the same ramping strategy-transition penalty as turn processing and the sector page (`STRATEGY_TRANSITION_TURNS`). `GET /api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]` now loads active subsidies and passes `getSubsidyMarginModifier` into `computeAllMarginModifiers`, and uses resolved `sectorCountryId` for the home-nation margin bonus. Sector margin breakdown shows **Active subsidies** when non-zero. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/route.ts`, `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/types.ts`, `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/sections/MarginsPanel.tsx`.

- **Corporate HQ relocation vs CEO residence** — `POST /api/corporations/[id]/relocate` previously allowed moving headquarters without the CEO living in the target region and did not reject cross-country targets on the API. The route now requires `targetState.countryId` to match the corporation’s country and the CEO’s `homeState` to equal the destination (aligned with CEO vote/accept rules). `POST /api/corporations/[id]/ceo/vote` and `ceo/accept` also reject country mismatches when `corporation.countryId` is set. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/relocate/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/ceo/vote/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/ceo/accept/route.ts`, `docs/design/corporations.md`.

- **IMF facility on corporation financials & share price** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]` now includes IMF facility payment (borrower) and receipts (lender) in net income using the same `computeImfFacilityPaymentTurn` basis as `processImfBailoutPayments` (latest `corporationHistory.income` cap). Financials tab and CEO budget subtab show **IMF Facility Payment** / **IMF Facility Receipts** under Interest. Turn share-price math in `sectorCalculations.ts` folds expected IMF cash into book-value and earnings components for borrowers and applies aggregated facility receipts for the IMF lender after all corps are processed.

- **Corporate bond coupons / maturity credits vs forex** — Bond turn converted ₳ coupon and principal flows using only `liquidCurrencyCode` to look up FX; corps with a HQ country but missing that field fell back to rate `1.0`, crediting local `liquidCapital` at anchor scale (e.g. ~100× too little for JPY). `processBondTurn` and `getCorpFxRate` now resolve home currency via `resolveCorpLiquidCurrencyCode` (explicit code, else `COUNTRY_CURRENCY_MAP[countryId]`), matching sector income. Corporate turn snapshots use the same resolution for `corpCapitalToAnchor` / `anchorToCorpCapital`. **Follow-up:** `getCorpFxRate` alone was not enough for **bond issuance** and other CEO routes: those paths still passed `corporation.liquidCurrencyCode` into `anchorToCorpCapital`, which **skips multiplication** when the field is unset—so the UI could show local-currency proceeds while the DB received raw ₳. All corp treasury routes now use `anchorToCorpLiquidCapital` / `corpLiquidCapitalToAnchor` paired with `getCorpFxRate`. Portfolio snapshot module comments updated to note parallel execution with bond turn. Key files: `src/lib/currency/corporationCapital.ts`, `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bonds/route.ts`, other `src/app/api/corporations/**` and `src/app/api/bonds/**` routes, `src/lib/turn/portfolioSnapshot.ts`.

- **Forex unit invariant fixes — character wallet operations** — Eight routes and one turn phase were passing raw ₳ amounts directly to `buildPersonalBalanceInc` / `buildPersonalBalanceBulkOp`. Because character `cashOnHand` / `currencyBalances` are denominated in home currency (not ₳), JPY players received ~106× too little on share proceeds and ~106× too much on share purchase debits. Comprehensive fix across: (1) character creation now converts starting wallet via `INITIAL_RATES`; (2) all 7 share routes (order place/cancel/fill, offer place/withdraw/accept, listing cancel) now load the live FX rate and multiply ₳ amounts before wallet ops, with a new `loadCharacterFxRate(db, currency)` helper that returns `{ rate, ok }` and hard-fails 503 on missing rates in API context; (3) `expireShareListings` turn processing falls back to `INITIAL_RATES` so turns never halt on a missing rate. Key files: `src/lib/currency/characterFunds.ts`, `src/app/api/auth/character/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/orders/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/orders/[orderId]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/orders/[orderId]/fill/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/listings/[listingId]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/listings/[listingId]/offers/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/listings/[listingId]/offers/[offerId]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/listings/[listingId]/offers/[offerId]/accept/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/shareListings.ts`.

- **Forex unit invariant fixes — corporate equity and escrow** — Three related currency unit bugs: (1) `CorporateCreditComputationInput.liquidCapital` was being passed home-currency `liquidCapital` values instead of ₳, causing equity-backed bond limits and dissolution settlements to be 100× off for JPY corps — renamed to `liquidCapitalAnchor` and callers now convert via `corpLiquidCapitalToAnchor`; (2) bond-default GET/dissolve/refinance routes were comparing home-currency `liquidCapital` directly to ₳-denominated thresholds; (3) `retireCharacter` credited ₳ escrow amounts directly to corp `liquidCapital` without conversion — fixed with `anchorToCorpCapital` conversion. Key files: `src/lib/bonds/corporateCredit.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bonds/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/cash/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/dissolve/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/capital/route.ts`.

- **Forex unit invariant fixes — corp founding starting capital** — `POST /api/corporations` set `liquidCapital` to the ₳-denominated founding cost without converting to home currency, so a JP corp (JPY) started with ¥1 instead of ¥106M. Route now sets `liquidCurrencyCode` from `COUNTRY_CURRENCY_MAP[countryId]` and initialises `liquidCapital` via `anchorToCorpCapital`. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/route.ts`.

- **Forex unit invariant fixes — central bank wealth ranking** — Three callsites computed wealth using `cashOnHand` directly, ignoring `currencyBalances` when forex is enabled. JPY players with ¥10M personal cash would rank as if they had $0. All three now load FX rates once and use `getTotalPersonalWealth(c, forexEnabled, rateMap)` for the cash component, converting all held currencies to ₳-equivalent for fair cross-currency ranking: (1) the public central-bank GET route (`wealthCandidates` display and user's `userCashOnHand` affordability figure); (2) `processCentralBankChairSelection` turn phase (`computeCharacterWealth` helper now accepts `forexEnabled` + `exchangeRates`, rates loaded once before the per-country loop); (3) the lobby POST route (wealth eligibility check and caller balance check). Key files: `src/app/api/country/[code]/central-bank/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/centralBankChairSelection.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/central-bank/lobby/route.ts`.

- **Signed-out flash navigating from /profile → /settings** — `SettingsPageContent`'s auth guard ran `router.push("/login")` as soon as `useUserData` reported `{loading:false, userData:null}`. If the shared `AuthDataContext`'s initial `/api/auth/me` fetch lost the race with a cold Vercel function the guard would bounce an authenticated user to the login screen even though their cookie was valid — reproducible as "going to /profile then clicking Settings signs me out". The page now refetches `/api/auth/me` once and waits ~800ms for the context to refresh before redirecting, and the redirect preserves a `returnUrl=/settings` so users land back where they intended after signing in. Key file: `src/app/settings/page.tsx`.

- **Imperial shareholder TypeError — profile, portfolio, discord bot** — Corporations can have shareholders of three types: regular characters (`characterId`), imperial characters (`imperialCharacterId`), or other corporations (`corporationId`). The profile page, portfolio API, and Discord bot sync-roles route all iterated shareholders and called `.toString()` on `characterId` without null-checking, causing a `TypeError` crash whenever a corporation with imperial shareholders was processed. This produced a full-screen error overlay on `/profile` (appearing as “logged out” to users) and ~15+ 500 errors per hour from the hourly Discord sync. Fixed with optional chaining/null guard in `src/app/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/character/portfolio/route.ts`, and `src/app/api/discord-bot/sync-roles/route.ts`.
- **auth/me returning 500 instead of 401 for expired/invalid JWT** — `jwtVerify()` was not wrapped in a try/catch in `/api/auth/me`. An expired or malformed token caused `jose` to throw `JWTExpired`, which `handleRouteError` captured to Sentry and returned as a 500. `AuthDataContext` then mapped the 500 to `user=null`. Fixed by wrapping `jwtVerify` in its own try/catch that returns 401. Key file: `src/app/api/auth/me/route.ts`.
- **Corporation bonds/sectors TypeError for legacy sectors without countryId** — `sumCorporateSectorNpv` and `computeSectorNpvSum` called `getCountryConfig(s.countryId)` without guarding against missing `countryId`, which is undefined on sector documents created before the field was added to the schema. `getCountryConfig(undefined)` returns `undefined`, and the subsequent `.centralBank.defaultPrimeRate` access throws a TypeError. This caused `/api/corporations/[id]/bonds` to 500 on every request for affected corporations. Fixed by skipping sectors without `countryId` in the NPV helpers and falling back to the corporation's HQ country in the turn processor. Key files: `src/lib/bonds/corporateCredit.ts`, `src/lib/bonds/corporateBondDefault.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`.
- **Corporation founding industry** — The “Found a Corporation” modal no longer defaults to Financial; players must explicitly choose an industry before founding, avoiding accidental wrong-sector corporations when confirming quickly.
- **Currency Wallet total & approximate conversions** — The multi-currency wallet's "Total (approx.)" row silently excluded every non-home currency, so a player holding £95K GBP + ¥500M JPY would see a total equal to their GBP alone, then shrink it further by running `convert()` on an already-home-currency number. The per-row "≈" hint next to foreign balances also passed a native balance as if it were internal units to `formatAmount`, causing it to render in the player's pinned display currency (e.g. `$505M` shown for a JPY balance when home is GBP). Fixed by summing balances with `convertFrom(native → home)` and always formatting the approximate hint in the player's home currency. Key file: `src/components/forex/CurrencyWallet.tsx`.

- **JP Sangiin class-staggered elections — not restarting after resolution** — `cleanupDuplicateElections` keyed live elections on `(countryId, electionType, state)` plus `senateClass` only for US senate races, so the two JP Sangiin classes that run concurrently in every region hashed to the same key. When a Class 1 cycle 2 spawned alongside an active Class 2 cycle 1 (or vice versa), the newer election was deleted as a "duplicate", which also made "Recalibrate LARP Schedule" appear to spawn cycle 2 elections that vanished the next turn. Fix scopes the dedup key by `chamberClass` for sangiin, scopes `deleteMany`/`sweepStaleOffice` and the loser-vacate match by `chamberClass` in `generalResolution` (so resolving Class 1 no longer wipes Class 2 officials), persists `chamberClass` on `electedOfficials` and `currentOffice`, and extends the `ElectedOfficial` and `OfficeType` types with the new field. Key files: `src/lib/turn/perpetualElections.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/generalResolution.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/officials.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/character.ts`.

- **JP Sangiin classes landing on the same cycle schedule** — `DEFAULT_DURATIONS.sangiin.durationHours` (144h = active election window) was also being used as the per-class cycle period in `canonicalTurns` and `expectedMaxCycle`. That collapsed the 6-year term (288 turns) into the 3-year half-election stagger, so every Class 1 cycle N+1 landed on the same turn as Class 2 cycle N (both ending turn 267, 411, …). "Recalibrate LARP Schedule" couldn't separate them because the canonical end-turn math was already aligned. Fix introduces `JP_SANGIIN_CYCLE_PERIOD_HOURS = 288`, uses it for the per-class cycle offset in recalibrate, and adds `UK_COMMONS`-style gap logic to `ensureJPCouncillorElections` so the next cycle doesn't spawn during the 144-turn half-election gap. Key files: `src/lib/constants/turnTime.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/elections/recalibrate-timers/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/perpetualElections.ts`.

### Refactored

- **`partyBudget` vestigial fields removed (`treasury`, `chairCharacterId`)** — The `partyBudget` collection now only holds GOTV / suppression / org-building budget percentages. `treasury` has been 0 on every document in production for months — actual money lives on `politicalParties.treasury` (national) and `statePartyOrg.treasury` (state). `chairCharacterId` was written by seeds, six gotv/suppression/org-building upsert routes, and various retire/leave/relocate/cleanup paths, but never _read_ for any authorization decision or display — the canonical chair pointer is `politicalParties.chairId` / `statePartyOrg.chairId`. Both fields dropped from the TypeScript type and seed writer; leftover `treasury: 0` writes in five upsert routes also removed. The legacy test-mode branch in `demographicTurnoutTurn` that only existed to let integration tests mutate `budget.treasury` in place has been collapsed — tests now inject a `StatePartyOrg` treasury source directly through the existing DI pattern. Deploy with `npx tsx scripts/migrations/dropPartyBudgetDeadFields.ts` once per environment to `$unset` both fields. Key files: `src/lib/db/types/partyBudget.ts`, `src/lib/admin/seed/seedPartyBudgets.ts`, `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`, `scripts/migrations/dropPartyBudgetDeadFields.ts`.

---

## [0.2.3] - 2026-04-16

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **CEO dissolve confirmation — payout + commodity preview** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]/dissolve` returns a preview; the corporation **CEO Office → Administration** dissolve flow (CEO self-serve, not site admin) shows personal cash after FX and illustrative global commodity % deltas before confirming. `src/lib/corporation/previewQuickDissolve.ts`, `CeoAdminSubtab.tsx`.

- **World nation cards — executive + leading party** — `/world` country cards show the current head of government (or President) portrait and the plurality-leading lower-chamber party with logo; vacancies show as muted “Vacant”. `src/lib/world/nationWorldSnapshots.ts`, `src/app/world/components/CountryCard.tsx`.

- **LOC deposit-based cap** — Line of credit limit is now a system-wide 70% of (national savings deposits + bank reserves) per currency exchange, replacing the previous 33%-of-net-worth per-player cap. `src/lib/lineOfCredit/locMath.ts`, `buildSnapshot.ts`.

- **Bank reserve accumulation** — LOC interest auto-payments now flow into the central bank's `reserveBalance` (home currency). As reserves grow the system LOC pool expands, creating a fractional-reserve lending cycle. `src/lib/turn/lineOfCreditTurn.ts`.

- **Balance Sheet tab on central bank page** — New "Balance Sheet" tab shows total deposits, bank reserves, outstanding loans, system cap, and available lending capacity for the exchange. `src/app/country/[code]/central-bank/CentralBankClient.tsx`, `route.ts`.

- **formatCurrencyFaceAmount** — Native face-unit formatting for forex volumes and balances (JPY whole numbers, two decimal places elsewhere). `src/lib/currency/formatCurrencyFaceAmount.ts`; used by `CurrencyWallet`, `ExchangeRatesTable`, and country forex pages.

- **Commodity price display helpers** — `formatCommodityPrice`, `getCommodityDisplayCurrency`, and `convertCommodityPrice` format commodity economics in the viewer’s display currency when forex is enabled. `src/lib/commodity-map/commodityPriceDisplay.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **GET /api/commodities/[type]** — Sector supply/demand rates match turn processing (`getEffectiveStrategyRates` during transitions); production-flow rows include strategy-only commodities; price history exposes rolling annualized % change for charts.

- **Commodity maps & detail UI** — World and country commodity views use updated aggregation and color scaling; drilldowns and stat cards use localized price formatting via `commodityPriceDisplay`.

- **Commodity state prices** — `processCommodityPriceTurn` writes a blended state price for **every** non-national state (including those with no local sector activity) so regional maps always have per-state values. `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.ts`.

- **Sector commodity flows** — Food demand for healthcare, logistics, and entertainment **live_venue**; vehicles for defense, healthcare (small), and chemical (moderate). `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/constants/sectorStrategies.ts`.

- **Tariff-aware commodity margin blend** — `getTariffBlendWeights` now returns **global / national / local** weights (50/25/25 with no tariff pressure, shifting toward 25/50/25 as effective tariff coverage rises). `computeBlendedMarginModifiers` and turn processing consume **national** commodity balance maps aggregated per country from `CommodityPrice` state rows (`buildLookups.ts`, `sectorCalculations.ts`). Corporation `GET` builds the same national maps for on-page margins; sector detail route passes country-keyed balances into the same helper.

- **Forex UI parity** — Main and per-currency forex pages use face-amount volume formatting, table-driven trade entry, clearer open-order vs order-book labeling, and `CurrencyTradeModal` market-side receive flooring. `WorldDropdown` adds a desktop **Currency Exchange** entry (global forex) after Stock Market.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **NPP portraits & Wikimedia state flags** — `next/image` optimization was failing for `/api/images/npp-politicians/*` (307 to Commons) and for direct `upload.wikimedia.org` URLs (server fetch vs browser). Use `unoptimized` for those sources via `bypassNextImageOptimization()` in `Avatar`, `HeroImage`, and state-flag `Image` usages. `src/lib/images/bypassImageOptimization.ts`.

- **Corporate dissolution payout under forex** — Returned `liquidCapital` is converted from corporate home currency to the CEO’s **personal home currency** using `getCorpFxRate` and `loadCharacterFxRate` before `buildPersonalBalanceInc`. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/dissolve/route.ts`.

- **Share self-issue debit under forex** — Validation and `$inc` use anchor cost × character FX rate and `getPersonalBalance` on a fresh character document instead of mixing total wealth in anchor units with a home-currency debit. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/self-issue/route.ts`.

- **Sector detail national commodity balances** — `GET .../sectors/[sectorId]` now sums `stateSupply` / `stateDemand` across **all** states in the sector’s country when building the national bucket for `computeBlendedMarginModifiers`, matching corporation detail and turn processing (previously only the sector’s home state was accumulated). `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/route.ts`.

- **Macro service commodity state prices** — The regional leg of the global/state blend uses **country-national** supply/demand (with `NATIONAL_COMMODITY_STABILIZER`) for `financial_services`, `healthcare_services`, `advertising`, and `real_estate_services` (`COMMODITIES_NATIONAL_REGIONAL_PRICE_BLEND`), instead of raw state S/D. Federal healthcare demand is attributed **per country** into national balances (not global-only) so national prices and regional legs match public spending. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.ts`.

## [0.2.2] - 2026-04-13

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Foreign exchange system** — Full multi-currency trading system with floating exchange rates for USD, GBP, and JPY. Each country’s currency rate is driven by its own macroeconomic indicators (prime rate, inflation, GDP growth, trade balance) with volume pressure from player trading and random noise. **Not yet enabled for players** — behind an admin toggle (`gameState.forexEnabled`). Design doc: `docs/design/currency-exchange.md`.
  - **Currency engine** (`src/lib/currency/`): Rate calculation pipeline (macro target -> drift -> volume pressure -> noise -> clamp), market maker for instant trades, spread fee distribution (50% destroyed as deflationary sink, 50% to central bank revenue), auto-convert for cross-currency purchases, and admin migration tools.
  - **DB types**: `ExchangeRate` (string `_id` = CountryId), `CurrencyOrder` (market/limit/direct orders with escrow), `TradeHistoryEntry`. Character documents extended with `currencyBalances` (campaign + personal per-currency map), `displayCurrencyPreference`, `autoConvertEnabled`. `GameState` extended with `forexEnabled` boolean. `CentralBank` extended with `tradeGrowth` and `forexRevenue`.
  - **API routes** (`/api/forex/`): `GET /exchange` (rates + order book), `POST /orders` (place market/limit), `DELETE /orders/[orderId]` (cancel with refund), `POST /orders/[orderId]/fill` (fill limit order), `POST /direct` (P2P trade request), `POST|DELETE /direct/[requestId]` (accept/reject). Admin: `POST /api/admin/forex/enable` (run migration).
  - **Turn processing**: `tradeGrowthMirror` phase (Group 14c.5) mirrors trade growth from FederalBudget to CentralBank. `forexTurn` phase (Group 14d.5) updates exchange rates, processes triggered limit orders (FIFO with escrow), and expires stale orders with refunds. Both gated behind `gameState.forexEnabled`.
  - **UI components** (`src/components/forex/`): `ExchangeRatesTable`, `RateChart` (SVG line chart with crosshair tooltip), `TradeForm` (market/limit with spread preview), `OrderBook`, `MyOrders`, `DirectTradeModal`, `CurrencyWallet`, `AutoConvertConfirm`.
  - **Forex page** (`/country/[code]/forex`): Full exchange interface with rates, chart, trading, and order management tabs. Feature-gated with “Coming Soon” state when forex is disabled.
  - **Stock market integration**: `ForexTable` component added to stock market page as a “Forex” tab showing live rates and order book.
- **Codebase-wide currency migration** — 60+ API routes updated to use dual-mode fund helpers from `src/lib/currency/characterFunds.ts` (`getCampaignFunds`, `getPersonalBalance`, `buildCampaignFundsInc`, `buildPersonalBalanceInc`, `buildPersonalBalanceBulkOp`). Routes include: bonds (buy/sell), shares (buy/sell/orders/fill/listings/self-issue), corporation creation, transfers, donations, canvassing, lobbying, central bank, character creation, NPP influence/boost, discord-bot blackjack, relocation, news purchase, portfolio snapshots, wealth list, and leaderboard. All behind feature flag — legacy `funds`/`cashOnHand` path still works when forex is off.
- **Guides section** — New `/guides` section with beginner guides for Corporations, Running for Office (US and UK/Japan), Investing, Bonds, Commodities, and Forex. Linked from the Help dropdown and mobile nav. Accessible without a character. Key files: `src/app/guides/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/corporations/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/running-for-office/us/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/running-for-office/intl/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/investing/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/bonds/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/commodities/page.tsx`, `src/app/guides/forex/page.tsx`.
- **Banned candidate withdrawal** — Elections now automatically withdraw banned players from active candidacies via `withdrawBannedCandidates`. Key file: `src/lib/elections/withdrawBannedCandidates.ts`.
- **Vacant CEO corporate sector decay** — Player corporations without an active CEO (`ceoId` missing/null or `ceoVacant`) transfer 10% per turn of each owned sector’s revenue and workers into the matching state unowned-sector pool; nationalized / `countryOwnerId` enterprises are excluded. Runs at the start of `processCorporationTurn` before sector P&L. Key files: `vacantCeoSectorShed.ts`, `corporation/index.ts`.
- **Election trends: seat projection over time** — Multi-seat general races (House, state senate, Commons, etc.) now store per-turn seat estimates on each `VoteTurnSnapshot` (same Hamilton allocation as the live tally). The election detail “Election Trends” chart adds a **Seat projection** tab when at least two counted turns include seat data. Key files: `tallyManagement.ts`, `voteTally.ts`, `enrichElection.ts`, `ElectionDetailCharts.tsx`.
- **Party colors in election charts** — Vote tally and election detail types extended with `partyColor` field. Election charts and non-presidential results panel display party-branded colors. Key files: `ElectionDetailCharts.tsx`, `tallyManagement.ts`, `enrichElection.ts`, `voteTally.ts`.
- **Japan region maps** — Added JIS-to-region mapping (47 prefectures to 8 regions) in commodity map registry. Japan now has `hasRegionMap: true` with GeoJSON from CDN. Commodity region maps read per-country `projectionCenter` and `projectionScale` instead of hardcoding UK values. Key files: `commodityMapRegistry.ts`, `commodityRegionMappings.ts`, `CommodityRegionMap.tsx`.
- **Corporation tariff display** — Sector margin types extended with `foreignTariffModifier` and `domesticTariffMalus`. MarginsPanel displays “Foreign tariff” and “Tariff friction” line items. SectorsTab shows a “tariff” warning badge on affected sectors. Key files: `CorporationPageTypes.ts`, `types.ts`, `MarginsPanel.tsx`, `SectorsTab.tsx`.
- **Navigation: Currency Exchange links** — WorldDropdown and mobile menu panel include “Currency Exchange” links to `/country/{code}/forex`.
- **Profile: currency wallet** — FinancialOverview shows multi-currency balance breakdown via `CurrencyWallet` component when forex is enabled.
- **Admin: corporation CEO vacant heal** — New admin heal tool at `POST /api/admin/heal/corporation-ceo-vacant` detects and repairs corporations with a missing or inconsistent `ceoId`. Key file: `src/app/api/admin/heal/corporation-ceo-vacant/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Financial services commodity demand for countries with only seeded bonds (JP, CA, DE)** — `processCommodityPriceTurn` derived latent financial services demand from bonds issued within `turn - 12`. Countries whose only sovereign issuance was at game start (turn 11) aged out of that window, leaving state-level financial services demand at 0 despite large outstanding sovereign debt. Window extended to 48 turns (one game year) so long-lived sovereign bonds keep contributing until they mature. Expect latent demand to appear across JP/CA/DE states and to increase modestly for US/UK. Key file: `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.ts`.
- **Bonds guide inaccuracies** — The "How to Evaluate a Bond" section implied the coupon should be compared to the prime rate for all bonds and that holding to maturity "always" returns $1,000. Corrected: corporate bonds must be compared to prime + the credit spread for the issuer's rating, and maturity redemption only applies to non-defaulted bonds. Added a "CEO recovery option: refinance" subsection to "Defaults & Recovery" documenting the refinance flow and new 2-refinance lifetime cap. Key file: `src/app/guides/bonds/page.tsx`.
- **Character page redirect loop** — `getCharacterById` in `src/app/character/[id]/page.tsx` wrapped its entire body in a try/catch that swallowed `redirect()` calls. `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` internally and must propagate; catching it caused ObjectId-to-sequential and NPP redirects to silently return `null`, which fell through to a `/map` redirect instead. Fixed by re-throwing `NEXT_REDIRECT` before logging the error.
- **Achievement duplicate-key race condition** — `awardAchievement` in `src/lib/achievements/index.ts` used a `findOne` -> `insertOne` pattern with no guard against concurrent calls. Two simultaneous award triggers for the same `(characterId, achievementId)` both passed the existence check and attempted `insertOne`, producing repeated `E11000` errors on the `characterId_1_achievementId_1` unique index. Fixed by wrapping `insertOne` in a try/catch that treats `E11000` as an idempotent “already awarded” result.
- **Wire service election party names** — `generateElectionNews` was emitting raw party `sequentialId` strings (e.g. `”1”`, `”2”`) as party labels in wire ticker headlines. Now batch-fetches party names from DB before formatting, using `countryId` to scope lookups correctly. Key file: `src/lib/news.ts`.
- **Election trends chart disappearing (UK & others)** — The trends panel treated “enough data” using whichever series matched the active tab. With electoral-vote history available but fewer than two national `turnSnapshots`, switching to vote share or cumulative votes blanked the entire chart block. Empty-state logic is now OR’d across EV vs national snapshots, the plotted series is derived so an invalid tab cannot hide everything, and vote tabs are disabled until two snapshot turns exist. Key file: `ElectionDetailCharts.tsx`.
- **Commodity stat card click-outside detection** — Fixed click-outside detection with separate refs for desktop/mobile. Redesigned action buttons: “View Nation Map” is now primary CTA when available, with “View Country Page” as secondary link. Key file: `CommodityCountryStatCard.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Financial services demand from bond issuance reduced 33%** — `FINANCIAL_DEMAND_ISSUANCE_FRACTION` lowered from `0.00005` to `0.0000335`. Offsets the 12→48 turn window expansion so aggregate financial services demand stays in the same range overall while still distributing across countries with only seeded bonds. Key file: `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`.
- **Bond refinance no longer mints phantom cash** — The bond-default refinance route previously credited the corporation's `liquidCapital` with the full face value of the new bond. This was a bug: refinancing rolls existing defaulted holders into the new bond at par (a debt-for-debt swap), so no new investors are buying and no new capital is being raised. The cash inc allowed a CEO to default → refi → extract cash as dividends → default again in a loop. Removed the `$inc: { liquidCapital: actualFaceValue }` from the refi route. Refinancing still clears the default, restores holders' claim from $0.10 to par, and keeps the corporation operating under a new (CCC-floored) coupon — it just no longer issues free cash. Key file: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/refinance/route.ts`.
- **Corporate bond refinancing cap (new, belt-and-suspenders)** — Added `MAX_BOND_DEFAULT_REFINANCES = 2` lifetime cap on bond-default refinances per corporation. Each successful refinance increments `Corporation.bondDefaultRefinanceCount`; after the cap, the refinance endpoint returns 400 and the crisis modal disables the button. With the phantom-cash fix above, this now acts as a guardrail against indefinite debt rolls rather than the primary defense against cash extraction. Key files: `src/lib/constants/bonds.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/bond-default/refinance/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/DefaultedBondCrisisModal.tsx`.
- **Marketing → advertising demand rate (20% → 60%)** — `MARKETING_ADVERTISING_DEMAND_RATE` raised from `0.2` to `0.6`. Corporate marketing budgets now convert 3× more aggressively into advertising commodity demand, applying stronger upward pressure on the advertising commodity price. At 0.60, a $1M/day total marketing budget adds 4,000 campaign-units/day (up from 1,333). Key file: `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`.
- **Forex volume pressure weighting** — Exchange rate updates now weight trade volume pressure at 20% and macro fundamentals at 80% (previously 100% additive). Prevents large single-turn player trades from overwhelming macro-driven rate movements. New constant: `VOLUME_DIRECTION_WEIGHT = 0.2`. Key files: `src/lib/constants/currencies.ts`, `src/lib/currency/rateCalculation.ts`.
- **Status bar: political influence display** — Displays as `Math.round(influence)%` (was `influence.toFixed(1)`). Updated tooltip describes PI as a proxy for name recognition rather than just a fundraising multiplier. Favorability tooltip updated to mention opponent attacks. Key file: `src/components/StatusBar.tsx`.
- **Corporate investment portfolio** — Removed the corporation page “Portfolio” tab. Holdings use the same portfolio layout as players at `/portfolio/corporation/[id]` (public) and CEOs can open `/portfolio?corp=...` from Budget for the in-app toggle with personal assets. Balance sheet links to the public portfolio page. Legacy `?tab=portfolio` on a corporation URL redirects to the new route.

### Removed

- **Wiki navigation links** — Removed wiki links from the navbar Help dropdown, mobile menu, and site footer. Wiki search integration and `/wiki` path references removed from navigation components. Admin wiki management remains available.

## [0.2.1] - 2026-04-12

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Government bond subsidy for natcorps** — State-owned enterprises (natcorps) now receive a government contribution that offsets bond interest expense, netting it to zero. The subsidy is visible as a “Government Bond Subsidy” line item in the Interest section of the Financials and CEO Budget tabs. Natcorps are also excluded from bond default checks. Key files: `src/lib/turn/bondTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/FinancialsTab.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/ceo/CeoBudgetSubtab.tsx`.
- **Admin: auto party chair on join toggle** — `GameConfig.firstJoinerBecomesPartyChair` (default on) controls whether joining a party with no national chair promotes the joiner; dashboard section Party mechanics on the main admin tab. `POST /api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/join` respects the flag. Key files: `src/app/api/admin/party/first-joiner-chair/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/FirstJoinerPartyChairPanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/parties/[id]/join/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Corporation and stock chart history gaps** — Backfilled missing `corporationHistory` and `marketCapHistory` entries for turns 12–23 (lost during a turn processor outage). Interpolated from surrounding data points. Cleaned 42 broken natcorp history entries with zeroed-out fields and fixed NaN price change values in stock exchange snapshots.
- **Stock exchange snapshot natcorp income** — `stockExchangeSnapshot.ts` now accounts for the government bond subsidy when calculating natcorp income, matching the corporation page display.
- **Japan (and other) home region list on character creation** — `GET /api/game/states` used `Cache-Control: public` while the payload differs by auth (admins see all states; players see enabled countries only). Shared caches could serve a stale subset so Japan appeared selectable but JP regions were missing. Cache is now `private`; the create flow waits for `/api/game/countries` before showing country tiles and clears a selection that is not server-enabled. **JP-only:** region documents without `countryId` still matched the admin/imperial empty Mongo filter but failed `{ countryId: { $in: enabled } }` for normal players — the states route now unions those rows when Japan is enabled, and create-character filters JP by known region ids when `countryId` is absent. Key files: `src/app/api/game/states/route.ts`, `src/app/create-character/page.tsx`, `src/app/register/components/PoliticianSection.tsx`.
- **Navbar client-nav race and false “signed out” state** — Parallel `/api/client-nav` responses could apply out of order after route changes; non-OK HTTP and repeated network failures cleared nav state and made the bar look logged out. Added per-fetch generation guards, `cache: “no-store”` on the request, and only treat a successful JSON guest payload as logged out (HTTP/transport errors keep last-known nav). Retries pass the same generation and skip when superseded. Key file: `src/components/NavbarWrapper.tsx`.
- **Characterless redirect vs profile** — Users without a character could be redirected away from `/profile` before the nav payload resolved; `/profile` is now allowed without a character alongside settings and create-character. Key file: `src/components/NavbarWrapper.tsx`.
- **Settings `useSearchParams` without Suspense** — Settings page wrapped in `<Suspense>` with a loading fallback to satisfy Next.js client bailout and avoid surfacing through root `error.tsx`. Key file: `src/app/settings/page.tsx`.
- **Settings character merge on error responses** — `/api/auth/character` error JSON is no longer merged into local character state. Key file: `src/app/settings/page.tsx`.
- **Profile header region link for legacy characters** — `countryId` now falls back to the profile URL’s country slug when the character document omits `countryId`, and the home-region link uses that resolved id (avoids invalid `getCountryConfig` / URLs). Key file: `src/app/profile/components/ProfileHeader.tsx`.
- **State party logo country scope** — `PartyLogo` on the state party page now receives `countryId` from the route so party sequential IDs resolve in the correct country. Key file: `src/app/country/[code]/region/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Post-registration onboarding** — Successful registration now routes to `/create-character` instead of `/settings` so new accounts start character creation immediately. Key file: `src/app/register/RegisterPageClient.tsx`.
- **Post–character-create RSC refresh** — After successful character creation, `router.refresh()` runs before navigating to the dashboard so server-driven UI (including nav) sees the new character. Key file: `src/app/create-character/page.tsx`.

- **Turn system pause not respected by cron** — The Vercel cron route (`/api/cron/turn`) was calling `processTurn()` unconditionally, ignoring the `isActive` flag. Pausing the turn system now prevents scheduled turns from firing. Key file: `src/app/api/cron/turn/route.ts`.
- **Turn controls showing stale status after Start/Pause** — `startTurnSystem()` and `stopTurnSystem()` updated the DB but did not invalidate the in-memory game state cache, causing the admin panel to display the old active/paused state for up to 15 seconds. Key file: `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`.
- **Character creation duplicate key error** — Duplicate key (E11000) on `userId` during concurrent or stale-state character creation now returns a clean 409 instead of a 500. Unique constraint on `characters.userId` removed; the application enforces limits via `activeCharacterCount`. Migration: `scripts/migrations/fix-characters-userid-index.ts`. Key files: `src/app/api/auth/character/route.ts`, `src/lib/admin/seed/runCoreSeed.ts`.
- **Maintenance mode blocking Discord registration** — Discord OAuth callback now checks `maintenanceMode` in addition to `testMode` and redirects to the maintenance page when active. Key file: `src/app/api/auth/discord/callback/route.ts`.
- **Register page maintenance redirect** — Register page converted to a server component that server-side redirects to `/maintenance` when maintenance mode is active, preventing the page from loading at all. Key file: `src/app/register/page.tsx`.

## [0.2.0] - 2026-04-10

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Beta launch** — A House Divided transitions from Alpha to Beta. Alpha Countdown component (`AlphaCountdown.tsx`) removed from the changelog page.
- **Private Share Listings** — Shareholders can now list shares for private sale via an accordion panel on the corporation shares tab. Buyers submit competing offers (50–200% of market price at listing time), the seller reviews and accepts any offer in full or in part. Unaccepted escrow is refunded. Listings expire after 24 hours with automatic escrow refunds and share returns via turn processing.
- **Admin activity tracking** — New `activityLog` collection records turn summaries (AP spend, action breadcrumbs), fund events (party transfers, donations, campaign donations), and login/logout events. TTL index auto-expires records after 30 days. Key files: `src/lib/db/types/activityLog.ts`, `src/lib/turn/activityLogging.ts`.
- **Suspicious character detection** — New `suspiciousDetection` turn phase evaluates 7 flag types (IP sharing, fund concentration, AP dump targeting, convertCash pattern, IP scatter, new account max activity) and pre-computes results into `suspiciousCharacters` for O(1) admin reads. Key file: `src/lib/turn/suspiciousDetection.ts`.
- **Admin: Activity Log tab** — Paginated, filterable event log under Players → Activity Log. Cursor-based pagination, expandable rows, filter by type/country/date range/text search. Key files: `src/components/admin/ActivityLogTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/activity-log/route.ts`.
- **Admin: Suspicious Activity tab** — Pre-computed flagged characters under Players → Suspicious. Severity header counts, per-flag detail, one-click dismiss with 30-day suppression, drill-down to activity log. Key files: `src/components/admin/SuspiciousActivityTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/suspicious/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/suspicious/[characterId]/dismiss/route.ts`.
- **Admin registration toggle** — `adminRegistrationEnabled` flag added to `GameConfig`. Admins can disable self-registration with the `ADMIN_REGISTRATION_KEY` from the admin dashboard once enough admins exist. The register route enforces the flag before key validation to avoid timing leaks. Key files: `src/app/api/admin/admin-registration/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/AdminRegistrationPanel.tsx`.
- **Player transfers pause** — New `playerTransfersPaused` field on `GameState`. Admin toggle blocks all character-to-character, party, coalition, and campaign fund transfers when enabled. `requirePlayerTransfers.ts` guard applied to all affected transfer routes. TurnControls panel shows status and toggle button. Key files: `src/lib/api/requirePlayerTransfers.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/turn/toggle-player-transfers/route.ts`.
- **Name moderation** — `MODERATE_PROFANITY_PATTERNS` added to `src/lib/moderation.ts` for character and display name validation. Covers stronger profanity not blocked in general chat, with leet-speak substitution patterns. Applied during character creation and name-change flows.
- **Getting Started recommendations** — New `getting-started` category in the recommendations system generates onboarding suggestions for new players (join a party, set demographics, vote on a bill, run for office). Each suggestion auto-disappears once the condition is met. Key file: `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts`.
- **Suggestions page redesign** — Action suggestions reorganized from priority tiers to named categories (Getting Started, Stat Recovery, Resource Optimization, Market Opportunities, Competitive, Party Actions). Each category shows top 5 recommendations and collapses by default except Getting Started. Key files: `src/app/actions/suggestions/page.tsx`, `src/app/actions/components/RecommendationCard.tsx`.
- **New player banner** — Profile page onboarding checklist replaced with a simpler `NewPlayerBanner` component. Checklist data fetches (vote tallies, wiki read status) removed from the profile page query. Key file: `src/app/profile/components/OnboardingCard.tsx`.
- **Imperial Characters** — Admin accounts can create ceremonial head-of-state characters (King/Queen for UK, Emperor/Empress for Japan) with dedicated profiles, royal house names, coat of arms, and starter corporations (Royal Estate for UK, Chrysanthemum Properties for JP with $50M starting capital). Imperial characters display on country pages with gender-aware titles and are linked to admin accounts with character switching support. New `imperialCharacters` collection, `/imperial/[id]` profile pages, admin creation form at `/create-imperial-character`, and settings integration with imperial-specific sections.
- **Gender-aware government labels** — UK government labels ("His Majesty's Government", "His Majesty's Cabinet") are now dynamically resolved based on the imperial character's gender. Supports "Her Majesty's" and "The Monarch's" variants across all UK pages including executive hub, cabinet, parliament, and legislature pages.
- **Admin Patreon access** — Admin accounts now have full access to all Patreon cosmetic features (borders, GIF avatars, highlight colors) regardless of subscription status, without displaying a fake Supporter+ badge.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Activity logging in auth routes** — Login and logout routes now fire-and-forget write to the `activityLog` collection. Logout reads the JWT before clearing the cookie to capture the user identity. Key files: `src/app/api/auth/login/route.ts`, `src/app/api/auth/logout/route.ts`.
- **Activity logging in transfer routes** — Character transfer, party transfer/donate/send, coalition transfer, regional party donate/send, and campaign donate routes now write fund events to `activityLog` for admin review. Existing business logic is unaffected.
- **TurnLog extended** — `activityLogging` and `suspiciousDetection` result blocks added to the `TurnLog` phases record. Key file: `src/lib/db/types/turnLog.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Cabinet page avatars** — Character avatars with Patreon frames now shown on cabinet pages. Party chips and sequential character profile links added. Key files: `src/app/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/`.
- **GIF avatar uploads** — Supporter and Supporter+ Patreon tiers can now upload animated GIF profile pictures. Key file: `src/app/api/upload/avatar/`.
- **GOTV action suggestion link** — Corrected link target from incorrect path to party treasury tab. Key file: `src/app/api/actions/`.
- **Whip chamber for government votes** — PM appointment and no-confidence whip directives now send the correct chamber identifier. Key file: `src/lib/turn/npp/`.
- **Mobile navbar help links** — Help dropdown links mirrored in mobile menu. Key file: `src/components/Navbar.tsx`.

## [0.1.10] - 2026-04-10

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Japan (JP) country addition** — Japan added as a fully playable parliamentary country. 8 regions (Hokkaido, Tohoku, Kanto, Chubu, Kansai, Chugoku, Shikoku, Kyushu-Okinawa), 6 parties, bicameral National Diet (465-seat Shugiin + 248-seat Sangiin with half-elections), PM formation via confidence vote, snap elections (PM-triggered Shugiin dissolution), cabinet-origin bills with Shugiin 2/3 override mechanic, 10 voter archetypes, 6 Japan-specific metrics (socialCohesion, technologicalInnovation, ruralUrbanDivide, agingPopulationStress, disasterResilience, tradeBalance), Nikkei stock exchange, Emperor as head-of-state NPP, JP sovereign issuer corporation for government debt. JP legislation types and policy effects are not yet implemented. Key files: `src/lib/constants/japan.ts`, `src/lib/turn/jpBillLifecycle.ts`, `src/lib/turn/parliamentaryGovernment.ts`.

- **Japan interactive map** — Full clickable map of Japan's 8 regions built with `react-simple-maps` and real prefecture GeoJSON data. Prefecture polygons merged into region shapes via TopoJSON. Supports mode filters and region list with overview link. Key file: `src/components/japan/JapanMap.tsx`.

- **Japan seed data suite** — Complete seed data for JP: 8 region `State` documents, 6 political parties, 10 voter archetypes with demographic compositions per region, state metrics with JP-specific scopes, state baselines, state party organization data, regional budgets, JP cabinet positions (15 positions) with ministerial orders, JP legislation types, and seat constants with seeder. Orchestrated via `scripts/seeds/seed-jp.ts`. 8 seed targets wired into admin seed tool.

- **Country management admin panel** — Admin Countries tab under World with overview cards showing player counts, toggle buttons with confirmation modals, and DB-driven `enabledForPlayers` / `status` fields on `CountryGameState`. API routes: `GET/PATCH /api/admin/country/[code]/settings`. Character creation and relocation gated on `enabledForPlayers`. 20+ API routes filter results by enabled countries for non-admin users (elections, congress, corporations, bonds, search, leaderboard, etc.). Key files: `src/app/api/admin/country/[code]/settings/route.ts`, `src/lib/countryAccess.ts`.

- **Country access gating** — `countryAccess.ts` utility with TDD test suite gates API responses and user actions by country enabled state. Layout-level gate prevents navigation into disabled countries. Admin users bypass all gates. `countryIdSchema` Zod helper and `enabledForPlayers` field on `CountryGameState` added. `countryId` indexes added to `characters`, `npps`, `politicalParties` collections.

- **General election card redesign** — Redesigned election card visualization with improved layout and added pagination for election listings. Key file: `src/components/elections/`.

- **Wealth list hourly snapshots** — Wealth list now uses hourly snapshots showing 24-hour wealth change and rank movement. Falls back to on-the-fly computation when no snapshot exists. Key file: `src/lib/turn/wealthSnapshot.ts`.

- **Avatar system unification** — Unified PFP display with miniaturized `ProfileBorder` support. Patreon border data plumbed through all major display areas. All avatars switched to square with rounded edges. Fullscreen image viewer added. Key file: `src/components/ui/Avatar.tsx`.

- **Party logos in candidate declarations** — Election candidate declaration badges now display party logos alongside candidate info. Key file: `src/components/elections/CandidateDeclarationBadge.tsx`.

- **Discord user account heal tool** — Admin tool to fix Discord-linked user account linkage issues. Key file: `src/app/api/admin/heal/discord-users/route.ts`.

- **Dynamic unemployment via Okun's law** — GDP growth phase now derives unemployment changes from GDP growth using Okun's law relationship, replacing the static policy-pushed model removed in 0.1.9. Key file: `src/lib/turn/gdpGrowth.ts`.

- **Design documents** — Added `docs/design/japan.md` and `docs/design/japan-elections.md` for Japan game systems. Added UK PM government persistence design spec. Added country management admin design spec and implementation plan.

- **Test coverage expansion** — New tests for `metricDecay`, `seatAllocation`, `candidateEnrichment`, `emptyPartyCleanup`, `generalResolution`, and simulation scenario tests. Updated `billEnactment` tests for `sendCountryGameEvent` migration.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Parliamentary government extraction** — Extracted shared parliamentary logic from UK-specific code into parameterized `parliamentaryGovernment.ts`. Both UK and JP use the same system. `ukGovernmentFormation.ts` and `ukGovernment.ts` now delegate to shared functions. `countryPhases.ts` loops over all parliamentary countries. Reduces ~700 lines of UK-specific code to ~90 lines of thin wrappers.

- **Stock exchange generalization** — Replaced all binary NYSE/FTSE dispatches with config-driven `exchangeRegistry.ts`. Turn processing, API routes, and UI components all generalized for multi-country. Any country with `exchangeName` in config automatically gets a stock exchange page, snapshot, and wealth list. Supports NYSE, FTSE, Nikkei, TSX, DAX.

- **Discord webhook consolidation** — Added `discordCountryGameWebhookUrls` record field and `sendCountryGameEvent` generic dispatcher. Legacy per-country webhook fields preserved with automatic fallback. Admin migration available.

- **Currency display centralization** — Created `getCurrencyPrefix` utility for consistent currency symbols across all budget pages (USD, GBP, JPY, CAD, EUR). `BudgetSummaryCard` now receives `countryId` prop.

- **World page redesign** — Split nation cards into "Select a Nation" (playable) and "Planned Nations" (coming soon) sections. `PlannedCountryCard` height and structure matched to `CountryCard`. Australia moved from featured/beta to coming-soon. Country order updated: US, UK, JP, CA, DE.

- **Globe DB-driven country coloring** — Globe now uses DB-driven country access status for coloring instead of hardcoded lists. Geo ID → CountryId lookup replaces path slug matching. Stable fallback keys for geo features without IDs.

- **Multi-country UI generalization** — Replaced per-country `if`-chains with component registries in legislature, executive, and cabinet pages. `CountryOverviewClient`, approval page, metrics pages, `NationalBudgetClient`, and `StatePartyLinksTab` all use config-driven lookups instead of `isUS`/`isUK` booleans. Region page officials display generalized for multi-country chamber types. `otherChamber()` supports shugiin/sangiin pairs.

- **Admin panel multi-country support** — Hardcoded US/UK scope toggles replaced with `COUNTRY_ORDER` in admin panels and dropdowns. `countryIdSchema` replaces hardcoded country enums in admin API schemas. NPP management uses `CountryId` type from imports.

- **Serverless performance tuning** — Reduced serverless invocations via caching and polling interval tuning. Parallelized queries in admin routes.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Stock market API type safety** — Added type assertions for unknown API response fields in stock market routes, preventing runtime type errors.

- **GDP growth corruption** — Reset corrupted GDP growth values across states. Misc UI updates for economy display.

- **Coalition duplicate members** — Prevented duplicate party entries in coalition members array. Added deduplication checks across invite/accept, join/accept, and admin/add routes.

- **Coalition chair sync on leadership change** — `processCompletedNationalElections()` now updates `coalition.chairCharacterId` when the chair party's leader changes after party elections.

- **Campaign song playback** — Fixed campaign songs stopping after ~1s due to zero-size iframe.

- **Market share display** — Normalized market share against effective market to prevent >100% display values.

- **UK government formation seed** — Seeds `governmentFormations` collection if missing. PM now survives elections (not cleared on election resolution). Verifies PM character exists before seeding as formed.

- **UK no-confidence cooldown display** — Cooldown note now shown on failed no-confidence vote panel.

- **Admin no-confidence handling** — Admin panel reads no-confidence votes from new collection. Clears `activeVoteId` and handles pass/fail correctly.

- **UK government auto-collapse** — Government auto-collapses to pending if PM character no longer exists (handles stale refs after reset).

- **Admin PM appointment** — Admin PM appointment now updates `governmentFormations` with "admin" formation type.

- **Registration form** — Replaced nested form element with anchor link for Discord login button.

- **Admin stale officials** — Cleans up stale vacant records after reassigning multi-seat offices.

### Refactored

- **Bill enactment country routing** — Fixed bill enactment and perpetual elections to use config-driven country routing instead of hardcoded country checks.

- **JP national policy handling** — `demographicEffects.ts` and `policyEffects.ts` extended for JP national scope processing.

- **No-confidence route** — Uses config-driven lower chamber key instead of hardcoded "commons".

## [0.1.9] - 2026-04-07

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **UK government formation redesign — player-driven PM appointment** — Complete overhaul of the UK government formation system. Party Chairs (majority/minority) and Coalition Chairs can manually nominate a Player Character for Prime Minister via a new “Appoint Prime Minister” button on the Commons Leadership tab and Executive page. Goes to a 24-hour Commons-wide vote. NPPs from qualifying parties auto-aye every 4 turns. Three formation paths: majority (≥326 seats), coalition (≥326 combined), minority (≥130 seats). No auto-triggers — government stays in “pending” state until a player acts. New types: `GovernmentFormation`, `PMAppointmentVote`, `NoConfidenceVote`. New collections: `governmentFormations`, `pmAppointmentVotes`, `noConfidenceVotes`. Key files: `src/lib/db/types/governmentFormation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/ukGovernmentFormation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/ukGovernment.ts`.

- **No-confidence vote system** — Any player character Commons MP can propose a no-confidence motion against a sitting PM. All Commons MPs vote. NPP voting uses favorability-based behavior (no auto-votes) but can be whipped with 100% compliance. 48-turn cooldown between motions. 24-hour voting window. If passed: PM removed, cabinet cleared, government returns to pending for fresh formation. Button shown on both Commons Leadership tab and Executive page, greyed out with tooltip during cooldown. Key files: `src/app/api/country/[code]/pm/no-confidence/route.ts`, `src/components/uk/GovernmentVotePanel.tsx`.

- **PM appointment and no-confidence whip integration** — New whip target types `”pmAppointmentVote”` and `”noConfidenceVote”` replace the old `”confidenceVote”`. Whips can be issued by any UK party via the Leadership sub-tab in Party Actions. `applyWhipVotesToGovernmentVote()` immediately applies NPP votes on whip creation. `autoAyeNPPsForAppointment()` respects whip overrides at 100% NPP compliance. Key files: `src/lib/congress/applyWhipVotes.ts`, `src/components/party/WhipPanel.tsx`.

- **Executive page status strip** — Dynamic status display across 5 states: “Awaiting Formation” (pending), “Formed” (majority), “Formed via Coalition”, “Formed via Minority”, “Formed (Lost Majority)”. Coalition governments show “Plurality Coalition” with coalition chip. Commons seats display includes formation type suffix (e.g., `###/326 (coalition)`). Key file: `src/components/uk/UKGovernmentLayout.tsx`.

- **Lost majority detection** — Per-turn seat update phase recalculates `totalSeatsSupporting` from `electedOfficials`. If a formed majority/coalition government's seats drop below 326, the Executive page status updates to “Formed (Lost Majority)” as a signal to players. PM stays in office until a no-confidence vote removes them. Coalition seats update dynamically when coalition membership changes. Key file: `src/lib/turn/ukGovernmentFormation.ts`.

- **GovernmentVotePanel component** — Unified vote display panel for both PM appointment and no-confidence votes. Shows vote type, nominee/target info, aye/nay tallies, countdown timer, and vote buttons for eligible Commons MPs. Replaces `PmNoConfidencePanel` and `MinorityAttemptPanel`. Key file: `src/components/uk/GovernmentVotePanel.tsx`.

- **AppointPMModal component** — Modal for selecting a PC nominee for PM appointment. Fetches eligible candidates from qualifying parties, displays with party name, highlights selection. Key file: `src/components/uk/AppointPMModal.tsx`.

- **Government formation migration script** — One-time migration from `parliamentaryGovernments`/`ukGovernments` to `governmentFormations`. Derives status and formation type from existing data, cancels active legacy votes. Key file: `scripts/migrations/migrateGovernmentFormation.ts`.

- **GDP growth from realized output** — GDP growth is now computed from actual sector revenue changes (owned + unowned) instead of averaging player-set `growthRate` values. New `stateOutputSnapshots` collection tracks per-turn output. All states get numeric GDP growth (no more `null` for states without owned sectors).

- **Unemployment derived from labor market** — Unemployment is now `(labor supply - filled jobs) / labor supply` instead of a directly policy-pushed value. Labor supply = population x laborParticipation rate. Filled jobs = owned sector workers + unowned sector workers. Two new policy-targetable driver metrics: `laborParticipation` (default 63%) and `matchingFriction` (structural floor, default 5%).

- **Macro economy calibration tests** — 19 scenario-based tests covering neutral, recession, overheating, stagflation, and disinflation scenarios plus 8 invariant checks (Phillips curve sign, demand pull sign, unemployment bounds, GDP identity).

- **Migration scripts** — `seed-state-output-snapshots.ts` populates initial output data; `seed-labor-market-metrics.ts` adds `laborParticipation` and `matchingFriction` to all stateMetrics.

- **Bill `countryId` backfill migration** — `scripts/migrations/backfill-bill-country-id.ts` sets `countryId` on bills missing the field using `resolveBillCountryId()`.

- **`resolveBillCountryId` unit tests** — `src/lib/congress/resolveBillCountryId.test.ts` covers pseudo-state ids, persisted `countryId`, `states` lookup, and US legacy fallback.

- **Route contract tests (congress bills + corporations)** — Collocated Vitest coverage for `POST /api/congress/bills` and `POST /api/congress/bills/[id]` (auth, validation, one happy path each) and for `GET /api/corporations/[id]` (invalid id / not found) plus `POST /api/corporations/[id]/settings` (auth, validation, CEO success). Uses `createMockDb` and partial `rateLimit` / `resolveQuery` mocks.

- **Country-agnostic cabinet office system** — Cabinet mechanics generalized across countries with `cabinetMechanics.ts` and `cabinetOrders.ts` configuration. 15 US positions (Secretary of State through Secretary of Homeland Security) and 15 UK positions (Chancellor of the Exchequer through Secretary of State for Wales). New unified `UnifiedCabinetMember` type and `cabinetMembers` collection helper. Key files: `src/lib/constants/cabinetMechanics.ts`, `src/lib/constants/cabinetMechanicsTypes.ts`, `src/lib/constants/cabinetOrders.ts`, `src/lib/constants/usCabinetMechanics.ts`, `src/lib/constants/usCabinetOrders.ts`, `src/lib/constants/ukCabinet.ts`, `src/lib/constants/ukCabinetMechanics.ts`, `src/lib/constants/ukCabinetOrders.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/unifiedCabinetMember.ts`.

- **Ministerial orders system** — Both US and UK cabinets have 2 ministerial orders per position (30 orders each, 60 total). Orders cost 1 ministerial action, last 24 turns, and apply targeted metric modifiers (+/- 3-4%). US examples: Secretary of Treasury's "Fiscal Stimulus" (-3% unemployment), Attorney General's "Federal Task Force" (-4% crime). UK examples: Chancellor's "Emergency Budget Review", Home Secretary's "Enhanced Policing Directive", Health Secretary's "NHS Emergency Funding". Action pool caps at 2, regenerates 1 per 24 turns. New API routes: `POST /api/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/[positionId]/order`, `/setting`, `/allocation`, `/briefing`. Key files: `src/lib/constants/usCabinetOrders.ts`, `src/lib/constants/ukCabinetOrders.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/[positionId]/`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **UK government formation is now player-driven** — Removed all auto-trigger logic (`resolveUKGovernmentFormation`, `triggerNextPMConfidenceVote`, `checkAndInitiateUKFormation`). Government remains in “pending” state indefinitely after elections until a Party Chair or Coalition Chair manually initiates PM appointment. Turn processing reduced to seat updates + vote resolution.

- **Turn processing: country-agnostic phase orchestration** — UK-specific turn phases moved from inline `turnSystem.ts` calls to `countryPhases.ts` registry. `runPostElectionGovernmentPhases` handles post-election reset; `runParliamentaryGovernmentPhases` handles seat updates, vote resolution, and NPP auto-aye. Future parliamentary countries extend the registry without editing `turnSystem.ts`.

- **PM appointment API routes are country-parameterized** — All routes under `/api/country/[code]/pm/` validate country support via `COUNTRY_CONFIGS[countryId].executiveFormation === “confidence_of_legislature”` instead of hardcoding UK. Database queries use the route's `countryId` parameter throughout. Any future parliamentary country will automatically work.

- **Race condition prevention on vote creation** — PM appointment and no-confidence proposal routes use atomic `findOneAndUpdate` with `activeVoteId: null` filter to prevent concurrent vote creation. Orphaned vote documents cleaned up on race loss.

- **Vote casting enforces time boundary** — Both PM appointment and no-confidence vote routes reject votes after `closesAt`, even if the turn processor hasn't yet resolved the vote.

- **Fiscal year uses GDP pipeline** — `processFiscalYear()` reads GDP growth from `stateMetrics` (realized-output pipeline) instead of a static 2.5% default. Each state's fiscal year uses per-state GDP growth. Debt penalty no longer directly mutates `gdpGrowth` — debt already affects the economy through sector margin modifiers.

- **Inflation rate-lag model** — Spot prime rate now gets 30% immediate effect on inflation (was ~8%). Remaining 70% propagates via trailing weighted average over 12 turns. Rate cuts/hikes are felt meaningfully on the same turn.

- **Commodity demand GDP-weighted** — National GDP growth average for retail/building-material demand scaling is now GDP-weighted (larger economies contribute proportionally more) instead of simple average.

- **Publisher / SEO surface** — Root metadata, Open Graph, Twitter, and JSON-LD describe multi-country play (US, UK, CA, DE). Landing footer adds About and Contact. `/news` is a server page with dedicated metadata plus crawlable intro text; interactive UI moved to `NewsPageClient`. Country politicians index includes a short server-rendered directory blurb. Wiki index metadata and hero copy expanded for clarity.

- **Congress bill country handling** — Server routes and `onBillEnacted` use `resolveBillCountryId()` instead of `uk_` `stateId` heuristics; bill detail responses include `countryId`. Client bill page and timeline prefer `countryId === “UK”` with `stateId` fallback until legacy rows are backfilled.

- **`onBillEnacted` national scope** — Treats any pseudo-state id that maps via `inferCountryIdFromStateId()` (including `ca_national` / `de_national`) as national for enacted-law scope. Discord “View Bill” links for national bills use `/congress/bills/[id]`; location line uses country name for non-US/UK nationals.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Growth cost formula** — Normalized prime rate multiplier from raw rate (3.75x) to `1 + rate/10` (1.375x). Growth costs were ~3x too expensive.

- **Concurrent turn processing** — Added atomic `isProcessing` lock on GameState to prevent duplicate cron invocations from double-processing sector costs via `$inc` stacking.

- **Growth API countryId crash** — Added state lookup fallback when sector/corporation `countryId` is undefined, preventing TypeError in the growth rate adjustment endpoint.

- **Vitest harness for election + UK government** — `requireAuthWithCharacter` is mocked in election entry integration tests and national party election tests; `ukGovernment.test.ts` mocks `@/lib/turnSystem` to avoid loading the full turn orchestrator (circular import timeout).

- **Share order fill amount** — Share order fill was sending `shares: 0` instead of the actual fill amount.

- **Cabinet page loading** — US cabinet page no longer endlessly loads on API error.

- **Coalition duplicate members** — Fixed a bug where parties could be added to coalition members multiple times. Added deduplication checks in invite/accept, join/accept, and admin/add routes.

- **Coalition chair not updating on leadership change** — Fixed `processCompletedNationalElections()` to update `coalition.chairCharacterId` when a party chair is elected if that party is the coalition chair party. Previously, coalition chairs showed stale leadership after party elections.

### Removed

- **Legacy UK government formation components** — `PmNoConfidencePanel`, `MinorityAttemptPanel`, `minorityAttemptNominee.ts`, `minorityAttemptDisplay.ts` deleted. Legacy API routes `/pm/minority-attempt` and `/pm/confidence/[voteId]/vote` removed. Legacy `applyWhipVotesToConfidence` function removed.

- **Legacy turn processing functions** — `resolveUKGovernmentFormation`, `triggerNextPMConfidenceVote`, `processNoConfidenceVotes`, `processConfidenceVotes`, and related helpers removed from `ukGovernment.ts`.

### Refactored

- **`corporateGdpGrowth.ts` → `gdpGrowth.ts`** — Replaced revenue-weighted growthRate averaging with realized output measurement. Old module deleted.

- **National metrics aggregation** — Removed `statesWithSectors` exclusion filter. All states (including those with only unowned sectors) now contribute to GDP-weighted national metrics.

## [0.1.8] - 2026-04-07

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Architecture audit script** — New `scripts/architecture-audit.ts` detects layer violations: `request.json()` in API routes, `jwtVerify()` outside auth modules, `src/lib` importing from `src/app/api`, and `src/lib` importing from `scripts/`. Outputs a summary table with violation counts and file paths.

- **Unit tests for auth helpers** — Added test coverage for `requireAuth()` and `requireAdmin()` helpers in `src/lib/api/requireAuth.test.ts` and `src/lib/api/requireAdmin.test.ts`.

- **Unit tests for `getOfficeLabel`** — `src/lib/utils/politics.test.ts` covers US/UK/CA/DE executive titles and Bundestag seating labels.

- **Japan readiness audit docs** — New audit documents for Japan country implementation: readiness audit plan, findings, backlog, and remediation plan. `docs/audits/2026-04-07-reset-japan-*.md`.

- **Seed bootstrap call graph** — Documentation of seed function dependencies and call order. `docs/engineering/seed-bootstrap-call-graph.md`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Architecture layer standardization** — Eliminated all architecture layer violations. Seed handlers moved from `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/` to `src/lib/admin/seed/` (11 files). `LEADERSHIP_ROLES` constant moved to `src/lib/congress/leadershipRoles.ts`. `initializeOfficials` moved to `src/lib/admin/bootstrap/initializeOfficials.ts`. `metricDefinitions` moved from `scripts/seeds/` to `src/lib/constants/metricDefinitions.ts` with re-export for backwards compatibility. Seed data files moved from `scripts/seeds/` to `src/lib/seeds/reference/` with re-exports for backwards compatibility (12 files: basePolicies, budgets, formulaGrants, gameConfig, legislationTypes, policies, politicalParties, stateBaselines, stateMetrics, statePartyOrg, states).

- **API validation standardization** — All API routes now use `parseJsonBody()` with Zod schemas instead of direct `request.json()` calls (16 routes updated). All routes using JWT verification now use `requireAdminOrApiKey()` helper instead of direct `jwtVerify()` calls (4 routes updated).

- **Design docs link fixes** — Updated relative links in design documents to use correct paths after file reorganization.

- **Office label system country-aware** — `getOfficeLabel(office, countryId)` now accepts optional `countryId` and uses country office config for correct executive, legislature, and sub-national titles. Added `executiveRealmPhrase` on US and UK configs for proper “of the United States” / “of the United Kingdom” wording.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Career history for presidential and executive offices** — US presidential resolution now appends `careerHistory` for winners (President and player VP) and for losing player candidates. UK PM appointment and US presidential succession record `appointed` events for players. Profile and retired profile career sections derive display titles with country-aware `getOfficeLabel`.

- **UK cabinet appointments** — Fixed country-scoped cabinet routes to use `countryId` parameter correctly. New routes: `GET /api/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/characters`, `POST /api/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/appoint`, `POST /api/country/[code]/executive/cabinet/fire`. `src/lib/uk/cabinetApi.ts`, `src/lib/uk/cabinetEligibility.ts`.

- **Profile/retired page cleanup** — Simplified retired profile page rendering, removed dead code paths.

## [0.1.7] - 2026-04-06

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **UK legislation overhaul — 55 legislation types** — Complete rework of UK legislation with 34 national (Parliament) and 14 regional (Council) policy types, plus 7 tax types (5 national, 2 regional). Every type has LARP-style titled options with descriptions, £/cap costs, economic/social scores, and weighted metric mappings. Categories adapted to UK political reality: NHS-based healthcare (not insurance), Universal Credit welfare, civil liberties (surveillance/drug policy instead of gun control/reproductive rights), devolution governance, and BBC/media regulation. Replaces the previous 27 UK types. Key files: `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts` (55 UK type definitions), `scripts/seeds/basePolicies.ts` (UK national + regional defaults).

- **UK regional budget constraint system** — UK regions operate under a balanced-budget mechanic unique to the UK. Regional budget = Council Tax revenue + Business Rates revenue + Westminster grant (from `uk_local_government_funding` national bill). Enacted regional spending cannot exceed budget. If over budget for >1 turn, forced austerity auto-downgrades the most expensive programme one option level per turn. Property and commercial value bases drift dynamically based on investment (0.3%/turn normal, 0.5%/turn in deficit, 25%–300% guardrails). `RegionalBudget` collection stores per-region fiscal state. Future Chancellor of the Exchequer office hook distributes Westminster grant (even 1/12th split until implemented). New turn phase in Group 14. Key files: `src/lib/turn/regionalBudget.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/regionalBudget.ts`, `src/lib/db/collections/regionalBudgets.ts`.

- **14 UK-specific game metrics** — New metrics: `nhsWaitingTime`, `mentalHealthAccess`, `socialCareQuality` (healthcare); `gcseAttainment`, `universityEnrollment`, `apprenticeshipRate` (education); `antiSocialBehaviourRate`, `knifeCrimeRate` (public safety); `floodRisk` (environment); `childPoverty`, `housingAffordability`, `roughSleeping` (social); `devolutionSatisfaction` (governance); `bbcTrust` (media). `propertyValueIndex` and `commercialValueIndex` track dynamic value bases for the budget system. 4 US-only metrics excluded from UK: `uninsuredRate`, `affordabilityIndex`, `highSchoolGradRate`, `collegeEnrollment`. Country scoping via `countryScope` field on `MetricDefinition`. Key files: `scripts/seeds/metricDefinitions.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/stateMetrics.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/uk/ukStateMetrics.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/uk/ukStateBaselines.ts`.

- **Country-aware federal multiplier** — `UK_FEDERAL_MULTIPLIER = 1/12` for UK (12 regions) vs existing `FEDERAL_MULTIPLIER = 1/50` for US (50 states). `getFederalMultiplier(countryId)` helper selects the correct value. Both `policyEffects.ts` and `demographicEffects.ts` now use country-aware multipliers. Key files: `shared/constants/formulas.ts`, `src/lib/policyEffects.ts`, `src/lib/demographicEffects.ts`.

- **UK regional budget UI** — Budget summary panel on UK regional metrics page showing Council Tax Revenue, Business Rates Revenue, Westminster Grant, total budget, enacted spending, and surplus/deficit with colour-coded border (green/yellow/red). Property Value Index and Commercial Value Index displayed under Economy metrics for UK regions. Budget info included in regional bills API responses. Key files: `src/components/uk/UKRegionPageTabsMetrics.tsx`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/legislature/bills/route.ts`, `src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/metrics/route.ts`.

- **Admin seeder: UK Legislation target** — New "UK Legislation" partial seed target that refreshes only UK legislation types without touching US types. Key file: `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedUkLegislation.ts`.

- **Admin seeder: Split US/UK budgets** — "Budgets" target split into separate "US Budgets" and "UK Budgets" checkboxes with independent handlers. Renamed UK "State" labels to "Region" (UK State Metrics → UK Region Metrics, UK State Party Orgs → UK Region Party Orgs). Key files: `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedBudgets.ts` (US only), `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedUkBudgets.ts` (new), `src/components/admin/UniversalSeeder.tsx`.

- **Sector page redesign** — Complete layout overhaul of the corporation sector detail page. New two-column layout with `HeroCard` (stats strip at top), `MarginsPanel` collapsed by default with categories grouped, and a collapsible `ManagementPanel` for CEO-only controls. `AttackPanel` restyled as a standard card and hidden when no actions are available. `MarketPositionPanel` gains a `compact` prop for sidebar use. `FinancialsPanel` drops the redundant stats grid. `MarketPie` gains a `size` prop. Key files: `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/`.

- **Wiki private article visibility** — Admin-only wiki pages can be marked private and are hidden from non-admin users. `src/app/wiki/`.

- **Coalition link in invite notifications** — Coalition membership invite notifications now include a direct link to the coalition page. `src/lib/notifications/`.

- **Staging server landing page notice** — When `testMode` is enabled in `GameConfig`, the landing page displays a blue staging-server banner explaining that this is a preview environment for upcoming features, restricted to Supporter+ Patreon members. The bottom CTA section also renders a staging-specific variant with "Register with Test Code" and "Get Supporter+ Access" (links to Patreon) buttons. `src/app/page.tsx`.

- **Discord bot: scoped API key, rate limits, and blackjack house edge** — The Discord bot API integration uses a scoped API key, enforces rate limits, and the blackjack minigame now applies a configurable house edge.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **UK budgets missing on game reset** — UK regional budgets are now seeded during game reset; the budget UI is guarded against missing budget documents to prevent render errors.

- **Settings sections hidden** — Resolved a Tailwind v4 cascade specificity issue that was causing settings page sections to be hidden. `src/app/settings/`.

- **Appointment notification attribution** — Admin-issued appointment notifications now read "by an admin" instead of showing a blank attribution. `src/lib/notifications/`.

## [0.1.6] - 2026-04-05

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Action recommendations system** — New personalized recommendation engine surfaces contextual action suggestions based on character stats, market conditions, and party state. `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts` implements five generators: stat threshold checks (low AP/funds/influence/favorability), unowned sector opportunities (consolidated by sector type, top 5 globally), competitive market position gaps, party treasury/org-building prompts, and vacant party positions. `GET /api/actions/recommendations` route assembles all context (home state economy, all-state economies, market positions, party budget/org, corporations) and calls `generateRecommendations()`. Results are sorted by priority and capped at 10. `src/lib/actions/recommendationsConstants.ts` holds all tuneable thresholds.

- **Action Suggestions page** — New `/actions/suggestions` dashboard with full hero header (actions hero image, stats strip showing AP/funds/influence/favorability), recommendations grouped by priority (Critical → High → Medium → Low), back button to Actions page, and per-category mute settings. `src/app/actions/suggestions/page.tsx`, `src/app/actions/suggestions/SuggestionSettingsModal.tsx`. The Actions page retains a narrow suggestions strip with priority indicator lights and a link to the full dashboard.

- **Commodity page redesign** — Full rebuild of the commodity detail page. New components: `HeroPanel` (price + supply/demand headline), `DemandDriverBanner`, `SupplyDemandBar`, `ProductionFlow`, `RegionalBreakdown`, `TopProducersConsumers`, and interactive world/country maps (`CommodityWorldMapView`, `CommodityCountryStatCard`, `CommodityRegionMap`). Charts live in `src/app/commodity/[type]/components/charts/`. `src/app/commodity/[type]/page.tsx`.

- **Sector market actions unified** — `AttackPanel` on sector detail pages now combines attack and split into a single "Market Actions" panel. Visiting another corporation's sector page exposes both attack (capture their market share) and split (take unowned share in the same state×sector) from a single view. `showAttack` prop gates the attack section so the panel renders for both own-corp and rival-corp contexts. `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/sections/AttackPanel.tsx`.

- **Sector subsidies** — Legislatures can now pass industry bills to grant or end sector subsidies. Active subsidies give a flat +15 percentage-point profit margin bonus to qualifying corporate sectors; federal and state subsidies stack freely (+30pp total). Subsidies can target all sectors (economy-wide) or a specific sector type, with an optional operating strategy filter and a domestic-only flag (federal = same-country HQ; state = same-state HQ). A new `"end_subsidy"` provision type nullifies an existing matching subsidy. New `"industry"` bill category covers subsidy legislation for both federal and state bills. Budget impact is tracked each turn as `spending.byCategory.sectorSubsidies` on federal and state budget documents (annual cost = qualifying sector revenue × `SUBSIDY_COST_MULTIPLIER`). A new Subsidies tab on the Congress page lists all active national subsidies. Corporation pages show an Active Subsidies panel listing subsidies that benefit the corp. New API endpoint `GET /api/subsidies?countryId=X`. Key files: `src/lib/subsidies/subsidyEffects.ts`, `src/lib/turn/subsidyBudgetTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporationTurn.ts`, `src/lib/legislationEffects.ts`, `src/components/corporation/SubsidyBenefits.tsx`, `src/app/api/subsidies/route.ts`.

- **Persistent unowned sectors** — Unowned sector revenue is now stored as `unownedSectors` documents (one per state×sectorType) instead of being computed as a gap from state GDP. Seeded at 10% of the GDP-derived market size per sector; grows each turn at the average `growthRate` of same-type same-state corporate sectors (fallback 1%/turn). New `processUnownedSectorGrowth` turn phase in Group 14. Auto-seeds on first turn after deploy if collection is empty; also available as "Unowned Sectors" target in admin Universal Seeder. Split and economy routes read from DB with fallback to computed gap for pre-seed edge cases. Key files: `src/lib/turn/unownedSectorGrowth.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedUnownedSectors.ts`.

- **Privacy Policy page** — New `/privacy` page covering data collection (Vercel Analytics, Speed Insights), MongoDB storage, HTTP-only cookie auth, and user rights. `src/app/privacy/page.tsx`.

- **Terms of Service page** — New `/terms` page with game rules, account responsibilities, prohibited conduct, and limitation of liability. `src/app/terms/page.tsx`.

- **Site footer** — A footer with links to Privacy Policy, Terms of Service, About, and Contact is now visible on all pages.

- **About & Contact pages** — New `/about` and `/contact` pages with full SEO metadata (OpenGraph, Twitter cards, JSON-LD structured data, canonical links). `src/app/about/page.tsx`, `src/app/contact/page.tsx`.

- **AdSense compliance** — Registration form includes a policy acceptance checkbox linking to Privacy Policy and Terms of Service. Policy links added to the site footer for all pages.

- **Sitemap expanded** — `sitemap.xml` now includes congress legislature pages, parties, world map, and corporations pages in addition to existing entries.

- **Politicians page server-rendered** — The politicians listing switched from client-side rendering to SSR for crawler and SEO visibility.

- **Patreon integration** — New OAuth flow for Patreon supporters. Players can link their Patreon account via Settings → Patreon to receive in-game benefits. Webhook handlers process pledge events (create, update, delete, members events) in real-time. Two tiers: `"supporter"` (base) and `"supporter-plus"`. 30-day grace period on expired pledges (`PATREON_GRACE_PERIOD_MS`). Achievement awarded for Supporter Plus. Admin Patreon Management tab for manual tier overrides and lookup. `src/lib/patreon/`, `src/app/api/patreon/`, `src/app/api/webhooks/patreon/`, `src/components/admin/PatreonManagementTab.tsx`.

- **Patreon profile borders** — 24 border styles across 5 groups selectable in Settings for active supporters. **Default:** `default-tint`. **Static** (Supporter+): `soft-glow`, `double-ring`, `etched-band`. **Animated** (Supporter+): `comet` (Comet Ring), `signal-beacon`, `aurora` (Aurora Ribbon), `prism`, `ember-crown`, `ion-storm`, `starlight` (Starlight Orbit), `pulse`, `spotlight`. **Frame** (Supporter+): `picture-frame`, `gallery-frame`, `silver-frame`, `obsidian-frame`. **Legacy:** gold/silver/platinum/crimson variants and `party-sync`. Tintable borders blend with the user's chosen highlight color. Borders render around profile avatars via `ProfileBorder` component on all profile and character pages. `src/lib/db/types/patreon.ts`, `src/components/patreon/ProfileBorder.tsx`.

- **Patreon supporter badge** — `PatreonBadge` component displays tier label ("Supporter" / "Supporter+"), supporter duration (e.g., "3 months"), and expiry indicator on profile pages. `src/components/patreon/PatreonBadge.tsx`.

- **Patreon cosmetic settings** — Settings page gains a Patreon Benefits section for active supporters: border style picker (grouped by category, live preview), highlight color picker, and GIF avatar toggle (Supporter+ only). Choices persist to `user.patreonProfileBorder`, `user.patreonHighlightColor`, `user.patreonAdPreference`. `src/components/settings/PatreonBenefitsSection.tsx`.

- **Animated GIF avatars** — Supporters can upload `.gif` profile pictures. The avatar upload route enforces that GIF uploads require an active `"supporter-plus"` tier; non-supporters' GIF uploads are rejected with a 403. `src/app/api/upload/avatar/route.ts`.

- **Patreon benefit notifications** — Users receive a system notification when their Patreon benefits are granted or updated, thanking them and linking to the changelog. `src/lib/patreon/service.ts`.

- **Corporation sector naming** — CEOs can now set custom display names for individual corporate sectors (e.g., renaming "Agriculture" to "Heartland Farming Operations"). Names appear throughout the UI and can be cleared to revert to the default sector type label. `POST /api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/name`, `src/components/corporation/SectorsTab.tsx`, `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/page.tsx`.

- **Election turnout wiring (Phases 1–2)** — Canvassing, GOTV, and voter suppression actions now measurably affect election outcomes. New `src/lib/electionEngine/resolvedTurnout.ts` unifies turnout calculation between polls and elections; it computes effective turnout per demographic group by combining static `StateDemographics` baselines with dynamic `StateDemographicTurnout` modifiers (±20 percentage points) from player actions and party spending. State elections (`accumulateVoteTurn`) and presidential elections (`accumulatePresidentVoteTurn`) now load turnout modifiers and pass live turnout rates to vote distribution. Poll commissioning uses the same resolver via `buildLiveTurnouts()`, ensuring poll projections and actual election results share identical turnout inputs. Added 9 integration tests proving turnout changes alter vote shares. Key files: `src/lib/electionEngine/resolvedTurnout.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/turnoutWiring.integration.test.ts`, `src/lib/electionEngine/tallyManagement.ts`, `src/lib/presidentialElectionEngine.ts`, `src/app/api/actions/poll/route.ts`.

- **Presidential influence double-counting fixed** — Presidential races no longer count candidate influence in both reach (via `useNationalInfluenceForReach: true`) and appeal (previously `includeInfluenceInAppeal: true`). Removed appeal-side influence weighting so ideology alignment matters more than raw fame. Adjusted diagnostic test bands to honest baselines (CA/NY: ~55% Dem, TX: ~42% Dem, PA: ~50% Dem). `src/lib/presidentialElectionEngine.ts`, `src/lib/presidentialBalanceDiagnostic.test.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **PoliticalCompass quadrant colors** — Updated to red (authoritarian-left), blue (authoritarian-right), green (libertarian-left), purple (libertarian-right) for clearer ideological distinction. Previously used blue/amber/teal blends. `src/components/PoliticalCompass.tsx`.

- **In-game update notifications** — When a new changelog version is posted (via the Discord webhook), all active players now receive a system notification announcing the update and linking to the changelog. `src/lib/discordChangelog.ts`.

- **Primary election display** — Replaced vertical list layout with compact card-based grid. Each party primary now displays as a card with prominent candidate name, party-colored left border, larger avatar (24px), and results bar always visible (even for uncontested races at 100%). Cards arrange in a responsive grid (1-4 columns based on viewport). New `PrimaryCard` and `PrimaryCardGrid` components. `src/components/elections/PrimaryCard.tsx`, `src/components/elections/ElectionCard.tsx`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Party organization rounding** — Fixed floating point display issues in party organization values (e.g., `53.791000000000002` now displays as `53.79`). Organization, cap, and momentum values are now rounded to 2 decimal places at storage and display time. `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/turnProcessing.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/calculations.ts`, `src/components/state/politics/PartyOrganization.tsx`.

- **InfoTooltip on mobile** — Prevents double-tap zoom via `e.preventDefault()`, adds `touch-manipulation` CSS and minimum touch target dimensions (`min-h-[24px] min-w-[24px]`), and blocks scroll propagation via `onTouchStart`. `src/components/InfoTooltip.tsx`.

- **Info icon blocking pointer events** — Info icons in `FinancialOverview` and `PoliticalStanding` used `inline` display without `pointer-events-none`, causing them to intercept clicks on surrounding text. Changed to `inline-block pointer-events-none`.

- **State officials card layout** — Fixed truncated names, overlapping NPP badges, and party labels extending past card borders in the House/State Senate sections. Avatar increased from 64px to 80px, names use `line-clamp-2` instead of `truncate`, party badges stack vertically with proper width constraints. `src/components/state/politics/OfficialCard.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Recommendation links country-aware** — All party and region links generated by `generateRecommendations()` now use `character.countryId.toLowerCase()` instead of hardcoded `"us"`, so UK/CA/DE players receive correct `/country/uk/...` URLs. `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts`.

- **Party org-building recommendation priority** — Raised from `"low"` to `"high"` — a party at 0/N organization is a significant missed opportunity, not a cosmetic suggestion. `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts`.

- **Recommendation details enriched** — `ActionRecommendation.action` now carries `targetStateName` (human-readable, e.g. "South East England" instead of "UK_SEE"), `targetUnownedRevenue` (for sector opportunity cards), and `targetPartyName` (party display name for party recommendations). API route fetches party `name` field alongside `slug`. `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts`, `src/app/api/actions/recommendations/route.ts`.

- **Competitive sector recommendations link to sector pages** — Market position recommendations now link to `/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]` when the sector `_id` is available, instead of the generic corporation page. The API route includes `sectorId` on each `CorpMarketPosition`. `src/app/api/actions/recommendations/route.ts`, `src/lib/actions/recommendations.ts`.

### Refactored

- **Corporation turn modularization** — `corporationTurn.ts` split into focused modules: `buildCorporationLookups.ts`, `processSectors.ts`, `fillPendingShareOrders.ts`, `snapshotMarketCap.ts`, and a thin orchestrator. Eliminates the 1000+ line monolith.

- **Election resolution modularization** — `electionResolution.ts` refactored into a thin orchestrator. Extracted: `enrichElection.ts` (candidate enrichment + dep fetching), `electionNotifications.ts` (batched result dispatch), `generalResolution.ts` (`resolveOneGeneralElection`), `electionResponseTypes.ts` (shared response interfaces), plus `buildPollingData`/`computeSeatEstimates` in their own modules. `src/lib/turn/election/`.

- **Rate limiting standardization** — All player-facing API routes now use consistent `checkRateLimit()` calls with predefined limit constants (`AUTH_LIMITS`, `CONGRESS_LIMITS`, `ELECTION_LIMITS`, `FEEDBACK_LIMITS`). `src/lib/api/rateLimit.ts`.

- **SharesTab modularization** — The monolithic `SharesTab.tsx` is decomposed into focused panel components under `src/components/corporation/shares/`: `MarketOverviewPanel`, `MyHoldingsPanel`, `BuyFromFloatPanel`, `PublicIssuancePanel`, `SelfIssuancePanel`, `LimitOrdersPanel`, `OpenOrdersPanel`, `ShareStructurePanel`, `ShareholderRegister`, `ShareholderPieChart`, `SignInPrompt`. Custom hooks live in `src/components/corporation/shares/hooks/`.

## [0.1.5] - 2026-04-04

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Tariffs system** — Legislatures can now pass trade bills (new `”trade”` category) to impose tariffs on foreign corporations operating within their country. Tariffs are scoped as economy-wide, sector-specific, origin-country, or corporation-specific, and stack additively up to 100%. Foreign corps face a margin penalty equal to the effective tariff rate; domestic corps pay a smaller supply-chain malus (up to -10pp at 100% tariff). Split capture multipliers scale linearly: domestic corps gain up to 1.5× advantage splitting tariffed foreign sectors; foreign corps lose down to 0.5× when splitting into tariffed markets. Commodity price blending shifts from 75/25 global/local toward 50/50 as tariff coverage increases. A bill at 0% rate nullifies an existing tariff (retained for audit). Tariffs are enforced by territorial invariant: a UK tariff on a US corp only affects its UK sectors. New Tariffs tab on all legislature pages; Trade Restrictions panel on corporation pages. Admin tools allow force-set and removal. Key files: `src/lib/tariffs/tariffEffects.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporationTurn.ts`, `src/lib/legislationEffects.ts`, `src/app/api/tariffs/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/tariffs/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/TariffRestrictions.tsx`.

- **Account-Character Separation** — Accounts and characters are now independent lifecycles. Registration creates an account only (email/username/password); character creation is a separate branded page at `/create-character`. Characters can be retired (soft-archived) while preserving the account, achievements, and a frozen profile snapshot. New `retiredCharacters` collection stores snapshots with full stats, career history, party name, demographics, and IRL active dates. Achievements are now account-bound (`characterAchievements.userId` is the primary FK instead of `characterId`); the `getAccountAchievements()` function replaces `getCharacterAchievements()`. Auth system resolves active character via `user.activeCharacterId` with userId ownership check. Navigation guard blocks game pages for characterless accounts (only Settings/Help/Wiki/Create-Character accessible). Settings page restructured into Account sections (always visible) and Character sections (requires active character). Character retirement cleans up elected offices, election candidacies, CEO positions, shareholdings, coalition chair, party membership/leadership, endorsements, and action logs. Game reset (soft) auto-retires all characters with snapshots instead of zeroing stats. Read-only retired character profile page at `/retired/[id]` shows archived career data. Admin panel gains Retire Character / Delete Account / View Retired actions on Users tab. Migration at Admin > Support > Migrations backfills `userId` on achievements, sets `activeCharacterId`/`activeCharacterCount` on users, creates `retiredCharacters` collection with indexes, and drops the unique `userId` index on characters. Key files: `src/lib/retireCharacter.ts`, `src/lib/achievements/index.ts`, `src/app/create-character/page.tsx`, `src/app/retired/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/components/settings/RetiredCharactersSection.tsx`, `src/components/settings/CharacterDangerZone.tsx`.

- **Corporation portfolio** — Corporations can now hold stocks and bonds. New Portfolio tab on corporation pages shows holdings with real-time prices, cost basis, unrealized P&L, and accrued bond interest. Buy and Sell modals support both character and corporation buyers/sellers. The SharesTab on character portfolios gains a **Buy as Corporation** toggle for CEOs. Limit orders extended to support corporate placers. A self-dealing guard prevents a corporation from trading its own shares. `creditSharesToCorp`/`debitSharesFromCorp` atomic ops added to the equity ledger; `avgCostPerShare` tracked per holder for cost-basis reporting. Corp-owned rows are guarded during bond dissolution and Discord bot routes. Rate limit keys namespaced separately for corp vs. character actions. Key files: `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/portfolio/route.ts`, `src/components/corporation/PortfolioTab.tsx`, `src/components/corporation/PortfolioSellModal.tsx`.

- **Image upload dimension hints** — Profile header, avatar, corporation banner/logo, and party logo upload areas show recommended pixel sizes and aspect ratios (with screen-reader descriptions via `aria-describedby`). `src/lib/constants/uploadImageHints.ts`, `ProfileHeaderImageUpload.tsx`, `ProfilePictureUpload.tsx`, `CorporationHero.tsx`, `CeoOfficeTab.tsx`, `ChairOfficeTab.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Central bank lobbying caps** — Maximum contribution per request raised from $50,000 to $500,000; default/step size in the UI is $10,000. Bounds live in `src/lib/constants/centralBankLobby.ts`; `POST .../central-bank/lobby` validates against the same values.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **County map showing uniform statewide color** — `distributeCountyVotes` applies Cook PVI shifts by checking `party === “democrat”` / `”republican”`, but the `candidateParties` map passed to it contained sequentialId strings (e.g. `”1”`, `”2”`), so `pviShift` was always 0 and every county received identical statewide vote shares. Fixed by fetching party docs before distribution and mapping sequentialId → lean name via `economicPosition` (negative = democrat, positive = republican). `src/app/api/elections/[id]/state/[stateId]/county-results/route.ts`.

- **NPP whip votes not overriding existing votes** — Whip directives skipped NPPs who had already cast a vote, so a second whip action or a whip applied after turn-processing had no effect. Whips now override conflicting existing votes (adjusting tallies by subtracting the old vote before adding the new one) while preserving votes that already align with the directive. `src/lib/congress/applyWhipVotes.ts`.

- **National budget surplus using stale spending** — `refreshNationalBudgetRevenue` calculated surplus using `budget.spending.total` from the previous calculation rather than recomputing from current enacted laws and debt interest first. This caused incorrect deficit values for sovereign bond issuance. `src/lib/budget/revenue.ts`.

- **Central bank “Fund another candidate”** — After any lobbying totals existed, the page only listed candidates who already had contributions, so players could not start funding a different nominee or wealth-pool candidate. The full candidate picker and **Fund another candidate** control stay available whenever there are eligible targets. `CentralBankClient.tsx`.

## [0.1.4] - 2026-04-03

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Error codes endpoint** — `GET /api/error-codes` returns the full list of API error codes and their meanings as JSON, enabling client-side error message lookup and integration documentation. `src/app/api/error-codes/route.ts`.

- **UK Regional Council** — Sub-national elected body for all 12 UK regions with 364 total seats (based on real-world local government council counts). Proportional multi-seat elections synchronized with Commons cycle (5-year terms, 72h primary/general). Full regional legislation system — Regional Councillors can propose and vote on regional bills, which auto-enact on passage (no governor veto via `stateBillLifecycle.ts`). NPPs enter elections and fill seats using region-appropriate party distribution via `getMajorPartiesForRegion()`. Legislature page at `/country/uk/region/[id]/legislature` shows "Regional Council" label with composition and bills tabs. Admin Universal Seeder gains "UK Regional Council" target that seeds elections synced to current Commons timing, populates NPP officials, and updates `stateSenateSeats` on State documents. Mutually exclusive with Commons seats. New office type `regionalCouncil` added to `OfficeType` union, `ElectedOfficial`, country config, election labels, and seat allocation (10% threshold). Election spawning via `ensureUKRegionalCouncilElections()` in turn system Group 9. Key files: `src/lib/turn/perpetualElections.ts`, `src/lib/turn/election/seatAllocation.ts`, `src/lib/turn/electionResolution.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedUK.ts`.

- **NI Parties seed target** — Admin Universal Seeder gains "NI Parties" target under UK that seeds only the Democratic Unionist Party (DUP) and Sinn Féin without affecting other parties. Uses upsert pattern — creates if missing, updates if existing. `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedUK.ts:seedNIParties()`.

- **Portfolio value charts** — Line charts for tracking portfolio value over time on both self profile (`/profile`) and other character profiles (`/character/[id]`). Users can toggle between view modes: Total, Stocks, Bonds, Cash, or a Breakdown view showing all three series. Charts require at least 2 turns of history data. Components: `src/components/charts/PortfolioChart.tsx` (updated with series view support), `src/app/character/[id]/components/PortfolioChartSection.tsx` (new client component).

- **Portfolio history breakdown tracking** — The `portfolioHistory` collection now stores per-turn breakdown values (`stockValue`, `bondValue`, `cashValue`) in addition to `totalValue`. The turn processor (`src/lib/turn/portfolioSnapshot.ts`) captures all three components when snapshotting portfolios. API routes return the full breakdown for charts. Type definition updated in `src/lib/db/types/portfolioHistory.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Legislature composition missing countryId** — Party logos in the legislature composition chart used US logos for UK parties because the composition API response and client-side mapping omitted `countryId`. Fixed in both the API route (`src/app/api/country/[code]/region/[id]/legislature/route.ts`) and the client mapping (`StateLegislatureClient.tsx`).

- **Regional Council elections not showing on UK region pages** — The `StateElections` component had a `!isUK` guard that hid the "State Elections" section entirely for UK regions, and `regionalCouncil` was missing from the election type filter. Fixed in `src/components/StateElections.tsx`.

- **Regional Council officials not showing on UK region Politics tab** — The Politics tab only rendered "Members of Parliament" with no section for Regional Council. Added `officeType` to `SerializedMP` interface, split officials by type, and added a "Regional Council" section. Fixed in `src/components/uk/UKRegionPageTabsPolitics.tsx`.

- **Chamber chart shows false leader on tied seats** — When two or more parties had equal seats, the chart arbitrarily declared one the "leader". Now correctly displays "Party A & Party B tied in [chamber]". Fixed in `src/components/ChamberChart.tsx`.

- **Regional Council election label missing** — Election cards showed "RegionalCouncil" (no space) because the label was missing from `ELECTION_RACE_LABELS` in `src/components/elections/electionHelpers.ts` and from `ELECTION_TYPE_LABEL_MAP` in `src/lib/utils/electionLabels.ts`.

- **Elections API missing regionalCouncil support** — The `typeLabel` mapping and multi-seat recalculation list in `src/app/api/country/[code]/elections/route.ts` didn't include `regionalCouncil`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **PortfolioChart component** — Now accepts a `view` prop (`"total" | "stocks" | "bonds" | "cash"`) to render different series. Color scheme: Total (primary/indigo), Stocks (success/green), Bonds (warning/amber), Cash (info/blue).

- **Profile page FinancialOverview** — Added portfolio chart section above the Personal/Campaign/Corporate tabs. Fetches portfolio history via server-side query and passes to client component for interactive viewing.

- **Character profile page** — Added portfolio chart section below the Finances summary card. Fetches portfolio history server-side and renders via `PortfolioChartSection` client component.

### API Changes

- **GET /api/character/portfolio** — Now returns `history` array with `stockValue`, `bondValue`, and `cashValue` fields for each turn.
- **GET /api/character/[id]/portfolio** — Now returns `history` array with `stockValue`, `bondValue`, and `cashValue` fields for each turn.

### Refactored

- **URL restructuring — full site migration to `/country/[code]/...` pattern** — Two-pass migration consolidating all geography-scoped URLs under a consistent `/country/[code]/...` hierarchy. Pass 1 moved state/region pages (`/state/OR` → `/country/us/region/OR`), legislature (`/legislature/us` → `/country/us/legislature`), executive (`/executive/us` → `/country/us/executive`), and all associated API routes (~54 route files). Pass 2 moved remaining `?country=` query-param pages: parties, coalitions, politicians, policy, approval, budget, elections, and path-based pages: central-bank, stockmarket — plus ~73 API routes and 9 admin API routes. Created centralized `src/lib/urls.ts` module with 45 URL helper functions (page + API) as single source of truth for all URL construction. Renamed `/national` to `/country/[code]/metrics`. Moved logo asset routes to `/api/logos/`. All old URLs have permanent 301 redirects via `next.config.ts` or in-app redirect shells. No database schema changes — translation between clean URLs and DB state IDs happens in the route layer.

- **Politicians nav moved from World to Nation** — Politicians is now country-scoped (`/country/[code]/politicians`), so the nav link moved from the World dropdown to the Nation dropdown in both desktop and mobile menus.

## [0.1.3] - 2026-04-02

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Coalition system** — National party chairs can form cross-party coalitions within the same country. Coalitions are purely organizational (no gameplay effects yet). Includes invite/accept/decline flow, join request flow, leave/kick mechanics, chair succession by seniority, chair transfer, and a 24-hour disband vote requiring majority of total members. New `coalitions` collection with embedded members, invites, join requests, and disband vote arrays. `coalitionId` field added to `PoliticalParty`. Per-country sequential IDs for URLs. 21 API route files under `src/app/api/coalitions/`. `src/lib/db/types/coalition.ts`, `src/lib/db/collections/coalitions.ts`.

- **Coalition notifications** — 10 new notification types: `coalition_invite_received`, `coalition_invite_accepted`, `coalition_invite_declined`, `coalition_join_request`, `coalition_join_accepted`, `coalition_join_declined`, `coalition_kicked`, `coalition_disband_vote_started`, `coalition_disbanded`, `coalition_chair_transferred`. New "Coalition" category in notification config.

- **Coalition UI** — Parties page gets a Parties/Coalitions tab switcher. "Create Coalition" button (grayed out with tooltip for non-chairs). Coalition card grid on Coalitions tab. Full coalition detail page at `/parties/coalition/[id]?country=X` with tabs: Overview (averaged policy positions, leadership by seniority, disband vote panel), Parties (member list with logos), Priorities (placeholder), Chair's Office (invites, join requests, kick, transfer, disband), Admin (add/remove parties, appoint chair). Invite acceptance banner follows the CEO acceptance pattern. `CoalitionLogo` component mirrors `PartyLogo`. `src/app/parties/coalition/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/parties/components/CoalitionCard.tsx`, `src/app/parties/components/CoalitionsTab.tsx`, `src/app/parties/components/CreateCoalitionModal.tsx`, `src/components/CoalitionLogo.tsx`.

- **Leave Coalition button** — Member party chairs see a "Leave Coalition" button in the coalition stats strip, allowing them to leave without visiting the Chair's Office tab.

- **Disband vote turn processing** — New `resolveExpiredDisbandVotes` phase in turn processing checks for expired 24-hour disband votes each turn. If majority voted yes, coalition is deleted and all members notified. Otherwise vote is cleared. `src/lib/turn/coalitionDisbandCheck.ts`.

- **Coalition cleanup in party deletion cascade** — `emptyPartyCleanup.ts` now removes deleted parties from coalitions, handles chair succession, and deletes coalitions with no remaining members.

- **Coalition sequential ID support** — `getNextSequentialId` now supports `"coalition"` type with country-scoped counters (`coalition_US`, `coalition_UK`, etc.). `src/lib/db/sequentialId.ts`.

- **Corporation attack sector button** — Sector detail pages now have an "Attack Sector" button allowing players to initiate hostile takeover actions directly from the sector page. `src/app/corporation/[id]/sectors/`.

- **Sector growth rate controls** — Admin-facing +/- buttons on sector cards to manually adjust growth rates for testing and balancing.

- **CEO tab reorganization** — CEO office tab restructured into subtabs (Overview, Budget Dashboard, Settings) with a new budget dashboard showing revenue and cost breakdowns per sector. `src/app/corporation/[id]/components/CeoOfficeTab.tsx`.

- **3-mode sector production policy** — Sectors can now switch between Normal, Aggressive, and Conservative production modes from the CEO tab. Each mode adjusts output volume and margin trade-offs. `src/app/corporation/[id]/components/CeoOfficeTab.tsx`.

- **Corporation HQ relocation** — CEOs can relocate corporate headquarters to another state via `POST /api/corporations/[id]/relocate`. Adjusts tax jurisdiction and regional bonuses. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/relocate/route.ts`.

- **Sector transition cooldown badges** — Cooldown timer now starts at transition initiation (not completion) and displays countdown badges on sector cards showing time remaining until strategy switch completes.

- **UK region admin tab** — UK region pages now have an Admin tab for Commons seat management: add, remove, and reassign seats per constituency. Red tint on tab label when inactive, matching US admin style. `src/app/state/[id]/components/`.

- **Cabinet nomination whips** — Party whips can now issue directives on cabinet nominations with 100% NPP compliance, joining leadership elections and confidence votes as whippable vote types.

- **Immediate whip vote application** — NPP bill whip votes now apply immediately instead of waiting for the next turn. Leadership election and confidence vote whip votes also apply immediately. `src/lib/turn/partyWhipTurn.ts`.

- **UK confidence vote whipping** — Confidence votes in the UK Parliament can now be whipped with 100% NPP compliance. `src/app/api/parties/[id]/whip/route.ts`.

- **UK Commons bills in unified processor** — UK Commons bills are now processed through the same unified bill lifecycle processor as US bills, ensuring consistent behavior for deadlines, enrollment, and expiry. `src/lib/turn/billLifecycle.ts`.

- **Proposed→active two-phase pattern** — Votes and cabinet nominations now use a two-phase lifecycle: a "proposed" state with a visible timer before transitioning to "active" and accepting votes. Prevents surprise votes.

- **DUP and Sinn Féin** — Added Democratic Unionist Party and Sinn Féin to default UK party seeds with verified Wikimedia Commons logos. `scripts/seeds/parties.ts`.

- **Admin leadership elections tab** — New sub-tab under Admin > Parties shows active leadership elections with pass, fail, and cancel actions. Added `cancelled` status to leadership election and vote types. `src/components/admin/AdminPartiesTab.tsx`.

- **Admin legislation tab overhaul** — Legislation admin tab refactored with country-specific tabs, sub-tabs for active/archived types, and pagination. API routes accept country filter and pagination params. `src/components/admin/AdminLegislationTab.tsx`.

- **Admin reset movement** — "Reset" button renamed to "Reset Password"; new "Reset Movement" button clears a player's relocation cooldown. `src/components/admin/AdminPlayersTab.tsx`.

- **Admin heal: stale campaigns** — Diagnose and delete `Campaign` documents that should have been cleaned up (completed/cancelled elections, inactive candidates, cross-country mismatches). `GET/POST /api/admin/heal/stale-campaigns`, `HealStaleCampaigns.tsx`.

- **Admin heal: federal/state budgets** — Heal tools for federal budget recalculation (re-seeds enacted laws, fixes cost fields) and state budget GDP unit correction (millions→dollars). `GET/POST /api/admin/heal/federal-budget`, `GET/POST /api/admin/heal/state-budget-gdp`.

- **Central bank chair resign button** — Central bank chairs can now resign from the central bank page. Profile links use `sequentialId` instead of ObjectId for clean URLs. `src/app/central-bank/[code]/CentralBankClient.tsx`.

- **Central bank auto-resign on relocation** — Central bank chairs are automatically resigned when relocating to a different country. Stays in role if relocating within the same country. `src/app/api/character/relocate/route.ts`.

- **Discord game event webhooks** — Country-specific US and UK game event webhooks announce major events (election results, government formation, confidence votes) to dedicated Discord channels. `src/lib/discord/gameEvents.ts`.

- **Discord confidence vote announcements** — UK confidence vote starts are announced to the UK game events webhook. `src/lib/discord/gameEvents.ts`.

- **Discord /government and /autocomplete** — New Discord bot API endpoints for government data and player/party autocomplete. `src/app/api/discord-bot/government/route.ts`, `src/app/api/discord-bot/autocomplete/route.ts`.

- **Discord stock chart command** — `GET /api/discord-bot/stock-chart` returns corporation price history chart data. Defaults to market-wide data with optional corporation and country filters. `src/app/api/discord-bot/stock-chart/route.ts`.

- **Discord changelog webhook** — Changelog updates are automatically posted to a Discord webhook. `src/lib/discord/changelog.ts`.

- **Game-time countdowns** — `gameTimeRef` added to countdown components so vote deadlines and timers display correctly relative to game time rather than wall-clock time. `src/components/ui/Countdown.tsx`.

- **Player Mail system** — Full in-game mail between characters. Inbox with unread counts, sent box, soft-delete (both sides must delete before hard-delete), mark-as-read on expand, 1-per-minute rate limit, and a report button for abuse. New `playerMail` and `playerMailReports` MongoDB collections. `PlayerMail` and `PlayerMailReport` types added to `src/lib/db/types/`. API routes: `GET/POST /api/mail` (inbox + send), `GET /api/mail/sent`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/mail/[id]`, `DELETE /api/mail/sent/[id]`, `POST /api/mail/[id]/report`.

- **Mail tab on notifications page** — Notifications page (`/notifications`) gains a Mail tab alongside the existing Notifications tab. Inbox/Sent toggle, expandable message view, inline delete and report buttons. Unread mail count shown as a badge on the tab and combined with notification count in the navbar unread badge. `/api/client-nav` and `/api/auth/me` both return `unreadMailCount`. `src/app/notifications/components/MailTab.tsx`.

- **Admin mail reports queue** — New "Mail Reports" sub-tab under Admin > Support. Filterable by status (pending/dismissed/actioned). Expanded view shows message body, sender/recipient links, and action buttons: Dismiss, Delete Mail, Warn Sender (system notification), Ban Sender. Optional admin note on all actions. `src/components/admin/MailReportsTab.tsx`, `GET /api/admin/mail-reports`, `PATCH /api/admin/mail-reports/[id]`.

- **Mail Composer Modal** — Replaces the inline `SendMailCard` on character profiles with a popout modal composer (`src/components/MailComposerModal.tsx`). Includes a formatting toolbar with **B** (bold) and **I** (italic) buttons that wrap the current textarea selection in `**...**` / `*...*` using `selectionStart`/`selectionEnd`. Closes on backdrop click or Escape. Shows "Sent." confirmation then auto-closes after 1.5 s. Two modes: `mail` (character-to-character) and `shareholder-address` (corporation broadcast). `src/components/OpenMailComposerButton.tsx` is a lightweight wrapper that owns `isOpen` state and renders the trigger button on profile pages.

- **Shareholder Address** — CEO action on the corporation page (CEO Office → Admin subtab). Sends a formatted message to all current shareholders as system notifications. 12-hour cooldown per corporation enforced server-side via `lastShareholderAddressAt` on the `Corporation` document. Cooldown and last-sent date displayed in the UI. Shareholder userId lookup is batched (one `characters.find` query). `POST /api/corporations/[id]/shareholder-address`. `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts` updated with `lastShareholderAddressAt?: Date`.

- **`renderMailBody` utility** — `src/lib/utils/renderMailBody.tsx` converts markdown-lite strings (`**bold**`, `*italic*`, newlines) to React nodes (`<strong>`, `<em>`, `<br />`). No external markdown library. Used by mail display and shareholder address notifications.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Game time capped to wall-clock** — `gameNow` is now capped to never exceed real wall-clock time, removing all previous workarounds for time drift. All vote deadlines use game time consistently.

- **UK map lean colors** — Swapped UK constituency lean colors to Labour-red and Conservative-blue (were previously reversed). `src/app/world/components/MapSVGContent.tsx`.

- **Leadership elections in whip panel** — Leadership elections moved to their own dedicated tab within the party whip panel for cleaner organization. `src/components/party/WhipPanel.tsx`.

- **UK South West England rebalanced** — Archetype population mix for South West England adjusted for better electoral balance.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Stock purchase 404** — Fixed stock purchase endpoint returning 404; replaced inline alert dialogs with toast popup notifications for all share operations.

- **Candlestick chart visibility** — Fixed candlestick chart bodies being invisible due to missing fill; increased chart resolution and data density for better readability.

- **Cross-country relocation cleanup** — Relocating between countries now properly clears party leadership roles, party membership, and resets the character to independent. Previously could leave stale party data.

- **UK confidence/no-confidence seat weighting** — All confidence, no-confidence, and minority attempt votes now use `seatsHeld` weight instead of treating each MP as one vote, correctly reflecting multi-seat holders.

- **UK NPP bill votes** — Fixed NPP vote tally display, party name resolution, and chamber tab switching for UK bills.

- **UK NPP confidence voting** — NPP MPs now correctly auto-vote YES on confidence votes; only governing-party NPPs auto-vote YES on minority attempts (previously all NPPs voted).

- **UK vote deadline fixes** — Multiple fixes for `closesAt` deadline handling: stored on vote creation, fallback for legacy votes missing the field, computed from game time not wall-clock, compared correctly at resolution time.

- **UK whip panel country awareness** — Whip panels now filter by country so UK parties don't see US leadership elections and vice versa. Commons/Lords added to whip chamber validation.

- **Federal budget heal** — Federal budget heal tool now fixes ALL enacted laws (not just seed-generated), re-seeds before recalculating, and clears stale cost fields. Per-law cost diagnostics added.

- **State budget GDP units** — Fixed state GDP being seeded in millions instead of dollars, causing budget calculations to be off by 6 orders of magnitude. Fiscal year starting year corrected to 2020.

- **Election percentage mismatch** — Fixed discrepancy between vote percentages shown on state election list vs election detail pages.

- **Election vote share chart Y-axis too wide** — When candidates were closely matched, the vote share line chart used a fixed 0–100% Y-axis, compressing all lines into a flat band at the top. The axis now zooms to data range with 15% padding when the spread is under 40 points. `yMin` prop added to `LineGraph`; `GeneralVoteCharts` computes dynamic bounds. `src/app/elections/[id]/components/ElectionDetailCharts.tsx`.

- **Corporation production policy revenue multiplier not applied** — `getRevenueMultiplier` was missing from the production policy trend calculation in `corporationTurn.ts`, causing revenue multipliers from production policy levels to be ignored during turn processing. `src/lib/turn/corporationTurn.ts`.

- **NPP primary penalty** — NPP primary vote penalty now applied consistently in both list and detail views.

- **Position badge display** — Position badges now hidden for irrelevant axes (zero-value or not applicable to the legislation type) on national and state policy pages.

- **UK MP party names** — MP list now shows party display name instead of raw sequentialId.

- **Vacant officials filtered** — Parliament members API now filters out vacant officials (including admin-vacated seats matched by characterName).

- **Legislation UI polish** — Fixed immigration category in bill proposal dropdown; LARP titles display correctly on bill cards and detail pages; provision layout moved to hero section; national-only categories (defense, foreign policy, immigration) hidden from state legislature dropdown.

- **Coalition bug fixes** — Fixed `isInCoalition` check and `partySequentialId` type coercion; sequential IDs returned instead of ObjectIds for invite/joinRequest partyId; join request button visibility for non-member national chairs.

### Refactored

- **NPP whip logic consolidated** — NPP whip resolution, alignment score calculation, and compliance logic consolidated into shared utilities, removing duplication across bill, leadership, confidence, and cabinet whip handlers.

### Performance

- **Turn processing optimization** — Turn processor refactored with shared state data passed between phases (avoiding redundant DB queries) and parallel execution of independent phases. `src/lib/turn/turnSystem.ts`.

- **Hot-path query trimming** — Frequently-hit database queries trimmed with projections and index hints to reduce response times.

- **Discord bot data pre-computation** — Stock exchange snapshots and investor rankings are now pre-computed at turn time and cached, eliminating expensive on-demand aggregation for Discord bot commands.

- **DB connection pool fix** — Fixed connection pool exhaustion in serverless environment by properly reusing MongoClient instances across hot function invocations. `src/lib/db/mongodb.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Party org build rate buffed** — `DOLLARS_PER_ORG` reduced from $100,000 to $75,000, making org growth from spending ~33% faster. `src/lib/constants/partyOrg.ts`.

- **Actions display includes party influence** — Profile page actions label now shows total including party influence bonus (e.g. "+4/turn" instead of "+3/turn"). Tooltip breaks down base + office + party contributions. `src/app/profile/components/PoliticalStanding.tsx`.

- **Party Influence tooltip enriched** — Party Influence card now shows current bonus actions/turn, max bonus cap, share of total party influence pool, and net gain/loss per turn. Data computed via party-wide aggregation query on both own-profile and public character pages. `src/app/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/character/[id]/page.tsx`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Party org NaN in London & Wales** — 8 `statePartyOrg` documents (7 London, 1 Wales) had `organization: NaN`, causing "No parties have active organization" display. Root cause: NaN propagates through `Math.min`/`Math.max` without `Number.isFinite()` guards. DB values restored from momentum estimates. Guards added in `turnProcessing.ts` and `demographicTurnoutTurn.ts` to treat non-finite org values as 0.

### Docs

- **Wiki and design docs updated** — All design documents updated to reflect v0.1.3 features. New wiki-synced design docs: `mail.md` (player mail system) and `coalitions.md` (cross-party alliances). Updated: `roadmap.md` (feature status refresh), `core-systems.md` (14-group turn processing table), `elections.md` (presidential travel), `corporations.md` (production modes, HQ relocation, shareholder address, CEO tabs, candlestick charts), `stock-market.md` (OHLC charts, Discord integration), `achievements.md` (tile grid redesign), `getting-started.md` (mail, coalitions, corporations), `parties.md` (coalition cross-references). Wiki config updated with `mail` and `coalitions` slugs for admin sync. `README.md` updated with current feature set, architecture diagram, and project structure.

## [0.1.2] - 2026-03-27 (ongoing)

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Unified legislature composition layout** — Extracted a shared `LegislatureCompositionSection` component (`src/components/legislature/`) that renders the hemicycle `ParliamentChart`, `SeatBar`, `SeatLegend`, `MajorityBanner`, plus a searchable/sortable/paginated member list with NPP badges. Used by US Congress, UK Parliament, and State Legislature pages. Shared types in `src/components/legislature/types.ts`. Removes ~400 lines of duplicated layout code across three page implementations.

- **NPP indicators on all member lists** — All legislature member list rows now show a small "NPP" badge next to NPP names. Previously only the UK Parliament page had NPP indicators. Badge positioned immediately after the member name link, before any leader badges.

- **State Legislature composition upgrade** — State Legislature pages now show the hemicycle chart, seat bar, legend, and majority banner (previously just a simple seat distribution list). Search, sort by region/name/seats, and pagination (25 per page) added. The separate "Members" tab is removed — members are now part of the Composition tab.

- **Canada Parliament page** — New page at `/legislature/ca` with Commons/Senate chamber switching, hemicycle composition chart, Bills tab (empty state), and Leadership tab (PM, Opposition Leader — all Vacant). API routes: `GET /api/legislature/ca/members`, `GET /api/legislature/ca/leaders`, `GET /api/legislature/ca/bills`. Canada's appointed Senate returns empty data gracefully.

- **Germany Bundestag page** — New page at `/legislature/de` with Bundestag/Bundesrat chamber switching, hemicycle composition chart, Bills tab (empty state), and Leadership tab (Chancellor, Opposition Leader — all Vacant). API routes: `GET /api/legislature/de/members`, `GET /api/legislature/de/leaders`, `GET /api/legislature/de/bills`. Germany's state-appointed Bundesrat returns empty data gracefully.

- **UK/State Legislature API enrichment** — `GET /api/legislature/uk/members` and `GET /api/state/[id]/legislature` now return `economicPosition` on party composition entries (for hemicycle left-right sorting). State route also returns `avatarUrl`, `partyName`, `countryId`, and required `isNPP` boolean on officials.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **`LegislatureHeader` chamber switcher generalized** — The `chamberSwitcher` prop now accepts arbitrary `options: Array<{ key: string; label: string }>` instead of hardcoded "senate"/"house". Supports Canada (Commons/Senate) and Germany (Bundestag/Bundesrat) chamber labels. `src/app/legislature/[code]/components/shared/LegislatureHeader.tsx`.

- **`useLegislatureData` hook extended** — Now accepts an optional `chamber` parameter and supports CA/DE URL patterns. Refetches when chamber changes. URL construction extracted to a `getEndpointUrls` helper. `src/app/legislature/[code]/components/shared/useLegislatureData.ts`.

- **`LegislatureClient` routing expanded** — `/legislature/ca` renders `CAParliamentPage`, `/legislature/de` renders `DEBundestagPage`. Generic "coming soon" fallback removed for these countries.

### Refactored

- **US Congress `CongressCompositionTab`** — Reduced from ~370 to ~160 lines by delegating chart + member list rendering to `LegislatureCompositionSection`. Senate class filter passed via `extraControls` prop, leader badges via `leaderBadges` Map.

- **UK Parliament `CompositionTab`** — Replaced ~156-line inline implementation (stat cards, custom seat bar, custom party list, inline MP list) with ~50-line mapper to shared component.

- **State Legislature** — Deleted `CompositionTab.tsx` and `MembersTab.tsx`. Replaced with `LegislatureCompositionSection` in the composition tab. Members tab removed from tab list.

### Added (previous)

- **Bill list layout toggle** — Both US Congress and UK Parliament bill list pages now have a Cards/Compact view toggle (top-right, persisted to localStorage). US defaults to Cards, UK defaults to Compact. Both views available on both pages. Shared components extracted to `src/components/bills/` (BillCard, BillCompactRow, VoteDonut, BillTimeline, BillVoteIndicator, BillListControls). CongressBillsTab reduced from ~650 to ~250 lines.

- **Bill vote status filters** — New All/Voted/Not Voted filter bar on bill list pages. Client-side filtering on the `myVote` field. Only shown to logged-in chamber members.

- **Inline bill voting** — Aye/Nay/Abstain buttons on each bill card and compact row, allowing players to vote without navigating to the bill detail page. Buttons POST to the existing bill vote endpoint. Current vote is highlighted. `e.preventDefault()`/`e.stopPropagation()` prevents link navigation on click.

- **Bill vote indicator** — Each bill in both views shows the player's vote status: "✓ Voted For" (green), "✗ Voted Against" (red), "— Abstained" (muted), or "Not yet voted" (italic muted). Hidden when not logged in.

- **UK bill list API enrichment** — `GET /api/legislature/uk/bills` now returns the full `BillDisplay` shape matching the US API: provisions with economic/social positions, timeline dates, `myVote`, `canVoteOrigin`, `legislationTypeName`, `effectDirection`. Previously returned a minimal shape with only title/sponsor/status/votes.

- **Individual voter list on bill detail** — New Tally/Votes tabs below the vote bars on the bill detail page. Tally tab shows the existing party breakdown + parliament charts. Votes tab shows every individual voter (name, party, vote direction) via a new `GET /api/congress/bills/[id]/votes` endpoint. Filters for party, player/NPP type, and vote direction. Seats column shown for multi-seat chambers (UK Commons, US House) but hidden for US Senate.

- **`BillDisplay` extended** — Added `canVoteOrigin`, `canVoteOther`, and `failedAt` fields to the `BillDisplay` interface and US bills API response.

### Added (previous)

- **Wire transfer (portfolio)** — Players can send personal Cash on Hand to any same-country politician via a new Wire Transfer card on the Portfolio page. Card uses the shared `PlayerSelector` component for name autocomplete with country scoping; recipient receives a `wire_received` in-app notification. Card renders below the stocks/bonds tab section. `POST /api/characters/[id]/wire`, `WireTransferCard.tsx`, `notificationConfig.tsx`.

- **Party logo on election card primary header** — Each party's primary section within an `ElectionCard` now shows the `PartyLogo` badge (h-3.5 w-3.5) before the party name, consistent with the election detail page. `ElectionCard.tsx`.

- **`PlayerSelector` country filter** — `PlayerSelector` now accepts a `countryId` prop and passes it as a query param to `/api/characters/search`, ensuring autocomplete results are scoped to the correct country. Used by the wire transfer card.

- **Party Influence** — Characters now accumulate `partyInfluence` each turn based on policy closeness to their party, leadership roles (Chair +3, Vice Chair +2, Treasurer +2, National Committee +1), and infamy penalty (logarithmic, capped at 4/turn). Influence distributes a 1.5× player-count bonus action pool proportionally each turn, scaled by policy alignment and capped at +3 per player.

- **Admin — UK government heal panel** — System → Heal tab includes a card to refresh `GET /api/admin/uk/government/heal`, run **Retrigger formation**, and **Appoint PM** (player Commons MP picker). `HealUKGovernment.tsx`, `AdminSystemTab.tsx`.

- **Legislation budget costs** — All US legislation types now have per-capita budget costs via `withPerCapitaCosts()`. Left positions (more spending) have positive costs; right positions (cuts/deregulation) have negative costs (savings). Costs scale by program type: healthcare/education ~$500-1000, infrastructure ~$250-600, regulatory ~$50-100. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Immigration policy split** — Replaced single `immigration` type with two distinct types: `border_security_enforcement` (border patrol, detention, deportation - affects migrationRate, publicSafetyConfidence, crimeRate) and `legal_immigration_visas` (visa caps, pathways, naturalization - affects migrationRate, populationGrowth, workforceSkill, gdpGrowth). `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`, `scripts/seeds/basePolicies.ts`.
- **11-bracket tax system** — All 9 US tax types expanded from 6–8 options to 11 with LARP-style titles, descriptions, and explicit economic scores (−5 to +5). Index 0 = maximum expansion, index 10 = full abolition. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Natural metric decay** — All metrics now naturally decay toward baseline at 0.25% per turn (~20 game years full revert). Prevents permanent metric drift after legislation expires or is repealed. `src/lib/demographicEffects.ts`.
- **Minimum wage rate field** — Minimum wage legislation options now store actual $/hour values via `minimumWageRate`, displayed in the proposal UI alongside the standard economic/social scores. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **New legislation types** — `state_spending_stimulus` (state economic recovery stimulus) and `state_housing` (state housing and development) added as state-level legislation types. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Archetype tax and media domains** — Added `tax` and `mediaInformation` to `PolicyDomain` type with full affinity values for all US and UK archetypes. Tax domain: small business +45, libertarians +50, public sector -30. Media domain: college liberals -35, rural traditionalists +25. `src/lib/archetypeAffinities.ts`.
- **Archetype position multipliers** — Bill enactment now applies position multipliers based on policy extremity: extreme positions (0, 6) get 1.5x impact, strong (1, 5) get 1.25x, moderate (2, 4) get 1.0x, center (3) gets 0.5x. This means extreme legislation has stronger archetype approval effects. `src/lib/archetypeAffinities.ts` `calculateShiftImpacts()`.

- **Presidential candidate travel** — Candidates in active presidential elections (primary or general) can spend 5 character actions to travel to any US state via `POST /api/elections/[id]/travel`. Travel state persists on `ElectionCandidate.travelState` until the candidate travels again. Candidates cannot travel to a state they are already in.
- **Travel presence campaign boost** — Candidates with an active `travelState` receive a passive +1.0% favorability/turn bonus in addition to media spending effects (`campaignTurn.ts`).
- **Travel badges on electoral map and primary rows** — The presidential electoral map EV summary row and primary phase candidate rows show a 📍 STATE badge when a candidate has an active travel state set. `PresidentialElectoralMap.tsx`, `ElectionDetailComponents.tsx`, `GeneralPhaseView.tsx`.
- **Admin — Heal stale campaign documents** — System → Heal tab includes a new card to diagnose and delete `Campaign` documents that should have been cleaned up but weren't. Three categories: completed/cancelled elections, inactive candidates (withdrawn/eliminated), and cross-country mismatches. Fixes players who still see the campaign tab after leaving a race or switching countries. `GET/POST /api/admin/heal/stale-campaigns`, `HealStaleCampaigns.tsx`.

- **Campaign action floor** — `calculateCampaignActions` now guarantees a minimum of 1 action/turn regardless of endorsement count (was 0 with zero endorsements). Formula: `1 + floor(sqrt(endorsements) × 3)`. Invalid inputs also return 1. `src/lib/campaigns/actions.ts`.

- **Fundraising levels 0–10** — Fundraising upgrades expanded from 5 to 10 levels. Income per turn: L0 $20k → L5 $200k → L10 $5M. Upgrade costs scale from $50k/10 AP (L1) to $10M/90 AP (L10). Income is now exclusively from the `FUNDRAISING_INCOME` lookup — character PI and `characterFunds` no longer contribute. `src/lib/campaigns/upgradeCosts.ts`, `src/lib/campaigns/income.ts`.

- **Campaign donations** — Any authenticated character can donate Cash on Hand to any active campaign (minimum $1). The national party chair can also donate from the party treasury. Each donation is logged in `campaign.donationLog` (capped at 100 entries) with donor name, type (`"character"` | `"party"`), amount, and turn number. `POST /api/campaigns/[id]/donate`, `src/lib/db/types/campaign.ts`.

- **Opposition research retargeting** — Campaigns with `oppositionResearchLevel > 0` can now change their research target via `POST /api/campaigns/[id]/retarget`. A 6-hour cooldown (`oppositionResearchCooldownUntil`) prevents spamming. Owner or manager only.

- **Campaign season multiplier** — During the final 4 turns before `election.endTime`, passive per-turn effects double (2×): media spending favorability boost and opposition research favorability drain. Timing-based — no player toggle required. `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.ts`.

- **Admin — Change home state** — New "Characters" sub-tab under Players in the admin panel. Accepts a username and state dropdown to update `character.homeState`. Validates state code against `STATE_IDS`. `PATCH /api/admin/characters/update-state`, `CharacterStateManager.tsx`, `AdminPlayersTab.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Party org scalar** — Both `partyOrgScalar` (state races) and `partyOrgScalarPresidential` now use an additive bonus formula: `1.0 + (org/100) × 0.6` (range: 1.0× at org=0 to 1.6× at org=100). Previously applied a penalty at low org (state: 0.5–1.0×; presidential: 0.05–1.0×). `src/lib/utils/demographicAppeal.ts`.

- **General phase upgrade cost scaling** — All campaign upgrade costs multiply by 1.5× (rounded up) when the election has entered the general phase (`primaryEndTime ≤ now < endTime`). `src/app/api/campaigns/[id]/upgrade/route.ts`.

- **Presidential-only player endorsements for campaign actions** — Player endorsements only contribute to the `calculateCampaignActions` formula for presidential elections. For all other race types, player endorsements are cosmetic and do not generate campaign actions. `src/lib/turn/campaignTurn.ts`.

- **`Campaign` type** — Removed `canvassingEnabled: boolean`. Added `oppositionResearchCooldownUntil: Date | null` and `donationLog: CampaignDonation[]`. `src/lib/db/types/campaign.ts`.

- **UK Government hub consolidation** — The full UK government experience (Downing Street hero, stats strip, Commons hemicycle, minority/confidence panels, executive PM card, seat tables, cabinet link) now lives at **`/executive/uk`**. **`/uk/government` permanently redirects** there. Removed redundant `UKExecutiveClient` in favor of server `UKGovernmentExecutiveHub`. `UKGovernmentLayout` supports optional Downing Street hero and `quickLinksMode="hub"`. UK elections “back” link targets `/executive/uk`.

- **LARP-style legislation names** — All US legislation types renamed to formal bill-style names: "Federal Education Funding" → "Federal Education Investment Act", "Clean Energy" → "Clean Energy Investment Act", "Defense Spending" → "National Defense Authorization Act", etc. ~50 types updated. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Absolute budget costs** — All legislation `annualCostPerCapita` values are now absolute spending levels ($0 = full abolition) instead of deltas from baseline. The budget system sets program cost to the new absolute value when a bill is signed. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Federal effect division** — Federal bills now apply 1/50th of their effect per state (was 1/3), preventing a single federal bill from dominating state-level metrics. `src/lib/demographicEffects.ts`.
- **Dual-axis scoring** — All US legislation options now have explicit `economic` and `social` integer scores where relevant, replacing options that were missing one axis. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Seed script deprecated type cleanup** — `seed-legislation.ts`, `seed-policies.ts`, and `seed.ts` now delete deprecated legislation type IDs before upserting, enabling clean re-seeding on live servers. Currently removes old `immigration` type replaced by the split types.

- **UK minority government formation** — After a UK election with no majority, the largest party (≥ 130 Commons seats) can attempt to form a minority government via `POST /api/uk/pm/minority-attempt`. The nominee is the governing-party **player** MP with the highest aggregate popular vote from the latest Commons wave (ties: more seats held, then name); NPPs cannot be nominated. NPP Commons MPs record yes automatically; **only MPs of the attempting party** may cast player votes via `POST /api/uk/pm/confidence/[voteId]/vote`. All players see attempt status and a vote breakdown on `/uk/government`; the vote passes at 130 yes. On pass, PM is appointed and `status` becomes `formed`. On fail, status resets to `minority_pending`. `ukGovernmentFormation.ts`, `ukGovernment.ts`, `minorityAttemptNominee.ts`, `minorityAttemptDisplay.ts`, `MinorityAttemptPanel.tsx`, `government/page.tsx`, `api/uk/pm/confidence/[voteId]/vote/route.ts`.
- **Admin UK government heal route** — `GET /api/admin/uk/government/heal` returns a diagnostic snapshot (gov status, seat tallies, active vote, current PM, player candidates). `POST` with `action: “retrigger_formation”` re-runs formation logic; `action: “appoint_pm”` directly appoints a specified character as PM.

### Removed

- **Medicare type** — Removed `medicare` legislation type as redundant with `federal_healthcare_funding` and `drug_pricing_medicare`. Seed scripts delete the old type ID on re-seed. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Cross-country support/attack/barnstorm blocked** — `simpleInfluence.ts` (used by raise, lower, and barnstorm actions on character and NPP profiles) now enforces same-country restriction. `resolveCountry()` derives country from `countryId` field with fallback to `homeState` prefix for NPPs. UK and US politicians can no longer target each other.

- **Cross-country campaign fund transfers blocked** — `POST /api/characters/[id]/transfer` now checks `sender.countryId !== target.countryId` and returns 400 before any funds move.

### Docs

- **Wiki — Getting Started rewrite** — Expanded from a bare 5-step list to a full onboarding page covering: country selection (US/UK), two-resource-pool split (Campaign Funds vs Cash on Hand), party influence mechanic, interpersonal actions (support/attack/barnstorm), presidential travel, UK Downing Street hub, and a first-week checklist. `docs/design/getting-started.md`.

- **Wiki — Stats & Actions expanded** — Added Cash on Hand stat, Party Influence stat, Support/Attack interpersonal action table, Barnstorm action, Presidential Travel action, and Party-Level Actions section. Out-of-state multipliers now explicitly call out which actions they apply to. `docs/design/stats-actions.md`.

- **Wiki — Player Progression expanded** — Added UK career path (Commons → MP → PM), Party Influence section explaining accrual and bonus action conversion, presidential Travel section, Cash on Hand in starting resources and stat table. `docs/design/player-progression.md`.

- **Wiki — Parties: Party Influence section** — New section documents the bonus action pool mechanic, pool sizing formula, closeness scalar, visibility (profile + members table + party header), and strategic implications. `docs/design/parties.md`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **President notified when bills await signature** — When a federal bill becomes `enrolled`, the sitting player president now gets an in-app notification (`bill_enrolled`, “Bill Awaiting Your Signature”), matching governor behavior for state bills. `notifyPresidentBillAwaitingSignature` in `billLifecycle.ts`; admin **force enroll** triggers the same notice. Skips vacant or NPP-only presidencies.

- **Relocation blocked after leaving an election** — `GET`/`POST` `/api/character/relocate` no longer treat a stale `electionCandidates` / `statePartyCandidates` row with `status: "active"` as blocking when the parent election is already finished (completed/cancelled or, for state party, not `voting`). Only **open** races block relocation. `relocationCampaigns.ts`.

- **Stock quote and market cap consistency** — Public listing quote (`reportedSharePrice ?? sharePrice`) and `marketCapitalization = round(quote × totalShares)` now match everywhere they are shown: corporation detail API and UI (hero, financials key metrics, shares market overview), portfolio holdings, Discord bot corp/financials payloads, exchange snapshot builder, and investor rankings. `GET /api/corporations/[id]` returns fundamental `sharePrice` (order fills and relocation), `quotedSharePrice` (exchange-consistent headline), and `modelSharePrice` (blended fair value). Relocation UI cost aligns with `sharePrice × totalShares` on the server.

- **UK confidence vote collection mismatch** — `processConfidenceVotes` was reading from `ukConfidenceVotes` while votes were written to `confidenceVotes`. All three vote-processing functions now use the correct collection.
- **UK majority formation never appointing PM** — After a majority election with no existing PM, `resolveUKGovernmentFormation` now calls `triggerNextPMConfidenceVote` so a PM is actually selected.
- **Post no-confidence formation bypassing seat check** — `resolveNoConfidenceVote` now calls `checkAndInitiateUKFormation` instead of `triggerNextPMConfidenceVote` directly, ensuring majority/minority logic runs after a government falls.
- **State party API numeric fields** — `GET /api/state/[id]/party/[partyId]` now coerces Mongo-backed numbers (including BSON `Long`, which `JSON.stringify` turns into `{ low, high, unsigned }`) to plain finite numbers before responding. That serialized shape made the client treat organization as NaN and show **0 / “gone”** party org. `coerceStoredNumber.ts`, state party route.
- **NPP VP never assigned on presidential win** — When an NPP won the presidency, `runningMateId` was always undefined (NPPs can't pick running mates), so VP was silently never created. The highest-`politicalInfluence` same-party NPP (excluding the winner, same `countryId`) is now auto-selected and assigned. `presidentResolution.ts`.
- **Vacant presidency never filled** — When the sitting president's office became vacant (`characterId: null`, no `nppId`), no succession logic existed. New `processPresidentialSuccession` turn phase (Group 11.5) runs every turn, detects the vacancy, promotes the VP to president, clears the VP slot, updates `characters`/`npps` `currentOffice`, and notifies the player. `presidentialSuccession.ts`, `turnSystem.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **UK demographic archetypes redesigned** — Replaced the 12 UK voter archetypes with attitudinal/demographic groups that work in every region, eliminating 4 dead-weight regional-identity slots (Scottish Nationalists, Welsh Communities, NI Unionists, NI Nationalists) that were zeroed out in 8–10 of 12 regions. New archetypes: Post-Industrial Workers, Urban Progressives, Suburban Homeowners, Young Renters, Rural Traditionalists, Retirees & Pensioners, Public Sector & NHS, Moderate Centrists, Populist Right, Green & Climate Activists, Small Business & Self-Employed, New Britons & Minorities. Regional character is now expressed through population percentages rather than dedicated geographic slots. All 12 archetypes have non-zero populations in every region.
- **UK legislative archetype affinities added** — `archetypeAffinities.ts` now includes `UK_DOMAIN_AFFINITIES` calibrated to British political context (NHS, net zero, sovereignty, etc.). Bill enactment correctly routes UK bills to UK archetypes and US bills to US archetypes via `billEnactment.ts`.
- **Migration script added** — `scripts/migrations/migrate-uk-archetypes.ts` updates live `stateDemographics` and `stateDemographicTurnout` collections to the new archetype IDs, preserving existing GOTV modifier values for renamed groups.

