## [0.1.1] - 2026-02-25

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Share consolidation** — CEOs may run a **stock split or reverse split** (`POST /api/corporations/[id]/shares/consolidate`): all shareholders and the public float scale in proportion; prices adjust so market cap is unchanged. Reverse split floor 1,000,000 shares; forward split cap 100×; **48-turn cooldown** (`lastShareStructureTurn`, `SHARE_STRUCTURE_COOLDOWN_TURNS`). Open limit orders must still be cancelled first. `SharesTab.tsx`, `shareConsolidation.ts`, `corporations.ts` constants.
- **Peer-to-peer share order fill** — Share listings separate buy and sell orders into distinct book entries; incoming market orders fill against the opposing side at the best available price. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/`.
- **Changelog hero image** — `/changelog` header uses Wikimedia Commons DEC VT100 terminal photo proxied at `GET /api/images/hero/changelog`. `ChangelogClient.tsx`, `api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`.
- **Corporation page hero** — `/corporation/[id]` uses a Campaign Operations–style hero: optional CEO-uploaded banner (`headerImageUrl`, `POST /api/upload/corporation-header`), brand-color gradient fallback, stats strip (share price, market cap, dividend %). `CorporationHero.tsx`, `corporation/[id]/page.tsx`, CEO Office banner upload.
- **Discord bot market share command** — `GET /api/discord-bot/marketshare` with optional `country` and `state` filters returns sector market share data with pagination and unowned totals, enabling the Discord bot to display corporate sector breakdowns. `src/app/api/discord-bot/marketshare/route.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **US country overview hero** — The United States overview at `/country/us` uses a Mount Rushmore banner image (Wikimedia Commons, proxied via `GET /api/images/hero/us-overview-mount-rushmore`); the world map card and header thumbnail remain the flag. `CountryOverviewClient.tsx`, `countries.ts`, `api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`.
- **Party organization simplified** — Removed momentum mechanic from party organization system. Org building now directly adds organization at `spend / $100,000` per turn instead of going through momentum equilibrium calculations. Organization decays at 0.25 per turn when not investing. The “momentum” field is repurposed to show org trend for display (positive = growing, negative = decaying). `src/lib/turn/demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/turnProcessing.ts`, `src/lib/constants/partyOrg.ts` (`DOLLARS_PER_ORG`, `ORG_DECAY_RATE`), `FundraisingManagementSection.tsx`.
- **Wire & news sector labels** — Tickers and feed text map sector type slugs (e.g. `real_estate`) to display names (`Real Estate`) via `formatSectorTypeSlugsInText` on `GET /api/news/wire`, `GET /api/news`, and `GET /api/news/[id]/replies`. Unowned sector capture uses `CORPORATION_TYPE_LABELS` when logging wire headlines. `formatSectorTypeSlugsInText.ts`, `economy/attack/route.ts`.
- **Compact currency display** — Stock market (listings, overview, stats, wealth list, total market cap) and related wire/API copy use shared `formatFundsCompact` / `formatCompactNumber` (`$263K`, `$1.2M`, etc.) instead of ad-hoc abbreviations. `formatters.ts`, `wireEvent.ts`, stock market components, corporation economy/bond routes.
- **Stock market listings** — Corporations table paginates at **10 per page** with prev/next and range summary. `stockmarket/.../StockList.tsx`.
- **Stock market timeframe selector** — Market index chart has **24h / 48h / 5y / All** buttons with client-side data slicing. X-axis shows game-year labels with real dates for 48h+ views; real timestamps for 24h. `MarketOverview.tsx`, `/api/stock-exchange/market-cap-history` adds `newestTurnDate`.
- **Market index candlesticks** — Overview index chart renders **OHLC candles** (weekly buckets: open/close = first/last cap in bucket, high/low = range). **Bucket count** caps so short ranges (e.g. 6m) average **≥2 weeks per candle**, avoiding all-green bars when `open === close`. **Doji** bars use **muted** color or red/green vs **prior bar’s close**. `MarketOverview.tsx`.
- **Market chart timeframe animation** — Switching timeframes triggers a CSS `scaleX` animation: compress-in (1.06→1, right-anchored) for shorter views, expand-out (0.94→1) for longer; opacity fade, 0.32 s easing. `MarketOverview.tsx`.
- **Corporation stats** — Hero strip and Financials “Key metrics” show **marketing strength** and **logistics efficiency** (with net/turn in Financials for logistics). `CorporationHero.tsx`, `FinancialsTab.tsx`.
- **Favorability natural decay** — Equilibrium lowered from 40% to **30%**; per-turn penalty rate **halved** (`(favorability − 30) × 0.05`). `shared/constants/formulas.ts`, `actionRefresh.ts`, wiki `FavorabilityDecayDiagram`, `docs/design/stats-actions.md`.
- **Actions batch confirm modal** — Multi-action confirm dialog renders via **portal** to `document.body` with higher z-index so compact view rows (`overflow-hidden`) no longer clip it. `ActionExecuteRow.tsx`, `vitest.config.ts`.
- **Election primary display** — `ElectionCard` (state elections tab) now renders primaries AP-style: per-party card with left color border, `Avatar` images, linked candidate names, 0% for unpolled candidates, “Uncontested” badge; donut chart removed; contested and uncontested groups unified into one format. `src/components/elections/ElectionCard.tsx`.
- **Party org metrics** — `organizationCap` and `orgPerTurn` rounded to 1 decimal; Momentum section grayed out with “(Coming Soon)” label. `StatePartyMetricsPanel.tsx`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Wire & news copy** — System headlines and posts replace raw state/region IDs (e.g. `CA`, `UK_EOE`) with display names via `formatStateIdsInText` in `GET /api/news/wire`, `GET /api/news`, and `GET /api/news/[id]/replies`; corporation founding wire events use HQ state name. `formatStateIdsInText.ts`.
- **Wealth leaderboard avatars** — `/api/stock-exchange/wealth-list` resolves profile images from character upload, then Google linked avatar, then Discord avatar; `lh3.googleusercontent.com` added to allowed `next/image` domains. `WealthList.tsx` uses a slightly larger avatar.

### Platform

- **Semantic version** — Bumped to **0.1.1**.

## [0.1.0] - 2026-02-24

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Stock market Stats tab** — Tab order is Stocks, Bonds, Commodities, Wealth List, then Stats; the Listings tab is renamed to Stocks (`?tab=stocks`, legacy `?tab=listings` still works). Stats shows sector-level equity breakdown for the selected exchange, a multi-line global sector market-cap history chart, and bond/commodity snapshots. `src/app/stockmarket/[country]/page.tsx`, `components/MarketStats.tsx`, `types.ts`.
- **Stock market Stats visuals** — `GET /api/stock-exchange` listings include `brandColor` and `dividendRate`. Stats adds a global metric toggle (revenue, profit, market cap, share price, dividend %) driving per-sector bar charts, a market-cap-by-sector pie chart, largest-companies-by-sector cards with brand or hash-based colors, and mcap-weighted average dividend per sector when viewing dividend %. `stockMarketColors.ts`, `SectorPieChart.tsx`, `MarketStats.tsx`, `types.ts`, `route.ts`.
- **Campaign Operations view modes** — Card vs compact layout toggle on the Actions page; preference stored in `localStorage` and synced via `PATCH /api/settings/actions-view-mode` when logged in. `src/app/actions/components/ViewToggle.tsx`, `ActionCardCompact.tsx`, `src/app/actions/page.tsx`, `actionsTypes.ts`.
- **Compact action row visuals** — Compact rows use blurred action imagery and tighter grid alignment for scan-friendly layout. `ActionCardCompact.tsx`.
- **Internal poll redesign** — Poll results screen rework (multiple layout/UX fixes); policy positions in topline and voter-group breakdown; flatter breakdown presentation; recommendations panel. `src/app/actions/poll/` (e.g. `PollResults.tsx`, `pollResults/*`), `src/app/api/actions/poll/route.ts`, `pollHelpers.ts`.
- **Admin test mode** — Admins can toggle `gameConfig.testMode` from the dashboard (`TestModePanel`). When on, email registration requires the configured test secret and new Discord registrations are blocked. `src/app/api/admin/test-mode/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/TestModePanel.tsx`, `src/lib/db/types/gameConfig.ts`.
- **Party leadership avatars** — National party `GET /api/parties/[id]` and state party `GET /api/state/[id]/party/[partyId]` include optional `avatarUrl` for chair, vice chair, and treasurer; party overview and state leadership panels render `Avatar` components with dashed placeholders for vacant seats. `PartyOverviewPanel.tsx`, `StatePartyLeadershipPanel.tsx`, related `types.ts` files.
- **Action batch simulation** — `simulateActionBatch` runs sequential previews for ×5/×10 batches using tiered AP costs and the same validation as live execution; returns `netFundsChange` for the confirm modal. `BATCHABLE_ACTION_TYPES` lists batch-eligible actions. Unit tests in `src/lib/actions.batch.test.ts`. `src/lib/actions.ts`.
- **Actions page ×5 / ×10** — `ActionExecuteRow` on each action card (card and compact views): batch buttons with `simulateActionBatch` for affordance, confirmation dialog, and `POST /api/actions/execute` with optional `count` (5 or 10) running sequential executions. `getActionPointCost` shared with simulation; campaign blocked at 100% PI in `canPerformAction`. `ActionExecuteRow.tsx`, `execute/route.ts`, `actions.ts` schema.
- **Sector production policy API** — `GET/PATCH /api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/policy` lets CEOs read and update sector production policy with Zod validation and auth guards.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Landing globe performance** — Home hero uses the same imperative d3-geo + TopoJSON pipeline as the `/world` map (`WorldMapSVG`): country paths update via DOM `d` attributes instead of per-frame React reconciliation. Smaller viewBox (`640×368`), globe-only, status legend aligned with the world page; shared `MapSVGContent` accepts an optional `layout`. `src/components/LandingGlobe.tsx`, `src/app/world/components/MapSVGContent.tsx`, `src/app/world/worldConstants.ts`; removed `RotatingGlobe.tsx`.
- **Semantic version** — Released as **0.1.0** (new minor line on the 0.x series). Prior patch history remains documented in entries below.
- **Changelog Alpha callout** — Iteration Alpha end banner uses a staggered letter “slot” animation spelling **NEXT FRIDAY** (April 1, 2026) instead of a live second-by-second countdown, with slower refresh and accessible labeling. `src/app/changelog/components/AlphaCountdown.tsx`.
- **Corporation detail API** — `GET /api/corporations/[id]` returns `currentTurn` and passes `secondaryType` plus active type-switch penalty into `computeAllMarginModifiers` so sector maintenance/margin matches turn logic. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`.
- **CEO office: type-switch cooldown** — Cooldown warning compares `typeSwitchCooldownUntilTurn` to current game turn and shows turns remaining instead of a raw threshold. `CorporationDetail.currentTurn` on client types. `CeoOfficeTab.tsx`, `CorporationPageTypes.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Fed chair lobby form missing** — Standalone lobby flow in `CentralBankClient.tsx` now renders `LobbyForm` after selecting a candidate from the dropdown; previously the form disappeared on selection. `src/app/central-bank/[code]/CentralBankClient.tsx`.
- **State economy commodity link wrong country** — "View Commodity Prices" link in `StateEconomy` now routes CA and DE states to their correct stockmarket page instead of always falling back to US. `src/components/state/StateEconomy.tsx`.
- **Presidential election entry blocked for independents** — `canEnter` on the election detail page now allows entry during the general phase for presidential elections (independents). The API already permitted it; the UI was hiding the button. `src/app/elections/[id]/page.tsx`.
- **Corporation type-switch cooldown too long** — Reduced `TYPE_SWITCH_COOLDOWN_TURNS` from 72 to 48 (total lockout: 72 hours = 24 penalty + 48 cooldown). `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`, `docs/design/corporations.md`.
- **UK Commons 652 seats instead of 650** — `UK_COMMONS_SEATS` in `states.ts` summed to 652; reduced `UK_SEE` (91→90) and `UK_EAE` (61→60) to match the 650-seat Parliament. `src/lib/constants/states.ts`.
- **UK Commons election spawning duplicate-key errors** — `spawnCommonsElection` and `spawnHouseElection` now include `seatId` (via `getSeatIdFromElection`) so spawned elections no longer conflict with the `unique_active_election_per_seat_v2` partial index when multiple UK regions resolve in the same turn. `src/lib/turn/election/electionSpawning.ts`.
- **UK Commons officials deleted on tally-finalized recovery** — `resolveGeneralElections` now fetches all tallies including finalized ones. Elections whose tally was already finalized (officials written) but were never marked `resolved` due to a prior exception now recover correctly: the next cycle is spawned and the election is marked resolved without re-processing or deleting officials. Per-election try-catch prevents one failure from aborting the entire loop. `src/lib/turn/electionResolution.ts`.
- **Cross-country whip directives** — UK party chairs can no longer issue whip directives on US bills or view US bills in the whippable-bills list. Bills are now filtered by country using the `stateId` prefix pattern (`^uk_`). `src/app/api/parties/[id]/whip/route.ts`, `src/app/api/parties/[id]/whippable-bills/route.ts`.
- **Demographics seed composition** — Population derivation now reads exclusively from `VOTER_GROUP_COMPOSITION` (no duplicated hardcoding); archetype compositions include `race.white` where appropriate; lean modulation strengthened; Option C fixes for sign handling and Layer 1 ideology defaults/tuning. `src/lib/seeds/stateDemographics.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/demographicCategories.ts`, `src/lib/seeds/demographicLeanValidation.test.ts`.
- **Admin national party appointment vs elections** — Appointing leadership via admin API no longer cancels active national party leadership elections; the election can finish and the winner assumes the role, consistent with state party behavior. `src/app/api/admin/parties/[partyId]/appoint/route.ts`.
- **Corporation CEO handoff** — CEO resignation clears CEO election votes so the next CEO election starts clean; CEO-gated corporation actions respect `ceoVacant` so vacant companies are not treated as still CEO-controlled. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/ceo/resign/route.ts`, `decline/route.ts`, `accept/route.ts`, and related queries using `ceoVacant`.
- **Admin log schema vs test mode** — `AdminLogAction` now includes `test_mode_enabled` and `test_mode_disabled`, matching `createAdminLog` calls from `/api/admin/test-mode` (fixes production TypeScript build). `src/lib/db/types/adminLog.ts`.
- **Internal poll vs last election** — Election comparison panel labels the modeled poll pool (appeal-weighted reach or in-race allocation) and shows **last completed cycle** party vote shares from `electionVoteTallies` alongside it, so the UI no longer reads like a mismatch with real results. `getLastElectionPartyShares` (`prevElectionPartyShares.ts`), `electionOpponents.ts`, `ElectionComparisonPanel.tsx`, `PollResults.tsx`.

### Platform

- **Test architecture & coverage** — Documented coverage gaps and expansion plan in `docs/engineering/test-architecture-and-gaps.md`. Vitest Phase 1–3 additions across auth, bills, primaries, scoring, corporations, bonds, UK government, parties, and president flows; shared `src/lib/test-utils/factories.ts` and `mockDb` assertion helpers (`mockDb.ts`, `mockDb.test.ts`).
- **Admin heal: corporation type-switch timers** — `GET/POST /api/admin/heal/corporation-timers` diagnoses corporations with type-switch fields and clears expired timers (optional `forceAll`). Admin System tab UI `HealCorporationTimers.tsx`.

