## [0.0.39] - 2026-02-22

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **NPP Recruitment System** — Third parties can now recruit NPP candidates through two mechanisms: (1) Initial spawn on party creation spawns NPPs across selected states/regions, (2) Ongoing recruitment through the party Actions tab. US parties select 4 states + locked home state (5 total), spawning 2 NPPs each (10 total). UK parties select 2 regions with no locked home, spawning 1 NPP each (2 total). `src/lib/npp/recruitment.ts`, `src/app/api/parties/[id]/recruitment/`, `src/components/party/NppRecruitmentPanel.tsx`.
- **Recruitment cost scaling** — NPP recruitment costs scale based on existing NPPs: base cost increases by state NPP count (5 actions/$100K for first, up to 25 actions/$1M for 4+), plus party-wide modifier (+1 action per 20 NPPs capped at +5, +10% funds per 20 NPPs capped at +100%). 24-turn party-wide cooldown between recruitments. `src/lib/npp/recruitment.ts`.
- **Recruitment slot limits** — Per-state recruitment slots based on state party organization: 0-24% org → 2 slots, 25-49% → 3, 50-74% → 4, 75-100% → 5. Ensures new parties can always recruit (minimum 2 slots) while rewarding organization investment.
- **State-level recruitment API** — State party leadership (Chair/Vice Chair) can recruit NPPs using state party resources. National leadership can recruit in states without active state leadership using national party resources. `src/app/api/state/[stateId]/party/[partyId]/recruitment/route.ts`.
- **Party creation state selection UI** — Two-step party creation modal: Step 1 collects party details, Step 2 shows state/region picker with alignment indicators (good/neutral/poor fit based on party positions vs state lean). US: 4 additional states + locked home. UK: 2 regions, no locked home. `src/app/parties/components/CreatePartyModal.tsx`.
- **Country-specific party creation config** — Added `partyCreationNPPs` to `CountryConfig` interface specifying `statesRequired`, `lockHomeState`, and `nppsPerState` per country. US: 4 states + locked home, 2 NPPs each. UK/CA/DE: 2 regions, no lock, 1 NPP each. `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`.
- **Creation states API** — New endpoint returns states for party creation picker with alignment indicators, house seats, and existing party presence. `src/app/api/parties/creation-states/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Cabinet party display** — Cabinet position cards now show party names and colors instead of raw party IDs for both members and nominees. Uses `getPartyHex()` for consistent color handling. `src/app/api/whitehouse/cabinet/route.ts`.
- **Party sync on membership changes** — `ElectedOfficial.party` field now syncs correctly when characters join, leave, or create parties. Previously could show stale party data. `src/app/api/parties/[id]/join/route.ts`, `src/app/api/parties/[id]/leave/route.ts`, `src/app/api/parties/route.ts`.
- **NPP party field on election win** — NPPs now have their `party` field correctly updated when winning elections for a different party. `src/lib/turn/electionResolution.ts`.
- **Cross-country party operations** — Added `countryId` checks to party deletion, cleanup, membership routes, budget operations, influence validation, and leadership whip matching to prevent cross-country data leakage. Multiple files in `src/app/api/parties/` and `src/lib/`.
- **State validation on party creation** — Party creation now validates that all selected states exist in the creator's country before spawning NPPs. `src/app/api/parties/route.ts`.

## [0.0.39] - 2026-02-23

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Heal Stale Admin Appointments** — New admin heal endpoint at `/api/admin/heal/stale-admin-appointments` removes duplicate `electedOfficials` records for the same seat. Prioritizes filled records (with characterId/nppId) over vacant ones; among equal fill status, keeps the most recent by `electedAt`/`updatedAt`. Also clears stale `currentOffice` from affected characters/NPPs. UI component added to Admin > System > Heal tab. `src/app/api/admin/heal/stale-admin-appointments/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/HealStaleAdminAppointments.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Relocation with office auto-resign** — Players holding office can now relocate to a new state. Instead of blocking relocation, a warning popup appears explaining they will automatically resign from their current office. The API auto-clears the `electedOfficials` record and `currentOffice` field. CEO auto-resign (already existed) continues to work. Only active campaigns still block relocation. `src/components/RelocateButton.tsx`, `src/app/api/character/relocate/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Cross-country party ID collisions** — Fixed all party lookups using `sequentialId` without `countryId` context. Since `sequentialId` is only unique within a country (e.g., sequentialId `1` exists in US, UK, CA, and DE), lookups must include `countryId` to avoid returning wrong party data. Updated 30+ files with three patterns: (1) Query-level filtering by `countryId` before building maps, (2) Composite map keys `${countryId}:${sequentialId}`, (3) Use of `getPartyMap(db, countryId)` utility. Added safety comments documenting pre-filtered data. Key files: `src/lib/nationalPartyElections.ts`, `src/app/api/elections/route.ts`, `src/app/api/discord-bot/race/route.ts`, `src/lib/elections/candidateEnrichment.ts`, `src/lib/charts/parliamentChart.ts`.
- **PartyLogo countryId prop** — All `PartyLogo` component calls now pass `countryId` to ensure correct logo lookup. Updated election detail charts, general election panels, running mate selector, chamber charts, and election log components.
- **CLAUDE.md party lookup documentation** — Added "Party Lookups — Always Use countryId" section documenting the requirement with correct/incorrect code examples.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Campaign Operations hero** — Actions page hero now shows favorability as a second meter stacked under political influence (shared decay display with profile). `src/app/actions/components/ActionsHero.tsx`.
- **UI reuse guidelines** — `docs/engineering/ui-reuse-guidelines.md` documents repeated dashboard/hero patterns and when to extract shared primitives vs keep route-local markup.
- **Personal Campaign Donation action** — New "convertCash" action on the Actions page that converts player-chosen amount of personal cash on hand (`cashOnHand`) into campaign funds (`funds`) at a 50% rate. Costs 2 AP. Infamy scales with amount via power curve: `15 × (amount / $1M) ^ 0.564` — ~4 at $100K, ~15 at $1M, ~55 at $10M, capped at 100. UI provides amount input with 25%/50%/Max quick-select buttons and live preview of campaign funds gained and infamy cost. Card blocked when `cashOnHand ≤ 0`. Added `cashOnHandChange` to `ActionResult` and `ActionLog.result`, `convertAmount` to execute schema. `src/lib/actions.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/gameState.ts`, `src/lib/api/schemas/actions.ts`, `src/app/api/actions/execute/route.ts`, `src/app/actions/actionsConstants.ts`, `src/app/actions/actionsTypes.ts`, `src/app/actions/components/ActionCard.tsx`, `src/app/actions/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/images/actions/[slug]/route.ts`.

### Refactored

- **Hero stats strip** — Introduced `HeroStatsStrip` (`src/components/ui/HeroStatsStrip.tsx`) for the common horizontal stats row under hero images; adopted on Campaign Operations, legislature overview, and Elections hub.

### Platform

- **Type and schema contracts** — Added `docs/engineering/type-and-schema-contracts.md` describing when static types vs Zod validation apply. `GET /api/game/config` returns `PublicGameConfig` (Discord webhook URLs removed). Session JWT claims are validated with `userPayloadSchema` in `verifyAuth`. US House/Senate leadership election code uses `SenateLeadershipElectionRole` / `HouseLeadershipElectionRole` and MongoDB `Filter<>` instead of unchecked `as any`; fixed House NPP auto-assignment party slug when no candidates (incorrect `minority_leader_house` string compare).
- **Client bundle / Turbopack build** — Split hex-only ObjectId helpers into `src/lib/utils/objectIdHex.ts` (no `mongodb` import) so Client Components that use `profileUrls.ts` no longer pull the MongoDB driver into the browser bundle (fixes `Can't resolve 'child_process'`, `dns`, etc. during `next build`).

