## [0.0.38] - 2026-02-22

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Extraction & Mining sector type** — New 15th sector type (`extraction`) with four raw material commodities: Iron Ore (`iron`, $30/ton), Coal (`coal`, $25/ton), Crude Oil (`oil`, $70/barrel), Rare Earth Minerals (`rare_earth`, $120/kg). Extraction sectors supply raw materials demanded by manufacturing, technology, energy, automobiles, and defense. Four strategies: Standard Mining, Deep Extraction, Precision Mining, Diversified Operations. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`, `src/lib/constants/sectorStrategies.ts`.
- **Logistics sector type** — New 14th sector type (`logistics`) supplying Freight & Transportation (`freight`) and Consulting Services (`consulting_services`). Three strategies: Standard Logistics, Express Freight, Supply Chain Consulting. `src/lib/constants/sectorStrategies.ts`.
- **Sector operating strategies** — Sectors can now switch between production strategies that alter their commodity supply/demand rates. Each sector type has 3–4 strategies (e.g., Manufacturing: Standard, Heavy Industry, Precision Electronics, Consumer Goods). Strategy switching costs 25% of daily revenue, takes 12 turns to transition (with -5% margin penalty during), and has a 24-turn cooldown. Strategy selector appears on both sector detail page and corporation Sectors tab. `src/lib/constants/sectorStrategies.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/strategy/route.ts`.
- **Strategy change confirmation panel** — Unified confirmation component shows commodity-by-commodity comparison table (output rate, input rate, market status) with estimated commodity margin before vs after switching. Fetches live global supply/demand from `/api/commodities` to show market status (surplus/balanced/shortage) per commodity. `src/components/corporation/StrategyChangeConfirm.tsx`.
- **Secondary corporation type** — Corporations can now set a secondary sector focus from the CEO page. Sectors matching the secondary type receive +2.5% margin (half of primary's +5%). Tradeoff: base sprawl penalty doubles from -0.5% to -1.0% per pair over 15 sectors (still reducible via logistics spending). New `secondaryType` field on Corporation DB type, CEO page selector, settings API, turn processor, and sector detail API. `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts`, `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`, `src/components/corporation/CeoOfficeTab.tsx`.
- **Primary/secondary type switching with penalty** — Changing primary or secondary corporation type incurs a -10% margin penalty on ALL sectors for 24 hours (`TYPE_SWITCH_PENALTY_TURNS = 24`), followed by a 72-hour cooldown (`TYPE_SWITCH_COOLDOWN_TURNS = 72`). CEO page warns before type changes and displays cooldown status. `typeSwitchTurn` and `typeSwitchCooldownUntilTurn` fields on Corporation. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/settings/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporationTurn.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **"Energy & Fuel" renamed to "Electricity"** — Commodity label changed from "Energy & Fuel" to "Electricity". Internal type key `energy` unchanged. Hero alt text updated. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`.
- **Sector type count increased to 15** — `SECTOR_TYPE_COUNT` updated from 13 to 15 to include logistics and extraction. Market size per state sector recalculated accordingly. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Extraction strategy balance** — Corrected base supply/demand rates for extraction strategies and fixed biotech healthcare strategy input rates. Sustainable agriculture strategy inputs balanced. `src/lib/constants/sectorStrategies.ts`.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **NPP Economy System** — Non-Player Politicians now generate campaign funds and spend action points like players. NPPs generate funds at 50% of player rate using logarithmic population scaling (compresses large-state advantage from 8x to ~4.7x). Diminishing returns soft cap reduces generation efficiency as NPP funds accumulate ($0-50K: 100%, $50K-150K: 75%, $150K-300K: 50%, $300K+: 25%). NPPs gain 2 action points per turn (capped at 100 vs player's 200) and spend on BuildDonorBase, Campaign (+0.5 PI), Advertise (+1.5 fav), and PartyDonation. AI decision logic uses hybrid approach: office context sets baseline priorities, personality traits (loyalty, ambition) modify weights. NPPs pay party tax identically to players. `src/lib/turn/nppFundGeneration.ts`, `src/lib/turn/nppActionProcessing.ts`, `src/lib/npp/actionAi.ts`, `src/lib/utils/fundGeneration.ts`.
- **NPP Profile Pages** — New `/politicians/npp/[id]` route displays NPP profiles with economic stats (funds, donor base level, action points), personality traits, office history, and political stats. Visual differentiation with "Non-Player Politician" badge. Legacy `/npp/[id]` route redirects to new location. Updated 36 files to use new URL format with two-pass link audit verification. `src/app/politicians/npp/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/lib/utils/profileUrls.ts`.
- **NPP Economy Admin Panel** — Admin > World > NPPs page now includes NPP Action Economy panel with enable/disable toggle, key stats (total NPPs, NPPs with funds, total funds, action points pooled, avg donor base level), and next processing turn indicator. `src/components/admin/NppEconomyPanel.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/npp/economy/route.ts`.
- **NPP Economy Migration** — Admin > Support > Migrations tab now includes NPP Economy Fields migration with Diagnose and Run Migration buttons. Migration initializes `funds`, `donorBaseLevel`, `actionPoints`, `lastActionProcessedTurn` on all NPPs and adds `nppEconomyEnabled` toggle to gameConfig. `src/app/api/admin/heal/npp-economy-fields/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/MigrationsTab.tsx`.
- **National Party Leadership Test Suite** — Comprehensive unit tests for national party leadership election functionality including eligibility, ballot building, and vote counting. `src/lib/nationalPartyElections.test.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **UK Parliament Bills Party Display** — UK Parliament bills route now displays sponsor party name and color, matching the US Congress bills route. Fetches UK parties filtered by `countryId: "UK"` and enriches formatted bills with `partyName` and `partyColor` fields. `src/app/api/legislature/uk/bills/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **NPP Incumbent Priority** — Restructured NPP election entry to process incumbents first across all races before filling remaining slots with non-incumbents. Previously, a non-incumbent could be assigned to a race before the incumbent for a different race was processed. Now uses two-phase approach: Phase 1 enters all incumbents into their defending seats (sorted by race priority), Phase 2 fills remaining slots. `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.ts`.
- **NPP Economy Config ID** — Fixed NPP fund generation and action processing silently failing because they queried `gameConfig` with `_id: "current"` instead of the correct `_id: "default"`. `src/lib/turn/nppFundGeneration.ts`, `src/lib/turn/nppActionProcessing.ts`.
- **Cross-Country Party Leadership Assignment** — Fixed bug where party leadership could be incorrectly assigned across countries (e.g., UK party leader assigned to US party). Added country validation to leadership assignment logic. `src/lib/nationalPartyElections.ts`, `src/app/api/parties/[id]/election/enter/route.ts`.
- **Cross-Country Party Sequential ID Collisions** — Fixed party lookups that used sequential ID alone, which could match the wrong country's party when multiple countries have parties with the same sequential ID. Turn processing files now use composite keys (`${countryId}:${sequentialId}`) for party maps: `primaryResolution.ts`, `demographicTurnoutTurn.ts`, `nppActionProcessing.ts`, `electionResolution.ts`, `emptyPartyCleanup.ts`. US-only contexts (Congress, Speaker) filter party queries with `countryId: "US"`: `congress/bills/route.ts`, `speakerRecalculation.ts`. Wiki utilities and page components derive country from state IDs using `getCountryIdFromStateId()`: `seatData.ts`, `searchIndex.ts`, `partyData.ts`, `region/[id]/page.tsx`, `wiki/elections/[id]/route.ts`.

