## [0.0.36] - 2026-02-21

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Maintenance mode** — Admin-toggleable maintenance mode with countdown timer. Non-admin users are blocked from all access and registration during maintenance windows. Maintenance check cached in-memory with 10s TTL. `src/app/api/admin/maintenance/`, `src/components/admin/`.
- **Bond default resolution** — Corporations that default on bonds now face a 96-hour credit penalty. Defaulted refinance cleanup and refinance preview corrected. `src/app/api/corporations/`, `src/lib/turn/`.
- **Corporate credit rating system** — Full credit rating tab with composite 0–100 gauge, weighted subscore cards, balance sheet context, what-if debt slider, peer comparison panel, and credit history SVG chart. Credit rating changes trigger wire events and CEO notifications. New `GET /api/corporations/[id]/credit-peer-stats` returns country and sector-type peer averages. `src/components/corporation/CreditRatingTab.tsx`, `src/lib/bonds/corporateCredit.ts`.
- **Central bank chair infamy mechanic** — Fed/central bank chairs now accumulate "Public Scrutiny" (0–100) based on inflation and GDP growth performance. High inflation and low growth increase scrutiny; the inverse reduces it. Positive recovery effects are dampened at high scrutiny levels (`1 - infamy/150` multiplier). Above 25 scrutiny, chair office benefits (actions + NPI) are halved. Chair gets +3 actions/turn and +0.5 NPI/turn base (1.5 actions and +0.25 NPI when penalized). Scrutiny resets on appointment/vacancy. Displayed on central bank page with tooltipped meter and per-turn change. `src/lib/turn/centralBankChairTurn.ts`, `src/app/central-bank/`.
- **National influence on public profiles** — National influence stat now visible on character profile pages, politicians page cards, and election candidate displays. Politicians page "NPI" sort now correctly sorts by national influence instead of state influence. Politician cards show 3 stats: National, State, and Approval. `src/app/character/[id]/page.tsx`, `src/app/politicians/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/politicians/route.ts`.
- **Wealth-based starting funds** — Character creation now grants starting funds based on wealth background: Low Income ($500K), Middle Income ($1M), High Income ($2M). Amounts shown in registration dropdown. `src/app/api/auth/character/route.ts`, `src/app/register/components/CharacterBackgroundSection.tsx`.
- **Wiki page sync** — Admin wiki management now supports syncing individual pages from design docs with per-row sync buttons and batch "Sync all" action. `src/components/admin/wiki/WikiPageTable.tsx`.
- **CEO offer decline** — New `POST /api/corporations/[id]/ceo/decline` route lets the pending CEO candidate reject the offer. Preserves seat vacancy state correctly. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/ceo/decline/route.ts`.
- **Commodity page synthetic demand** — "Base Economic Demand" and "GDP-Scaled Retail Demand" now appear as system entries in the Top Consumers list on commodity detail pages, showing where non-corporate demand originates. `src/app/api/commodities/[type]/route.ts`, `src/app/commodity/[type]/page.tsx`.
- **Bonds page sovereign/corporate toggle** — Bond table now has a toggle between Corporate and Sovereign bonds, defaulting to Corporate. Sovereign bonds display the issuing country's flag as their logo instead of a generic icon. `src/app/stockmarket/[country]/components/BondTable.tsx`.
- **Building materials macro demand** — Building materials now have GDP-driven construction demand per state (fraction of GDP scaled by GDP growth). Real estate sectors also now demand building materials (rate 0.20) in addition to supplying them — reflecting that real estate development consumes construction materials. Shown as "GDP-Scaled Construction Demand" on the commodity page. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/turn/commodityPriceTurn.ts`.
- **Profile header banner image** — Optional wide hero image for your character, uploaded from Settings; persisted on `Character.profileHeaderImageUrl` and shown on self profile (`ProfileHeader`) and public character pages. `src/app/api/upload/profile-header/route.ts`, `src/components/ProfileHeaderImageUpload.tsx`, `src/app/profile/components/ProfileHeader.tsx`, `src/app/character/[id]/page.tsx`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Settings profile media previews** — Header image and avatar upload controls use compact previews (`ProfileHeaderImageUpload` `variant="compact"`, `ProfilePictureUpload` `size="compact"`) so the settings identity row is not dominated by large image areas. Full-size banner upload UX remains available elsewhere via default variants. `src/app/settings/page.tsx`, `src/components/ProfileHeaderImageUpload.tsx`, `src/components/ProfilePictureUpload.tsx`.
- **Admin panel mobile rework** — Main tab bar now shows compact labels under icons on mobile instead of hiding them. Replaced all inline styles with Tailwind classes and removed JS hover handlers. Sub-tab bar uses smaller touch targets on mobile. Dashboard quick links use explicit responsive grid columns. Header, system warning, and section spacing tightened for mobile. Added `.scrollbar-hide` CSS utility (was used but never defined). `src/components/AdminTabs.tsx`, `src/components/admin/tabs/`.
- **Public character profile parity** — Other players' profiles now show the same detailed PoliticalStanding component as self-view: tooltipped stat cards for Actions, State Influence, National Influence, Favorability, Infamy, and Donor Network with per-turn rates. Added Career History timeline and styled Finances section. `src/app/character/[id]/page.tsx`.
- **Commodity margin rebalance** — Commodity margin modifiers now use the output-blend approach (compute per-level, blend 75/25) matching how prices are blended. `COMMODITY_LOG_K` raised from 12 to 65; per-commodity contributions soft-capped at ±50%. Global stabilizer reduced from 25K to 1,500; new state-level stabilizer of 250 prevents extreme ratios without dampening real signals. Sector margins can now go negative — sectors in terrible commodity markets drain corporate liquid capital. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporationTurn.ts`, sector and corporation API routes.
- **Sector type match/mismatch modifier** — Sectors matching the parent corporation's type get +5% margin bonus; mismatched sectors get -15% penalty. Encourages focused corporations. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.
- **Logistical sprawl penalty** — Corporations with more than 15 sectors incur -0.5% margin penalty for every 2 sectors over the threshold. Discourages unchecked expansion. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.
- **Corporation sectors tab redesign** — Replaced wide horizontal table with per-sector cards using label-above-value responsive grid (2→3→4→7 columns). Added sort control with dropdown for all metrics plus asc/desc toggle. `src/components/corporation/SectorsTab.tsx`.
- **Performance: auth/me parallelization** — State, party, and unread queries in `/api/auth/me` now run in parallel, reducing response time. `src/app/api/auth/me/route.ts`.
- **Performance: turn processing batching** — Election resolution batch-fetches character/NPP data; campaign processing batch-counts endorsements via aggregation. `src/lib/turn/`.
- **Performance: API caching & projections** — Cache-Control headers and field projections added to read-heavy routes. Wiki index cached. Election round-trips reduced. Landing page DB reads parallelized. `src/app/api/`.
- **Performance: notifications $facet** — Paginated fetch and total count combined into a single `$facet`aggregation, halving notification query round-trips.`src/app/api/notifications/`.
- **Performance: wiki & profile routes** — Added caching, projections, and Suspense boundaries to wiki and profile routes. Reduced turn-system data transfer. `src/app/api/wiki/`, `src/app/profile/`.
- **Performance: MongoDB connection tuning** — Configured connection pool size and idle timeout. Added retry logic for initial connection. `src/lib/mongodb.ts`.
- **Performance: Sentry tuning** — Trace sampling reduced to 10% in production. SSE connections excluded from performance stats. Unified client instrumentation. `src/lib/sentry/`.
- **Central bank hero images** — Updated Federal Reserve and Bank of England hero images to higher-quality Wikimedia Commons photos. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Commodity margin accuracy** — Fixed margin modifiers being nearly inert due to three compounding issues: raw-value blend instead of output-blend, K=12 too low, and 25K stabilizer dominating real activity. See "Commodity margin rebalance" above. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`.
- **NPP whip country parameter** — Fixed national party whip panel failing to load bills because the `country` query parameter was not passed to the whippable-bills, whippable-leadership, and whip API endpoints. Error messages now show specific API errors instead of generic "Failed to load bills". `src/components/party/WhipPanel.tsx`, `src/app/parties/[id]/page.tsx`.
- **State party appointments** — Removed vice chair and treasurer appointment UI from state party pages — these positions are elected, not appointed. `src/components/`.
- **Bond refinance cleanup** — Defaulted bond refinance records now cleaned up correctly; refinance preview no longer errors on defaulted bonds. `src/app/api/bonds/`.
- **Commodity stabilizer scope** — Base supply/demand stabilizer moved to global pool only, fixing double-counting that distorted local market balances. `src/lib/turn/`.
- **MongoDB connection resilience** — Retry logic added for initial MongoDB connection; maintenance fetch bounded in middleware to prevent hanging requests. `src/lib/mongodb.ts`, middleware.
- **Profile Suspense boundary** — Resolved merge conflict in profile page Suspense boundary after perf-audit merge.

