## [0.0.32] - 2026-02-17

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Abandon sector** — CEOs can abandon a sector from the corporation page Owned Sectors tab. Abandoning deletes the sector and returns its revenue to the unowned pool. Confirmation required. `POST /api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/abandon`, Abandon button in sectors table.
- **Party donation** — Members can donate personal funds to their state party or national party from the Treasury tab. State party: `/api/state/[id]/party/[partyId]/donate`. National party: `/api/parties/[id]/donate`. Minimum $1,000 per donation. Donate section visible only to members.
- **Share trading system** — New Shares/Interact tab on corporation detail page. Players can buy and sell shares at market price via a universal public float market maker. Limit orders (buy/sell) with escrow and share reservation; orders fill automatically each turn via `fillPendingShareOrders()`. New `ShareOrder` collection with open/filled/cancelled lifecycle. `publicFloat` field on Corporation tracks available market supply. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/buy/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/sell/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/orders/route.ts`.
- **CEO share issuance** — CEOs can issue new shares to the public float (0–50% of outstanding) with dilution preview. CEO self-issuance at 15% premium sends funds to corporate liquid capital. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/issue/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/self-issue/route.ts`.
- **Dividend system** — CEOs can set a dividend rate (0–100%) with 24-hour change cooldown. Dividends are paid pro-rata to shareholders each turn from pre-dividend income. `dividendRate` and `dividendRateChangedAt` fields on Corporation. Turn processor distributes to character `cashOnHand`.
- **Shareholder register** — Corporation detail page shows all shareholders with ownership percentages and avatars. Shareholders tracked via `Corporation.shareholders` array.
- **Share price formula** — Blended share price: 20% last trade price + 40% balance sheet value + 40% income-based (15× P/E). NPV discount rate raised from 10% to 25% annually to reduce aggressive valuations. `SHARE_PRICE_PE_MULTIPLE`, `NPV_ANNUAL_DISCOUNT_RATE` in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.
- **CEO shareholder backfill** — Corporations created before shareholder tracking auto-detect unaccounted shares and attribute them to the CEO on first read. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`.
- **Retail as a commodity** — "Consumer Goods" is now an 11th commodity type (`retail`). Retail sectors supply it (rate 0.5 of revenue). Demand is driven by GDP growth (50% national average + 50% state-level) via `computeRetailDemandMultiplier()`. Positive GDP growth → demand exceeds supply → price rises → retail surplus bonus. Negative GDP growth → oversupply → price falls. Displays on commodity pages and stock exchange commodities panel like all other commodities. `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`.
- **Retail reduced commodity input penalty** — Retail sectors face only 25% of negative commodity input penalties (`RETAIL_NEGATIVE_COMMODITY_PENALTY_FACTOR = 0.25`). Retail can absorb or substitute supply chain shortages more easily than heavy industry. Positive modifiers (oversupply benefits) are unaffected. `applyRetailPenaltyFactor()` in `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`, applied in turn processor and both API routes.
- **Split escalation cost system** — Each sector split now costs marketing strength in addition to cash. First split costs 1 MS, second costs 2, third 4, fourth 8, etc. (formula: `2^splitEscalation`). Escalation decays by 1 level each turn, so costs halve over time. New `splitEscalation` field on Corporation documents. `src/app/api/state/[id]/economy/attack/route.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts`.
- **Commodity shortage badges** — Sector detail page now shows severity badges (Mild, Moderate, Severe, Critical) next to input commodities experiencing a shortage. Badge severity is based on demand/supply ratio: Mild (1-1.5×), Moderate (1.5-2×), Severe (2-3×), Critical (3×+). `src/app/corporation/[id]/sector/[sectorId]/page.tsx`.
- **Single source of truth for profit margin modifiers** — New `computeAllMarginModifiers()` shared utility in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts` computes all margin modifiers (9 state metrics + commodity). Used by both the corporation API and sector detail API, eliminating duplicate logic.
- **Empty party auto-cleanup** — Turn processor now automatically deletes non-default parties with 0 members. Also deletes all associated data: state party organizations, party budgets, state/national/committee party elections and candidates/votes, and bill whip positions. `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/emptyPartyCleanup.ts`.
- **MobileSelect component** — New `MobileSelect` component in `src/components/ui/MobileSelect.tsx` for mobile-friendly dropdowns. Uses a scrollable bottom sheet modal with search functionality instead of native `<select>` picker (which can have scrolling issues on some mobile devices).

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Share issuance 24h cooldown** — Public share issuance and CEO self-issue (capital injection) are now limited to once per 24 hours per corporation. Both routes share the cooldown. `lastShareIssuance` field on Corporation. `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/issue/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/shares/self-issue/route.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts`, corporation page Shares tab.
- **Unowned sector capture bonus** — When splitting unowned sectors (target has 0 MS), capture is 25% more favorable. `UNOWNED_CAPTURE_BONUS_MULTIPLIER = 1.25` in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`. Applied in economy attack route and economy API for estimated capture display.
- **State economy tab defaults to corp sector** — When viewing a state page Economy tab and you own a corporation, the sector selector now defaults to your corporation's sector type (e.g. Technology, Energy). Manual selection of another sector is preserved. `src/app/api/state/[id]/economy/route.ts`, `src/components/state/StateEconomy.tsx`.
- **Home location profit margin bonuses** — Sectors in a corporation's HQ state now get +10% profit margin; sectors in the same nation (different state) get +5%; international sectors get 0%. Applied in turn processor, corporation API, and sector detail API. Displayed in margin breakdown on corporation page and sector detail page. `getHomeLocationMarginBonus()`, `computeAllMarginModifiers()`, `corporationTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]/route.ts`.
- **Stock market ticker and price change** — Ticker now shows corps by rolling 24h % change (gainers first, then losers), then commodities, with current price and 24h % displayed. Stock exchange API adds `priceChange24h` from `corporationHistory`; commodities API replaces % of base price with 24h % from `commodityPriceHistory`. Stock listings table adds 24h % column and sort option. Commodities panel and detail page now show 24h change. `src/app/api/stock-exchange/route.ts`, `src/app/api/commodities/route.ts`, `src/app/api/commodities/[type]/route.ts`, `src/app/stockmarket/[country]/page.tsx`.
- **Marketing strength rate increased 23×** — `MARKETING_STRENGTH_PER_MILLION` increased from 0.214 to 5.0. A $100K/day marketing budget now gains ~0.02 MS per turn (0.5 MS/day), up from ~0.001 per turn. At $1M/day: 5 MS/day. This makes marketing investment meaningfully impactful. `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.
- **Marketing strength gain shown per turn** — Corporation page now displays "+X/turn" for marketing strength growth, with tooltip showing the exact rate and formula. API now correctly computes per-turn rate (was previously showing daily rate as per-turn).
- **Corporation API includes commodity modifiers** — The corporation API (`/api/corporations/[id]`) now fetches commodity prices and includes the commodity margin modifier in sector effective margin and profit calculations. Previously commodity effects were applied in the turn processor but not reflected on the corporation page, causing displayed margins and profits to be incorrect.
- **Corporation page shows commodity modifier** — The sector card tooltip on the corporation page now includes a "Commodity markets" line showing the commodity margin modifier, matching the sector detail breakdown.
- **Split UI shows MS cost** — The state economy page split button now shows the current MS cost alongside the cash cost, and is disabled when the player lacks sufficient marketing strength.
- **Commodity shortage system reworked to logarithmic scaling** — Replaced quadratic buyer penalty (`-15% × shortage²`) and linear seller bonus (`+15% × shortage`) with symmetric logarithmic formula: `modifier = K × Σ(rate × ln(D/S))` where K=8 (`COMMODITY_LOG_K`). Self-balancing curve prevents runaway snowball effects while remaining uncapped. A fully-weighted resource at 2× demand gives ~5.5% modifier. Same curve applies symmetrically to both input costs (buyers) and output demand (sellers). Oversupply now also affects both sides (buyers benefit, sellers suffer). `computeCommodityMarginModifier()` and `computeCommoditySurplusBonus()` in `src/lib/constants/commodities.ts`.
- **Sector API now includes surplus bonus in commodity modifier** — The sector detail API (`/api/corporations/[id]/sectors/[sectorId]`) now combines both `computeCommodityMarginModifier()` (input cost) and `computeCommoditySurplusBonus()` (output demand) into the `commodityModifier` field, matching the turn processor behavior.
- **Sector detail commodity label updated** — "Commodity shortage" modifier row renamed to "Commodity markets" with dynamic color (green for bonus, red for penalty) and updated tooltip describing logarithmic scaling.
- **Styled Slider component** — New reusable `Slider` component in `src/components/ui/Slider.tsx` with theme-aware styling, color variants (primary, warning, error, success, secondary, muted), and proper fill gradient. CSS in `src/app/globals.css` with 8px track and 22px thumb.
- **Org building shows org growth** — The org building slider and stats now display org growth directly instead of momentum values. Slider shows "+X.XX org" and stats box shows "Org growth per turn". Description updated to "$100k/turn = +1.0 org/turn at equilibrium".
- **Momentum display as org growth** — The "Momentum" display in the party header and metrics panel now shows org growth value (momentum × 0.25) instead of raw momentum. Label kept as "Momentum" for familiarity. Bar range changed from ±10 to ±2.5.
- **Org building budget limit increased** — `MAX_ORG_BUILDING_PERCENT` increased from 25% to 75% in `src/lib/api/schemas/settings.ts`, allowing parties to invest more heavily in organization building.
- **ORG_PER_MOMENTUM tuned** — Reduced from 0.5 to 0.25 so that $100k/turn spending yields exactly +1.0 org/turn at equilibrium (equilibrium momentum = 4.0, org growth = 4.0 × 0.25 = 1.0).

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Admin Legislation tab lag** — Admin > Politics > Legislation no longer causes a large lag spike on open. Optimizations: (1) Admin bills API now fetches only legislation types referenced by bills instead of the full collection; (2) New `/api/admin/committee-politicians` returns lightweight `{ id, name, isNPP }` for committee dropdowns instead of full politician data; (3) Legislation types API supports `?minimal=1` for committee use (projection: \_id, name, policyDomain, positions); (4) Fixed committee-assignments response extraction when API returns `{ assignments, ... }`. `src/app/api/admin/bills/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/committee-politicians/route.ts`, `src/app/api/game/legislation-types/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/LegislationTab.tsx`.
- **Commodity price color logic reversed** — On the commodity detail page (`/commodity/[type]`) and stock market commodities panel (`/stockmarket/[country]`), price increases were shown in green (success) and decreases in red (error). This was backwards for commodities: price above base indicates shortage (bad), price below base indicates oversupply (good). Colors are now correct: red for price increases, green for decreases.
- **UK legislation types showing in US bill proposals** — The legislation types API now filters by country (`?country=us` or `?country=uk`). US Congress and state legislatures only see US legislation types, UK Parliament will only see UK legislation types. Types without `countryScope` are treated as US-only for backwards compatibility. `src/app/api/game/legislation-types/route.ts`.
- **Corporation page profit margins were wrong** — The corporation API was not computing commodity margin modifiers for sectors, causing displayed effective margins and profits to differ from the actual turn-processed values. Now uses the same `computeAllMarginModifiers()` as the turn processor.
- **Duplicate momentum decay** — Momentum was being decayed twice per turn: once in `demographicTurnoutTurn.ts` and again in `partyOrgTurn.ts`. Removed the duplicate section from demographicTurnoutTurn; decay is now only applied in partyOrgTurn.
- **Equilibrium momentum formula** — UI was using `G / D` (gain / decay rate) instead of correct `G × (1-D) / D`. At 20% decay, this showed equilibrium 25% higher than actual (5× instead of 4×). Fixed in `FundraisingManagementSection.tsx`.
- **Turn processing capContributions null error** — `partyOrgTurn` threw JSON parse error when `spo.capContributions` was undefined. Added null check before deep-cloning in `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/turnProcessing.ts`.
- **Presidential election results showing "Unknown"** — Completed elections showed "Unknown" for all candidates because the API only fetched `status: "active"` candidates, but all candidates are marked `withdrawn` when an election completes. Now fetches all candidates for completed elections. Also removed one-per-party deduplication for completed elections so all participants are shown. `src/app/api/elections/[id]/route.ts`.
- **President/VP not removed from prior office** — When a Senator (or other office holder) won the presidency, their prior `electedOfficials` record was not cleared. Now clears any non-president/VP electedOfficials records for the new president and VP. `src/lib/turn/election/presidentResolution.ts`.
- **State party tax rate missing from destructuring** — `taxRate` was returned by `useStatePartyData` but not destructured on the state party page, causing the tax save API call and `StatePartyFundraisingPanel` to reference an undefined variable. Added `taxRate` to the destructuring. `src/app/state/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`.

