## [0.0.31] - 2026-02-16

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Corporation system** — Players can found corporations ($1M cost), choose from 13 sector types (Financial, Media, Manufacturing, Healthcare, Retail, Automobiles, Technology, Energy, Agriculture, Real Estate, Defense, Telecommunications, Entertainment), and expand into state markets. Corps have liquid capital, marketing budgets, CEO salary, shareholders, brand colors, and logos. `corporations` and `corporateSectors` collections. Per-turn processing: revenue growth, maintenance costs, marketing strength accumulation, CEO salary payments. `src/lib/db/types/corporation.ts`, `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporationTurn.ts`, `src/app/api/corporations/`.
- **Stock exchange pages** — NYSE (`/stockmarket/us`) and FTSE (`/stockmarket/uk`) listing pages with scrolling ticker, market cap, revenue, income, and CEO info. Mobile-responsive card layout. `src/app/stockmarket/[country]/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/stock-exchange/route.ts`.
- **Corporate-driven GDP growth** — State GDP growth is now computed as a revenue-weighted average of owned corporate sectors' growth rates. States with no owned sectors show N/A. National GDP growth uses GDP-weighted averaging so larger economies contribute more. `src/lib/turn/corporateGdpGrowth.ts`.
- **Unemployment affects corporate profit margins** — State unemployment rate modifies corporate sector profit margins ±5%. Below 3% unemployment: tight labor market squeezes margins (linear scale to -5%). Above 3%: cheap labor boosts margins (linear to +5% at 10%+). `getUnemploymentMarginModifier()` in `src/lib/constants/corporations.ts`.
- **Corporation tooltips and UI** — All corporation displays feature tooltipized labels, pie chart for sector market share, brand color support, and card-based sector layout. `src/app/corporations/page.tsx`.
- **Corps intensity map** — World map now includes a corporate intensity view showing corporation density per state/region. `src/app/api/discord-bot/sectors/route.ts`.
- **Discord bot corporation commands** — New `/corporation` and `/sectors` API routes for Discord bot integration. `src/app/api/discord-bot/corporation/route.ts`, `src/app/api/discord-bot/sectors/route.ts`.
- **Country-aware national budget page** — The budget page (`/budget`) now accepts a `?country=` query parameter and shows appropriate content for each country. US shows the full federal budget with revenue, spending, debt, and state grants. UK shows a placeholder describing the planned HM Treasury budget features (income tax, VAT, corporation tax, NHS spending, devolved administration block grants). Legacy `/budget/federal` redirects to `/budget?country=us`. `src/app/budget/page.tsx`, `src/app/budget/NationalBudgetClient.tsx`.
- **Dynamic party organization cap system** — Complete rework of how party organization caps are calculated and updated. Caps are now derived from election performance rather than static values. Each election type (governor, senate, house, stateSenate) contributes additively: Governor 25, Senate 25, House 17.5, State Senate 17.5, plus 15 base. Cap contributions have `current`, `target`, `rate`, and `nextElectionTurn` fields on `StatePartyOrg.capContributions`. Election resolution sets targets based on seat share; turn processing applies rates toward targets. New files: `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/constants.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/calculations.ts` (32 tests), `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/presence.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/turnProcessing.ts`, `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/electionIntegration.ts`.
- **Party presence requirement** — Org building now requires at least one player character OR elected official in the state. `StatePartyOrg.hasPresence` boolean tracks this. Presence is checked via `checkPartyPresence(db, stateId, partyId)` querying both `characters` and `electedOfficials` collections.
- **Momentum-based org growth** — Org building cost increased from $10k to $100k per momentum point. Growth rate: 0.5 org per momentum per turn. Momentum drift when no budget: -0.25 per turn. Momentum decay: 20% per turn. NPP momentum is half of player values. `src/lib/turn/partyOrg/constants.ts`.
- **Party org migration admin tool** — Admin Panel -> Support -> Migrations tab includes "Party Organization Rework" migration. `src/app/api/admin/migrations/party-org-rework/route.ts`.
- **Stable race identifiers** — New `seatId` field on elections provides a permanent, machine-readable identifier for each political seat (e.g., `US-senate-PA-1`, `UK-commons-LON`). New `seats` collection stores 263 permanent seat documents. `src/lib/seats/seatId.ts` provides `buildSeatId()`, `parseSeatId()`, `getSeatIdFromElection()`, and `getHistoricalRaceId()` utilities.
- **Seats seed target** — Admin Panel -> System -> Seeder now includes "Seats" target (263 US + 12 UK seats). `src/app/api/admin/seed/handlers/seedSeats.ts`.
- **Backfill election seatIds migration** — Admin Panel -> Migrations includes "Backfill Election Seat IDs" with dry-run support. `src/app/api/admin/migrations/backfill-seat-ids/route.ts`.
- **Discord webhook race IDs** — Election notification embeds now include a `url` field linking to `/elections/{seatId}` and a "Race ID" field. `src/lib/turn/perpetualElections.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Corporation turn processing in turn system** — `processCorporationTurn()` and `updateCorporateDrivenGdpGrowth()` are now called each turn. Revenue growth, maintenance costs, marketing strength, CEO salary, and state GDP growth all update automatically. `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`.
- **Party org turn processing** — Added `processPartyOrgTurn(currentTurn)` phase to turn system. Updates cap contributions toward targets, applies momentum drift/decay, and org changes. `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`.
- **Election resolution org updates** — `resolveGeneralElections` now calls `updatePartyOrgOnElection()` after processing winners. Replaces old `updatePartyOrgAfterElection` calls.
- **Running mate selector UI improvements** — Replaced plain text party display with colored party chips. Added search-by-name input and party filter chips. `RunningMateSelector.tsx`.
- **Admin heal: cross-country party organization** — New heal tool in Admin > System > Heal to diagnose and delete cross-country `statePartyOrg` records. `src/app/api/admin/heal/cross-country-party-org/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Bill proposal policyOptionId** — Bills were not sending `policyOptionId` when proposed, causing the wrong policy option to be stored. Fixed in both frontend (bill proposal form) and backend (bill creation API). Also fixed display to show correct policy option on enacted bills. `src/app/api/congress/bills/route.ts`.
- **Legislation type cache after seeding** — After re-seeding legislation types, the CDN cache was serving stale data. Added cache bypass headers for legislation type API. `src/app/api/legislation-types/route.ts`.
- **Presidential election navbar link** — `isSeatId()` required 3+ hyphen parts but `US-president` has only 2. Changed minimum to 2. `src/app/api/elections/[id]/route.ts`.
- **Running mate selection with seatId URLs** — Running mate API routes failed with seatId URLs. Added `isSeatId()` check to both routes.
- **Running mate country filter** — Running mate selection now only shows characters from the same country as the election.
- **State party page showing old cap of 25** — Now uses `computeCap(capContributions)` from the new system. `src/app/api/state/[id]/party/[partyId]/route.ts`.
- **Party organization not decaying without presence** — Momentum drift and decay now apply regardless of presence, so abandoned orgs decay toward 0.
- **US parties showing organization in UK regions** — Party creation now filters states by the party's `countryId`. State page filters out cross-country party orgs.
- **National Budget link missing from navbar** — Restored link for all countries in desktop and mobile nav.
- **Character profile links using ObjectId instead of sequentialId** — Comprehensive fix across 75 files to use `sequentialId` for character profile URLs.
- **GDP growth showing for states without corporations** — States with no owned corporate sectors now show N/A instead of stale GDP growth values. National average excludes these states.
- **Characters holding multiple seats after winning new election** — When a character won a new seat of the same office type (e.g., Senate Class 2 while holding Class 1), they were not removed from their original seat. Fixed by comparing full seat identity (type + state + senateClass) instead of just office type. Added `senateClass` to `OfficeType` for senate seats. `src/lib/turn/electionResolution.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/character.ts`.

### Removed

- **Old party org decay system** — Deleted `src/lib/turn/election/partyOrgDecay.ts` and `updatePartyOrgAfterElection()`. Replaced by new momentum-based org system.

