## [0.0.30] - 2026-02-13

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Profile metrics tooltips (complete)** - All remaining stat labels on the profile page now have `InfoTooltip` explanations. Added to: Influence (State), National Influence, and Donor Network in `PoliticalStanding.tsx`. Added to all Financial Statement rows (Cash on Hand, Base Generation, Donor Network Bonus, Office Salary, Party Taxes, Net Income) in `FinancialOverview.tsx`. `FinancialOverview.tsx` now imports `InfoTooltip` and defines a shared `INFO_ICON` inline SVG matching the existing pattern.
- **Admin Discord link reset** - New "Reset Discord" button in Admin > Players > Users tab. Unlinks Discord from ALL accounts sharing the same Discord ID, allowing the user to re-link from their original account. Fixes issue where users who accidentally logged in with Discord after unlinking would create a duplicate account, blocking re-linking. API: `POST /api/admin/users/reset-discord`. Added `discordId` and `discordUsername` to admin user list API response. Added `discord_reset` to `AdminLogAction` type. `src/app/api/admin/users/reset-discord/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/UsersTab.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/users/route.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/adminLog.ts`.
- **Admin heal state party elections** - New heal tool in Admin > System > Heal to fix state party elections missing turn fields (`startTurn`, `endTurn`, `durationTurns`). Diagnose button shows affected elections; Heal button adds missing fields calculated from timestamps. `GET/POST /api/admin/heal/state-party-elections`, `HealStatePartyElections.tsx`, `AdminSystemTab.tsx`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **National party whip endpoint** - National Party Chairs/Vice Chairs trying to whip federal bills received "State party organization not found" because `WhipPanel.tsx` always called the state party endpoint. Created `POST /api/parties/[id]/whip` for national party whips on Senate/House chambers. Updated `handleWhip` and `handleLeadershipWhip` in `WhipPanel.tsx` to use the national endpoint when `isNational` is true and chamber is not `stateLegislature`. National whips use `issuedBy: "nationalParty"` in the `billWhips` collection.
- **National Vice Chair NPP influence** - National Party Vice Chairs could not use the NPP Influence panel on the National Party page. The state party influence API (`/api/state/[id]/party/[partyId]/influence`) only checked for State Chair/Vice Chair authorization. Added National Chair/Vice Chair checks to both GET and POST handlers.
- **State party election NaN turns** - State party leadership elections with missing `startTurn`/`endTurn` fields displayed "NaN turns remaining". Added defensive defaults in the election API response (`startTurn ?? 0`, `endTurn ?? 0`, `durationTurns ?? 96`). Updated `TurnsRemaining` component in `StatePartyLeadershipElections.tsx` to show " - turns remaining" when values are invalid.
- **Party org building spending not applied** - Organization building spending was not updating momentum because `processPartyGOTV` checked `partyBudget.treasury` (always 0) instead of the actual treasury. Tax revenue flows into `statePartyOrg.treasury` (state) and `politicalParty.treasury` (national), but spending was checking the wrong collection. Fixed by loading actual treasury from `statePartyOrg`/`politicalParty` and deducting from the correct source. GOTV, voter suppression, and org building now all draw from the correct treasury.
- **Tax bill category validation** - Proposing bills with category "Tax" was rejected by the API schema. Added "tax" to the `proposeBillSchema` category enum in `src/lib/api/schemas/congress.ts`.

