## [0.0.29] - 2026-02-12

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Sentry error monitoring** - Full `@sentry/nextjs` integration across all three runtimes (browser, Node.js server, Edge). Browser config includes Session Replay (10% baseline, 100% on error) and App Router transition tracking. Server config captures local variables in stack frames. `withSentryConfig()` wraps `next.config.ts` with source map uploads, ad-blocker tunnel route (`/monitoring`), and widened client file uploads. `global-error.tsx` now reports to Sentry instead of `console.error`. Config files: `instrumentation-client.ts`, `sentry.server.config.ts`, `sentry.edge.config.ts`, `instrumentation.ts`.
- **CodeQL security scanning** - Weekly automated code scanning via GitHub Actions. Runs on push/PR to master and on a Monday 06:00 UTC schedule. `.github/workflows/codeql.yml`.
- **npm audit in CI** - `npm audit --audit-level=high` added to CI pipeline to catch known vulnerabilities on every push. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
- **Vitest coverage reporting** - CI now runs `vitest run --coverage` with `@vitest/coverage-v8`. Coverage includes all `src/lib/**` files, excludes test files. `vitest.config.ts`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
- **commitlint** - Enforces Conventional Commits format on all commit messages via `@commitlint/cli` + `@commitlint/config-conventional`. Husky `commit-msg` hook validates before commit. `commitlint.config.mjs`, `.husky/commit-msg`.
- **Dashboard redirect** - `/dashboard` now redirects to `/profile` instead of 404. Fixes 22 references across the codebase that linked to `/dashboard` (register redirect, error boundaries, 404 page, settings, elections). `src/app/dashboard/page.tsx`.
- **State bill voting UI** - `StateBillCard` now shows Aye/Nay/Abstain vote buttons for state senators. Highlights current vote, shows loading state, and calls `POST /api/state/${stateId}/legislature/bills/${billId}/vote`. Props: `canVote`, `stateId`, `onVoted`. `src/app/state/[id]/legislature/components/StateBillCard.tsx`, `BillsTab.tsx`, `StateLegislatureClient.tsx`.
- **Onboarding checklist** - New players see a dismissible onboarding card on `/profile` with 4 steps: join a party, set background, cast first vote, read the wiki. Progress bar tracks completion. Dismiss calls `PATCH /api/character/me` to set `onboardingDismissed`. `src/app/profile/components/OnboardingCard.tsx`, `src/lib/db/types/character.ts`, `src/app/api/character/me/route.ts`.
- **Game mechanics tooltips** - InfoTooltip components added to Actions, Favorability, and Infamy stat labels on the profile page explaining what each stat does and how it's earned. `src/app/profile/components/PoliticalStanding.tsx`.
- **New notification types** - `turn_advance`, `resource_income`, `election_opened` added to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with full config entries (icons, badges, categories). `src/lib/db/types/notifications.ts`, `src/app/notifications/notificationConfig.tsx`.
- **Playwright visual screenshots** - `toHaveScreenshot()` assertions added to 5 E2E tests: home page, login page, register page, elections list, map page. `e2e/smoke.spec.ts`, `e2e/critical-flows.spec.ts`, `e2e/performance.spec.ts`.
- **Country-agnostic confidence votes** - New `ConfidenceVote` type in `parliamentaryGovernment.ts` and `getConfidenceVotesCollection()` in `ukGovernment.ts` for PM/Chancellor succession across all parliamentary countries. `triggerNextPMConfidenceVote(countryId, now, excludeCharacterIds)` reads `CountryConfig` for chamber key and executive title. Replaces UK-specific hardcoded logic at `ukGovernment.ts:176,379`.
- **`executiveLabel` in CountryConfig** - New config field for country-specific executive residence names (US: "White House", UK: "10 Downing Street", CA: "Parliament Hill", DE: "Federal Chancellery"). Used by `Navbar.tsx` and `NationDropdown.tsx`. `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Navbar config-driven** - `Navbar.tsx`, `NationDropdown.tsx`, `WorldDropdown.tsx` no longer use `isUKContext` ternaries or hardcoded country string comparisons. All country-specific labels, paths, and links now derive from `getCountryConfig(countryId)`. Presidential election link conditionally shown via `executiveFormation === "direct_election"`.
- **`engines` field** - `package.json` now declares `"engines": { "node": ">=20" }`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **404 emoji accessibility** - All 4 emoji elements on the not-found page now have `role="img"` and descriptive `aria-label` attributes. `src/app/not-found.tsx`.
- **Canvassing turn stub documented** - `getCanvassingActionsForTurn()` in `demographicTurnoutTurn.ts` now has a comment explaining it returns `[]` intentionally because canvassing applies immediately via API, not via the turn queue.

### Refactored

- **Error handling standardization** - 11 API routes wrapped with try/catch + `handleRouteError`: `cron/turn`, `auth/discord/login`, `auth/discord`, `congress/members`, `elections/composition`, `elections/snapshot`, `character/me`, `politician/[id]`, `politician-overrides`, `admin/state/[id]/assign-seat`, `admin/state/[id]/vacant-seats`. Two routes (`parties`, `admin/npps`) migrated from deprecated `withRouteError` wrapper.

