## [0.0.28] - 2026-02-10

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Discord OAuth login and registration** - Users can now log in or register via Discord. If a Discord-linked account exists, they're signed in directly; otherwise a new account is auto-created from the Discord profile and the user is redirected to character setup. Both login and register pages show a "Continue with Discord" button. The existing account-linking flow in settings is preserved. `src/app/api/auth/discord/callback/route.ts`, `src/app/api/auth/discord/login/route.ts`, `src/app/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/register/page.tsx`.
- **Public leaderboard API** - `GET /api/v1/leaderboard` public endpoint for Discord bots and scrapers. Supports `?metric=influence|favorability|funds`, `?limit=1-50`, `?country=us|uk`, and `?playersOnly=true`. Returns ranked entries with party colors, state names, office labels, and profile URLs. Includes 60s public cache headers. `src/app/api/v1/leaderboard/route.ts`.
- **World map interactive filters** - Population, GDP, GDP per capita, and political party color filters added to the world map with color-coded country fills. Zoom in/out buttons with smooth animation. Fetches party data from API for party-color mode. `src/app/world/WorldClient.tsx`.
- **Electron focused display mode** - `NavbarWrapper` reads the `ahd-display-mode` cookie and hides the site navbar when set to `"focused"`, allowing the Electron app to provide its own navigation controls. Display mode exposed to client via `window.__AHD_DISPLAY_MODE`. `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/components/NavbarWrapper.tsx`.
- **Verbose hourly turn logs** - Turn processing now logs detailed phase-by-phase results to a `turnLogs` collection with 24-hour TTL auto-deletion. Each log captures turn number, game/real timestamps, duration, warnings, and results from all 24+ phases (action refresh, fund generation, elections, bills, campaigns, etc.). Viewable in Admin > Support > Logs > Hourly Logs. `src/lib/db/types/turnLog.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/logs/hourly/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/LogsTab.tsx`.
- **NPP entry debug diagnostics** - Admin debug endpoint and UI for diagnosing NPP primary entry issues. Shows game time vs real time, open primaries summary, sample primary data, and per-state NPP analysis (eligible NPPs, already running, party breakdowns). Admin > Support > Debug tab with "Run NPP Entry Debug" button and JSON download. `src/app/api/admin/debug/npp-entry/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/DebugTab.tsx`, `src/components/admin/tabs/AdminSupportTab.tsx`.
- **NPP incumbent priority** - NPPs who currently hold a seat now get priority to re-enter that seat's primary in the next election cycle. When selecting an NPP to enter a primary, the system checks `officialsByNPP` to identify incumbents and sorts them first. Incumbent matching uses office type + state for state-level races (house, senate, governor, stateSenate) and office type only for national races (president, commons). `src/lib/turn/nppBehavior.ts:317-349`.
- **Clear NPP cooldowns admin button** - Admin Debug tab now includes a "Clear All NPP Cooldowns" button that removes stale `electionCooldowns` from all NPP documents, allowing them to enter primaries immediately. `src/app/api/admin/npps/clear-cooldowns/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/DebugTab.tsx`.
- **Vacate NPP primaries admin button** - Admin Debug tab now includes a "Vacate All NPP Primaries" button that withdraws all NPP candidates from active primaries, allowing them to re-enter on the next turn based on updated eligibility rules (country/region restrictions, incumbent priority). `src/app/api/admin/npps/vacate-primaries/route.ts`, `src/components/admin/DebugTab.tsx`.
- **Party Actions sub-tabs** - State and National Party pages now have sub-tabs within the Actions section: NPP Influence (existing feature reorganized), Whip (new), and NPP Recruitment (coming soon placeholder). `src/app/state/[id]/party/[partyId]/page.tsx`, `src/app/parties/[id]/page.tsx`.
- **Whip system UI** - Party Chairs and Vice Chairs can now issue whip directives to NPP legislators on bills and leadership elections. Chamber tabs (Senate, House, State Legislature) filter available targets. Shows existing whips (max 2 per bill/chamber) and compliance estimates. National party can whip federal chambers directly; state legislature whip requires selecting an NPP-only state. `src/components/party/WhipPanel.tsx`.
- **NPP-only states endpoint** - `GET /api/parties/[id]/npp-influence-states` returns states where a party has zero player characters, enabling national party leadership to target NPP influence actions. `src/app/api/parties/[id]/npp-influence-states/route.ts`.
- **National whippable bills endpoint** - `GET /api/parties/[id]/whippable-bills` returns federal bills where the party has NPP legislators who can be whipped, grouped by chamber. `src/app/api/parties/[id]/whippable-bills/route.ts`.
- **National whippable leadership endpoint** - `GET /api/parties/[id]/whippable-leadership` returns active federal leadership elections (Speaker, Majority/Minority Leader, Pro Tempore) where party NPPs can vote. `src/app/api/parties/[id]/whippable-leadership/route.ts`.
- **Whip compliance estimates** - The whip POST endpoint now returns compliance feedback: how many NPPs fell in line vs. ignored the whip, with flavor text ("defied the whip", "remained unconvinced", "stood their ground"). Based on `calculateComplianceChance(npp)` using loyalty and stubbornness traits. `src/app/api/state/[id]/party/[partyId]/whip/route.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Discord bot lookup enriched** - `GET /api/discord-bot/lookup` response expanded with `partyId`, `officeType`, `politicalInfluence`, `favorability`, `funds`, `discordUsername`, and `activeElection` (with `electionId`, `electionType`, `electionState`, `enteredAt`). Fixes type-safety issues in `Promise.all` tuple inference. `src/app/api/discord-bot/lookup/route.ts`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **NPP cross-country/region primary entry** - NPPs were incorrectly entering primaries outside their home region. Two bugs: (1) `selectBestPrimary()` in `nppEntryLogic.ts` treated UK "commons" as a national race alongside US "president", returning `true` without checking country - US NPPs could enter UK primaries. (2) `processElectionEntry()` in `electionEntry.ts` used `isNationalRace` for both "president" and "commons", allowing UK NPPs from one region to enter commons primaries in other regions. Fix: Only US "president" is truly national (any NPP from that country can run); UK "commons" is regional and requires homeState to match election state. Added `npp.countryId === e.countryId` check for presidential races. `src/lib/turn/nppEntryLogic.ts`, `src/lib/turn/npp/electionEntry.ts`.
- **Globe and world map touch support** - `WorldMapSVG` and `RotatingGlobe` now handle `onTouchStart`/`onTouchMove`/`onTouchEnd`/`onTouchCancel` events mirroring existing mouse drag logic. Added pinch-to-zoom for two-finger gestures and tap detection that dispatches synthetic click events for country navigation on mobile. `src/app/world/WorldClient.tsx`, `src/components/RotatingGlobe.tsx`.
- **Mobile horizontal overflow** - Added `overflow-x: hidden` to `html` and `body` in `globals.css` as a global safety net. Added `overflow-x-hidden` to main wrappers on 15 pages (profile, news, actions, character, npp, parties, politicians, notifications, settings, campaign, national, politician). Fixed `CongressClient` tab group by removing `w-fit` from `overflow-x-auto` container. Rewrote actions page stats bar from `grid`+`divide-x` to `flex`+`overflow-x-auto` with semantic color tokens.

---

## [0.0.27] - 2026-02-10

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Archetype approvals system** - Politicians now build or lose approval with specific voter archetypes (young_renters, evangelicals, rural_traditionalists, union_trades, soccer_moms, college_liberals, small_business, public_sector, retirees, libertarians, new_immigrants, secular_professionals) based on their legislation votes. Each vote for/against a bill adjusts the politician's standing with archetypes affected by that policy. Schema: `Character.archetypeApprovals` and `NPP.archetypeApprovals` (`Record<string, number>`, -100 to +100). `VoteImpact.archetypeImpacts` tracks per-vote changes. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/npp.ts`, `src/lib/db/types/statePolicy.ts`.
- **Domain-specific archetype affinities** - 11 policy domains (education, healthcare, environment, immigration, criminal_justice, defense, economic, welfare, infrastructure, governance, foreign_policy) each define unique per-archetype reactions to rightward policy shifts. For example: evangelicals (+35) love rightward education shifts (vouchers), public_sector (-40) strongly opposes them; rural_traditionalists (+40) favor immigration enforcement while new_immigrants (-50) strongly oppose it. Affinity values range ±50. `DOMAIN_AFFINITIES` constant and `calculateShiftImpacts()` function in `src/lib/archetypeAffinities.ts`.
- **Shift-based approval calculation** - Archetype approval impacts now depend on the policy SHIFT (new position minus old position), not the absolute policy level. A bill that moves education policy 2 steps right gives evangelicals +10 approval (2 × 35 × 0.15, clamped). This creates a more nuanced system where the same archetype can approve one education bill and oppose another depending on direction and magnitude. Scale factor `SHIFT_IMPACT_SCALE = 0.15`, impacts clamped to ±10 per bill.
- **Current policies API** - `GET /api/game/current-policies?stateId=federal` returns current policy position indices for all legislation types in a state/federal jurisdiction. Used by bill proposal UI to calculate shift-based preview impacts. `src/app/api/game/current-policies/route.ts`.
- **Unit tests for archetype affinities** - 14 tests covering domain mapping, shift impact calculations, clamping, zero-affinity exclusion, and domain coverage. `src/lib/archetypeAffinities.test.ts`.
- **Archetype approval decay** - Archetype approvals decay 0.5% per turn toward 0 (neutral), creating ~22% decay per game year. Recent votes remain relevant while old history fades. New turn phase 14c in `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`. Implementation: `src/lib/turn/archetypeApprovalDecay.ts`.
- **Effective favorability in elections** - Election vote weights now use per-archetype effective favorability: `effectiveFavorability = favorability + archetypeApproval × 0.5` (clamped 0-100). A politician loved by evangelicals (+80 approval) gets 90% effective favorability with that group even if base favorability is only 50%. `calcEffectiveFavorability()` helper added to `src/lib/electionEngine.ts`. `EnrichedCandidate` interface extended with `archetypeApprovals` field. `fetchEnrichedCandidates()` now includes archetype approvals for characters and NPPs.
- **Effective favorability in polls** - Poll results now show per-archetype approval ratings and effective favorability. Each group result includes `archetypeApproval` (-100 to +100) and `effectiveFavorability` (0-100). Vote potential calculations use per-archetype effective approval. `calcEffectiveFavorability()` added to `src/lib/actions/pollCalculations.ts`.
- **Archetype approvals in bill UI** - Bill proposal modals now display "Archetype Approvals" section below "Metric Effects" showing which voter archetypes gain or lose approval from each policy option. Up/down arrows with green (positive) or red (negative) coloring. `PolicyEffectIndicators` component updated to accept `archetypeApprovals` prop with fallback to deprecated `groupApprovals`. Updated in `ProposeBillModal.tsx` and `StateLegislatureClient.tsx`.
- **Bill vote policy shifts** - Voting on a bill now shifts the voter's personal policy position toward the bill's stance. `applyBillVotePolicyShift()` utility in `src/lib/policyShift.ts` calculates ±0.25 shift per provision based on the voted option's position relative to center. Applied in both Congress (`src/app/api/congress/bills/[id]/route.ts`) and state legislature (`src/app/api/state-legislature/bills/[id]/route.ts`) vote handlers. Unit tests in `src/lib/policyShift.test.ts`.
- **Cabinet resignation on government transition** - `clearCabinetOnTransition()` utility in `src/lib/clearCabinetOnTransition.ts` clears all cabinet members when executive leadership changes. Triggered in three scenarios: US presidential transition (new president inaugurated), UK PM appointment (new PM selected after government formation), and UK no-confidence vote passing (PM removed). Removes all entries from `cabinetMembers` collection for the relevant country. Unit tests in `src/lib/clearCabinetOnTransition.test.ts`.
- **World map projection interpolation** - Replaced `react-simple-maps` with imperative d3-geo rendering on the `/world` page. `WorldMapSVG` in `src/app/world/WorldClient.tsx` renders ~177 countries via direct `<path>` DOM updates at 60fps. Toggle between 2D EqualEarth and 3D Orthographic (globe) projections with seamless geographic morphing animation (1200ms eased interpolation between raw projection functions). Mouse-wheel zoom (0.8×–3×), drag rotation/pan with momentum, and idle auto-rotation (0.12°/frame) in globe mode. Back-hemisphere countries fade out based on centroid angular distance.
- **Ukraine conflict visualization** - Ukraine (ISO 804) rendered in amber (`#d97706`) on both the rotating globe (`src/components/RotatingGlobe.tsx`) and world map (`src/app/world/WorldClient.tsx`). Russia–Ukraine shared border extracted via `topojson.mesh()` filter (`Number(a.id) === 643 && Number(b.id) === 804`) and rendered as an animated dashed red SVG path (marching ants: `stroke-dasharray="4 3"`, 1.5s `stroke-dashoffset` keyframe animation). In globe mode, `geoOrthographic clipAngle(90)` automatically clips border to the visible hemisphere. Tooltip shows "Active Conflict" status in amber for Ukraine.
- **OG image and embed previews** - Dynamic `og:image` metadata for social media embeds. `generateMetadata()` in layout files provides page-specific titles, descriptions, and preview images. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts` serves proxied hero images for embed cards.
- **UK executive hero image** - UK Government page (`/uk/government`) now uses a Downing Street hero image instead of the generic UK flag. Added `"downing-street"` slug to `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Approval impacts apply at bill enactment only** - Archetype approval changes now apply when a bill is enacted (signed into law or veto overridden), not when legislators cast votes. This ensures approvals reflect actual policy changes, not just voting intentions. `recordVoteImpacts()` calls removed from `billLifecycle.ts` and `stateBillLifecycle.ts`; approval logic moved to `processProvisionEnactment()` in `src/lib/billEnactment.ts`.
- **Bill enactment calculates shift impacts** - `onBillEnacted()` now looks up the previous policy position before updating, calculates the shift, and applies archetype impacts to all legislators who voted FOR the bill. Uses `calculateShiftImpacts()` from `src/lib/archetypeAffinities.ts`. Handles both Characters and NPPs with bulk updates and value clamping.
- **UI shows shift-based approval previews** - `PolicyEffectIndicators` component now accepts `policyDomain`, `currentPolicyIndex`, and `proposedPolicyIndex` props. When provided, calculates shift-based impacts using `calculateShiftImpacts()` instead of static values. Bill proposal modals (`ProposeBillModal`, state legislature's `ProposeStateBillModal`) fetch current policies and pass shift data.
- **Double arrows for major impacts** - Archetype approval indicators now show double stacked arrows (↑↑ or ↓↓) for major impacts (magnitude ≥ 5) and single arrows for minor impacts (magnitude < 5), providing visual distinction between strong and weak archetype reactions.
- **Legislation seed cleanup** - Removed placeholder `getEconomicApprovals`, `getSocialApprovals`, `getMixedApprovals` functions and `archetypeApprovals` property from policy option builders in `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`. Approvals are now calculated at runtime based on policy shift.
- **Discord bill enacted webhook enriched** - Bill enactment Discord embeds now include the bill title, affected policy area, and a direct link to the bill page. `src/lib/discordWebhooks.ts`.
- **RotatingGlobe single animation loop** - `src/components/RotatingGlobe.tsx` refactored to use a single `requestAnimationFrame` loop with `isDraggingRef` instead of restarting the loop on drag state changes. Eliminates the separate deceleration loop on mouse-up; momentum is handled by the main loop.
- **World map drag panning** - Flat map mode in `WorldMapSVG` now supports drag-to-pan via `mapPanRef` (`[number, number]` offset applied to the equal-earth projection translate). Globe mode continues to use drag-to-rotate. Cursor shows grab/grabbing in both modes. Mouse handlers consolidated onto the outer card `<div>`.
- **World map fills container** - Removed `p-4 sm:p-8` padding wrapper and `max-w-4xl` constraint from `WorldMapSVG`. SVG now renders edge-to-edge within the card; Map/Globe toggle buttons remain as absolute overlays (`z-10`).
- **Zoom floor raised** - WorldClient minimum zoom raised from 0.5× to 0.8×; RotatingGlobe minimum scale raised from 120 to 160, preventing the map from shrinking so far that countries become unreadable.
- **Politicians page tagline** - Updated from generic description to "A full list of all active politicians. Search, filter, and rank by various factors."

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Profile picture upload caching** - Uploading a new profile picture could show the old cached image due to browser caching. Fixed by adding timestamp to avatar filenames (`avatars/{characterId}-{timestamp}.{ext}`) for cache-busting. Also now deletes all old avatar files for the character by prefix, handling format changes (jpg->png->gif). `src/app/api/upload/avatar/route.ts`.
- **NPP primary entry query** - NPPs were not entering primaries because the election query included `status: "upcoming"` elections where the primary phase hadn't started yet (startTime still in future). Changed query to `status: "active"` only, ensuring NPPs only enter elections with open primaries. Added diagnostic logging to track skip reasons (already running, no elections, cooldown, org=0, chance failed). `src/lib/nppElectionBehavior.ts`.
- **NPP primary entry org gate removed** - NPPs were being blocked from entering primaries if their party had low organization in their home state. Third parties with org=0 could never enter any race, even empty ones. Removed the org gate entirely from `src/lib/nppElectionBehavior.ts` so NPPs can enter primaries regardless of party organization level. Removed `nppOrgEntryMultiplier()` function, `statePartyOrg` query, and `skippedOrgZero` counter. Updated tests in `src/lib/thirdPartyMechanics.test.ts`.

