## [0.0.26] - 2026-02-08

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Wiki UI** - Rich WYSIWYG editor with markdown toolbar for creating and editing wiki pages. `WikiEditorClient`, `WikiEditorToolbar`, `TemplateSelector` components. Auto-saves drafts to localStorage every 30 seconds with restore prompt on return. Toggle markdown live preview pane. Edit button on all wiki pages for authenticated users.
- **Wiki Templates** - Pre-populated section stubs for game-mechanic, strategy-guide, and reference pages. `TemplateSelector` component. `/api/wiki/templates` endpoint.
- **Wiki Review Workflow** - Admin review queue at `?tab=content&sub=wiki-review` with side-by-side diff view. Approve/reject actions via `/api/admin/wiki/review/[slug]/approve` and `.../reject`. `WikiReviewTab` and `WikiReviewActions` components.
- **Task Management System** - In-app task tracking for bugs, features, and improvements. MongoDB `tasks` collection with `Task` type (`title`, `description`, `type`, `priority`, `status`, `createdBy`, `completedAt`). REST API under `/api/admin/tasks` (GET list with filters, POST create, PATCH update, DELETE) and `/api/admin/tasks/[id]` and `/api/admin/tasks/summary`. Dashboard widget (`TasksWidget`) shows critical/high/in-progress/total counts and top 5 priority tasks. Dedicated page at `/admin/tasks` with client-side filtering by type, status, and priority. `ahd-task-manager` skill enables Claude to query, create, and update tasks from any session.
- **Task manager enhancements** - Comment history and add-comment form in `TaskDetailModal`. Tags display on task cards. Tags input in `TaskFormToast`. `LessonCard` inline editing (category, lesson text) in `TasksPageClient`. DELETE `/api/admin/tasks/lessons/[id]` route for removing individual lessons.
- **UK Commons Elections** - UK regions, parties, demographics, and Commons elections fully implemented and operational. 12 UK electoral regions (9 England regions + Scotland + Wales + Northern Ireland) hold perpetual Commons elections using multi-seat proportional allocation. Government formation triggers after elections resolve, determining majority/minority government. PM confidence vote system processes MP votes (95% same party support, 5% opposition support) with 24-hour voting period and automatic NPP voting. Includes comprehensive UK seed script (`scripts/seed-uk.ts`), perpetual election setup (`ensureUKElections`), government formation (`resolveUKGovernmentFormation`), confidence vote processing (`processConfidenceVotes`), 7 default UK parties (Labour, Conservative, Lib Dems, SNP, Plaid Cymru, Green, Reform UK), regional demographics, and `/uk/elections` page for viewing active Commons elections.
- **Senate Vacancy Appointments** - Governors can appoint replacements when Senate seats become vacant. Appointed senators serve until the next regular Class election. Includes `isAppointment` and `appointedBy` fields on `ElectedOfficial` type, resignation API (`/api/officials/[id]/resign`), governor appointment APIs (`/api/governors/appoint-senator`, `/api/governors/eligible-appointees`), vacancies listing API (`/api/vacancies`), `ResignButton`, `AppointSenatorModal`, and `VacanciesPanel` components, `/officials` page for viewing vacancies, and migration script (`scripts/migrations/add-appointment-fields.ts`).
- **PM No-Confidence Vote system** - Ruling party MPs can propose motions of no confidence against the Prime Minister. Only members of the ruling party/coalition vote. 24-hour voting period with automatic NPP auto-voting based on PM favorability. If majority votes yes, PM is removed from office. 48-turn cooldown between votes. Includes `UKGovernment`, `PmNoConfidenceVote`, and `UKConfidenceVote` types in `src/lib/db/types/ukGovernment.ts`, collection getters in `src/lib/db/collections/ukGovernment.ts`, three API routes (`/api/uk/pm/no-confidence`, `/api/uk/pm/no-confidence/[id]`, `/api/uk/pm/no-confidence/[id]/vote`), turn processing in `src/lib/turn/ukGovernment.ts` integrated at phase 10b, `PmNoConfidencePanel` component, and display on UK Government page (`/uk/government`).
- **19 UK legislation types** - Full set of UK Parliament bill types added to `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts` with `countryScope: "uk"` and `nationalOnly: true`: `uk_nhs_funding`, `uk_nhs_social_care`, `uk_brexit_trade`, `uk_immigration`, `uk_climate_net_zero`, `uk_north_sea_energy`, `uk_housing_planning`, `uk_leasehold_reform`, `uk_education_standards`, `uk_tuition_fees`, `uk_fiscal_spending`, `uk_corporation_tax`, `uk_universal_credit`, `uk_trident_defence`, `uk_policing_crime`, `uk_bbc_licence_fee`, `uk_scottish_devolution`, `uk_hs2_rail`, `uk_local_government`. Each has 7 policy options (≤ 4 words), `effectTargetsWeighted`, per-option `metricEffects` (progressive ±ratePerTurn), and Commons/Lords committee positions. Run `seed-legislation.ts` and `seed-policies.ts --reset` to apply.
- **`UK_NATIONAL_DEFAULTS`** - Dec 2019 Boris Johnson baseline policy map for all 19 UK types added to `scripts/seeds/basePolicies.ts`. `buildBasePolicies()` now routes UK types through `UK_NATIONAL_DEFAULTS` and skips state records for them.
- **`standardUKCommitteePositions()` helper** - Generates 4 positions per UK type using `"commons"` / `"lords"` chamber keys. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Discord webhook integration** - Game events (election results, bill enactments, government formation/collapse, leadership elections, new primaries) and player news posts broadcast to configurable Discord webhook URLs. Stored in `gameConfig.discordGameWebhookUrl` and `discordGameNewsUrl`. Admin config at `PATCH /api/admin/config/discord`; test embeds at `POST /api/admin/discord/test`. `sendGameEvent` and `sendNewsEvent` helpers in `src/lib/discordWebhooks.ts`. Admin Integrations sub-tab (System -> Integrations) for configuring and testing webhooks.
- **News post titles** - Optional title field (max 100 chars) on news posts. Displayed above content in the feed. Passed through in Discord embed as the embed title.
- **News post moderation** - Slur filter in `src/lib/moderation.ts` blocks racial, ethnic, religious, and LGBT slurs on both title and content. Swear words are permitted. Returns 400 with a neutral error message.
- **News post cooldown** - 30-minute cooldown per character between news posts. Returns 429 with remaining time in minutes.
- **News post cost** - Posting news costs 5 actions and $75,000 CF. Checked before submission; deducted on insert. Cost shown on Post button in composer.
- **Discord auto-react** - When the posting user has Discord linked (`User.discordId` set), their news post receives an automatic `agree` reaction from their own account on creation.
- **Admin news post deletion** - `DELETE /api/admin/news/[id]` cascades to all replies and associated `newsReactions` documents.
- **Referral system** - Users can share their User ID as a referral code during registration. Referred users receive 10% bonus to starting stats and funds, plus 30 extra starting actions. Referrers receive +15 actions and +$1M funds when the referred user creates a character. `User.referredBy` and `User.referralCount` fields added. `/settings` Referrals section shows personal referral link and total count. Validated via `/api/auth/register` (24-hex ObjectId format check, self-referral guard).

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **National metrics architecture** - National stats are now precomputed population-weighted averages of state-level metrics, written as derived documents into the `stateMetrics` collection (`_id: "federal"` for US, `"uk_national"` for UK) by `computeNationalMetrics()` in `src/lib/nationalMetrics.ts`. Runs each turn as phase `"nationalMetrics"` after policy effects and before history snapshot (`src/lib/turnSystem.ts`). Replaces the broken on-the-fly averaging that mixed US and UK data.
- **`NATIONAL_SCOPE` shared constant** - Extracted to `src/lib/constants/nationalScope.ts` (exports `NATIONAL_SCOPE: Record<string, CountryId>`, `NATIONAL_SCOPE_IDS: Set`, `getNationalDocId()`). `src/lib/metricHistory.ts` now imports from this instead of maintaining a local copy. Adding a new country requires one line here.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Cross-country metric contamination** - State approval and national average calculations previously mixed US and UK metrics together due to unfiltered `stateMetrics.find({})` calls. Fixed in three places: `getStateApprovalForElection.ts` (now groups states by country and computes per-country averages), `state/[id]/metrics/route.ts` (reads precomputed national doc for the state's country), and `national/metrics/route.ts` (excludes national aggregate docs from global comparison).
- **State metrics API rejected national scope IDs** - The guard `stateId.length !== 2` rejected `"federal"` and `"uk_national"`. Now accepts 2-char US state codes, `UK_`-prefixed region codes, and keys of `NATIONAL_SCOPE`. `src/app/api/state/[id]/metrics/route.ts`.

- **`countryScope` field on all legislation types** - All 57 existing `LegislationType` objects now carry `countryScope: "us"` (55 types) or `"international"` (2: `defense_spending`, `foreign_policy`). Field added as optional to `LegislationType` in `src/lib/db/types/legislation.ts`.
- **Per-option `metricEffects` populated** - All 48 non-tax legislation types now have `metricEffects: [{ category, metricId, ratePerTurn }]` on every policy option, using progressive values [±0.4 -> 0 -> ∓0.4] by stance. 9 tax-rate types excluded (rates live in budget docs). Implemented via `.map()` post-processing in `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **Policy option names shortened** - ~120 `policyOptions[].name` values exceeding 4 words shortened to ≤ 4 words across all 57 types. `scripts/seeds/legislationTypes.ts`.
- **`LegislationTypePosition.chamber` widened** - Extended from `"house" | "senate"` to include `"commons" | "lords"` in `src/lib/db/types/legislation.ts` and `src/components/admin/lawtype/types.ts`.
- **`NATIONAL_DEFAULTS` corrected for Jan 2020 baseline** - Fixed 3 value mismatches vs. Trump administration baseline: `clean_energy` −1->+1, `minimum_wage` −1->+2, `federal_healthcare_funding` −1->+1. Renamed orphaned `defense_foreign_policy` key -> separate `defense_spending` + `foreign_policy` entries. Added 22 previously missing type entries. Comment updated with benchmark documentation. `scripts/seeds/basePolicies.ts`.

- **`approvalModifiers.ts` - threshold recalibration for UK parity** - UK national averages were producing no active modifiers (stuck at 50%) because all thresholds were tuned to US extremes. Thresholds lowered across the board so population-weighted UK averages trigger realistic conditions. Key changes: `migrationRate` threshold `>= 1.0 -> 0.4`; `crimeRate` threshold `>= 7000 -> 5000`; `violentCrimeRate` `>= 400 -> 280`; `renewableEnergy` `>= 35 -> 30`; `broadbandAccess` `>= 92 -> 90`; `physicianRate` `>= 3.0 -> 2.5`; `airQuality` `>= 48 -> 35`; `mediaPolarization` `>= 45 -> 40`; `incomeInequality` `>= 0.38 -> 0.36`; `medianAge` `>= 43 -> 40`; `foodInsecurity` `>= 13 -> 12`; `budgetBalance` threshold split into `Government Deficit` (≤ −1.5, −1) and `Fiscal Crisis` (≤ −4.0, −3). Effect magnitudes also reduced (Recession −5 -> −4, High Crime Rate −4 -> −3, High Corruption −5 -> −4, etc.) so stacking drives variation more than any single condition.
- **New approval conditions (10+)** - Added: Strong Economic Growth (+2, GDP growth ≥ 2.5%), Strong Recycling Culture (+2, recycling ≥ 45%), Clean Water Supply (+2, water quality ≥ 96%), Low Reoffending Rate (+2, recidivism ≤ 30%), High Poverty Rate (−2, poverty ≥ 15%), High Preventable Mortality (−2, preventable mortality ≥ 270), High Carbon Footprint (−1, carbon emissions ≥ 13), Stagnant Economy (−1, GDP growth ≤ 1%), Government Deficit (−1, budget balance ≤ −1.5), Weak Healthcare Capacity (−2, physician rate ≤ 2.2 and affordability ≤ 65). Total: 31 positive, 37 negative.
- **UK Parliament seat count** - Composition tab and `/api/legislature/uk/members` now sum `seatsHeld` per official instead of counting officials, so NPP bloc entries (holding multiple seats) are counted correctly.
- **Admin Integrations tab not rendering** - `VALID_SUBS.system` in `AdminTabs.tsx` was missing `"integrations"`, causing the sub-tab click to silently fall back to Seed. Added to valid list.
- **News post party badge** - `PartyBadge` in `NewsPost.tsx` was showing raw slugs (e.g. `uk_labour`) because `charAt(0).toUpperCase()` doesn't split on underscores. Now splits on `_` and uppercases words ≤ 2 chars (`uk` -> `UK`).
- **Discord embed party name** - Party lookup was querying collection `"parties"` (does not exist); corrected to `"politicalParties"`.
- **Register page `referralCode` crash** - `formData` initial state was missing `referralCode`, causing a TypeScript error and broken controlled input.
- **`electionResolution` test assertions** - `primaryDurationHours` assertions updated from 24 -> 48 to match `DEFAULT_DURATIONS.house` which was changed to 48 in a prior session.

### Refactored

- **`discord.ts` split** - OAuth helpers (avatar URL, OAuth URL builder, `fetchDiscordUser`) extracted to `src/lib/discord-client.ts`. Webhook integration (embeds, `sendGameEvent`, `sendNewsEvent`) extracted to `src/lib/discordWebhooks.ts` (server-only, imports MongoDB). All import sites updated. Prevents MongoDB from being bundled in client-side code.

