## [0.0.25] - 2026-02-07

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Approval over time chart** - `/national` page now shows a pure-SVG line chart of government approval per turn, with hover crosshair, turn labels, and reference lines at 40% and 50%. History (capped at 20 turns) is persisted to the `governmentApprovals` collection each turn via `snapshotApprovalHistory()` in `governmentApproval.ts`. `GET /api/national/approval` now accepts `?country=UK` and returns `{ governmentApproval, history[] }`. Chart component: `src/components/charts/ApprovalChart.tsx`.
- **Approval modifiers rework** - Expanded from 32 to 58 named conditions (27 positive, 31 negative). All label names now describe the **metric state** (e.g. "High Corruption" not "Corrupt Government"). Effects scaled down (max ±5) to reduce single-modifier dominance. Added many single-condition modifiers that fire more easily. New conditions include: High Immigration Pressure (−3, migration rate ≥ 1.0), Aging Population (−2), Declining Population (−2), Corruption Concerns (−2), Low Public Trust (−2), Rising Inequality (−2), High Homelessness (−2), Poor Air Quality (−2), Food Insecurity (−2), Polarized Media (−2), High Violent Crime (−2), High Unemployment (−2), Low Life Expectancy (−3), High Broadband Access (+2), Free Press (+2), Green Energy Transition (+2), Low Unemployment (+2), High Public Trust (+2), High Voter Turnout (+2), Balanced Budget (+2), High Social Mobility (+2), High Life Expectancy (+2), Falling Crime (+2), Affordable Cost of Living (+2), Low Poverty Rate (+2), and more. Removed "Migration Magnet" (was +3 positive). Design doc updated: `docs/design/government-approval.md`.
- **`ApprovalTooltip` component** - `src/components/ApprovalTooltip.tsx`. Hover over any approval percentage to see a tooltip listing active positive/negative modifiers and the net sum. Renders via a React portal (`createPortal`) to escape `overflow-hidden` hero card containers. Wired into the state page stats strip, country overview leadership strip, and national metrics page header.
- **Metric quality badges** - Each metric card on the national metrics page now shows an absolute-score badge (Excellent / Very Good / Good / Fair / Bad / Very Bad) computed via `scoreMetric()` in `src/lib/utils/metricScoring.ts`.
- **UK national metrics page** - `/national?country=uk` now supports UK regions. `isUK` param drives region-aware titles, breadcrumbs, links (`/uk/region/…`), and footer nav.
- **UK map approval layer** - `GET /api/uk/map/overview` now returns per-region approval scores; `UKMapClient.tsx` has an Approval mode with green/yellow/red heatmap and approval labels in the region list.
- **UK state baselines** - 12 UK region baseline docs seeded to `stateBaselines` collection; available via admin seed route (`ukBaselines` target).
- **UK policy isolation** - `processStatePolicyEffects` now fetches `"federal"` policies for US states and `"uk_national"` policies for UK regions separately, preventing cross-country policy contamination.
- **National approval vs global averages** - `calculateApprovalFromAverages` compares a country's metric averages against global averages (all countries), eliminating the structural ~50% floor that averaging relative state scores produced.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Country overview page rework** - Removed About, Leadership, and Core Metrics info sections. Stats strip now shows live data: President (with avatar + character link, or "Vacant"), Senate Majority Leader, Speaker of the House, and Government Approval - all fetched in parallel from `/api/whitehouse`, `/api/congress/senate-leadership`, `/api/congress/speaker`, and `/api/national/metrics`. "Status" stat renamed to "Registration" (Open / Beta / Coming Soon). UK strip simplified to Executive, Head of State, Approval, and Registration. `LeaderStatItem` component handles player (linked) / NPP (name only) / Vacant states. `CountryOverviewClient.tsx`.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Orphan senate elections** - `ensurePerpetualElections` now uses `SENATE_CLASSES[stateId]` (the correct 2 classes per state) instead of iterating all 3. Admin endpoint `POST /api/admin/officials/heal-senate` deletes pre-existing orphan elections. `GET` is a dry-run.
- **Security hardening** - `/api/admin/turn/init` guarded with `requireAdmin` (was completely unauthenticated). Universal search ReDoS fixed by escaping user input before `new RegExp()`. Login timing attack mitigated with dummy bcrypt compare. Register email/username existence no longer leaked via separate error messages. Hero image URL endpoints validate protocol. HTTP security headers added (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy`). `discordTag` field max-length validated.
- **Hero height consistency** - `politicians/page.tsx` and `actions/page.tsx` corrected from `h-[180px] sm:h-[240px]` to the site-wide standard `h-[175px] sm:h-[220px]`.
- **Seed route TypeScript errors** - `as any` assertions on string `_id` arrays in `deleteMany`/`updateOne` calls that the MongoDB driver types incorrectly required `ObjectId` for.

### Chore

- **Project skills** - 8 Claude Code project skills created in `~/.claude/skills/project_skills/`: `ahd-api-route`, `ahd-commit`, `ahd-country-system`, `ahd-design-system`, `ahd-housekeeping`, `ahd-release`, `ahd-security-audit`, `ahd-turn-system`.
- **Directory housekeeping** - 7 completed plans archived to `docs/plans/archive/completed/`; loose docs moved to `docs/audits/` and `docs/design/`; `.gitignore` updated with `.trae/` and `scripts/audit/report-*.md`.

---

## [0.0.24] - 2026-02-06

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Career history tracking** - Characters now accumulate a career timeline recording elections won, elections lost, appointments, resignations, and removals. Shown on the profile page as a chronological timeline with color-coded event dots.
- **Live updates (SSE)** - Server-Sent Events endpoint (`/api/events`) pushes real-time game events to connected clients. A global `LiveRefreshBanner` appears when a new turn is processed, prompting users to refresh without forcing a page reload. Client-side `useGameEvents` and `useLiveRefresh` hooks available for custom integrations.
- **Automated news feed** - Election results and bill signings/vetoes now automatically generate system news posts on the National News page. Election results are aggregated by type (e.g. "US House Results (12 races): Democrat 7, Republican 5") with player winners highlighted. System posts have a distinct visual treatment with category badges.
- **Committee chair appointments** - The Speaker of the House and Senate Majority Leader can now appoint committee chairs for their respective chambers directly from the Committees tab. Appointees are notified and receive the committee_member achievement.
- **Committee delay mechanic** - Committee chairs can delay bills that touch their policy area by 24 hours. Each chair can delay a bill once per chamber vote. Delay history is shown on the bill detail page.
- **Bill voting deadline enforcement** - Federal bill votes now properly enforce `votingEndsAt` and `overrideVotingEndsAt` deadlines, preventing late votes.
- **NPP veto override participation** - Non-player party members now cast votes during federal veto override proceedings, matching their behavior in regular bill votes.
- **State bill & override notifications** - State bill sponsors now receive notifications on bill pass/fail/override outcomes. Congress members are notified when a federal veto override vote opens.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Turn system resilience** - Each turn sub-step (action refresh, fund generation, elections, bills, etc.) is now individually wrapped in error handling. A single failing phase no longer crashes the entire hourly turn; instead the turn continues and reports warnings for any phases that failed.
- **Admin turn API** - Process and batch turn endpoints now return a `warnings` array when phases fail non-critically. Batch processing no longer halts on warned turns (only on critical failures where the turn didn't advance).

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Federal seatsHeld vote weighting** - Player character votes on federal bills and veto overrides now correctly use `seatsHeld` weight instead of always counting as 1. Consistent with state legislature voting and NPP voting.
- **Override vote key parsing** - Veto override resolution no longer crashes on `npp_` prefixed vote keys when tallying results.
- **Bill withdraw during active status** - Bills can now be withdrawn while in `active` voting status, not just `proposed`.
- **State bill provision sanitization** - State bill provisions are now properly validated and clamped to valid ranges.
- **Empty notification templates** - `veto_override` and `override_failed` bill statuses now correctly notify sponsors and co-sponsors.

### Removed

- **Dead shared types** - Deleted `shared/types/` directory (Player, GameState, ActionType, Election types that didn't match actual DB types and were never imported).
- **Dead shared constants** - Deleted `shared/constants/gameConfig.ts` (unused DEFAULT_GAME_CONFIG, SENATE_CLASS_OFFSETS, OFFICE_ACTION_BONUSES) and `shared/constants/states.ts` (deprecated 5-state MVP file).
- **Dead formula functions** - Removed 15 unused functions from `shared/constants/formulas.ts`: calculateFundraiseIncome, calculateCampaignInfluenceGain, calculateCampaignFavorabilityGain, calculateAdsInfluenceGain, calculateAdsFavorabilityGain, calculateDonorBaseCost, calculateMediaAppearanceCost, calculateAttackFavorabilityDamage, calculateAttackInfluenceDamage, calculateAttackInfamyGain, calculateVotes, calculateInfamyDecay, calculateInfluenceDecay, calculateNPPInfluenceDecay, calculateFavorabilityDrain, and related constants. Actual action formulas live in `src/lib/actions.ts`.

