## [0.0.22] - 2026-02-05

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **SEO: robots.ts** - Crawler directives allowing public pages, disallowing authenticated routes and API.
- **SEO: sitemap.ts** - Dynamic sitemap with 9 static routes (landing, wiki, changelog, politicians, news, world, login, register, elections).
- **SEO: OpenGraph & Twitter metadata** - Root layout now includes `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:type`, `twitter:card` tags; wiki dynamic pages enhanced with OG/Twitter metadata.
- **SEO: JSON-LD structured data** - WebApplication schema (name, description, applicationCategory: "Game") in root layout.
- **SEO: Login & register metadata** - Page-specific titles and descriptions via server-component layout wrappers.
- **Shared `SectionLabel` component** - Replaced 5 local `SectionHeader` functions and 17 inline accent-bar labels across 22 files with a single reusable `<SectionLabel>` component.
- **Skeleton loading states** - Actions, Parties, Politicians, and Congress pages now show shaped skeleton placeholders instead of plain "Loading…" text.
- **Error states** - Parties page shows error banner with `role="alert"` on data fetch failure.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Theme compatibility** - ~50 hardcoded `zinc-*`, `gray-*`, and hex color values across 54 files replaced with semantic theme tokens (`bg-card`, `text-muted`, `border-card-border`, `bg-success/warning/error/info`). All 6 themes (Default, Light, OLED, USA, Pastel, Dark Pastel) now render correctly everywhere.
- **Election badges/warnings** - Phase badges and warning banners use semantic tokens instead of fixed blue/amber/green/yellow.
- **Character profile pages** - Favorability meters, text, and borders fully themed.
- **Election charts** - SVG hex colors in vote trend graphs, polling bars, and map fills replaced with CSS custom properties.
- **Stats strips overflow** - `flex-wrap` -> `overflow-x-auto` on stat bars below hero headers; no more broken dividers on small screens.
- **Consistent spacing** - Hero pages and content pages use standardized `py-8` / `py-12 sm:py-16` vertical padding.
- **Button sizing** - Primary variant `h-12` -> `h-10` for consistency.
- **Actions page fonts** - Removed 4 `@fontsource` imports (playfair-display, source-sans-3); uses design system fonts.
- **Card shadows** - `shadow-xl` -> `shadow-panel` (cards) and `shadow-modal` (overlays) across ~32 files.
- **Color contrast (WCAG 2.1 AA)** - Bumped `--muted` values for Default, OLED, and Dark Pastel themes to meet 4.5:1 contrast ratio.
- **Keyboard navigation** - 7 dropdown menus and 6 modals now support Escape to close, with `aria-expanded`, `aria-haspopup`, `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal` attributes.
- **Form accessibility** - `htmlFor`/`id` pairs added to ProposeBillModal, CabinetNominateModal, WhiteHouseClient. Error divs use `role="alert"`. Policy sliders have `aria-label`.
- **Heading hierarchy** - `h3` -> `h2` corrections on banned page, global-error, character profile. Theme buttons have `aria-pressed`. Focus-visible ring on TurnControls input.
- **Politicians API N+1** - Replaced `find({})` + in-memory filtering with MongoDB `$lookup` aggregation that filters by country and ban status server-side.
- **Pre-existing test fix** - `campaignTurn.test.ts` mock updated with `.find()` support for bulk candidate queries.

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Country-aware registration** - Registration form now begins with a country selection step (US 🇺🇸 / UK 🇬🇧). State list filters to the selected country, label adapts ("Home State" / "Home Region"), and party dropdown fetches real parties from the API grouped as Major Parties and Community Parties.
- **Party hero images** - Parties can now set a hero banner image; regional party naming support added.
- **Admin: Heal Senate Classes** - New "Heal" sub-tab in Admin -> System with a dry-run diagnostic and a one-click fix that removes senate official/election records for classes that don't belong to their state.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Action cost scaling** - Action point costs for `advertise`, `fundraise`, and `buildDonorBase` now scale with character progression:
  - `advertise`: 5–9 AP based on current favorability (tiers at 30 / 50 / 70 / 85)
  - `fundraise`: 3–18 AP based on donor base level (exponential; caps at level 5)
  - `buildDonorBase`: 6–26 AP based on donor base level (exponential; caps at level 5)
- **Fund cost scaling** - Fund costs for `advertise` and `buildDonorBase` now scale by tier × state GDP per capita, matching the existing `campaign` system. `poll`, `pollLarge`, and `rest` costs unchanged.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **Senate class spawning** - `ensurePerpetualElections` now only creates elections for each state's actual 2 senate classes (from `SENATE_CLASSES`) instead of all 3. Previously every state accumulated a spurious third-class election on each turn tick.

### Refactored

- **`NavbarWrapper` -> `useReducer`** - 11 separate `useState` calls consolidated into single typed `useReducer` with 9 action types, reducing cascading re-renders.
- **`Navbar` -> `React.memo`** - Wrapped with `React.memo()` to prevent unnecessary re-renders when NavbarWrapper internal state changes.
- **Election map dynamic imports** - `PresidentialMapWithStateDetail`, `StateCountyMapCompact`, `StateCDMapCompact` now use `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false` and skeleton loading fallback.

