## [0.0.21] - 2026-02-04

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Automatic congressional leadership elections** - Speaker, House Majority/Minority Leader, Senate Pro Tempore, and Senate Majority/Minority Leader elections open automatically (12h window) after each US chamber election resolves. Includes deduplication, incumbent auto-nomination, turn-based auto-resolution, and NPP fallback if no candidates ran.
- **AP/NYT-style primary results** - Per-party primary sections redesigned: candidate rows with proportional bars (leader at 100%, others scaled relative). Uncontested races show a badge. Trend graph retained for competitive races.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **CI lint (`no-country-literals`)** - 48 hardcoded country-ID comparisons across 15 files replaced with `COUNTRY_CONFIGS.<X>.id`.
- **House of Commons page** - Live Parliament page with composition tab (seat summary, party bar, MP list), bills tab, and leadership tab. Loading skeleton and partial-error retry included.
- **UK bill proposal endpoint** - `POST /api/legislature/uk/bills` requires seated MP or admin; deducts national influence for extra provisions.
- **Version in mobile menu** - Mobile nav footer now shows `vX.X.X · commitHash` linking to `/changelog`.
- **UK Parliament seat count** - Members API now queries `electedOfficials` instead of `characters`/`npps` separately; NPP-held seats appear correctly after elections.
- **Bill proposal auth** - `canPropose` now checks `electedOfficials` and uses `getAuthUser().catch(() => null)` so unauthenticated GETs don't error.
- **UK Commons cycle duration** - `durationHours` corrected 240 -> 480 turns; cycle 1 anchored to turn 240 (end of LARP 2024).
- **Election status/timer discrepancy** - `getGameTime()` now uses `lastTurnProcessed` as `effectiveNow` instead of real-clock `new Date()`, fixing phase/timer drift after batch turns.
- **House election cycle anchoring** - Cycles realigned to even years 2022/2024/2026; cycle 1 bootstrap ends turn 144 (`HOUSE_CYCLE1_END_TURN`).
- **`recalibrate-timers` stale clock** - `ensurePerpetualElections`/`ensureUKElections` now receive `lastTurnProcessed` instead of `new Date()`, preventing elections from spawning already-expired.
- **`sync-date` reset incompleteness** - Clears `pausedAt`/`nextScheduledTurn` on reset and deletes `primarySnapshot`, `nppEndorsements`, `playerEndorsements` alongside other election-linked collections.
- **`useState` literal type inference** - Cast `BILL_CATEGORIES[0]` as `string` to fix build error with newer `@types/react` narrowing to literal type.
- **UK election year label** - All callsites now pass `STARTING_YEAR = 2020`; previously `UK_STARTING_YEAR (2024)` produced labels ~4 years ahead.
- **`sync-date` stale game-time cache** - Now calls `invalidateGameTimeCache()` after updating gameState.
- **`sync-date` silent gameState update failure** - Throws 500 if `updateOne` `matchedCount` is 0, preventing stale `lastTurnProcessed` from producing wrong year labels.
- **`ensureUKElections` cycle 1 duration** - Cycle 1 `endTime` now uses `UK_COMMONS_CYCLE1_END_TURN = 194h` instead of the full 480h duration.
- **Senate class self-healing** - `ensurePerpetualElections` now bootstraps all three classes if none have completed, and recovers individual missing classes in partial-failure scenarios.
- **`sync-date` insert-first ordering** - New elections inserted before old ones are deleted, making retries safe and preventing data loss on partial failure.
- **Candidate mismatch warning** - `resolveGeneralElections` now warns when vote tallies reference missing candidate documents.
- **Presidential resolution silent no-op** - `resolvePresidentElection` now returns `false` and logs an error (instead of silently returning `true`) when the EV winner has no candidate document.

- **CI lint false positives** - ESLint now ignores `.worktrees/` directories; eliminates ~950 spurious errors from stale worktree files.
- **TypeScript test errors** - Added missing `vitest` imports to `election.test.ts`, `state.test.ts`, `phase1-integration.test.ts`, `phase2-integration.test.ts`; added `countryId` to test fixtures in `actionRefresh.test.ts`, `calculator.test.ts`, `demographicTurnoutTurn.test.ts`, `demographics.test.ts`, and `demographicTurnout.test.ts`.

### Refactored

- **`useState` -> `useReducer`** - `FeedbackModal`, `TreasuryPanel`, `NotificationsPage`, `FeedbackTab`, `ElectionsManageTab`, `DemographicsManager` each converted from 11–15 `useState` calls to a single typed `useReducer`.
- **Closure-narrowing non-null assertions** - Replaced `election!.winnerId!` in closure callbacks with captured `const winnerId` in two election routes.
- **`withRouteError` deprecated** - Marked `@deprecated`, pointing to the `handleRouteError` try/catch pattern.
- **Campaign turn N+1 queries** - `processCampaignTurn` now bulk-fetches all candidate characters and NPPs with two `$in` queries instead of one `findOne` per campaign; opposition research target resolution similarly batch-resolved.
- **Influence panel shared state** - Extracted `useInfluencePanelState` hook and `influence/types.ts` shared interfaces across `NPPInfluencePanel`, `StatePartyInfluencePanel`, and `NationalPartyInfluencePanel`, eliminating ~27 duplicate `useState` declarations.
- **`handleInitialize` unified in `OfficialsManager`** - Inline executive init button extracted into `handleInitialize("executive")`, removing ~20 lines of duplicated fetch logic.

