## [0.0.20] - 2026-02-04

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **UK Parliament Infrastructure** - Foundation for House of Commons page implementation:
  - **API Endpoints:** Three new endpoints for UK Parliament data:
    - `/api/legislature/uk/members` - Returns 650-seat Commons composition with party breakdown
    - `/api/legislature/uk/bills` - Returns Commons bills with pagination support
    - `/api/legislature/uk/leaders` - Returns Prime Minister and Opposition Leader
  - **Legislature Data Hook:** New `useLegislatureData` React hook for fetching legislature data with:
    - Parallel API fetching for optimal performance (members, bills, leaders)
    - Support for both UK Parliament and US Congress endpoints
    - Comprehensive error handling with partial failure support
    - Loading states and refetch functionality
    - Full test coverage with happy-dom environment
  - **Legislature Header Component:** Reusable `LegislatureHeader` component for both US/UK:
    - Hero image section with stats strip (majority party, seats, leaders)
    - Optional chamber switcher for bicameral systems (US only)
    - Responsive design matching existing Congress page patterns
    - Full test coverage (8 tests)
- **Roadmap System** - Admin-managed roadmap with three phases (Alpha/Beta/Release):
  - New `roadmapItems` MongoDB collection with CRUD API routes
  - Admin Roadmap Manager under Content tab with add/edit/complete/delete/reorder
  - Wiki roadmap page now shows live data with progress bars per phase
  - Public API endpoint at `/api/roadmap` for the wiki page
  - **Roadmap Categories** - Optional category/subcategory grouping for roadmap items:
    - New `roadmapCategories` collection with CRUD API at `/api/admin/roadmap/categories`
    - Admin UI: collapsible "Manage Categories" panel with subcategory chips, reorder, delete
    - Items can be assigned a category and subcategory via inline dropdowns
    - Wiki roadmap groups items by category within each phase with mini progress bars
    - Subcategories shown as indented groups; uncategorized items appear under "General"
- **Version Display** - Settings dropdown now shows `vX.X.X · commitHash` linking to `/changelog`
- **Public Changelog** - New `/changelog` page rendering `PUBLIC_CHANGELOG.md` with player-facing changes
- **Developer Changelog toggle** - Admin-only toggle on changelog page switching to analytical dev view with search, monospace code rendering, and color-coded sections
- **Achievements Redesign** - Overhauled the profile achievements section:
  - **Rarity-based visual styling** - Achievement cards now display colored borders and glows based on rarity tier (Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary)
  - **Progress bar** - Shows total unlocked achievements with percentage at the bottom of the section
  - **Locked achievement display** - Expanded view shows all achievements grouped by category, with unearned ones grayed out and hidden achievements shown as "???"
  - **Creative renaming** - All 45 achievements renamed with political puns and historical references (e.g. "Filibuster Buster", "Mr. Smith Goes to Washington", "Fat Cat")
  - **Admin sync tool** - New "Sync Names" button in admin panel to update existing DB achievement names from seed data without affecting earned data
- **County-Level Election Maps** - New county and congressional district visualization system for detailed election results:
  - State election results page (`/elections/[id]/state/[stateId]`) with interactive SVG maps
  - County map component with hover tooltips displaying vote breakdown, margin, and partisan lean
  - Compact county map on Senate/governor/state senate election pages with link to full map
  - Congressional district map with seat distribution summary
  - County vote distribution algorithm using partisan lean and population data
  - Map data generation script from Census TopoJSON (51 states, 3047 counties)
  - API routes for county and CD result computation
- **Dedicated Campaign Page** (`/campaign/[id]`) - Standalone campaign page with three access tiers (owner, party, public)
- **Campaign API** (`GET /api/campaigns/[id]`) - Campaign data scoped to the viewer's access level
- **Campaign navbar API** (`GET /api/campaigns/mine`) - Lightweight endpoint for nav links
- **Actions/turn display** - Campaign page shows actions earned per turn with endorsement count and formula breakdown
- **Campaign tooltips** - Hover tooltips on all resource stats, operation categories, budget line items, upgrade costs, maintenance, and cumulative stats
- **Campaign Song feature** - Characters can set a YouTube video as their campaign song with custom audio player UI. Appears on profile page below policy compass. Autoplay settings for owner and viewers.
- **Admin Law Types Creator** - Admin panel feature (Game > Law Types) to create and manage legislation types with multi-metric effects, demographic targeting, scope options, persistence modes, and step-by-step wizard
- **Universal Game Seeder** - Admin panel section under System > Universal Seeder with full seed, partial seed, reset toggle, admin-authenticated API, and live feedback
- **Custom error pages** - 404, global error, 403, and enhanced loading state with political-themed designs

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Code Quality Improvements** - Major refactoring across two phases:
  - **Phase 2**: Extracted 11 domain services from 3 large API routes (1,128 lines removed)
  - **Phase 8**: Extracted 5 congressional services (470 lines removed), refactored leadership election routes
- **Navigation Consolidation** - Consolidated Executive and Legislature dropdowns into "The Nation" dropdown for desktop and mobile
- **Campaign panel redesigned** - Removed custom dark theme styling; now uses the app's standard design system
- **Campaign separated from election page** - Election detail page shows compact campaign summary card with link instead of embedding full UI
- **Campaign landing page** (`/campaign`) - Now redirects to user's active campaign page
- **CampaignsListPanel** - Links now point to `/campaign/[id]` dedicated page
- **Executive dropdown** - Campaign links resolve to user's own campaign and party campaign pages
- **Cabinet position cards** - Redesigned with role descriptions, succession order badges, and avatar images
- **White House page cabinet section** - Enhanced with contextual information and improved visual design
- **Landing Page** - Reduced AI/NPP terminology references (removed NPP metric card, explanation section, and feature card)
- **Presidential election results page** - Added unified electoral college distribution bar (538 votes, 270 marker) and expanded stats table with endorsements
- **Notifications system overhaul** - All 37 notification types styled, pagination, type filtering, search, delete, bulk selection, auto-mark-as-read, URL-based filters, date grouping
- **Admin Panel Overhaul** - Redesigned all admin tabs with improved layouts, collapsible sections, Tailwind migration, and consistent styling across Users, Logs, Achievements, NPP Management, Officials, Elections, Demographics, Resources, and Game Reset panels
- **Profile page visual overhaul** - Hero card with party-colored gradient, stat backgrounds, shadow effects, improved depth and visual hierarchy

### Technical

- **Runtime Stability & Consistency Sweep** - Technical debt reduction across three areas:
  - **Non-null assertion cleanup** - Fixed closure-narrowing `!` assertions in 4 election files (`parties/[id]/election/route.ts`, `state/[id]/party/[partyId]/election/route.ts`, `nationalPartyElections.ts`, `statePartyElections.ts`); captured winner IDs as constants before closures to eliminate runtime crash risk
  - **Component state reduction** - Converted 5 high-complexity components from multiple `useState` calls to single `useReducer`: `FeedbackModal` (15->1), `TreasuryPanel` (15->1), `NotificationsPage` (12->1), `FeedbackTab` (11->1), `ElectionsManageTab` (11->1); eliminates state sync bugs where async updates could race each other
  - **API error handler standardization** - Marked `withRouteError` HOF as `@deprecated` with JSDoc pointing to the canonical `handleRouteError` pattern

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **County/CD map errors** - Fixed API queries, FIPS code parsing, population/partisan lean data loading, lean direction display, position sign convention, and CD-level partisan lean values
- **Third party colors on maps** - Maps now fetch actual party colors from database instead of using hardcoded colors
- **UK region hero images** - All 12 UK regions now display working hero images from Wikimedia Commons
- **Banned page theming** - Fixed hardcoded colors to use theme tokens for proper dark/light theme support
- **Election vote calculation bug** - Fixed approval rating multiplier that was drastically inflating vote totals; now uses balanced formula (50% approval = 1.0x neutral)
- **Presidential state lean multiplier bug** - Reduced lean strength from 1.1 to 0.15 and increased minimum vote floor from 15% to 50%
- **Status bar actions/funds not updating** - Footer bar now updates immediately when completing an action
- **NPP primary behavior** - NPPs receive 25% score penalty against players, can no longer be in multiple primaries, more likely to drop out facing players, prefer uncrowded primaries

