## [0.0.19] - 2026-02-03

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **UK 2020 Political Alignment** - Realistic starting conditions for UK gameplay with 2020 regional polling data for all 12 regions and 7 parties
- **Multi-Country Scalability (Phases 1–3)** - Foundation through full implementation of multi-country support:
  - **Phase 1**: Database indexes on `countryId`, required `countryId` on all country-scoped models, migration script, integration tests
  - **Phase 2**: Unified `/country/[code]/...` routing, generic country/map/region pages, generic `LegislatureDropdown` and `RegionDropdown` components, legacy route redirects
  - **Phase 3 - Canada**: 13 provinces/territories, 5 parties, 338-seat House of Commons, 105-seat Senate, Prime Minister executive, CanadaMapPaths SVG
  - **Phase 3 - Germany**: 16 states, 6 parties, 736-seat Bundestag (MMP), 69-seat Bundesrat, Chancellor executive, GermanyMapPaths SVG
  - Parameterized tests for all 4 countries, ESLint rule preventing hardcoded country literals, World page
  - Adding a 5th country now requires only config + seed data + map SVG (~1 day vs 1-2 weeks previously)
- **Full Legislation-Metrics Coverage** - All 56 state metrics now affected by legislation: extended 20+ existing laws with secondary effects, added 12 new legislation types, new `npm run simulate` command, recidivism rate metric, and prison rehabilitation laws
- **State-Level Demographic Turnout System** - 21 Layer 1 demographics with independent turnout modifiers, turnout decay, party GOTV, player canvassing, campaign season multiplier, diminishing returns, election integration, turnout visualization, admin controls, and comprehensive tests
- **Presidential Elections System** - Complete presidential election implementation:
  - Electoral College (538 EV, ME/NE district split), primaries (national appeal), general (per-state vote accumulation)
  - Presidential election map mode on map page and election detail page
  - Presidential primary scoring with national political influence and heavier policy weights
  - Admin controls: Start Primary, Start General, Place Candidate, Resolve Election, Remove Candidate
  - One candidate per party enforcement
  - 269–269 EV tie-breaker via deterministic coin flip (SHA-256)
  - ME/NE district lean proxies (UNIT_LEAN)
  - Presidential achievements (Presidential Hopeful, Presidential Nominee, President)
  - Independents allowed but penalized (0.3x), VP selection, NPPs can run
  - Presidential vote weights with steeper party org curve and state lean
  - Unit tests for presidential election engine and electoral vote constants
- **Product Roadmap wiki page** - New `/wiki/roadmap` page with audit, gap analysis, and phased plan
- **Navbar direct links to active presidential race** - Elections and Presidential Election links go directly to active election page
- **Turn system optimizations** - Presidential vote accumulation pre-loads data in 5 queries instead of ~200+; bulkWrite for action refresh, fund generation, and election timers; parallel processing for party elections, NPP behaviour, and party actions
- **Profile settings redesign** - New layout with sidebar navigation, hero section with avatar upload, scroll spy, and improved visual hierarchy
- **State page design improvements** - Back link to map, governor profile link, theme tokens, tab URL persistence, demographics mobile layout, card consistency, loading/error states

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **UK 2020 alignment** - UK party national tax rates reset to 0%; state party org levels now vary by region and party strength
- **Multi-Country Phases 1–2** - `countryId` now required on country-scoped models; all country-specific conditionals refactored to `CountryConfig` pattern; API routes scope by `countryId`; components accept `countryId` prop; navbar is country-agnostic
- **Party treasury tab redesign** - Replaced billboard stat cards with income statement card and always-visible command card; state selector shows full names
- **Demographic overhaul** - Strengthened voter group default leans for clearer ideological differentiation; ideology-modulated group leans shift based on state conservative/progressive composition; state lean recalibrated to pure turnout-weighted average; lean display thresholds updated
- **Electoral map balance** - State seed ideology configs tuned for realistic swing-state distribution (Left ~222 EVs, Center ~81 EVs, Right ~235 EVs)

### Removed

- **Hardcoded country conditionals** - Eliminated all hardcoded `if (countryId === "US")` / `if (countryId === "UK")` conditionals throughout codebase

### Deprecated

- **Legacy routes** - `/map`, `/dashboard`, `/uk/map`, `/uk/region/[regionId]` now redirect to `/country/[code]/...` structure; will be removed in a future version

