## [0.0.15] - 2026-02-21

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Agent instructions** - `agentinstructions.md` at project root: project overview, pointers to technical architecture, changelog etiquette, version etiquette, and design docs.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Refactored three largest components** - Split monolithic files into focused subcomponents for maintainability:
  - **CongressClient.tsx** (2,056 -> ~270 lines): Extracted `CongressCompositionTab`, `CongressBillsTab`, `CongressCommitteesTab`, `CongressLeadershipTab`, shared helpers and constants into `src/app/congress/components/`.
  - **elections/[id]/page.tsx** (1,401 -> ~280 lines): Extracted types, helpers, charts, panels, and components into `src/app/elections/[id]/components/`.
  - **StatePageTabs.tsx** (1,257 -> ~95 lines): Extracted `PoliticsTab`, `DemographicsTab`, `LawsTab`, `PartiesTab`, `AdminTab` into `src/components/state/`.
- **Follow-up refactors** - Further modularization of extracted components:
  - **CongressLeadershipTab** - Parameterized House/Senate leadership sections via `HouseLeadershipRoleSection` and `SenateLeadershipRoleSection` in `LeadershipRoleSection.tsx`; moved `ElectionDropdown` to `LeadershipShared.tsx`.
  - **ElectionDetailPanels** - Split `GeneralElectionPanel` and `GeneralElectionNoTallyPanel` into separate files; `ElectionDetailPanels.tsx` now re-exports them.
  - **CongressBillsTab** - Extracted `ProposeBillModal` (~300 lines) into `ProposeBillModal.tsx`.
- **lib/db/types** - Split monolithic `types.ts` (1,211 lines) into domain modules under `lib/db/types/`: user, character, party, statePartyOrg, statePartyElection, nationalPartyElection, state, demographics, stateMetrics, officials, policy, gameConfig, gameState, adminLog, election, display, npp, voteTally, primarySnapshot, nppInfluence, notifications, legislation, leadership. `@/lib/db/types` now resolves to the barrel index.

