## [0.0.14] - 2026-02-21

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **The White House Page** - New `/whitehouse` page showing President, Vice President, and all 15 Cabinet positions. Accessible from the USA dropdown in the navbar. All positions currently display as vacant.
- **Party Action Generation** - National and state parties now generate 5 action points per hour, capped at 100 total. Actions beyond the cap are lost until the party spends actions to go below 100.
- **NPP Profile Pictures** - Integrated Wikimedia Commons image scraper to fetch and cache ~100 real politician portraits. New NPPs are automatically assigned a random avatar.
- **Admin: Backfill Avatars** - Utility in NPP Management to assign images to legacy NPPs that lack them.
- **Discord Integration** - Users can add their Discord tag in Settings; optionally displayed on public profile pages with Discord branding.
- **State Party Nav Link** - "State Party" option added to the global State Dropdown for easier access.
- **NPP Badge & Avatars** - State Party Member lists now show user avatars and distinct "NPP" badges for AI characters.

### Changed

- **Global Monetary Policy chart currency colors** — Chart now imports `CURRENCY_COLORS` from `currencyDisplay.ts` instead of defining a local subset, so EUR, CNY, BRL, and all other currencies render with the same theme-aware color palette used across the forex page. `src/components/forex/GlobalMonetaryPolicyChart.tsx`, `src/components/forex/currencyDisplay.ts`
- **Central bank hero images for ECB, PBoC, and BCB** — Added hero images (Wikipedia Commons photos) for the European Central Bank (Frankfurt building), People's Bank of China, and Banco Central do Brasil. Ireland's ECB config also updated. `src/app/api/images/hero/[slug]/route.ts`, `src/lib/constants/countries.ts`

- **Party Actions Tab** - Added "Actions" tab to both national and state party pages. NPP Influence moved from Overview to this tab. New "Party Resources" display shows Treasury and Actions with progress bar and generation info (+5/hour, cap 100).
- **Admin Panel Reorganization** - "NPPs" moved to a top-level tab (was under Elections); improved layout and accessibility.
- **State Party Page** - Redesigned Members tab to prioritize real players, include NPPs in list, and show avatars.
- **National Party Members** - Party page Members tab now lists NPPs below real players; NPPs link to `/npp/[id]` and show an "NPP" badge; "Send to Member" only offers player characters.
- **State page governor** - Governor portrait and name now display correctly when the governor is an NPP (name and avatar from NPP record).
- **Appointment Panel Visibility** - Fixed logic so only Admins see the "Direct Appointment" panel, while State Chairs see the "Leadership Election" panel.
- **Tax Calculation** - "Expected Income" on State Party page now includes tax revenue from NPP members.
- **State Politics tab** - Replaced legacy policy sliders with compact `DetailedPolicyDisplay`; uses correct weighted average for party strength.
- **Political lean** - Restored lean indicator in top stats bar on state page; map page shows Political Lean map mode with blue/red shading; lean display logic shared between state and map (scaled −5..+5, consistent labels/colors).
- **Demographic lean calculation** - Rewrote to use weighted average per category (by population), then by category weight (like elections); result scaled by 6 so values span −5..+5.
- **Demographic category weights** - Education 20->25%, wealth 15->20%; race and ideology reduced to keep sum 100.
- **Version & changelog etiquette** - Project version synced to CHANGELOG (0.0.14); README and docs/changelog-etiquette.md document version/changelog rules; alpha-phase version = changelog version; beta/release TBD.
- **Alpha warning on lander** - Banner added: "Alpha - features and data may change."

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **NPP type** - Added `avatarUrl` to NPP interface; NPP generator assigns random avatar from image cache when creating new NPPs.
- **Build errors** - Congress members route NPP import; debug demographics State collection type; state page null check order; NPPManagement stats type; AdminTabs TabId.

