## [0.0.12] - 2026-02-21

### Added

- **Auto run for re-election** — New toggle in Settings → Policy Positions lets characters opt in to be automatically entered into upcoming elections in their home district each cycle. A new `autoReelectionEntry` turn phase (runs after `perpetualElections`) queries characters with `autoRunForReelection: true`, matches them to active/upcoming non-presidential elections by `homeState` + `countryId`, and inserts `electionCandidates` entries. Respects the primary entry deadline; skips characters with any prior candidacy entry in the election (preserving manual withdrawals); skips characters blocked by another active candidacy. Presidential races are excluded. `src/lib/db/types/character.ts` (`autoRunForReelection` field), `src/app/api/settings/reelection-preference/route.ts`, `src/lib/turn/autoReelectionEntry.ts`, `src/lib/turnSystem.ts`, `src/app/settings/components/PoliticsSection.tsx`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx`

- **Leadership candidacy limits**: One active candidacy at a time across Speaker, House leadership, and Senate leadership; must withdraw from one race before declaring in another.
- **Admin start/reset without chamber membership**: Admins can start or reset Speaker, House leadership, and Senate leadership elections without being a House member or Senator.
- **Candidate avatars in leadership dropdowns**: Speaker and House/Senate leadership candidacy lists show profile pictures (Avatar) when available instead of letter placeholders.
- **Voting UX**: Leadership election dropdown opens by default when the user can vote; summary text says " - vote for one below" when eligible.
- **Speaker & House leadership - 12-hour plurality elections**: Speaker, Majority Leader, and Minority Leader use a 12-hour voting window (admin-started). Only the relevant party runs and votes (majority for Speaker/Majority Leader, minority for Minority Leader); **plurality** winner (top vote-getter) wins. NPPs in the majority party vote for the candidate closest to their policy; resolution when the window ends. API: `GET/POST /api/congress/speaker`, `GET/POST /api/congress/house-leadership`.
- **Leadership UI**: House tab shows **Majority** and **Minority** sections with party seat counts; roles show portrait, **name (D-TX)**, and election/assign UI. Leaders API returns `state` for display.
- **Senate leadership**: President Pro Tempore elected by Senate (declare, all Senators vote, majority wins). Other House/Senate roles assignable by admin via `GET/POST /api/congress/leaders`.
- **Bill detail**: Parliament chart (ayes/nays by party with party filter) and tabbed vote tally table by chamber.
- **Congress & law audit**: Bills and policy screens use refined economic/social position labels when set; position block omitted when both axes zero. Legislation types (e.g. School Standards, Housing) and base policies updated (social axis, 2026 alignment). Design doc `docs/design/congress-leadership.md`.
- **Senate leadership - same as House**: President Pro Tempore, Majority Leader, and Minority Leader use 12-hour plurality elections (only that party runs and votes). API: `GET/POST /api/congress/senate-leadership` with `role: pro_tempore | majority_leader | minority_leader`. `getSenateComposition()` and collections `senateLeadershipElections`, `senateLeadershipNominations`.
- **Leader badges on Composition**: Congress -> Composition tab shows badges (Speaker, Maj. Leader, Min. Leader, Pro Tempore, etc.) next to the member's name for the current holder. Leaders fetched from `/api/congress/leaders` and passed into the member list.

### Fixed

- **Bond holdings missing from corp tangible book value** — When a corporation buys bonds (sovereign or corporate), the purchased bond asset was not included in the tangible book component of the share-price formula. Only `issuedBondDebt` (bonds issued by the corp) was in the formula; held bond positions were tracked in `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` but never wired in. Added `bondHoldingsAnchor` field to `SharePriceInput` and included it in the `tangibleBook` calculation: `liquidCapital + sectorNPV + bondHoldings − issuedDebt`. Wired from `bondAndImfPortfolioAnchorByCorpId` in both `sectorCalculations.ts` and `recomputeSharePrices.ts`. `src/lib/turn/corporation/sharePriceFormula.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/sectorCalculations.ts`, `src/lib/turn/corporation/recomputeSharePrices.ts`
- **NPP Speaker votes**: NPPs in the majority party are now identified using `ElectedOfficial.party` when set, otherwise the NPP document's party, so all majority-party NPPs (including those without `party` on the official record) vote in Speaker elections and when there is a single candidate they receive almost all NPP votes.
- **Senate leadership admin flow**: Start election and reset election no longer require the requester to be a Senator; admins can start/reset from the Senate leadership tab.
- **Duplicate elections** - race-condition cleanup and atomic insert checks.
- **Extra House seats in small states** - authoritative `HOUSE_SEATS` cap.
- **Primary party-switch exploit** - candidacy withdrawn on party leave during active election.
- **PartyLogo** - handle undefined `partyId` (Congress Composition tab).

